window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101: Space Life (Part 1)","paragraphs":["When He Zhiran came back, she saw that Mo Jiuye had already propped up half of his body with his elbow.","She hurried over: \"I told you that you can't get up, so why are you getting up?\"","Mo Jiuye's face was a little red, and he had an expression that seemed to want to say something but held back.","\"I...I want to go to the bathroom...\"","He Zhiran immediately associated that with Mo Jiuye's body. Her face instantly turned red.","Mo Jiuye noticed her embarrassment and subconsciously lowered his head, his face had already turned into a monkey's butt...","Although He Zhiran felt this kind of embarrassment for the first time, considering Mo Jiuye's current physical condition, she tried her best not to think too much.","She bought a set of loose-fitting home clothes and a pair of men's underwear for Mo Jiuye in the store space.","\"Your clothes are all broken, wear this for now.\"","With that said, He Zhiran took the top of the home clothes and briskly put it on Mo Jiuye.","As for the underwear and pants below, considering the embarrassment between the two, He Zhiran briefly explained how to wear them, and then let Mo Jiuye wear them himself.","At the same time, she did not forget to remind him to be careful of the wound.","For this set of home clothes, Mo Jiuye did not feel anything too strange, only that the style and fabric were somewhat different from the clothes he usually wore.","The only thing was that pair of underwear. After listening to He Zhiran's introduction, he also understood what it was used for.","Although he went to wear it himself, he was still a little embarrassed, but he still wore it as she said.","What surprised him was that this thing called underwear turned out to be very comfortable when worn...","After a long time, Mo Jiuye finally regained his messy thoughts and said softly, \"I put it on.\"","Only then did He Zhiran turn around and carefully helped him down from the operating table and slowly walked towards the bathroom.","At this moment, the two people's hearts, like frightened deer, could be heard very clearly in this quiet space.","Making the atmosphere in the space even more embarrassing.","Supporting Mo Jiuye out of the operating room, they came to the bathroom door.","He Zhiran finally broke the silence.","\"This is the bathroom, be careful by yourself.\"","\"Okay!\"","Mo Jiuye casually responded and opened the door to walk in.","After a long time, He Zhiran did not hear any movement inside.","She knocked on the door.","\"How are you? Are you okay?\"","After waiting for about thirty seconds without hearing Mo Jiuye respond, just as He Zhiran thought something had happened to him and was about to break down the door, Mo Jiuye finally stammered out: \"Can you...come in for a minute?\"","He Zhiran instinctively thought that Mo Jiuye must have had a physical problem.","Without doubting him, He Zhiran immediately pushed open the bathroom door and walked in.","She only saw Mo Jiuye standing there whole and intact, but the expression on his face looked as constipated as it could get.","\"What's wrong with you anyway?\" He Zhiran asked.","Mo Jiuye's words were still somewhat incoherent.","\"I... I couldn't find where the toilet was...\"","He Zhiran...","She blamed herself.","Letting an ancient person go to the bathroom alone, she should have explained in advance.","She walked past Mo Jiuye and came to the white porcelain toilet bowl and gently lifted the lid.","\"Look, this is it.\"","Mo Jiuye stared at the flawless white toilet bowl for a long time.","\"Are you sure this is it?\"","He Zhiran had no choice but to demonstrate it herself.","She casually grabbed a bottle of toilet cleaner and poured it into the toilet bowl, then pressed the flush button.","Mo Jiuye saw with his own eyes that the blue water was flushed clean, and he suddenly understood the principle.","While marveling at the magic of the toilet, he invited He Zhiran out.","This time, He Zhiran did not have to wait long. After hearing a splash of water, the bathroom door opened.","Since Mo Jiuye had already gotten up anyway, He Zhiran carefully helped him get acquainted with the purpose and usage methods of many modern items in the store space, .","At this moment, Mo Jiuye had turned into a country bumpkin who had never seen the world. When He Zhiran explained, he kept asking all kinds of questions.","He even wanted to try it out himself.","Just then, He Zhiran's stomach made a gurgling sound.","She only then remembered that she and Mo Jiuye had not eaten anything for a whole day.","Although there were plenty of ingredients in the store space, He Zhiran was a little tired after being busy all day, so she gave up the idea of ​​cooking by herself.","She took out her phone and opened the Taobao page.","The pop-up dialog box made her very happy. In the past few days, two more items were sold in her store, increasing her income by 1.12 million.","With so much income, He Zhiran felt that she did not need to worry at all, and could fully realize her dream food freedom in Taobao.","Therefore, when purchasing food, she would not consider the price at all. As long as it was delicious, she wanted to eat, nutritious, she could buy some.","Mo Jiuye sat opposite her, watching a square little box appear on the table in front of him from time to time, and then a large package appeared again...","In a short while, the dining table was filled with all kinds of packages, and it would not be an exaggeration to call it a small mountain.","These things were all very novel to Mo Jiuye, and his eyes kept turning on these fresh objects.","After picking and choosing on Taobao for a long time, He Zhiran finally bought the food.","She unpacked them one by one in front of Mo Jiuye.","Egg tartlets, durian puff pastry, French mini baguettes, instant noodles, beef jerky, spicy sticks, canned food, and all kinds of snacks were readily available.","In addition, He Zhiran also bought all kinds of delicious fruits.","Kyoho grapes, water honey peaches, apples, strawberries, cherries, pineapples, bananas, and her favorite durian.","Finally, she opened the biggest package.","This was a whole set of barbecue dinner set.","The ingredients in the set were very rich.","The beef, mutton, pork belly were all marinated.","There were also various vegetables, mushrooms and small seafood.","Most importantly, the seller also gifted a barbecue pot with the set, and the dipping sauce was divided into spicy and non-spicy flavors.","After He Zhiran unpacked all the items, Mo Jiuye's eyes were not enough to take it all in.","She patiently explained these foods to him, then moved all the snacks and fruits to the side to make room for them to enjoy the barbecue dinner set.","He Zhiran washed the barbecue pot clean, plugged it in, and prepared small porcelain plates of dipping sauce for both of them.","Right in front of Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran skillfully started barbecuing.","The sizzling sound broke the silence of the space.","Soon, the aroma lingered around the two.","He Zhiran clipped a piece of beef and put it in Mo Jiuye's plate.","\"Dip it in the sauce in the plate, it tastes especially fragrant, try it quickly.\"","Mo Jiuye was also hungry by now, not to mention he had been attracted by the smell for a long time.","Picking up the beef in the plate, he couldn't care less about it being hot. As He Zhiran said, he dipped some sauce.","The moment it entered his mouth, Mo Jiuye fell deeply in love with this taste."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102: Space Life Part 02","paragraphs":["From a young age, this was the first time he had eaten such delicious meat.","He Zhiran also liked eating this grilled meat. After helping Mo Jiuye grab a piece, she started wolfing it down. Her facial expression of enjoyment couldn't be concealed at all.","Not only was the beef tasty, but the mutton and pork belly were equally delicious. Plus those small seafood items and various meatballs were, for Mo Jiuye, simply heaven-sent flavors of the human world.","It was just that, owing to his injuries, He Zhiran only let him have a little taste.","Just then, He Zhiran purchased another bottle of Coke and one of Sprite.","Her favorite beverage was Coke. Considering that the Coke flavor wasn't easy for people to accept, she took the initiative to buy Mo Jiuye a bottle of Sprite.","She handed the Sprite to Mo Jiuye and taught him how to open the bottle cap.","After Mo Jiuye opened the Sprite bottle, he looked again at the Coke in He Zhiran's hand.","\"How come our drinks are different?\"","He Zhiran explained: \"Mine is called Coke. The flavor is a bit peculiar. I was afraid you wouldn't be used to it, so I bought you Sprite instead.\"","Mo Jiuye poured the Sprite into a cup and took a shallow sip.","\"Mm, nice and cool, very refreshing.\"","Seeing that he didn't reject the Sprite flavor, He Zhiran nonchalantly poured herself a cup of Coke.","She had just taken a sip when Mo Jiuye brought over an empty cup.","\"Can I try your Coke?\"","He Zhiran now felt that Mo Jiuye was just a child who hadn't grown up, finding everything novel.","She laughed and helped pour him a cup of Coke, then placed it in front of him.","\"Go ahead and try it!\"","Mo Jiuye drank a mouthful and felt that he really liked this flavor.","He tipped his head back and finished the entire cup of Coke in one go.","Seeing his manner, He Zhiran knew that he actually preferred Coke over Sprite.","So she switched their drinks around.","\"I really enjoy drinking Sprite too, so why don't we swap.\"","\"Sounds good, I like this Coke.\"","The two of them ate and drank. Unknowingly, they finished all four sets of the grilled meat platter He Zhiran had bought.","He Zhiran patted her somewhat protruding belly, now stuffed full. She cleared the table clean.","Then she brought out all kinds of fruit.","Both of them were rather stuffed at the moment. He Zhiran was thinking that it was hard to come by an opportunity to eat her favorite things to her heart's content like this, so she should do her best.","Mo Jiuye sampled a little of every fruit, finally favoring the \"stinky\" durian like He Zhiran.","After eating fruit, it was already late night. Considering they still had to think of a way to leave this space tomorrow morning and possibly face new dangers again, rest and recuperation were crucial.","Thus, under He Zhiran's urging, the two went to the bedroom together.","Inside the bedroom was a large king-sized bed. As always, He Zhiran slept on the inside and Mo Jiuye on the outside.","In any case, it wasn't their first time sleeping side-by-side, so He Zhiran didn't feel awkward at all.","Lying on the soft, big bed, Mo Jiuye's thoughts were racing and restless.","By now he already knew all her secrets.","He didn't feel any sense of discomfort at all about this. On the contrary, he really liked these things.","Everything in her space, including He Zhiran herself, was so beautiful in Mo Jiuye's eyes.","Mo Jiuye felt Heaven bless and bestow him with such a wonderful woman.","At the same time, he also felt pity for He Zhiran.","After all, he was no longer the prestigious Duke who everyone respected. He had already become an exiled prisoner through and through.","Not only so, but He Zhiran had also gotten implicated because of him and his family, forced to live this kind of difficult and dangerous life everywhere.","Listening to her now steady breathing beside him, Mo Jiuye gently turned his head.","Looking at her serene, sleeping face, Mo Jiuye secretly swore in his heart that for the rest of his life he would do everything in his power to prevent her from suffering any grievances.","...","After sleeping soundly through the night, when He Zhiran opened her eyes the wall clock already displayed 8 AM.","Maybe because she had slept too late last night, or the space was too comfortable, this was the first time in two lifetimes she had slept this late.","He Zhiran rubbed her still groggy eyes and turned her head to see Mo Jiuye wasn't by her side.","Getting up and putting on her shoes, she walked out of the bedroom—only to see Mo Jiuye already busying about in the kitchen.","Steam rose from the pot on the stove. He kept his head lowered, cutting something there.","Seeing this, He Zhiran felt somewhat disoriented.","Dressed in plain home clothes, his ink-black hair cascading down his back like a waterfall, wearing two big slippers on his feet, and still holding a kitchen knife in his hand...","Hearing the sound, Mo Jiuye raised his head. His usually icy cold face actually revealed a warm smile to her.","\"You're up? Breakfast is almost ready.\"","With just this simple sentence, He Zhiran's heart instantly softened.","She didn't know when she had seen countless scenes like this on TV shows. She never expected something similar would happen in her own real life as well.","In order not to spoil this beautiful scene, after murmuring a \"Good morning,\" He Zhiran immediately buried her head in the bathroom to wash up.","When she came out after freshening up, she saw Mo Jiuye carrying over a steaming hot bowl of noodles to the dining table.","Seeing his somewhat slow movements, He Zhiran suddenly remembered his injuries.","She rushed over in large strides and took the noodles from Mo Jiuye's hands.","\"You still have wounds. Let me.\"","In truth, enduring the pain as he did these things was difficult for Mo Jiuye.","He wasn't doing it for anything else. He wanted to treat He Zhiran well, and it had to start from all the little things and details.","Mo Jiuye's wounds did hurt quite a bit. He didn't decline her help and just smiled at He Zhiran, giving her a reassuring look.","\"They're just external injuries. Things like this are nothing to me.\"","He Zhiran didn't think so at all. She had personally seen every one of his wounds.","She was the one who had stitched and dressed so many of them. How could they be simple external injuries?","Not doubting he had good intentions, after putting down the noodles on the table, He Zhiran pulled Mo Jiuye to the treatment room. While helping inspect his condition, she also changed his dressings.","Mo Jiuye didn't budge. He insisted on watching her finish the noodles before going to get his wounds examined.","He Zhiran didn't want to disappoint his good intentions either. She went back to the kitchen to dish out another bowl of noodles and brought it back. The two of them sat together and finished all the noodles.","The noodles didn't taste fantastic, but from the small details like the tea egg and vegetable leaves inside, it was apparent this man had put care into making them.","Mo Jiuye similarly felt his cooking skills were nothing great.","He thought to himself that he would have to learn more when there was a chance in the future.","After He Zhiran helped change Mo Jiuye's dressings, she also hooked him up to an IV.","\"I'm planning to try descending downwards until I reach the ground. Then I'll come back to take you out with me.\"","Mo Jiuye well knew that in his current condition, wanting to carry He Zhiran down safely from a high place was utterly impossible.","Considering they had been gone for a full day and night, his family must be worried sick. So he didn't object.","After all, now he understood the existence of this space and agreed with He Zhiran's methods too.","\"Alright, you have to be extra careful. If it doesn't work, then wait until my injuries heal before we think of another way.\""]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103: The Inquisition","paragraphs":["He Zhiran prepared two-handedly, showing Mo Jiuye the iron claws she had prepared in advance.","\"Don't worry, I still have this as a backup.\"","As her words fell, He Zhiran's figure disappeared on the spot.","Out of the space, her body quickly plummeted downwards.","He Zhiran did not dare to be careless. In less than a second outside the space, she returned to the space again.","Mo Jiuye just watched her disappear, appear, disappear, appear, going back and forth in and out of space many times, until He Zhiran did not come back. His heart was in his throat.","He Zhiran's actions went very smoothly. The last time she came out of the space, she was about ten meters away from the ground.","She directly used the iron claws to hook onto a tree branch, and her whole body slid down the rope to the ground.","This was a secluded valley, with an extremely primitive atmosphere.","What bothered He Zhiran the most was that it was surrounded by mountains on all sides here, and there was no way out at all.","He Zhiran carefully observed the surroundings and planned to find a direction to walk and see.","Just as she was about to take the first step, she vaguely heard a series of footsteps.","Judging from experience, such footsteps must be at least three people.","He Zhiran quickly hid behind a boulder, held her breath, and at the same time, took out a mini pistol and a tranquilizer gun from the space.","The footsteps grew closer and closer. Through the cracks in the rocks, four men in black could be seen walking towards her.","The man walking at the forefront said impatiently, \"We've been searching here all night. Even if they were smashed to pieces, there should be some trace. \"","\"You mean Mo Jiuye is not dead?\"","\"That's impossible. Mo Jiuye was seriously injured. Jumping off such a high cliff, how could he possibly have any hope of surviving?\"","Just as the few men in black walked while discussing whether they were dead or alive, a crisp sound suddenly broke the tranquility of the valley.","At the same time, the man in black walking at the forefront had already fallen to the ground.","In order not to give those men in black a chance to breathe and react, He Zhiran fired two more shots in a row, knocking down two more men in black.","The only surviving man in black felt something was wrong. He dodged towards He Zhiran's hiding place and walked over carefully. At the same time, he angrily said, \"Mo Jiuye, come out and have a real fight with me. Don't be a shrinking turtle.\"","He Zhiran did not respond, but instead changed her position, raised the tranquilizer gun in her hand and shot at the man in black.","The man in black fell to the ground with a cry. After He Zhiran checked that there was no danger around, she finally walked out from behind the big rock.","She first tentatively checked the breath of the man in black, then took him into the space with a flash.","Mo Jiuye was anxiously pacing back and forth outside the operating room door.","Seeing He Zhiran carrying a lifeless-looking man in black, he asked solemnly, \"Are there any other men in black outside?\"","He Zhiran casually threw the man in black on the floor.","\"I knocked him out with a tranquilizer gun to see if I could get any useful information out of him.\"","Hearing that the man in black had only fainted, Mo Jiuye hurriedly squatted in front of him and ripped off the black face cover.","Then he found a chopstick, pried open the man's mouth, and took out a poison sac from inside.","He Zhiran was not idle either, finding ropes to tie up the man in black together with Mo Jiuye.","In order to save time, He Zhiran took out drugs that could wake people up and injected them into the man in black.","Soon, the man in black woke up.","Seeing the completely unfamiliar environment around him, the man in black was clearly somewhat at a loss.","\"Where is this place?\"","\"Don't worry about where this place is. Answer my questions obediently, and I'll make your death less painful.\" He Zhiran said gloomy.","Only then did the man in black notice his back.","He looked back over his shoulder and saw Mo Jiuye at a glance.","\"Mo Jiuye, you're really not dead?\"","Mo Jiuye was too lazy to beat around the bush with him and said coldly, \"Speak, who sent you to kill me?\"","The man in black sneered: \"Do you think I would tell you?\"","As he spoke, he was about to bite through the poison sac in his mouth to commit suicide.","Who knew, after circling his tongue in the gap between his teeth, he still couldn't find the poison sac.","The man in black instantly broke out in a cold sweat.","\"Mo Jiuye, you're despicable.\"","Mo Jiuye still remained expressionless.","\"The real despicable people are the masterminds behind you.\"","Just as the man in black was about to say something, He Zhiran had already taken a syringe and injected it into the muscles of his arm before he could react.","The man in black was shocked.","\"What have you done to me?\"","He struggled, but his limbs were all tied up tightly, and he couldn't move at all.","He Zhiran sneered, \"You'll know in a while.\"","What she injected into the man in black was a drug specially developed by a certain country to deal with prisoners.","The user would first appear excited, and then feel the pain of being bitten by countless ants all over the body five minutes later.","This kind of pain would become more and more intense, to the point that it would make people reach death's door.","What’s more sinister is that after being injected with this drug, no matter how strong the body's reaction is, it is impossible to faint. One can only stay conscious and endure it all.","Sure enough, the man in black was very excited at first, showing a fearless attitude, and even threatened that even if they cut his flesh with a knife, he would not reveal the mastermind behind him.","As time passed bit by bit, the expression on the man in black's face gradually became distorted.","At first it was still good, he gritted his teeth to endure.","Unexpectedly, this pain became more and more intense, making him want to smash his head to death.","Seeing that the time was right, He Zhiran spoke at last: \"I can clearly tell you now that if you don't say, I guarantee to make you live like this forever.\"","The bloody eyes of the man in black stared fiercely at He Zhiran, emphasizing every word: \"How sinister and ruthless you are.\"","He Zhiran didn't care.","\"I don't deny this. Doing something without hesitation for a purpose is not something only I would do.\"","\"You...\" The man in black was furious with anger.","But the pain he felt in his body made it more and more unbearable for him.","Finally, the man in black gritted his teeth and said, \"We were just mercenaries taking money to solve problems. I don’t know exactly who wanted you dead.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not believe the man in black’s words at all. If he really didn’t know who the mastermind was, he could have said so from the start. There was no need to persist until now.","In order to obtain the truth, He Zhiran took another syringe again. With the needle pointed at the man in black's arm, she said coldly:","\"Judging from your appearance, your physical endurance is quite strong. Why not give you some more medicine.\"","The man in black recognized what He Zhiran was holding in her hand. It was this thing that made him feel worse than death after being stabbed by it earlier.","If he was stabbed again, he was afraid the pain would kill him.","Seeing that the needle tip was about to touch his arm, the man in black shouted: \"It's Prince Heng! We are all his warriors of death.\"","Stay tuned for more chapters coming out later today!"]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104: Don't Want to Die, Can't Die","paragraphs":["He Zhiran stopped her actions and looked towards Mo Jiuye.","After all, the original owner was not clear about the deceits in the royal court. They still had to let Mo Jiuye determine the authenticity of this matter.","Mo Jiuye took a step forward, \"You said that Prince Heng sent you to assassinate me. Do you have any evidence?\"","The man in black was seeking death at this moment so he naturally did not conceal anything.","\"The person who died in front of me just now was the team leader. He had Prince Heng's token.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran flashed out of the space and searched the few black clothed men that she had just killed.","Sure enough, she found a silver token on one person with the character \"Heng\" clearly engraved on it.","She took the token back to the space and handed it to Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye took the token and examined it before nodding towards He Zhiran.","He Zhiran immediately understood and pulled the man in black out of the space again.","Despite facing an enemy, He Zhiran was true to her word and directly ended the man's life with one strike.","Returning to the space again, she asked Mo Jiuye, \"Do you also have a grudge with Prince Heng?\"","Mo Jiuye smiled self-deprecatingly.","\"Everyone in the royal court knows that I have had a deep friendship with Nan Qi since we were young. Naturally, the other princes see me as a thorn in their side.","Prince Heng doesn't know that a rift has grown between Nan Qi and I. It's understandable that he worries I'll return to court one day and wants to get rid of me while I'm weak.\"","After this explanation, He Zhiran understood.","The Mo Family's property confiscation and exile probably didn't happen without this Prince Heng's push.","\"If that's the case, since Prince Heng's first assassination attempt failed, he will surely continue sending assassins. It looks like we really can't let our guard down in the future.\"","This was also Mo Jiuye's worry.","He alone was easy to deal with. At worst, he could perish together with those people.","But with the Mo Family's women and children, and now a woman he wanted to protect for life, Mo Jiuye didn't want to die and couldn't die.","\"Right now, the best way to stop Prince Heng from taking action against me again is to spread word that Nan Qi and I have fallen out.\"","He Zhiran nodded.","\"That is indeed a good method. Prince Heng is only concerned because of your relationship with Nan Qi. If he believes you've broken ties with Nan Qi, he'll surely lower his guard against you.","Moreover, he lost so many assassins this time. He'll surely weigh things carefully before sending people out again.\"","The logic was sound. But both felt some difficulty. How could they make Prince Heng believe that he had truly split from Nan Qi?","After thinking it over, neither could come up with a reasonable method.","Considering that their family still didn't know to worry for them, they decided leaving here first was more urgent.","Given Mo Jiuye's injuries preventing him from moving, He Zhiran decided to let him stay in the space temporarily while she went out alone to find a way out.","At first, Mo Jiuye didn't agree. He worried He Zhiran would encounter danger without help in the wilderness.","He Zhiran assured him that she would immediately retreat into the space if danger arose.","Reassured by the space's magic, Mo Jiuye felt somewhat more at ease.","After exhorting her to be cautious, he finally let her leave.","He Zhiran exited the space and searched the few black clothed men's bodies again, taking all of their sparse belongings before heading in the direction they had come from.","She believed there must be a way out to the outside world here, otherwise how did these black clothed men get here?","He Zhiran took out a Swiss army knife from the space to clear a path. She defended against scratches from the thorns while watching for snakes and bugs underfoot...","The time returned to dawn.","The Mo Family had almost not slept the entire night.","When Peng Wang beckoned for most of the group to continue on, Old Lady Mo was the first not to leave.","\"Officer Peng, my son and daughter-in-law are still of unknown life or death. I cannot leave.\"","The sisters-in-law and Mo Hengyao saw this and also expressed their determination to stay and wait for Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran to return, even if it meant being whipped to death here.","Considering Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, Officer Peng's attitude towards the Mo Family was still decent.","\"I've already told the Eighth Old Zhou to go search for them and meet up with us after three days. In three days, whether they're alive or dead will surely be determined. You waiting here is of no use. It'd be better to hurry on the road.\"","But his words had no deterrent effect on the Mo Family's women.","Led by Old Lady Mo, the women insisted on not leaving.","Even as the guards' whips were raised to fall on them, it did not make them retreat.","Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai looked at each other before walking over to the Mo Family.","The two first respectfully saluted Officer Peng.","Fang Chuanzhou then righteously said, \"Officer, the Mo Family has shown our Fang Family much benevolence on this journey. I once said I would look up to them for life. Now that this couple's life or death is unknown, we will accompany the Mo Family to wait together.\"","Xie Tianhai also stepped forward to declare, \"Officer, our Xie Family will also share the Mo Family's fortunes.\"","Peng Wang had been an escort officer for many years but this was still his first time encountering something like this.","His anger was immediately provoked. He snatched the whip from Zhang Qing's hand and fiercely lashed Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai.","Seeing them punished for her family's matter, Old Lady Mo immediately ran over to stand in front of them.","The Mo Family's other women closely followed Old Lady Mo's footsteps, uniformly shielding Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai behind them.","At the same time, the Fang and Xie family members also ran over, prepared to jointly confront the officers together.","The He Family watched this scene from afar with aloof disinterest.","Peng Wang knew these prisoners were serious. Even if he ordered all the officers attack together, it likely wouldn't shake their determination to stay and wait.","Although he knew they couldn't continue on, he couldn't lose face as an officer either.","He raised his whip and fiercely lashed the Third Sister-in-Law, who was closest to him.","The Third Sister-in-Law didn't even shout in pain or have any intention of dodging. Her gaze was firm with resignation to her fate.","Seeing this, the other women rushed up to protect the Third Sister-in-Law.","Even with his anger, Peng Wang was still shocked by the Mo Family women's resignation to their deaths.","He had to admit that whether it was the Mo Family's battle-scarred men or these powerless women, they were admirable enough.","With a sigh, Peng Wang threw away the whip in his hand.","\"Wait then! Three days. If they still haven't returned, even if I have to drag you, I'll have people drag you away.\"","\"Thank you Officer Peng for your consideration. Three days is enough,\" Old Lady Mo solemnly saluted Peng Wang.","She was clearer than anyone that if her son and daughter-in-law were still alive, they would surely be able to catch up and meet them within three days.","If not, they were likely doomed.","For now, Old Lady Mo could only pray to heaven that they were still alive."]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105: The Mohists are still waiting for you to return.","paragraphs":["When everyone saw Peng Wang agree, they simultaneously breathed a sigh of relief.","The women from the Fang Family and Xie Family rushed over to comfort the Mo Family women, hoping they could see things more openly. The Mo Family women did not expect that the Fang Family and Xie Family, who had only received some kindness from the Mo Family, would stand up for them when they needed help the most. The saying that adversity reveals true feelings was really not just empty talk. Now it was happening right in front of them.","Even as she felt gratified, Old Lady Mo was even more worried about Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's safety.","...","He Zhiran was worried about her family's circumstances in her heart, and was increasingly anxious to leave this place.","Since it was a mountain valley, she could not determine which direction the exit was in. At this moment, she felt somewhat annoyed with herself that when she was interrogating those men in black just now, she had actually forgotten to ask about the location of the exit.","Now that those men in black were dead, He Zhiran could only circle around the foot of the mountain.","Just as she was desperately pushing aside thorns and brambles to move forward with difficulty, a huge creature suddenly burst out in front of her.","It was a black bear.","The first thing He Zhiran thought was that when encountering such a thing, one could not collide with it head-on. It would be best to climb up a tree first, and then make a move.","Just as He Zhiran had already found a suitably tall tree to climb, she suddenly discovered that the black bear was not coming towards her direction.","From a distance of about a hundred meters from He Zhiran, The Eighth Old Zhou instantly spotted her figure.","\"Miss He, hide quickly! This black bear is very strong. Don't let it hurt you.\"","Perhaps because The Eighth Old Zhou was trying to avoid the black bear, he moved extremely lightly. As a result, He Zhiran did not notice his presence at first.","Only after hearing the familiar voice did she see The Eighth Old Zhou clinging to a swaying tall tree, shouting at her with difficulty.","He Zhiran quickly reminded: \"Your tree is about to break, don't move.\"","From The Eighth Old Zhou's miserable state, it was evident that he had been targeted by this black bear for quite a while.","Moreover, He Zhiran was also very clear in her heart that an ordinary person would definitely not be a match for a black bear.","In order not to endanger The Eighth Old Zhou, He Zhiran quickly climbed up a tall tree, took out a repeating crossbow from her space, aimed at the black bear's eyes and shot an arrow.","This arrow hit right on target, landing squarely on the black bear's left eye.","He Zhiran's actions did not pause at all. She aimed at the black bear's right eye again and shot a second arrow.","The black bear wailed in pain, seemingly maddened, and managed to grab the big tree where The Eighth Old Zhou was hiding based on its sense of touch, shaking it violently.","Seeing that the tree trunk The Eighth Old Zhou was clinging to had already cracked a little, He Zhiran immediately leapt down from the tree. She took out a Swiss army knife and rushed to attack the black bear.","The black bear's attention was completely on The Eighth Old Zhou's side, which actually gave He Zhiran a lot of convenience.","It was just that He Zhiran's army knife hacked at the black bear's neck quickly, accurately and ruthlessly.","The black bear became even more frenzied. Relying on its senses, it attacked He Zhiran.","Seeing this, The Eighth Old Zhou was greatly shocked: \"Little...\"","Before the word \"heart\" could come out, his whole body fell from the tree.","Disregarding the pain on his body, The Eighth Old Zhou picked up the big knife at his waist and desperately hacked at the black bear.","Although He Zhiran was unable to make a move against the black bear for the time being, her dodging skills were still extremely agile.","However, The Eighth Old Zhou was not so lucky.","The black bear could not see with its eyes. It could only attack the person closest to it based on its senses.","Just when He Zhiran took a breath and was about to hack the black bear again, the black bear's huge claw had already slapped The Eighth Old Zhou on the shoulder.","Although The Eighth Old Zhou was in pain, he did not dodge.","He was very clear in his heart that only by keeping the black bear's attention on himself would He Zhiran have a chance to escape.","Just as the black bear continued to attack him, he shouted loudly: \"Miss He, run! The Mo family is still waiting for you to return.\"","By this time, how could He Zhiran possibly flee?","She was very clear in her heart that the current black bear was already at its limit. Even if she did not make a move, it would die from blood loss.","He Zhiran unhesitatingly raised her army knife and hacked at the black bear's original wound again without any hesitation.","Blood splattered everywhere, spraying her whole body and face.","The black bear's head drooped to one side in an instant, no longer having the ability to fight.","It just swayed a few times before crashing heavily to the ground with a thud.","Seeing the black bear fall down, The Eighth Old Zhou's legs turned soft and he plopped down on the ground, gasping for breath.","Even so, he still did not forget to ask about He Zhiran’s situation.","\"How are you, are you hurt anywhere?\"","He Zhiran casually waved her hand: \"I’m fine.\"","On the contrary, He Zhiran saw with her own eyes that The Eighth Old Zhou was slapped by the black bear’s big paw. She guessed that his injury would not be too minor.","\"Move your shoulder and let me see.\"","Doing as she said, The Eighth Old Zhou instantly grimaced in pain.","Only then did he realize that the slap from the black bear just now was very powerful.","He Zhiran guessed that The Eighth Old Zhou’s bone must have been injured.","She strode forward and touched the injured area through his clothes.","\"Your joint is a little dislocated, but it's okay, only in one place.\"","This was better than He Zhiran had imagined. She guessed that the injured black bear had affected its strength. Otherwise, with that slap, The Eighth Old Zhou would definitely have suffered a comminuted fracture.","Having such close contact with He Zhiran again, The Eighth Old Zhou's heart pounded nonstop.","In order to conceal his unease, he kept his head down the whole time.","He Zhiran was unaware of The Eighth Old Zhou's thoughts. Taking advantage of his absent-mindedness, she forcefully reset his bone back into its original position with one move.","Caught off guard by the sudden pain, The Eighth Old Zhou muffled a grunt.","At the same time, his facial expression also became grimacing, even looking somewhat ferocious, due to the unexpected pain.","Seeing The Eighth Old Zhou's expression, the image of Mo Jiuye seriously injured immediately appeared in He Zhiran's mind.","His abdomen was slashed open by such a large gash, yet he could still descend the cliff with her without changing his expression.","If it hadn't been for the two of them taking shelter inside the space in time, Mo Jiuye might have fought desperately to ensure her safe landing even at the cost of his life.","Furthermore, before he lost consciousness, he hadn't even frowned once.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran didn't know why, but she felt a burning sensation on her face.","Just when she was immersed in her own thoughts, The Eighth Old Zhou spoke.","\"Why didn't I see Mo Jiuye together with you?\"","He Zhiran quickly regained her composure.","\"He's injured and not very mobile. I plan to find the exit first before taking him out together.\"","Hearing this, The Eighth Old Zhou struggled to stand up with effort.","\"I know the exit. I'll help you take him out together.\"","With Mo Jiuye in the space, how could He Zhiran possibly let The Eighth Old Zhou follow her?","\"You're also injured. Let me fix your injury first. I can go get him myself.\"","After speaking, He Zhiran immediately turned around to find several evenly thick tree branches. She used smooth vines to tie and secure The Eighth Old Zhou's injured area.","Having done all this, in order not to give The Eighth Old Zhou a chance to follow her, He Zhiran turned her head and walked back towards the direction she came from."]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106: Let's split up when we leave the Valley.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran's steps were extremely fast. After making sure that the Eighth Old Zhou had not caught up, she dove into a nearby cave and flashed into the space.","Mo Jiuye saw her covered in blood and was so nervous that his heart almost jumped out.","\"Are you hurt? Let me see.\"","At the moment, he couldn't care less about embarrassment. He pulled He Zhiran towards the operating room, preparing to take off her clothes for an examination.","He Zhiran forcibly grabbed him.","\"I'm fine. This isn't my blood.\"","Before she could explain clearly, Mo Jiuye asked again: \"Did you encounter assassins again?\" It was evident how nervous he was about He Zhiran.","In order not to make Mo Jiuye worry, He Zhiran spoke extremely fast: \"No men in black. It was just a black bear.","Also, the Eighth Old Zhou came alone and found me. He was just injured by the black bear. I told him to wait not far away.\"","At first, when Mo Jiuye heard that He Zhiran had encountered a black bear, although he still had lingering fears, he knew He Zhiran's skills and was not too scared afterwards.","However, when he heard the name the Eighth Old Zhou, his heart involuntarily soured.","But Mo Jiuye knew clearly that this was not the time for him to feel sour.","\"Let's go out now to avoid arousing the Eighth Old Zhou's suspicions.\"","\"Your clothes are all torn. I’ll help you buy a similar set and we’ll go out after you’ve changed.\"","After speaking, He Zhiran opened Taobao on her phone and helped Mo Jiuye buy a short-sleeved black outfit.","The clothes were too new. To avoid the Eighth Old Zhou's suspicions, He Zhiran deliberately took out some dust from the space and wiped it on the clothes.","That way, no matter who it was, they wouldn't notice anything wrong.","Time was urgent. The two of them couldn’t bother with much. He Zhiran helped him change his clothes with her own hands before leaving the space together.","He Zhiran knew best about Mo Jiuye’s injuries. She knew he couldn’t walk too far at the moment. His speed was limited to inching along. Once there was a large movement, the wound would definitely split open.","Therefore, she had already made up her mind to take Mo Jiuye out for the sole purpose of letting the Eighth Old Zhou see him.","He Zhiran supported Mo Jiuye and walked step by step to the Eighth Old Zhou's position.","At this time, the Eighth Old Zhou had already stood up. Looking at the dead black bear, he was furious inside.","If it hadn't been for this damned thing showing up, he wouldn't have gotten hurt. And in the end it was the He clan who saved his life...","While he was lost in thought, He Zhiran had already supported Mo Jiuye to come close to him.","\"Master Zhou, my husband is seriously injured and cannot walk too far.\"","Only then did the Eighth Old Zhou look at Mo Jiuye. Although he looked quite spirited, his somewhat pale complexion had already explained everything.","Also, looking at Mo Jiuye, he seemed unable to stand upright. His injuries must be serious.","\"Alas! It's all because I was careless and got hit by the black bear. Otherwise I could have carried him to keep up the pace.\"","Facing this situation, the Eighth Old Zhou felt very helpless too.","How could the petite He Zhiran carry someone as tall and big as Mo Jiuye?","Moreover, Mo Jiuye had an abdominal injury. Even if someone could carry him away, they would still have to worry about touching the wound.","For a moment, the Eighth Old Zhou was at a loss.","Seeing this, He Zhiran brought up the plan she had thought of long ago.","\"Master Zhou, looking at my husband’s current condition, even if we walk out of this valley I’m afraid he still won’t be able to keep up with the troops. \"","The Eighth Old Zhou did not deny this: \"That's true. Our itinerary has been delayed for many days. I suppose we’ll have to speed up for the rest of the trip.\"","He Zhiran deliberately put on a look of deep thought.","After a long time, she said, \"Master Zhou, I thought of a way. See if it works?\"","The Eighth Old Zhou raised his eyebrows: \"What good idea do you have? Just say it.\"","\"My husband obviously cannot walk in the mountains. If you and Brother Peng can trust us, I plan to take my husband around the mountain.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou frowned when he heard this.","In principle, apart from doing this there was no other way. But he didn't think this method was feasible.","\"Do you know? Going around the mountain will delay seven or eight days. Moreover, the main force will not be able to stop and wait. How will you catch up with everyone's itinerary like this?\"","This seemed almost impossible to the Eighth Old Zhou, yet he couldn’t think of a better way.","He Zhiran smiled and said, \"Rest assured Master Zhou. After leaving the valley, I plan to rent a car in the city. That way, not only can my husband continue to recuperate, but we can also speed up a lot.\"","When the Eighth Old Zhou heard this, he fell into thought.","In all his years working as an escort officer, this was the first time he had encountered such a situation.","In the past, not to mention letting prisoners travel alone, even if they were seriously injured, there would be no special treatment. Injured people would have to keep up at whatever pace the rest took.","Unless they didn’t want to live anymore, no one would dare ask for such a request.","But the person making this request now was not someone else, but the woman who made his heart race whenever he saw her.","At this moment, the Eighth Old Zhou was extremely envious of Mo Jiuye for getting so much care and concern from He Zhiran.","Although he knew clearly that Brother Peng was quite nice to He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye, letting them travel separately was such a big deal that he didn’t know how to respond at the moment.","If anything went wrong, not only would the Eighth Old Zhou get in trouble, but everyone in their whole escort team would face severe punishment, even losing their jobs.","If he didn’t consider the others, the Eighth Old Zhou would have agreed without hesitation.","Not for anything else. He just didn’t want to see He Zhiran in a difficult position.","He Zhiran saw that the Eighth Old Zhou was struggling over this. After reassuring him, her eyes fell on the black bear.","The entire black bear was a treasure trove. Its bones, meat, paws, fat, blood and brain marrow could all be used in medicine.","In her previous life, hunting wildlife had already been strictly prohibited. These were all precious things that humans did not even dare wish for.","Now this treasure was right in front of her eyes. He Zhiran did not want to miss out.","Although she couldn’t take away the entire bear under the Eighth Old Zhou’s watch, she could at least keep some valuable parts.","So she borrowed the Eighth Old Zhou’s big knife and took the bear’s paws and gallbladder.","He Zhiran found some vines to tie these things up with.","\"Master Zhou, the rest is basically meat. Take what you can manage.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou did not stand on ceremony either. Although he had never eaten bear meat before, he had heard that it tasted quite good."]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107: Enter Pingyang County","paragraphs":["So, the Eighth Old Zhou took back the big knife from He Zhiran and cut several pieces of fresh bear meat, then learned from her and tied them up with vine sticks, preparing to take them up the mountain together.","Seeing that there was still so much meat left, the Eighth Old Zhou was really reluctant. He made a slightly embarrassed suggestion:","\"I went down the mountain before dawn to look for you all, and I haven't eaten anything until now. Why don't we roast some of the bear meat here and eat our fill before leaving the valley?\"","His words were not at all false. After reaching an agreement with Peng Wang in the middle of the night to look for Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, the Eighth Old Zhou did not wait a moment. Holding a torch, he went alone, first following the direction they had disappeared in to look for them.","Soon afterwards, he discovered countless corpses of people dressed in black. By the time he searched to the cliff, he carefully noticed that there were many footprints of people who had walked there.","The cliff was almost the end of this mountain. He guessed that it was possible the two had fallen down from here.","Therefore, he had rushed down the mountain overnight and entered this valley.","Without the Eighth Old Zhou having to say much, He Zhiran also knew that being able to find this valley must have taken quite some time. Having walked for so long, it would be strange if he wasn't hungry.","\"Okay, let's roast the bear meat here and eat our fill before heading out together.\"","In order to take care of the two injured grown men, He Zhiran took the initiative to set up a rack.","As always, she skewered the bear meat on branches and grilled it over the fire.","Mo Jiuye now fully understood He Zhiran's space. He knew that when she was roasting meat, she might take out some seasonings from her space.","In order not to let the Eighth Old Zhou notice anything amiss, he deliberately pulled him aside to ask about his family's situation.","He Zhiran seized this opportunity to take out a few seasonings that weren't too strong in flavor from her space and sprinkle them on the bear meat.","Soon, the grilled bear meat was ready. The three of them sat around the campfire and ate their fill before setting off together.","The Eighth Old Zhou led the way in front, while He Zhiran supported Mo Jiuye behind.","Due to their slow pace of walking, it took until the afternoon for the three to make it out of the valley.","The scene before them was not unfamiliar at all - it was precisely where they had climbed Mount Oxtail.","The Eighth Old Zhou looked at the skies and pointed in one direction, saying: \"If you keep going this way, you should reach Pingyang County after about two hours.\"","He Zhiran knew that this was where they would part ways. In order to put the Eighth Old Zhou's mind at ease, she promised again:","\"Old Zhou, rest assured. I guarantee we won't fall too far behind. I'll have to trouble you to help explain things to Elder Brother Peng, as well as our families - please let them know that my husband and I are perfectly safe and will see them in a few days.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou nodded. \"Don't worry, I will definitely pass on your message. Take care on the road.\"","And so the three parted ways. They walked until the Eighth Old Zhou's figure disappeared from sight before He Zhiran brought Mo Jiuye to a secluded place to flash into her space.","If the Eighth Old Zhou had not been present just now, there was no way He Zhiran would have allowed Mo Jiuye to walk such a long distance.","She estimated that by now, it was likely his wounds had reopened.","The first thing she had to do was help Mo Jiuye examine his injuries again.","He Zhiran placed the few large bear paws and single bear gallbladder she was carrying somewhere random - anyway, there was preservation functionality within the space, so she wasn't worried the bear meat would go bad.","By now, Mo Jiuye could indeed feel some discomfort from his wounds, and obediently allowed He Zhiran to examine him.","After the examination, He Zhiran heaved a deep sigh.","Mo Jiuye's condition was better than she had imagined. Other than the most serious wound on his lower abdomen, there were basically no issues with the stab wounds on the rest of his body.","Fortunately, the stitches had no signs of tearing open. It was likely due to him moving around too much, which caused friction on the wound.","He Zhiran helped Mo Jiuye redress and bandage the wound properly, and earnestly said:","\"You stay in the space for now. I can travel faster by myself, so I'll do my best to enter Pingyang County before night falls.\"","Mo Jiuye understood clearly that in his current state, wanting to accompany her would only slow her down, so he did not refuse.","\"Alright, take care on the road.\"","\"Mm.\" He Zhiran acknowledged before flashing out of the space.","The journey went smoothly. She managed to reach Pingyang County before sunset.","Unlike entering those other county towns previously, there was a fee just to enter the city here...","By the city gates stood a small square table, on top of which sat a very conspicuous wooden chest.","All the commoners entering the city would throw some copper coins into that chest.","In He Zhiran's understanding, such occurrences were mostly due to greedy officials finding baseless excuses to exploit the common people.","In order to avoid attracting unnecessary trouble, He Zhiran also learned from those commoners by throwing five copper coins into the chest.","She then observed that the commoners who had paid to enter the city all wore expressions as though they had grievances to air but could not speak of them.","Evidently, they were dissatisfied at having to pay just to enter the city.","Just as she was thinking of finding someone to inquire in detail about what was happening, suddenly a loud commotion rang out.","\"Make way, make way! My horse got spooked. Anyone who doesn't want to die, get out of the way!\"","He Zhiran moved to stand by the roadside. Squinting towards the source of the voice, she saw a foppishly-dressed young master recklessly charging down the streets on a tall horse.","After crashing into several roadside stalls and finally calming down, the horse came to a stop right next to He Zhiran.","The young master dismounted with a stream of curses, landing right beside He Zhiran.","\"Scram! Do you want to die, daring to block this young master's path?\"","As he spoke, the young master lifted his leg, preparing to kick He Zhiran away.","But the moment he raised his leg, his eyes landed on He Zhiran's appearance.","Even concealed under the tattered coarse linen clothes, her beauty still could not be obscured.","The young master was instantly stunned. His raised leg lowered back down unknowingly.","\"Which family's young miss are you? Why not come with this young master to have some fun?\"","Seeing this kind of person made He Zhiran feel a wave of disgust.","\"Get lost. Take a good look at your own lacking virtues.\"","Having said thus, He Zhiran turned to leave.","If it wasn't to avoid trouble, when facing such a person, she would surely have beaten him up.","That foppish young master was a rogue through-and-through. How could he allow her to just leave like this?","He Zhiran had just taken a step away when the young master blocked her path.","\"Oh? This young miss has quite the fiery temper; I like it!\"","As he spoke, the young master reached out to put his arm around her shoulder.","He Zhiran was incensed by this shameless person. She grabbed his arm in a flash and executed a perfect over-the-shoulder throw.","\"Ahhhhh!\"","Accompanied by the young master's miserable shriek, his entire body slammed heavily onto the hard ground. The pain caused his face to contort extremely.","Gritting his teeth to endure the pain, he pointed at He Zhiran and cursed loudly, \"You cheap whore! Do you know who this young master is? If I say the word, I can make you disappear from this world! And your whole family too - not a single one will remain!\""]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108: If You like it, I'll do it.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran's anger also rose, simply going all out.","She went forward and grabbed Young Master's collar, constantly slapping him.","\"This is the consequence of a loose tongue. Remember this from now on. When you see Madam, walk around, otherwise I will beat you every time I see you.\"","At this time, many onlookers had already gathered around.","They felt relieved at the same time and worried for this reckless woman.","It was known that this young master usually acted arrogantly in Pingyang County and bullied men and women everywhere without saying that he also had a county mayor father to cover for him. Wherever the common people met him, they were extremely miserable.","Today, seeing him being humiliated, how could the commoners not be happy in their hearts?","Seeing that He Zhiran showed no sign of stopping beating, a kind aunt came forward to dissuade her.","\"Girl, vent your anger then run away quickly. When his people come, I'm afraid you won't be able to escape even if you want to.\"","He Zhiran was also tired from beating, so she naturally stood up.","\"Auntie, what is this person's identity that he is so rampant in broad daylight?\"","The aunt looked around cautiously before whispering:","\"Girl must be from out of town? This is the only son of our Pingyang County's county mayor, named Sun Jiabao. Offending him is the same as offending the county mayor. Listen to my advice and leave quickly while the yamen people have not yet come!\"","He Zhiran nodded: \"Thank you auntie for the reminder.\"","Although causing trouble after entering the city was not her original intention, things had already happened. She still had things to do that were not yet done, so how could she just leave like this?","After she finished speaking, He Zhiran squeezed out of the crowd and continued walking towards the city.","In less than a hundred meters away, she saw a team of catchers with big knives rushing towards Sun Jiabao's direction.","He Zhiran was really lucky that she walked fast. If she was blocked by these catchers, it would definitely cause a lot of trouble.","Although she was not worried about being arrested, she disliked trouble.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran walked a few more steps quickly, turned into an alley, and then flashed into the space.","After dealing with Sun Jiabao just now, although it was a one-sided crush, He Zhiran’s hair and clothes were a bit messy.","Seeing her appearance, Mo Jiuye suddenly became nervous.","\"What happened?\"","He Zhiran shrugged indifferently: \"I met a rogue and taught him a lesson, that’s all.\"","She said it lightly, but Mo Jiuye was not at ease and continued to ask for details.","He Zhiran had no choice but to tell Mo Jiuye about beating up Sun Jiabao.","Mo Jiuye was so angry that his face was livid. He wished he could go out now and smash Sun Jiabao into ten thousand pieces.","He actually dared to molest his woman. He really did not want to live anymore!","However, he also knew his current situation clearly, and could only try his best to suppress his anger.","Seeing Mo Jiuye angry, He Zhiran comforted him: \"Don't be angry. After all, I didn't suffer any loss.\"","Mo Jiuye no longer made a sound. After all, he could do nothing now, and it was useless to say more.","One of He Zhiran’s purposes for entering the space was to avoid those catchers, and the other was to give Mo Jiuye an update and change her outfit at the same time.","In front of Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran bought a set of men’s clothing on Taobao Treasures.","After simply washing up in the bathroom and putting on the men’s clothing, in order to make herself look more like a man, she also simply applied some make up.","She thickened her eyebrows, enlarged her mouth, made her face darker, and stuck on a small mustache.","After getting dressed up, He Zhiran walked out of the room.","Mo Jiuye was also taken aback when he saw her appearance.","He was still worried before that even if He Zhiran wore men's clothing, she would not look like a man given her appearance. Unexpectedly, when she came out this time, he did not even recognize her!","If he did not know there were only the two of them in the space, Mo Jiuye would definitely ask.","Seeing Mo Jiuye's expression, He Zhiran knew her outfit was very successful.","She turned around proudly in front of Mo Jiuye, then sat in a chair and crossed her legs arrogantly, suddenly becoming playful.","\"Master is tired. Massage me.\"","Seeing her ridiculous appearance, Mo Jiuye almost laughed out loud.","Still, he very cooperatively came to stand behind her.","\"Yes Sir, I’ll massage you right away.\"","It was the first time He Zhiran had seen Mo Jiuye so relaxed. She couldn’t help laughing loudly.","\"Hahaha... Mo Jiuye, who asked you to cooperate with me so much? Are you looking to laugh yourself to death?\"","Mo Jiuye couldn't help smiling at the corners of his lips. What he said made He Zhiran very happy.","\"As long as you like it, I will oblige.\"","Neither of them knew this was the first time they had been so comfortable with each other since they got married.","After laughing for a while, He Zhiran felt it was about time and left the space again.","Coming out of the alley, she heard people talking on the street.","\"I heard that the county mayor sent all the catchers to search around the city to catch the woman who beat young master Bao.\"","\"That woman is quite powerful. The catchers have been searching for so long and still haven't found anyone.\"","\"Maybe she already left the city. How can they find her by searching in the city?\"","\"Ah... I hope that woman has already left the city. If she really falls into the hands of the county mayor, she will undoubtedly die.\"","\"...\"","He Zhiran walked along the road. All she heard along the way was about her beating Sun Jiabao.","Not only that, those catchers with knives could be seen everywhere.","He Zhiran was confident that no one would recognize her, so she walked calmly on the street.","It was already dark now. Hiring a carriage would have to wait until tomorrow morning.","What she needed to do now was to find out about the county mayor.","In ancient times, the best places to gather information were tea houses or restaurants.","So He Zhiran found a tea house with many customers, chose a window seat, asked the waiter for a pot of tea, and sat there slowly drinking it.","The topic in the teahouse today was no different from outside, almost all about Sun Jiabao being beaten.","Judging from the tone of those people, there was a hint of relief in it.","Perhaps because they were in awe of the county mayor’s authority, they did not dare express it directly.","This information did not satisfy He Zhiran’s needs. She mainly wanted to understand the situation of this county mayor.","Just as she was about to get up and leave to listen elsewhere, an old man and a child walked in at the door.","The old man scanned the room and saw that all the seats were taken. He came to He Zhiran and said, \"Young brother, may we share a table?”","Seeing this, He Zhiran sat back down and gestured for them to sit.","\"Please have a seat, elders.\"","The old man saw that she was polite. After thanking her, he pulled the child to sit across from her.","He called the waiter and ordered a pot of tea.","Just as He Zhiran was thinking about how to draw some words from the old man, he actually took the initiative to speak first.","\"Judging from young brother's accent, you are not from our Pingyang County, right?\""]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109: Night Watch the County Magistrate","paragraphs":["He Zhiran smiled and said, \"To be honest, I'm just passing through this place to visit relatives, and I'll be leaving tomorrow.\"","With a mysterious look, she glanced around and whispered, \"Old man, I've been hearing everyone talk about the son of the county magistrate being beaten. Is it true?\"","The old man was cautious. After hearing He Zhiran's words, he looked around and leaned closer, saying mysteriously, \"Since young sir is from out of town, this old man might as well tell you about the situation in Pingyang County.\"","He Zhiran pretended to be very interested and listened attentively.","The old man whispered, \"Sun Jiabao is the only son of the county magistrate's family. He has been spoiled since childhood and relies on his father's position to bully and oppress the people in Pingyang County. The common folks dare not speak up in anger...\"","\"If I may say so, I truly admire the young woman who stood up for justice and fought him today. She spoke up for the people of Pingyang.\"","Seeing that He Zhiran was interested, the old man paused and continued speaking.","\"You must have noticed when you entered the county that there is a fee of 5 wen per person. It may not be much for the wealthy, but for ordinary people, it's difficult to afford even a single entry or exit. They work for a day and can only earn up to 15 wen, which is barely enough to support their families. Taking out another 5 wen as an entry fee is like taking their lives away.\"","\"Especially for those from the surrounding rural areas who come to the city for work, they can't afford to go back home at night just to save the 5 wen fee. Instead, they find a corner to spend the night.\"","The old man shook his head helplessly and said, \"This world truly doesn't allow the common people to live well...\"","After the old man took a few sips of tea, He Zhiran asked the most crucial question.","\"Old man, is it the county magistrate's decision to charge 5 wen per person to enter the city?\"","The old man sighed helplessly, looked around again, and whispered, \"Who else would dare to make such a decision besides the county magistrate?\"","\"And where does the money collected go?\" He Zhiran continued asking.","The old man smiled bitterly, \"Where do you think? It all goes into their private coffers.\"","Although He Zhiran had already guessed this outcome, hearing it firsthand made her even more infuriated.","She clenched her fist under the table, hating the various injustices of this era even more.","Having learned everything she wanted to know, He Zhiran had no intention of staying any longer. She bid farewell to the old man, stood up, and left the teahouse at a leisurely pace.","With her spatial ability, she didn't need to worry about finding an inn. At the moment, what He Zhiran wanted to do most was to punish the corrupt county magistrate and his son, who were full of wickedness.","After all, the night was long, and she had nothing better to do.","He Zhiran strolled around for a while and found the residence of the county magistrate.","Seeing that it was still early, she entered her space.","Finally seeing He Zhiran return, Mo Jiuye breathed a sigh of relief.","Although he had witnessed He Zhiran's abilities, he still worried that she might encounter danger on her own outside.","\"What did you find out?\" Mo Jiuye asked with concern.","He Zhiran told Mo Jiuye everything the old man had said, along with her own plans.","\"After midnight, I plan to visit the county magistrate's residence.\"","Mo Jiuye could anticipate what He Zhiran was up to even if he were to count his toes.","He deliberately straightened his body, showing that he was in a state of no hindrance.","\"I'll accompany you,\" he said.","\"No, you have injuries on your body. I can handle it alone,\" He Zhiran refused decisively, leaving no room for Mo Jiuye to argue.","If she couldn't handle the residence of a mere county magistrate, she wouldn't need to mix in the future.","Taking advantage of this free time, He Zhiran personally went to the kitchen and prepared a delicious meal for the two of them.","Among them was a dish she had been longing for, Braised Bear's Paw.","The pressure cooker softened and seasoned the bear's paw until it was tender and flavorful. As soon as it came out of the pot, the fragrance filled the air.","In addition, she cooked a few other side dishes.","Mo Jiuye couldn't stop praising He Zhiran's cooking skills. Unlike before, he no longer expressed his enjoyment of the food.","\"If you open a restaurant with your culinary skills, it will definitely be a hit.\"","He Zhiran wasn't very confident in her cooking skills, but she had full confidence in the spices in the space.","Even if she was a novice in cooking, with so many spices, she could still make delicious dishes.","Especially in this ancient era of scarce resources, the food people usually ate was very plain. As long as the dishes had some new variations and improved flavors, they would naturally become exquisite delicacies.","However, with He Zhiran's temperament, she had no interest in opening a restaurant. Even if she did, she only wanted to be a silent backer.","After eating and drinking their fill, the couple chatted for a while. He Zhiran used Mo Jiuye's need to recuperate as an excuse to ask him to rest in the bedroom first.","She quickly changed into a set of night clothes and swiftly left the space.","The place she appeared happened to be the side gate of the county magistrate's residence. He Zhiran had already observed it in advance and found that there were not many people moving around there, making it relatively safe to enter and exit.","After careful observation and seeing no danger around, He Zhiran took out a miniature drone from the space, and at the same time, she held a small monitor in her hand.","She pressed the switch on the remote control, and the drone slowly ascended into the air.","He Zhiran used the remote control to manipulate the drone while observing the layout inside the county magistrate's residence with the small monitor.","After getting a general idea, she took a quick run-up and flipped over the courtyard wall.","It seemed that all the personnel had been dispatched to search for the person who harmed Sun Jiabao. There were only two guards in the county magistrate's residence today.","Those two guards didn't seem to be industrious people either. At the moment, they were hiding in a corner, dozing off.","According to the information observed by the drone, He Zhiran first arrived at a larger courtyard.","Even though it was late at night, the place was still brightly lit.","He Zhiran agilely climbed over the wall and then jumped onto the roof of the main house. She gently lifted a roof tile and looked inside the house.","Only an old man in his fifties, with a fat head and big ears, was pacing back and forth with his hands behind his back.","Inside the room, a chubby woman of the same age as her was standing by the bed, wiping away tears.","The person lying on the bed was undoubtedly Sun Jiabao.","Sun Jiabao's face was wrapped up like a dumpling, and he was rolling back and forth on the bed.","\"Dad, I don't care. You must capture that woman for me. I want to make her suffer.\"","The woman patted Sun Jiabao's body and said with pity, \"My son, rest assured, your dad has already sent all the officials to search and will not let the person who harmed you escape.\"","Sun Lin also stopped in his tracks and said ominously, \"Anyone who dares to harm my son in Pingyang County will suffer a fate worse than death.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, two women dressed as old maids entered, each holding a soup bowl.","The woman personally took the soup bowl and coaxed Sun Jiabao to take the medicine.","He Zhiran, feeling bored at this point, took out a homemade incense from his space, lit it, and stuffed it into the gap in the roof.","Before long, everyone in the room, including the two old maids, fell into a deep sleep."]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110: Never thought I'd see you here again.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran nimbly leapt down from the roof and directly entered the room.","As the magistrate of the county, Sun Lin exploited the common people and allowed his son to wreak havoc in the countryside. Such a despicable person was unfit to be an official.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran took out a dagger from her interspatial ring and directly cut off Sun Lin's tongue and hands.","She wanted to see how a disabled and mute person could still be an official.","As for Sun Jiabao, who bullied men and overpowered women, and did all kinds of evil, she would make him an idiot for the rest of his life.","He Zhiran took out her self-made poison \"Loss of Spirit\" from her interspatial ring again.","By adding one more ingredient to Loss of Spirit, Sun Jiabao would become an idiot for the rest of his life.","Sun Jiabao was currently unconscious. He Zhiran directly injected the temporarily prepared medicine into his body using a syringe.","After settling everything, He Zhiran unknowingly left this place and went to the location she had observed that was likely the storehouse.","She was lucky. The observed location turned out to be the storehouse of the county magistrate's residence.","There were two guards in front of the storehouse door. He Zhiran carefully circled behind them and nimbly hit the back of their necks.","Seeing that the two guards had fainted dead away, He Zhiran quickly entered the storehouse.","It had to be said, the family fortune of a corrupt official was abundant.","The not very large storehouse was filled with gold, silver, pearls and jewels, silks and satins, calligraphy and paintings, and some jade articles.","Many large items she had taken from the national treasury were already hanging in her online store. This freed up a lot of space in her interspatial ring.","He Zhiran eyed everything. With a wave of her hand, she took away all the items that could completely fit in her interspatial ring.","Mo Jiuye couldn’t sleep at all in the interspatial ring. After He Zhiran left, he came out of the bedroom.","Just as he was somewhat worried about He Zhiran, a pile of things suddenly appeared in front of him, almost hitting him...","Without thinking, seeing so many valuables, Mo Jiuye knew clearly that He Zhiran had succeeded. He only hoped that she would not be too greedy and would pay more attention to her own safety and come back sooner.","After finishing what needed to be done, He Zhiran did not plan to stay any longer.","She left the county magistrate's residence, ran to a secluded place, and flashed into the interspatial ring.","Seeing her return safe and sound, Mo Jiuye finally felt relieved.","Having just punished the corrupt magistrate and his son, He Zhiran felt a little excited at the moment.","\"That dog of a magistrate was quite rich. With just a small effort from me, I got such gains.\"","When those valuables were moved into the interspatial ring, Mo Jiuye had already checked them.","There were at least 150,000 taels of silver bills and silver alone.","What's more, there were also several large boxes of copper coins. Needless to say, these copper coins were all the entrance fees collected from the commoners at the city gate.","For a small county magistrate to have such wealth, it was imaginable how much hard-earned money he had exploited from the common people...","Mo Jiuye stared at the valuables in front of him: \"What do you plan to do with these?\"","He Zhiran glanced around. The space she had finally cleared out was filled up again, and even more so.","\"I plan to sell all these bulky items in the trading system, and as for the silver, I hope I can find a way to return it to the commoners of Pingyang County.\"","Mo Jiuye also agreed with this.","He pondered for a moment and said,","\"It's a good idea to want to return the silver to the commoners, but our time simply does not allow us to do these things.\"","He Zhiran was also at a loss. She certainly could not deliver the silver to every household. Not to mention the risk of being easily discovered, it was indeed impossible to accomplish within the time constraints, just as Mo Jiuye had said.","\"Let's put this plan on hold for now. When I go out to hire a carriage tomorrow, I’ll ask around again to see if there is a good way to do it.\"","He Zhiran had travelled all day and dealt with the dog magistrate at night. At this moment, she was indeed a little tired.","After chatting with Mo Jiuye for a few sentences, the two went back to the bedroom to rest.","Early next morning, He Zhiran went out again in men’s clothing.","The place she appeared was only one street away from the county magistrate's residence.","He Zhiran walked slowly towards the main street. Her foremost goal was to hire a carriage.","The street was especially bustling today. The commoners had already learned about what happened to the county magistrate's family. Knowing that a disabled mute would no longer be able to be an official in the future, they dared to speak more openly.","Most of their discussion topics were about the county magistrate’s storehouse being emptied and the county magistrate changed into a mute unable to speak and his son who bullied men and overpowered women becoming an idiot.","This matter was extremely gratifying for the commoners.","There were even some daring people who planned to go to the county magistrate's residence in groups to watch the fun.","Those commoners who had been oppressed by the county magistrate and his son, cried and cursed the wrongdoings they had suffered through tears and mucus.","He Zhiran only casually observed these scenes as she passed by.","After finding out the location of the carriage shop, she quickened her pace.","Unexpectedly, as soon as she turned into another street, He Zhiran spotted a familiar person with her discerning eyes.","This familiar person was Fei Nanyu.","Fei Nanyu was walking hurriedly with another person who looked like his attendant. They seemed to have some urgent matters to deal with.","Seeing Fei Nanyu, He Zhiran immediately thought of something.","She waved at Fei Nanyu.","Fei Nanyu only glanced casually at her before turning his head to continue on his way.","Seeing that she was ignored, He Zhiran subconsciously lowered her head to glance at the men's clothing she was wearing, before suddenly realizing why.","Not to mention Fei Nanyu, whom she had only met twice, even Mo Jiuye, whom she was with all day, had almost failed to recognize her.","He Zhiran walked briskly for a few steps towards Fei Nanyu.","\"Master Fei.\"","Fei Nanyu stopped in his tracks and looked at the speaker, somewhat uncertain.","\"Are you calling me?\"","If she was not worried that her appearance would be recognized by the government officials on this public street, He Zhiran would have definitely torn off her fake beard and wiped her face clean to reveal her true face. But this was not an option here.","Therefore, He Zhiran could only reveal her identity verbally, \"Master Fei, I am He Zhiran, Mo Jiuye’s wife.\"","Fei Nanyu was taken aback for a moment before carefully examining her facial features.","Looking closely, she did resemble Mo Jiuye’s wife, and her voice could not be faked.","After gazing at her for a moment and confirming that the person in front of him was indeed He Zhiran, Fei Nanyu's expression instantly became more relaxed.","His attitude was still very modest. \"Madam Mo, I didn't expect us to meet again here.”","He Zhiran looked around and pointed to her outfit, “Master Fei, I’m currently dressed as a man.”","Fei Nanyu suddenly understood and said with a smile, \"Master He.\"","He Zhiran nodded to indicate that she accepted this form of address. She then asked,","\"What brings Master Fei to Pingyang County?\"","Fei Nanyu felt that there was no need to conceal the purpose of this trip, so he spoke directly, \"I won’t hide it from Master He. I arrived in the capital city following Prince Qi, but Prince Qi received an imperial decree to go to Dongfeng County for disaster relief as soon as he arrived. We set off for Dongfeng County overnight and only found out when we arrived that in addition to the flooding, there was also a plague outbreak.","The magistrate of Dongfeng County obtained a questionable cure that was said to be able to treat and control the plague. However, there was a lack of one medicinal ingredient. Prince Qi then tasked me to travel along the road west towards the surrounding county cities, to see if I could buy that medicinal ingredient.”"]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111: Do you have a purpose in doing this","paragraphs":["The prescription to treat the plague was provided by He Zhiran, and no one was clearer about the types of medicinal materials than her.","\"I wonder what kind of medicinal materials Mr. Fei is looking for?\"","\"Now I'm only lacking the medicinal material called huanglian, I've been to two county towns but haven't found any.\"","Originally I was going to use Prince Qi's waist card to ask the magistrate here for help, but I just heard that the magistrate's home was robbed by thieves last night, so I'm thinking of going to the next county town to take a look.\"","In He Zhiran's perception, huanglian was not a rare medicinal material at all.","She just didn't know why it couldn't be bought around here.","She rolled her eyes and came up with an idea.","He Zhiran wasn't sure if the attendant by Fei Nanyu's side could be trusted, so she made a gesture at him: \"Mr. Fei, may I have a word?\"","Fei Nanyu naturally knew her intention.","\"No problem, he can be trusted.\"","Since Fei Nanyu had said so, He Zhiran no longer needed to be evasive.","\"Mr. Fei, I know why there is a shortage of huanglian around here.\"","Fei Nanyu raised his brows: \"Why?\"","He Zhiran had a mysterious look.","\"I won't hide it from Mr. Fei. The common folk on the streets say that I was the one who severely injured the magistrate's son. I wanted to give them a lesson.\"","\"Who would have thought, when I was eavesdropping on their conversation on the roof, I accidentally got a piece of information.\"","Fei Nanyu asked impatiently: \"What information?\"","He Zhiran then switched to fabrication mode.","\"The magistrate said that the small warehouse in the eastern suburb had already been filled with piles of huanglian. In the past few days, the silver and money collected at the city gate could not even be stored.\"","\"In order to verify the authenticity, I went to the place the magistrate mentioned that night. There really was a small warehouse there. After checking it, there was not only a large amount of huanglian inside, but also several boxes of silver and copper coins.\"","When Fei Nanyu heard that there was so much huanglian, his eyes lit up instantly.","He didn't have time to think about why the magistrate would hoard so much huanglian. He urged: \"Please lead the way, Madam Mo. If those huanglians can be brought to Dongfeng County, the people of Dongfeng County will be saved.\"","All of this was fabricated by He Zhiran, so how could she possibly take Fei Nanyu to some magistrate's warehouse right away?","\"Mr. Fei, my husband is seriously injured and waiting for me to buy medicine to take back. What do you think, shall we set a time and I'll take you there later?\"","Hearing that Mo Jiuye was seriously injured, Fei Nanyu suddenly remembered why they were in Pingyang County.","Moreover, he was a tactful person who knew it was improper to ask outright, so he cupped his fist towards He Zhiran.","\"Master Mo's injury is more urgent. See you tonight at the east gate.\"","\"Alright, I'll be there on time.\" After He Zhiran finished speaking, she turned around and left.","To save some time, she went to the carriage shop first.","She had thought it would be simple to hire a carriage, but she found that not only were there carts for rent at the carriage shop, but also draft animals for sale to pull the carts.","The Da Shun Dynasty had strict control over horses. Apart from some specially licensed official families, if other people wanted to own a carriage, they had to go to the government to apply for a permit first.","Not only that, the prices of horses were also very expensive. The horses in the carriage shop couldn't even sell one per month. Over time, the boss was no longer willing to run the horse business, so they only sold oxen, donkeys and mules.","He Zhiran pondered for a while. Hiring a carriage was not as convenient for her and Mo Jiuye to travel alone as walking.","After all, she had secrets, and their identities were also special.","With this in mind, He Zhiran decided to buy a mule, and then asked the boss to help harness it to a cart. This way, she could drive the mule cart herself to catch up with the main unit.","If Peng Wang allowed it, they could also have a means of transportation on the road ahead.","On the contrary, after catching up with the main force, she could sell the mule cart.","He Zhiran was always decisive in doing things. Once she had an idea, she would take action immediately.","She selected a mule that looked quite strong, and also bought a canopy cart.","Altogether it cost ten taels of silver.","The boss helped harness the cart, and He Zhiran drove the mule cart east.","Fortunately, in her previous life, she had followed the army to the countryside to help farm work, and had learned driving skills from the villagers.","Although her mule cart driving skills were a little rusty at first, after a brief period of fumbling, He Zhiran gradually became skilled at it.","Because of what happened to the magistrate, the checks on the commoners entering and leaving the city gate today were extremely strict.","He Zhiran's makeup helped her pass, although she had to wait in line for a while, she still left the city smoothly.","She drove straight to the eastern suburbs. If she remembered correctly, she saw an abandoned yard there when she passed by. He Zhiran decided to go there and take a look.","Soon, relying on her memory, she drove the mule cart to the yard.","The yard was not big, and the houses looked quite tidy. Perhaps because no one had lived there for a long time, the yard was already overgrown with weeds.","He Zhiran parked the mule cart and walked straight in.","After opening the door of the front house and taking a look around, He Zhiran couldn't help but marvel at her good fortune.","The room inside was empty, perfect for the warehouse she had spoken of.","She glanced at the space's big clock, there was still some time before the appointment with Fei Nanyu. He Zhiran instantly flashed into the space.","Mo Jiuye was trying to prepare lunch in the kitchen. Seeing He Zhiran return, he put down the spatula in his hand and walked over.","\"What's the situation outside?\"","He Zhiran briefly recounted what the common folk were talking about in Pingyang County, and told him that she had met Fei Nanyu and why Fei Nanyu had appeared in Pingyang County.","\"I found an abandoned yard in the eastern suburb. I'm thinking of buying some huanglian and putting it in there, and handing over the silver and copper coins from the magistrate's house to him as well.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't understand why He Zhiran wanted to do this.","\"Do you have any purpose for doing this?\"","He Zhiran slowly explained her thoughts to him.","\"I told Fei Nanyu that these huanglians were privately hoarded by the dog magistrate. Think about it, with Fei Nanyu's astuteness, he will definitely ponder the purpose of hoarding so much huanglian.","Right now, Nan Qi has been sent by the Emperor to provide disaster relief in Dongfeng County. Once he makes achievements there, he will definitely gain the Emperor's favor.","Judging from the current situation at court, Nan Heng must be the one who least wants Nan Qi's disaster relief to succeed. He will definitely secretly create obstacles to hinder Nan Qi's actions.","If Fei Nanyu goes back and tells Nan Qi about the magistrate hoarding large amounts of huanglian, the first thing Nan Qi will think is that the magistrate was working for Nan Heng, with the purpose of preventing his disaster relief efforts.","Furthermore, Nan Qi might even suspect that the plague in Dongfeng County was man-made, and Nan Heng would undoubtedly be the prime suspect.\""]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112: I thank you for those people in Dongfeng County.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran's eyes grew brighter and brighter as she listened. She had already guessed Mo Jiuye's purpose in her heart.","Therefore, she took over the conversation and continued:","\"This way, Nan Qi will harbor more hatred towards Nan Heng. With Nan Qi's intolerable temperament, when he returns to the capital, he will definitely think of ways to make trouble for Nan Heng.","Nan Heng will be too busy defending himself to temporarily ignore the assassination against me for the time being.\"","He Zhiran nodded with a smile.","\"That's only part of the reason.\"","Mo Jiuye raised an eyebrow: \"Could it be that you have other purposes?\"","He Zhiran was full of confidence.","\"I also want to take this opportunity to help Fei Nanyu and ask him to spread the word about your break up with Nan Qi after he returns to the capital. This way, Nan Heng will completely abandon the assassination against you.","Also, didn't we plan to distribute the silver coins from the dog magistrate among the common people last night? I plan to ask Fei Nanyu for help with this as well. With his capabilities, he will surely be able to accomplish it.\"","After hearing her words, Mo Jiuye admired this woman's wisdom even more.","There was an involuntary tone of indulgence in his words. \"You really are exceptional to have thought of so many things with that little head of yours.\"","Flattered by the praise, He Zhiran nearly jumped for joy.","\"It's called killing two birds with one stone. Not only did I find a reliable person to return the dog magistrate's money to the commoners, but I've also relieved Nan Heng's wariness against you.\"","Seeing her grinning, Mo Jiuye couldn't help reaching out to pat her head.","\"Alright, you've been out for so long and must be tired too. Rest for a while and we'll have lunch.\"","He Zhiran felt very pampered by Mo Jiuye's doting care.","She obediently went to wash her hands in the bathroom, then sat obediently at the dining table waiting for the meal.","Mo Jiuye busily made two dishes with the ingredients he found in the fridge, one being cucumber fried pork, the other stir-fried eggs with cabbage...","When the dishes were brought to the table, He Zhiran's eyes instantly widened.","She could still accept the cucumber fried pork, as many people in her previous life ate this combination.","But what on earth was that stir-fried eggs with cabbage?","Forget about wondering what these two ingredients would taste like together, it seemed Mo Jiuye didn't even get the process right.","The egg pieces were about the size of fingernails, with some still wrapped in cabbage leaves.","Also, not knowing how much soy sauce he had added, the whole dish looked black.","The cucumber fried pork didn't look much better either. Not only was there no soy sauce, but the ingredients were also covered in wok char...","Looking at his creations, Mo Jiuye was clearly somewhat embarrassed.","He rubbed his head awkwardly, \"Uh...I failed a bit with the dishes, but I tasted them earlier and they are edible.\"","He Zhiran was not the fussy type. In her previous life when she was young, her parents neglected her and she couldn't even eat food like this back then.","Moreover, Mo Jiuye had personally cooked for her, so she could not disregard his good intentions.","\"It's alright, you'll get the hang of cooking with more practice,\" she encouraged.","After speaking, she picked up her chopsticks and put a mouthful of food in her mouth. The taste was not yet unpalatable, so He Zhiran simply ate a few more bites.","Seeing that she did not show displeasure, Mo Jiuye immediately smiled again.","\"Eat slowly, I'll help serve the rice.\"","When Mo Jiuye came back with two bowls of rice, the smile on his face turned into an embarrassed look again.","He placed a bowl of rice in front of He Zhiran, \"I didn't grasp the water ratio for the rice well, it looks a bit like congee...\"","He Zhiran took a look, and indeed that was the case.","The rice Mo Jiuye made was a little too watery to be considered rice, yet a little too dry to be congee...","Still, she encouraged again, \"It's alright as long as it's cooked and I can eat it.\"","Mo Jiuye knew clearly in his heart that she was comforting him, and he immediately felt a warmth there, with an even stronger desire to cook for her for the rest of their lives.","After the meal, He Zhiran made preparations to leave the space, bringing Mo Jiuye along this time.","After all, they were going to meet Fei Nanyu later, so Mo Jiuye hiding would inevitably arouse the other party's suspicions.","The two appeared together in the abandoned room.","He Zhiran had bought large quantities of honeysuckle from Taobao Treasury, piling up half a room's worth.","She then placed the silver and copper coins taken from the magistrate's residence on the other side of the room.","As for those silver notes, He Zhiran chose to keep them.","The reason she kept them was that the silver notes were easy to store, so there was no need for the dog magistrate to also store them here. If they were seen by Fei Nanyu, it would be equivalent to telling him there were not 300 taels of silver here.","He Zhiran did this to avoid possible troubles.","With all the items in the room arranged, the two pushed the door and went out together.","The weeds in the yard had grown back, clearly showing signs that no one had been here for a long time.","He Zhiran circled the yard several dozen times with the mule cart to create traces of frequent recent activity.","Once everything was ready, she bought an antique-style lock from Taobao Treasury and locked the front door.","Then she damaged one of the windows with a tool.","Glancing at the clock in the space, it was almost time she had arranged to meet Fei Nanyu.","He Zhiran purchased a few more antique-style quilts from Taobao Treasury and spread them in the cart compartment so that Mo Jiuye wouldn't feel too bumpy sitting inside.","Driving the mule cart and paying a fee of ten coins, the two returned to Pingyang County once again.","To make it look like she had come from the city, He Zhiran deliberately took a roundabout route before arriving at the designated meeting place.","Fei Nanyu was already waiting there and hurried up to them when he saw He Zhiran driving over with a mule cart from afar.","Mo Jiuye flipped open the carriage curtain to exchange greetings, then Fei Nanyu suggested He Zhiran sit inside while he and his attendant rode outside to drive the cart.","On the way, Fei Nanyu asked with concern how Mo Jiuye got injured.","The two had already anticipated Fei Nanyu would ask this, so they decided to tell the truth.","After listening, Fei Nanyu did not say anything, only sighing before changing the topic.","The few chatted casually along the way and soon arrived at the abandoned residence.","Mo Jiuye's injuries were still quite severe, so he was forcibly kept in the cart by He Zhiran.","He Zhiran led the other two into the yard.","Seeing the footprints in the yard, Fei Nanyu did not actually doubt anything and followed He Zhiran to the front door of the main building.","He Zhiran pointed to a window next to them and said, \"The door is locked, so I got in through there.\"","Without any suspicion, Fei Nanyu strode to the window.","He Zhiran shook it forcefully a few times and the window opened.","Fei Nanyu jumped through the window. Seeing so much honeysuckle, his usual calm composure completely disappeared.","\"Lady Mo, you have truly performed an enormous service this time. I thank you on behalf of the commoners of Dongfeng County.\"","\"Mr. Fei is too polite. I still have a favor to ask of you.\" He Zhiran said.","\"Lady Mo, please tell me whatever you need. As long as Nanyu can accomplish it, I will surely spare no effort.\"","He Zhiran pointed at the silver coins on the ground, \"Mr. Fei must also have heard that Pingyang County's magistrate is a dog official. In the few years since he took office, he has exploited the common people without end. This silver must have been seized from those commoners.","Since we've found this money, I think it should be returned to its rightful owners.\""]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113: The son is unfilial, let the mother worry","paragraphs":["Fei Nanyu was very clever.","\"Mrs. Mo means to ask me to help return this silver to its rightful owner.\"","He Zhiran just liked dealing with smart people.","\"Mr. Fei also knows that my husband and I are in a hurry to be on our way and simply don't have the time for this, not to mention our status makes it inappropriate...\"","Fei Nanyu already agreed with her idea and nodded, \"If Mrs. Mo trusts me, I will definitely take care of this properly.\"","After a pause, he went on, \"The county magistrate Sun hoarded so much wolfsbane, he must have gotten someone's order to do so. Judging from the current situation in Dongfeng County, the plague is likely man-made, either to make Prince Qi's disaster relief effort fruitless, or even cost Prince Qi his life due to the plague.","It's obvious to us all who stands to benefit most from such an outcome. I'm thinking once Prince Qi learns of this matter, he will certainly retaliate.","Presumably by then, Prince Heng will be too busy dealing with it to continue going after Young Master Mo.","Also, after I return to the capital, I will think of an appropriate reason to spread word that Young Master Mo and Prince Qi had a falling out.","Once Prince Heng believes that, he will also completely abandon the idea of assassinating Young Master Mo. Then your future days will be peaceful.\"","He Zhiran had not expected Fei Nanyu to consider all this so quickly, and his guesses at things that might happen aligned perfectly with her own speculations.","What comforted her even more was that Fei Nanyu took the initiative to suggest spreading word of the rift between Mo Jiuye and Prince Qi of the South after returning to the capital.","This saved her and Mo Jiuye the embarrassment of having to ask him for this favor.","He Zhiran sincerely bowed to Fei Nanyu, \"Thank you Mr. Fei for considering my Mo family. I thank you on behalf of all in the Mo family for your kindness.\"","Fei Nanyu quickly helped steady her, \"Mrs. Mo is too polite. If we speak of kindness it was you who saved me first and helped me so greatly today, I should be the one expressing gratitude.\"","The two exchanged pleasantries for a while. Seeing it was getting late, He Zhiran took her leave. Handling the wolfsbane and silver money was now Fei Nanyu's business.","Back in the mule cart, she briefly told Mo Jiuye what had transpired before setting off driving the mule cart.","To accommodate Mo Jiuye's health, she did not dare drive too quickly.","Not until they had traveled over ten li did He Zhiran feel it was safe and send Mo Jiuye into her space to recuperate.","It wasn't until the sun had set that He Zhiran stopped to rest.","She parked the mule cart in a safe spot, then bought some feed for the mule before slipping into her space.","And so, He Zhiran would drive the mule cart by day and rest in her space at night.","On the sixth straight day of travel, Mo Jiuye guessed they were probably not far from the exiled convoy.","At this point He Zhiran had changed back into her original clothing.","The stitches had been removed from Mo Jiuye's wounds and he could move unencumbered again. He insisted on replacing He Zhiran in driving the mule cart.","He Zhiran simply sat beside him, appreciating the different ancient scenery.","Before nightfall they finally caught sight of the exiled convoy up ahead.","He Zhiran considered that her space could provide fruits her family members could not enjoy here. She wanted to take this chance to buy some relatively ordinary fruit varieties by the standards of this time period and bring them back as gifts of thanks for the officers who had let her and Mo Jiuye slip away from the convoy for so long without reporting it.","After all, if the officers had not tacitly allowed this, they would have likely reported such an irregularity to the court long ago.","Seeing He Zhiran was ready, Mo Jiuye sped up the mule cart. In the blink of an eye they had caught up to the convoy.","The officer walking at the rear of the convoy saw who was in the cart and gaped in shock.","Without further thought he raced to the front of the convoy shouting loudly, \"Chief, Mo Jiuye is back!\"","Mo Jiuye slowed the mule cart until it gradually reached the Mo family members' position.","At the same time, Peng Wang at the front also heard the shout and walked over, coincidentally meeting them by the Mo family convoy.","Mo Jiuye first nodded politely at Peng Wang, then went before Old Lady Mo and fell to his knees with a thud,","\"Your son has been unfilial and caused you worry.\"","As he spoke he solemnly kowtowed to Old Lady Mo.","Old Lady Mo's eyes were already brimming with tears. She tottered over to Mo Jiuye and helped him stand, choking back sobs,","\"As long as you're back, as long as you're back...\"","Seeing this, the sisters-in-law also kept wiping their eyes.","Mo Hanyue was even more dramatic, throwing herself into He Zhiran's arms weeping loudly.","\"Sister-in-law Nine, you've finally returned! Hanyue hasn't been able to sleep at night from worrying about you...waah...Sister-in-law Nine, Hanyue missed you and Brother Nine so much!\"","He Zhiran held Mo Hanyue, gently comforting her, \"Don't cry now Hanyue. See, we're back safe and sound.\"","Mo Hanyue's were tears of joy. Of course she wouldn't cry for long. She nestled in He Zhiran's embrace acting spoiled for a bit before returning to Old Lady Mo's side.","At this time Mo Jiuye had gone before Peng Wang. After being away for so long he had to provide an explanation.","\"Big Brother Peng, this matter came up suddenly. My wife and I accidentally fell off a cliff. Thankfully Lord Zhou was timely in his rescue, bringing us out of the valley...\"","Peng Wang looked Mo Jiuye over carefully and patted his shoulder.","\"Old Eight already told me about this when he returned. Don't blame yourself for it, as long as you rejoined us.","Having just gotten back, spend time comforting your family. They were worried sick for you two this time.\"","Mo Jiuye gratefully saluted Peng Wang with folded hands, \"Many thanks for Big Brother Peng's understanding.\"","Peng Wang looked at the skies. He ordered traveling another half hour before stopping to rest.","He Zhiran considered that Old Lady Mo and the sisters would have much to discuss with Mo Jiuye after his dramatic return. She tactfully led the mule cart along behind.","The Eighth Old Zhou was in the middle of the convoy. Seeing He Zhiran alone he couldn't help hurrying over.","\"Lady He, were you and Mo Jiuye safe on the road?\"","He Zhiran gave him a proper smile, \"Many thanks for your concern Lord Zhou. Our journey went smoothly. To rejoin you sooner we bought a mule cart in Pingyang County which made traveling much easier.\"","Peng Wang was not far away. He Zhiran saying this also indirectly explained the mule cart's origins.","The Eighth Old Zhou had not thought that deeply about it. He glanced at the mule cart and said softly,","\"The rules say exiled convoys cannot have livestock transports. But don't worry, I'll tell the chief about this. Considering the special circumstances, not to mention you spent money buying the cart, it wouldn't do to just abandon it.\"","Peng Wang rolled his eyes at the Eighth Old Zhou. If it wasn't for He Zhiran's presence he would have dragged him off already to privately chew him out.","This Eighth Old Zhou truly never learned. He clearly knew nothing could happen with Lady He yet always tried to cozy up to her."]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114: I don't do things that people criticize.","paragraphs":["When The Eighth Old Zhou had arranged to look for people back then, that was still understandable since it involved the big picture.","But now that the young couple had narrowly escaped death and returned safe and sound, this tactless guy was still lingering around in front of them...","While Mo Jiuye was talking to his family, he also saw The Eighth Old Zhou's actions.","He somehow just felt annoyed in his heart.","He reassured his family for a few sentences and walked towards He Zhiran's direction.","As if to declare his sovereignty, he took over the donkey cart reins in He Zhiran's hands, and at the same time pulled her to his other side, drawing a clear line with The Eighth Old Zhou.","The Eighth Old Zhou was not a tactless person either.","He simply couldn't control himself just now, which led him to talk to He Zhiran.","Mo Jiuye's current actions couldn't be more obvious, clearly hinting for him to keep his distance from He Zhiran.","He Zhiran was his lifesaver, he would never take the initiative to undermine their marital relationship.","So The Eighth Old Zhou deliberately coughed twice, \"I still have things to do over there, let's talk another day.\"","Mo Jiuye indifferently replied: \"Master Zhou, please go ahead with your business.\"","Peng Wang saw The Eighth Old Zhou walk away and chased after him, pounding him in the chest with his fist.","\"Old Eight, I don't want to say any more words. Watch yourself.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou also knew that his approaching of He Zhiran just now was indeed somewhat inappropriate.","\"Boss, don't worry! You know me, The Eighth Old Zhou, the best. I would never do anything that would cause criticism.\"","\"Humph! In short, I have said my piece, whatever happens from now on is up to you!\" After saying that, Peng Wang was too lazy to continue blathering and left with his hands behind his back.","Peng Wang had already tacitly acknowledged the existence of the donkey cart and did not ask about it further.","Half an hour later, the troop stopped by a not very big lake.","There was a water source here, convenient for everyone to make dinner.","The sisters-in-law were happy to see the Ninth Younger Brother and Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law come back, and they started cooking more enthusiastically.","Mother Mo always held onto her son, ceaselessly fussing over him.","The Fang and Xie families also came over now and told He Zhiran about what had happened after they went missing.","At the same time, they also told her a big news.","That was that when the He family was carrying He Ming down the mountain, they slipped and accidentally dropped the person.","He Ming rolled down the slope and by the time the He family members caught up, he had already stopped breathing.","The He family was heartbroken over this for several days.","Regarding He Ming's death, He Zhiran only listened casually without making any judgement.","...","After the family ate a reunion dinner in the wild, He Zhiran took the sisters-in-law to the donkey cart to move fruit.","She had prepared relatively few types of fruit, only apples and peaches commonly seen in this era.","But they were plentiful in quantity and could definitely allow everyone to have their fill.","Eldest Sister-in-Law carried down a basket of apples first and when she opened the grass mat on top, everyone was instantly stunned by what was inside.","Second Sister-in-Law excitedly exclaimed, \"Oh my gosh! This is the first time I've seen such huge apples from young to now.\"","Fourth Sister-in-Law chimed in, \"That's right, not only are these apples huge, the color is much redder than any we've eaten before.\"","The gluttonous Eighth Sister-in-Law had already impatiently taken out two apples from the basket.","\"Such nice apples, Mother and Hanying must like eating them. I'll go bring some to them now.\"","When buying fruit for her family members, He Zhiran did not skimp at all.","She had specifically chosen the best quality Red Delicious apples on Taobao, guaranteed sweetness and thirst-quenching with every bite.","Seeing Eighth Sister-in-Law's greedy look, He Zhiran laughed, \"Sisters, there are plenty of apples, everyone feel free to eat.\"","The sisters-in-law stared at the big apples without moving.","They really couldn't bear to eat such good-looking apples.","Seeing the sisters-in-law not making a move, He Zhiran simply stopped urging them and urged them to keep moving the fruit instead.","She had prepared two big baskets of Fuji apples in total. Counting the government clerks and the other two families, everyone could at least get two each.","The peaches she loaded in the cart were also carefully chosen by He Zhiran, similarly large in size and beautiful in color.","When the sisters-in-law saw the honey peaches bigger than their fists, drool nearly flowed out.","The peaches they had eaten before were not only tiny in size, but the flesh was also extremely firm, crunchy with every bite, with nothing attractive about them other than being a little sweet.","However, the peaches Ninth Younger Brother and Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law brought back today were completely different.","Without even taking a bite, just feeling them in their hands, they could see the peaches were big, thick-fleshed, and juicy.","The sisters-in-law simply loved the fruit He Zhiran brought back and couldn't keep their hands off them.","Fourth Sister-in-Law unconsciously touched the purse given by her natal family members when they left.","She hadn't spent her silver at all and everyone had been using Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law's money so far.","If possible, she also wanted to buy some tasty treats for her family like Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law.","\"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, where did you and Ninth Younger Brother buy such nice fruit?\"","The other sisters-in-law were also very curious about this and looked toward He Zhiran when Fourth Sister-in-Law asked.","He Zhiran had already thought up an excuse for the fruit's appearance long ago.","\"Sisters-in-Law, my husband and I happened to see the fruit while traveling, the seller was pushing a wooden cart through streets and alleys. I also don't know where such fruit will be sold down the line.\"","With this, she directly dashed Fourth Sister-in-Law's thoughts of continuing to buy fruit.","Fourth Sister-in-Law was clearly very regretful.","\"What a pity, who knows when we'll encounter such nice fruit again.\"","Seeing this, Third Sister-in-Law chimed in, \"If we come across fruit like this again, it'll be my treat for everyone.\"","Seeing the two of them talking to each other, the other sisters-in-law were envious inside at their having silver.","Eldest Sister-in-Law sighed, \"Once we settle down in the Northwest, I'll go out to find a job to do, then I can also help the family somewhat.\"","Second Sister-in-Law echoed, \"Eldest Sister-in-Law, I'll go with you when the time comes.\"","Seeing the sisters-in-laws' thoughts going astray, He Zhiran hastily reminded, \"Sisters, let's first carry the fruit over and distribute it to everyone.\"","The sisters-in-laws' attention immediately fell back onto the two types of fruit, with some even unconsciously swallowing their saliva.","Four baskets of fruit. Two people carried one basket, and returned to where the families had concentrated to set up tents.","Seeing the Mo family women carrying several large baskets, the government clerks spontaneously crowded around without needing to be called.","Now the entire Mo family's women listened to He Zhiran's arrangements.","Eldest Sister-in-Law asked, \"Ninth Younger Sister-in-Law, how should the fruit be distributed?\"","\"Two of each fruit per person first, then we'll see about the rest,\" He Zhiran said. She had already taken the lead to grab two peaches and two apples to deliver to Mother Mo.","Seeing this, Mo Hanying also came over to help distribute the fruit.","Everyone became all smiles when they saw the Mo family's women take out such nice fruit from the baskets. Even those government clerks no longer put on any airs and lined up orderly to receive theirs.","After Zhang Qing got the apples, he couldn't wait to take a big bite in front of the crowd, instantly giving He Zhiran a big thumbs up.","\"Lady He, you've really got it, to actually manage buying such delicious fruit!\""]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115: Don't Talk to me in Circles.","paragraphs":["As the Fang Family and Xie Family were enjoying the delicious fruits, they did not forget to come and express their gratitude.","Especially little Xie Lin, the sweet-talking child smiled at He Zhiran and said, “Thank you, auntie. When auntie has a little brother in her family, Lin'er will definitely play with him.”","Hearing Xie Lin’s words, everyone around burst into loud laughter.","Some even started jokingly asking He Zhiran if there were any movements in her belly.","He Zhiran did not think much about Xie Lin’s childish words at first. However, when the adults started teasing her, she immediately blushed in embarrassment.","Standing not far away, Mo Jiuye watched all this and fell into deep thoughts.","He thought that the child he and He Zhiran would have must be very good-looking. At that time, the whole family would gather around the little one and play together happily. Just thinking about that scene made him delighted already.","As Mo Jiuye's thoughts drifted further away, countless images of him and He Zhiran with children and grandchildren around their knees appeared in his mind unknowingly...","He Zhiran's blushing only lasted for a moment. In order to cover up her embarrassment, she casually sat with everyone, chatting and laughing.","Watching them get along so well from afar, He Zhiyuan felt that his intestines turned green with regret.","He should have learned from the Xie Family and the Fang Family to curry favor with Mo Jiuye earlier.","That way, wouldn’t his He Family also be able to enjoy such delicious fruits?","Thinking of this, He Zhiyuan unexpectedly went to Mo Jiuye according to his own intention.","Mo Jiuye glanced at him but had no intention of talking to him.","He Zhiyuan thought that since he took the initiative to come over, even if Mo Jiuye was unwilling, he would at least ask, “What are you here for?”","But Mo Jiuye did not.","He Zhiyuan acted on impulse when he came this time. Now faced with this situation, he was caught in a dilemma.","Since he already came, he could not leave without saying anything.","After thinking for a moment, He Zhiyuan gritted his teeth and spoke up, “Mo... Master Mo.” It suddenly occurred to him that addressing in this way would be more appropriate.","Mo Jiuye raised his eyebrows but still did not speak. He just signaled him to continue.","He Zhiyuan looked mysterious. After taking a furtive look around, he whispered, “In fact, someone instigated me when I withheld the grains and fodder from the border pass back then.”","Even without He Zhiyuan saying it, Mo Jiuye was clear in his heart.","However, deliberately pretending to be unaware in front of He Zhiyuan, he wanted to see what tricks He Zhiyuan was playing.","\"It looks like Master He is ready to sell out his boss?\" Mo Jiuye spoke with an icy tone that contained extremely obvious mockery.","Although the tone made He Zhiyuan a little embarrassed, the arrow had left the bowstring. Since he already started talking, he did not think of continuing to conceal anything.","Whether he could make up with Mo Jiuye depended on this move.","Hence, He Zhiyuan also became serious.","“I’m afraid Master Mo can’t imagine that the one who instructed me to withhold grains and fodder back then was Second Prince Prince Rui.”","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye’s eyes suddenly became profound.","“You’re saying it was Prince Rui?”","He Zhiyuan nodded, “It was indeed Prince Rui.”","This was completely different from what Mo Jiuye had guessed before.","Back then, it was clear to him that someone must have instigated He Zhiyuan’s withholding grains and fodder to the border pass. However, they speculated the person was Nan Heng.","By then, the situation in court was pretty clear. Nan Heng was born to the principal wife of Emperor Shunwu, the legitimate crown prince. His ability was slightly lacking, but his position was auspicious. Those who supported making him the crown prince took up half the court halls.","Nan Qi was born to Concubine Yuan, with a status second only to that of Nan Heng.","However, Nan Qi’s superb conduct won the support of many ministers, half of whom became his faction.","As for Nan Rui, whom He Zhiyuan had just mentioned, his mother was not favored, nor did Emperor Shunwu like this son. He seldom had any presence in front of others since young.","His usual performance was showing no interest in politics and being engrossed in poetry and painting with scholars all day.","If what He Zhiyuan said was true, Mo Jiuye could not understand for the moment what Prince Rui’s intention for doing so was.","To confirm whether He Zhiyuan's words were true or false, he asked, “Why would he do so when we have no enmity at all?”","It was as if he had hit Mo Jiuye’s trigger, and He Zhiyuan’s expression immediately changed upon hearing this.","He gave a sinister laugh. As he started to explain, his words also carried more confidence than before.","“Master Mo is a smart man, you must know the purpose of my telling you these.”","Watching He Zhiyuan with his petty face, Mo Jiuye just wanted to slap him.","Nevertheless, to extract some useful information from him, Mo Jiuye clenched and relaxed his fist and held back his anger.","“I’m merely a simple warrior who does not understand those winding tricks. So Master He should speak plainly with me.”","He had thought that upon saying this, Mo Jiuye would immediately change his attitude and try to please him.","However, the result was completely opposite from what he imagined. Not only did Mo Jiuye not show any intention to fawn on him, he even intimidated him with that icy cold gaze.","Seeing Mo Jiuye's cold eyes, He Zhiyuan could not help shuddering.","He even associated it with Mo Jiuye possibly taking some drastic measures to force him to yield if he did not disclose everything he knew today.","As for what measures, He Zhiyuan dared not imagine. With Mo Jiuye’s decisive and ruthless means on the battlefield, he would definitely suffer.","After so much trouble, he still had to confess in the end...","Having figured things out, He Zhiyuan decided not to worry about gains and losses any longer. He did not believe that after revealing such a huge secret, Mo Jiuye would remain indifferent.","“The poetry and painting Prince Rui engages in every day is just a front. His intention is to make Prince Heng and Prince Qi lower their guard and think he would not become a stumbling block on their path to being the crown prince.","How would they expect that Prince Rui has secretly rallied many ministers in private? On the surface, those ministers still belong to either Prince Heng or Prince Qi’s faction, but they are actually working for Prince Rui.","Back then, his intention of asking me to withhold grains and fodder on the way to the borders was to make Prince Qi suspicious of Prince Heng. This was meant to intensify conflicts between them to the point of drawing swords against each other.","And indeed, things went just as Prince Rui predicted. Prince Qi’s subordinates submitted many impeachments against Prince Heng repeatedly. As a result, the two became like fire and water and even started oppressing each other secretly.”","At this moment, Mo Jiuye still could not distinguish the authenticity of He Zhiyuan’s words.","However, what he said was reasoned and plausible; it was not impossible.","“What benefits did Prince Rui promise you that made you so willing to be used by him?”","This question was key. If He Zhiyuan’s answer was reasonable, Mo Jiuye would overturn all his prior cognition.","“I won’t hide this from Master Mo, but I have an illegitimate daughter named He Meiyu who has been raised outside ever since she was young. Meiyu is talented and accomplished. She got to know Prince Rui by chance at a poetry party once, and they developed feelings for each other. After Prince Rui learned of her status, he personally proposed to me.","He promised that Meiyu’s position would be the principal wife, so I considered that no matter whether Prince Rui had ulterior motives or not, he was a prince after all. For my little illegitimate daughter to become a principal wife would be a blessing that I would never achieve even after three lifetimes of cultivation.","After I agreed, Prince Rui put forward another condition that after entering his residence, Meiyu must take on a new identity so that outsiders would not think there was any connection between us.","His intention was that he did not want others to accuse him of forming factions and private interests.","Two months later, Prince Rui brought Meiyu home as promised. Meiyu's identity was merely the daughter of a wealthy merchant.”"]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116: What did He promise You","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye understood a lot more.","To put it simply, the reason why He Zhiyuan could get involved with Prince Rui was because the intermediary was He Meiyu.","He had also heard that the family background of Prince Rui's consort was nothing special. She was just from an ordinary merchant family in the Capital city.","And not long ago, there was news spreading around the Capital city that Prince Rui's consort had fallen ill and died.","Judging by He Zhiyuan's expression now, he did not seem to be lying.","Mo Jiuye continued asking, \"What happened after that?\"","\"Afterwards, Prince Rui took Meiyu along with him to secretly meet me, using the excuse that she missed her family.","As we continued to meet, Prince Rui and I gradually became more familiar with each other, and he took the opportunity to tell me about recruiting me.\"","Mo Jiuye asked insistently, \"What benefits did he promise you?\"","He Zhiyuan smiled self-deprecatingly, \"Naturally, it was the position of empress for Meiyu. Prince Rui said that as long as he could smoothly take that position, Meiyu would definitely be the future empress.","By then, he would announce Meiyu's true identity in front of all the civil and military officials of the court, making me the father-in-law who stood above tens of thousands of people, second only to the emperor.\"","Mo Jiuye sneered coldly, \"Too bad your daughter had a short life.\"","He Zhiyuan sighed.","\"It was all because I was not a good judge of character. I thought Prince Rui would keep his promise to me. But after I was demoted by the emperor, his attitude towards me changed dramatically.","It was not until the news of Meiyu's death came out that I completely gave up the dream of becoming the emperor's father-in-law.","Prince Rui was also not worried that I would reveal his matters, because by doing so, it would be equivalent to me directly admitting that I had detained the border troops' rations.\"","Having said that, He Zhiyuan bowed deeply to Mo Jiuye.","\"Young Master Mo, now that we have both fallen to being exiled, I'm telling you all this in the hope that you can let go of past grudges and take care of my family a little.","I was able to get to where I am today with Prince Rui's maneuvers behind the scenes. After experiencing exile for this period of time, I have seen through many things and will no longer have any improper thoughts.\"","Mo Jiuye put his hands behind his back, his gaze still cold.","\"You and I were never on the same side to begin with. Moreover, your actions back then almost cost the lives of so many troops at the border. No matter what, I will never forgive you for that.","Considering that you told me all these today, as long as you follow the rules and don't provoke me in the future, I guarantee I won't take action against you on my own initiative.\"","Mo Jiuye had thought that after arriving in the northwest, he would find an opportunity to take He Zhiyuan's life and avenge the border troops whose rations were withheld by him that year.","If it were not for the border troops not losing their lives due to his withholding of rations, Mo Jiuye would have taken his life long ago.","For him to be able to make such a guarantee to He Zhiyuan today was already the greatest concession.","Upon hearing this, He Zhiyuan suddenly straightened up. He stared at Mo Jiuye in disbelief.","He had never imagined that Mo Jiuye had intended to kill him.","He probably only held back because there were still those officials present.","Thinking of this, He Zhiyuan suddenly felt a chill down his spine, and cold sweat involuntarily broke out on his forehead.","His intention in voluntarily telling Mo Jiuye these things was not to earn the other party's forgiveness, but to make his whole family live a little better.","Even if it was just one or two of those fruits to satisfy their cravings, it would still be good.","Unexpectedly, things did not go according to plan at all, putting him in a dilemma.","After thinking for a while, He Zhiyuan gritted his teeth and said, \"Young Master Mo, I told you all these in good faith. You can't go back on your word!\"","Mo Jiuye sneered coldly.","\"You took the initiative to tell me. I didn't ask.\"","This almost angered He Zhiyuan to the point of fainting. He was not entirely without a temper either.","\"People in court all say you are a gentleman, but I see you have the face of a petty man.\"","Instead of getting angry, Mo Jiuye smiled.","\"Whether one is a gentleman or has the face of a petty man depends on who one is facing. What reason do I have to be a gentleman when dealing with a thoroughly petty man?\"","These words left He Zhiyuan speechless. He also realized that Mo Jiuye had a personality that could not be persuaded no matter what. In the end, it was pointless for him to say any more.","Finally, He Zhiyuan flung his sleeve and walked away angrily.","At the same time, Mo Jiuye also fell into contemplation, thinking about how to deal with it in the future if what He Zhiyuan said was true.","He had just figured out a solution for Nan Heng's matters when another hidden figure like Nan Rui popped up.","Zhi Ran was eating fruit with the women and did not think too much when he saw He Zhiyuan come over. He assumed it was just a behavior to curry favor with Mo Jiuye.","Seeing that the women were almost done eating, Zhi Ran urged everyone to go rest.","There were not too many fruits left, enough to give each of the Mo family two.","So Zhi Ran took the initiative to have everyone take two and leave, keeping them to eat on the road tomorrow.","Everyone left happily with two fruits each, returning to their own tents to rest.","Zhi Ran let Old Lady Mo sleep in the carriage with Mo Hanyue.","The inside of the carriage was soft and cushy, certainly more comfortable than the tents.","Considering her son's injury, Old Lady Mo insisted on sleeping in the tent.","Now that Mo Jiuye knew the secret of the space, Zhi Ran was even less demanding about the lodging arrangements. No matter where they slept, they would ultimately enter the space anyway.","Mo Jiuye also understood this principle. He helped Zhi Ran persuade Old Lady Mo.","In the end, Old Lady Mo could not refuse the two of them and obediently took Mo Hanyue with her into the carriage.","Now that Mo Jiuye knew about the existence of the space, Zhi Ran no longer intended to wash up outside. They could take care of it once back in the space.","When she returned to the tent, she saw Mo Jiuye had a pensive look.","Zhi Ran subconsciously thought it must have something to do with He Zhiyuan.","Afraid that the walls had ears, to be safe, Zhi Ran directly pulled Mo Jiuye into the space with her.","The two sat down at the dining table tacitly.","Zhi Ran asked, \"What happened?\"","Mo Jiuye did not hide anything at all and told Zhi Ran what He Zhiyuan had just said.","\"I can't confirm whether what He Zhiyuan said is true or false, but I still have to be vigilant.\"","Upon hearing this, Zhi Ran's mind started searching for the records about Prince Rui in the history books.","However, in her knowledge, Prince Rui's presence was very insignificant. If not for Mo Jiuye's mention today, she might have completely ignored this person altogether.","To verify the authenticity of the matter, Zhi Ran brought over several history books in front of Mo Jiuye.","Seeing a pile of books on the table, Mo Jiuye asked, \"What are these?\"","Zhi Ran specifically handed over a traditional Chinese edition of a history book to Mo Jiuye.","\"This records some things about the Da Shun Dynasty. It might help us.\"","Without hesitation, Mo Jiuye immediately started flipping through it.","Zhi Ran was not idle either. Since her transmigration here, she had read through the history books multiple times. Most of the contents were superficial descriptions. If one really wanted to discover some unknown matters, one still had to dig deeper into unofficial historical records."]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117: I should be dead by Now.","paragraphs":["Therefore, He Zhiran directly chose to read \"Wild History\".","At this moment, the two of them had already entered a state of immersed reading, earnestly flipping through the books in their hands.","When Mo Jiuye saw the place where he died after being exiled, he took a sharp breath and looked deeply at He Zhiran.","\"Is it because of these books that you can foresee some things in advance?\"","Now, apart from her identity as a time traveler, Mo Jiuye had almost learned all of her secrets.","Therefore, He Zhiran had no intention of hiding anything.","\"Yes, it's true. I can foresee some things because of these books.","You saw the items I purchased on my phone, and those peculiar things should all come from the future.\"","\"The future?\" Mo Jiuye was not unfamiliar with this term, but he felt that everything was beyond his realm of understanding.","He Zhiran shrugged and continued, \"When I first obtained this space, I was also curious about why there were such peculiar things here.","After a long period of research and analysis, I determined that this space is indeed a creation of the future.\"","As she said that, she took the book from Mo Jiuye's hand and pointed to a corner of the cover.","\"Look here, the publication date of this book is 2020, and we are currently in the year 303, with more than a thousand years in between.\"","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment.","\"Are you saying that this book was written by people from the future?\"","\"Not entirely. I guess that people from the future compiled these records together,\" explained He Zhiran.","With that, Mo Jiuye completely understood.","He pointed to the section in the book where he died in exile and asked the question in his heart.","\"According to the book, I should be a dead person right now, but I am still alive in this world. This must be related to you, right?\"","He Zhiran did not deny this.","\"The book indeed records that after your exile, you died shortly after leaving the capital. However, the cause of death remains a mystery.","I speculate that you were summoned to the palace by the emperor late at night and severely injured after receiving a hundred beatings. This could be one possible cause of death, and the other is that those who wanted to take your life sent someone to assassinate you.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. \"Indeed, with your warning and the cushion you gave me for protection, I couldn't bear fifty beatings, let alone a hundred, especially without any preparation.","In that situation, anyone who wanted to take my life would have found it as easy as turning their hand.\"","Mo Jiuye was not afraid of death; he had long been prepared to sacrifice himself for his country.","However, he didn't want to die in such an obscure manner.","Now that he could live well, it was all thanks to He Zhiran.","Gratitude unspoken, Mo Jiuye deeply engraved all of this in his heart. In the future, he would strive to make her the happiest woman in the world and wholeheartedly protect her.","The two of them continued to bury themselves in their books. Mo Jiuye quickly skimmed through the content of his posthumous life, paying special attention to the situations of important figures.","Only then did Mo Jiuye realize why He Zhiran didn't accept the silver ticket given by Fei Nanyu.","Originally, Fei Nanyu turned out to be the future emperor, and he achieved remarkable political accomplishments, earning him the title of an emperor for all ages.","This was something that Mo Jiuye could never have imagined.","Including Nan Qi, who became the next emperor of the Da Shun Dynasty, he met an early demise due to his lust for women.","And Nan Rui, he was only briefly mentioned in the historical records.","The previous content was fine, almost identical to Nan Rui's current situation, without mentioning any ambitions he had.","Moreover, Nan Rui's death occurred shortly after Nan Qi ascended the throne.","At this moment, he was incredibly shocked, even sharing the same thoughts as He Zhiran.","That is, if he didn't die, it meant that this history had changed, but he didn't know how it would develop in the future.","If he got involved, would he be able to stir up this situation?","These were just thoughts in Mo Jiuye's mind, after all, with his current identity, he couldn't do anything.","He Zhiran finally found a record about Nan Rui in the \"Wild History.\"","She quickly called Mo Jiuye over and they watched it together.","Mo Jiuye didn't recognize simplified characters, so He Zhiran read it to him.","\"The book says that Nan Rui hid his talents for several years and secretly built his own power. However, because he didn't dare to be too bold, his influence was not very extensive.","Later, when Nan Qi and Nan Heng competed with each other, he finally revealed his true colors.","The only time Nan Qi and Nan Heng joined forces was to eliminate Nan Rui.\"","Mo Jiuye took a deep breath. Based on the records in this book, combined with what He Zhiyuan said, he could already conclude that Nan Rui was not as simple as he appeared.","And when he was able to instruct He Zhiyuan to seize grain and supplies, it was partly to deepen the conflict between Nan Qi and Nan Heng, and also with the intention of getting rid of Nan Rui.","After all, everyone knew about his close relationship with Nan Qi.","Nan Heng was most wary of Nan Qi because he had Mo Jiuye, an invincible ally.","\"In that case, we have to watch out for Nan Rui too.\"","He Zhiran shrugged, it seemed like solving Nan Heng's matter had just led to the need to be on guard against Nan Rui.","Luckily, Emperor Shunwu only had these three sons. If there were more, they would really have a hard time dealing with them.","\"Do you have any good strategies now?\"","Mo Jiuye sneered, \"Nan Rui is wary of me for the same reason as Nan Heng. They are both worried that I will have a chance for a comeback and continue to assist Nan Qi.","Now, it depends on when he decides to take action against me. If he can wait until Fei Nanyu spreads the news of the rupture between me and Nan Qi, then he probably would stop trying to assassinate me to avoid trouble.","Otherwise, if he has already sent someone, we need to be prepared in the next few days.\"","He Zhiran agreed wholeheartedly with Mo Jiuye's words.","\"For the next period of time, we should be more vigilant.\"","Saying that, He Zhiran took out her phone using telekinesis.","She directly opened the Taobao app and planned to select some self-defense tools for the women in their family.","The first thing that appears on Taobao is an information box, displaying the sales situation and income of the store.","He Zhiran glanced at it casually and saw that her income had increased by 700,000. With a clear understanding, she closed the information box.","Inside Taobao, she searched for women's self-defense items, and the most common ones were mini stun guns and anti-wolf sprays.","The mini stun gun looked compact and practical, so she decisively purchased one.","In front of Mo Jiuye, she opened the packaging and aimed the top of the mini stun gun at the table, pressing the switch.","A buzzing sound was heard.","Mo Jiuye asked, \"What is this?\""]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118: Self-defence Weapon","paragraphs":["He Zhiran patiently explained the function of the mini stun gun to him.","\"Do you think it's appropriate to give something like this to Mother, Sisters-in-law and Auntie for self-defense?\"","Mo Jiuye took over the stun gun and fiddled with it for a while, also imitating He Zhiran's actions to operate it.","\"This thing is very convenient to use and small and easy to hide, but I feel it's not suitable for them to use.\"","He Zhiran raised her eyebrows: \"Why?\"","\"You saw the assassins last time too. They would initially use bows and arrows for long-range assassination. If the assassination failed, they would then choose close combat.","The women in our family don't know any martial arts. Even if the assassins got close, I'm afraid they wouldn't be able to use the stun guns in time and would be killed in one move.\"","After listening to Mo Jiuye's explanation, He Zhiran also realized this point.","Thinking again of the pepper spray that was less lethal than the stun gun, she felt it was even more unnecessary to take it out to show Mo Jiuye.","Judging from the current situation, the self-defense tool the sisters-in-law need should have a certain range attack capability, the more powerful the better.","In this regard, only guns are most suitable.","It's just that if guns are brought in front of the sisters-in-law, there must be a proper excuse.","After thinking for a moment, suddenly she had a flash of inspiration.","He Zhiran used her mind to take out a mini pistol smaller than her palm.","Mo Jiuye raised his eyebrows: \"Are you going to give them this?\"","He Zhiran nodded: \"From the current situation, this is the most suitable for them. Not only does it have great lethality, but it can also attack from a distance.","I also thought of a good excuse, just say that we bought it from a foreigner on our way to chase the exiled team.\"","Mo Jiuye was no stranger to foreigners, who were nothing more than some blond and blue-eyed big guys.","He had seen such people with his own eyes when he passed by a seaside pier once out of curiosity and took a close look.","Although he couldn't understand what those foreigners were saying, the things they took out of their pockets were all things he hadn't seen before.","He Zhiran thought it was not a bad idea to reveal the mini pistol under such an excuse.","Moreover, he also felt that the mini pistol was the most suitable for his family women to defend themselves.","Even if he was unfortunately killed by those assassins, his family would at least have a means to save their lives and still have great hope of survival.","Mo Jiuye said gratefully with appreciative eyes,","\"That's very good, just as you said.\"","There were only two mini pistols at the moment. If He Zhiran wanted more, she would have to take them out of the space repeatedly.","After getting Mo Jiuye’s consent, she immediately flashed out of the space.","Sitting in the tent, He Zhiran kept taking out mini pistols with her mind.","It was not until ten identical mini pistols appeared in front of her that she retracted back into the space.","After arranging the life-saving gadgets for the women at home, He Zhiran continued to explain some content in Historical Records to Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye had already figured out that the reason Nan Qi resented him was because he had been switched at birth.","It's just that he had the mark unique to Mo men on him.","If there was such a mark on Nan Qi’s body too, he might have suspected that the mark on him was forged later.","However, he clearly knew that there was no Mo family mark on Nan Qi's body.","From this point of view, Mo Jiuye was very confident about his identity.","He was a genuine member of the Mo Family, not to mention that he looked almost seventy to eighty percent like his Fourth Brother, so there was no possibility that he had been switched.","There were more and more doubts about this matter, and they racked their brains but couldn't figure out the reason.","After all, there are no winds that do not rise waves. Nan Qi would not groundlessly suspect that he was not of royal blood for no reason.","It is not ruled out that Nan Qi's political opponents deliberately provoked him in order to achieve the goal of making Nan Qi want to kill Mo Jiuye with his own hands.","However, from Mo Jiuye’s understanding of Nan Qi, he was not the kind of person without a brain at all.","There must be some convincing reasons for this.","Or maybe Nan Qi was indeed not of royal blood, and he learned about this from Concubine Yuan.","If Concubine Yuan really did such a thing, she would definitely rot it in her belly for life without saying it out.","Then it could only mean that Nan Qi had overheard something.","The more they analyzed, the more confused they became. They simply stopped thinking about it.","After all, it had been determined that Mo Jiuye was a genuine member of the Mo Family. As for what Nan Qi's identity was, it was already irrelevant to them.","That night was destined to be sleepless. When the two got up from the dining table, the hour hand of the big clock on the wall had already pointed to the three o'clock direction.","There were only two hours left before the usual wake-up time.","Mo Jiuye reminded: \"We still have to travel later, so we should rest a little.\"","When searching for Nan Rui's historical records just now, she didn’t feel anything. Now that she relaxed, He Zhiran felt a little sleepy too. After simply washing up in the bathroom, she lay back in bed to rest.","Neither of them dared to sleep too deeply for fear of people finding out that they were not in the tent when they got up late.","In a daze, He Zhiran felt the person next to her move, and she immediately opened her eyes too.","The two got out of bed tacitly, tidied up, and then left the space.","After breakfast, while the officials were over there tidying up the tents, He Zhiran gathered all the women in the family together.","She pretended to pile goods into the mule cart, but she was actually going to put those mini pistols into the prepared wooden box and hand them over to her family as soon as possible.","Mo Jiuye felt that since they had guessed that Nan Rui might take action against him, they should arrange the gadgets that could save the lives of their family members early.","Mo Jiuye pretended to tidy up items in the carriage and casually took out the wooden box containing ten mini pistols.","In order to prevent others from seeing, he only opened the box a crack, allowing his family to see what was inside.","The women gathered outside the carriage, peeking into the box.","Seeing her daughter-in-law about to ask loudly, Old Lady Mo scolded with a cold face:","\"Xie, are you afraid other people don't know what we're doing?\"","Second Sister-in-law looked at her stern-faced mother-in-law and stuck out her tongue.","\"I know I was wrong, Mother.\"","Seeing this, although others were still very curious about the things in the box, they did not ask aloud.","Mo Jiuye scanned around and saw that others were busy tidying up. He said to the women in a low voice:","\"The things in the box are hidden weapons that we bought from foreigners on the way.","Such hidden weapons have great lethality and are easy to operate.","Considering that there may still be dangers on the road ahead, in order for everyone to have a means of self-defense, He Zhiran and I decided to give everyone a weapon for self-defense.\"","Second Sister-in-law had always been careless. She was not interested in any hidden weapons, only attracted by the two words \"He Zhiran\" mentioned by Mo Jiuye.","It seemed that her Ninth Younger Brother's cold temperament had warmed up with Ninth Sister quite quickly judging by such an intimate form of address.","It probably wouldn't take long before there would be an addition to the Mo family."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: Used to be My Subordinate","paragraphs":["Second sister-in-law's deviation of thoughts does not represent the thoughts of others.","First, there is the always calm and composed Lady Mo, who has spent half her life as a military officer's wife and has some understanding of the power of hidden weapons.","Looking at the solemn expression on her son's face while speaking, she knew that this hidden weapon was definitely extraordinary.","\"Jiuye, rest assured, I will keep a close eye on your sisters-in-law and Hanyue, and prevent them from easily exposing this hidden weapon to others.\"","The eldest sister-in-law spoke first, \"We will all follow Mother's and Ninth Brother's arrangements.\"","The other sisters-in-law also expressed their agreement in low voices, promising to keep this hidden weapon well-hidden and away from prying eyes.","Time was running out, so Mo Jiuye explained the usage and precautions of the mini pistol to his family.","If anyone didn't understand, they would privately ask those who had already learned.","After distributing one mini pistol to each person, Peng Wang's side also began preparing for the journey.","On this day, everything was calm and uneventful.","Even so, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not let their guard down.","They had even decided not to rest in the space in the evenings for the next few days, in case an assassin appeared and they couldn't detect it in the space.","The team continued to march calmly for three days and finally arrived at a county town where they could replenish their supplies and stayed at an inn.","To their surprise, besides their group, the inn was almost empty, to the point where one could describe it as deserted.","The innkeeper sat lazily at the entrance.","Peng Wang took the initiative to greet the innkeeper.","\"Innkeeper Liu, how have you been?\"","The weariness in Innkeeper Liu's tone couldn't be concealed.","\"Lord Peng, if you had come two days later, I'm afraid you wouldn't be able to stay at my inn.\"","Peng Wang noticed the lack of business in the inn and asked, \"Innkeeper Liu, what happened exactly?\"","\"Ah... it's better not to mention it. Not long ago, a group of notorious bandits appeared in our Xiangyang County. These people, they never steal from ordinary folks' homes, but specifically target wealthy families, and secretly help those poor families.\"","Peng Wang didn't understand, \"Isn't that a good thing? What does it have to do with your inn?\"","Innkeeper Liu smiled bitterly.","\"That's true. It doesn't have anything to do with my inn. But those bandits' actions scared away many out-of-town merchants who are afraid to do business in our Xiangyang County. As a result, the inns in our county have almost no business.\"","Peng Wang heard about these bandits who robbed the rich to help the poor for the first time and decided to ask more details.","\"As Innkeeper Liu said, those bandits rob the rich to help the poor. They can't possibly steal from every household, right?\"","\"You're right. Even if it's a wealthy family, they only target those who are unscrupulous in their wealth,\" replied Innkeeper Liu.","Peng Wang furrowed his brows, \"If that's the case, why are those merchants so worried?\"","Innkeeper Liu sighed once again.","\"The thing is, those bandits have been glorified by the common people. Everyone who has some money wants to stay away from them. As a result, the number of out-of-town people coming to Xiangyang County keeps decreasing.\"","In this regard, Peng Wang could only listen to the gossip. After all, these government officials were very poor, and the prisoners didn't have much money, so there was no worry about theft.","Moreover, people said that those notorious thieves were engaged in robbing the rich to help the poor, which had nothing to do with them.","Without delving further, Peng Wang asked the shopkeeper Liu to help arrange the guest rooms and let everyone rest.","As usual, those who couldn't afford the room fee went to the backyard shed...","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye still chose to share a room. During the night's rest, Mo Jiuye suddenly felt something strange.","He quickly rushed out of the room and leaped onto the roof.","He Zhiran followed, but unfortunately, Mo Jiuye was too fast. When she went out, she couldn't see Mo Jiuye's figure at all, so she had to return to the room and wait.","Mo Jiuye chased after several dark figures on the roof and ran far away until they were far from the residence. Only then did the cloaked individuals stop.","\"Who are you?\" Mo Jiuye asked in a deep voice.","The cloaked individuals, noticing someone chasing after them, originally intended to lead the person to a more secluded place before taking action.","When they heard this familiar voice, they instantly removed the masks covering their faces and knelt down before Mo Jiuye.","\"Subordinate Liang Hao pays respects to Duke Gong.\"","\"Liang Hao, what are you doing here?\" Mo Jiuye was obviously surprised.","As he spoke, he quickly stepped forward and helped the kneeling individuals up.","Liang Hao pointed to the several people behind him and said, \"Duke Gong, we heard that your mansion was ransacked and your family was exiled. We resigned from our official positions and waited here to meet with you.\"","Mo Jiuye looked at the people behind Liang Hao.","Song Chao, Wang Dali, Xu Qingfeng, Li Mingrui.","These people were all talents nurtured by his father and brothers. After he returned to the capital, these people continued to stay at the border to guard it.","Unexpectedly, these people were so loyal to the Mo family that they chose to resign and follow him here in such circumstances.","Mo Jiuye didn't entirely agree with their actions.","\"You have worked hard to achieve your current positions. Why go through such hardships again?","Moreover, with the entire Mo family expelled, there is no future for following me.\"","Liang Hao and the others knelt down again and said, \"We have accompanied Duke Gong through life and death for many years. We are well aware of whether you have colluded with the enemy and betrayed the country. These baseless rumors are absurd.","The court has treated a meritorious person like you unfairly, and we will not sacrifice our lives for such an incompetent ruler.\"","Their words were resolute and powerful, displaying Liang Hao and the others' dissatisfaction with the court.","Mo Jiuye knew well that these people had already resigned from their official positions, and no matter how much he said, it would be in vain.","\"In that case, what are your plans for the future?\"","The five individuals answered in unison, \"Wherever Duke Gong is, we will be there.\"","Mo Jiuye had no objections to this. These few were unwanted orphans since childhood. They were brought to the military camp by his father and brothers for training, and even now, they were still alone without any attachments wherever they went.","\"For now, I am a banished criminal of the court. I can only regain my freedom after reaching the northwest. It's inconvenient for you to travel with the banished group. Let's meet in the northwest.\"","\"No, we will accompany Duke Guo all the way to ensure your safety and that of your family,\" Liang Hao retorted.","Mentioning the safety of his family made Mo Jiuye hesitate.","Having Liang Hao and the others with him would indeed be of great help in times of danger.","\"Since that's the case, you can follow the team from a distance without arousing suspicion,\" he paused and added, \"Also, I am no longer Duke Guo, so you should use a different title for me in the future.\"","Liang Hao pondered for a moment. \"How about we continue to address you as Ninth Master, just like before?\"","According to Mo Jiuye's understanding, they were all commoners without any official positions now, and these people were older than him. It wouldn't be inappropriate for them to call him by his name.","However, considering Liang Hao and the others' respectful attitude towards the Mo family, he doubted they would agree to address him by his name. So Mo Jiuye went along with their suggestion.","\"Alright, let's go with that!\""]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120: This is about Eight.","paragraphs":["Seeing the dressing of several people, Mo Jiuye suddenly remembered what Liu boss said about the great robber Jiang Yang in the inn today.","\"Are you guys the great robber Jiang Yang who recently appeared in Xiangyang County?\"","Speaking of this, several people were somewhat ashamed to scratch their heads.","\"Don't hide it from Master Jiu, we did some robbing the rich and helping the poor in Xiangyang County.\"","Mo Jiuye raised his eyebrows, motioning them to continue.","\"When we first came here, we were going to wait for Master on the official road during the day and find an inn in Xiangyang County at night.","Who knew, after being here for a few days, we heard that there were several wealthy families in Xiangyang City who, relying on the money in their hands, did some unkind things.","We have nothing to do here all day, so we wanted to do something for the common people. That's how things spread outside happened.\"","Mo Jiuye couldn’t help but laugh: \"You guys are really something. I heard that you scared away so many foreign merchants that they didn't even dare to come to Xiangyang City to do business, so the inn I stayed in today can’t even stay open.\"","Hearing this, Liang Hao and others felt a little unbelievable.","\"No way? We only robbed a few times, and we haven't done anything for a good few days now. If Song Chao hadn't said he couldn't sleep today, we wouldn't have gone out either. I didn't expect to meet Master so coincidentally tonight.\"","Mo Jiuye looked at the sky. He had been out chasing for nearly half an hour. He knew He Zhiran must be worried about him, so he didn’t intend to stay here any longer.","\"I'm staying at the inn you just passed. The officials will go out tomorrow morning to purchase some supplies and then continue on their way.\"","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was about to leave, Li Mingrui hurriedly reminded Liang Hao: \"We still have very important things to tell Master.\"","Mo Jiuye asked, \"What is it in the end?\"","\"Master, this matter is related to Eighth Master.\"","Mo Jiuye frowned. \"You mean my eighth brother?\"","Liang Hao nodded: \"Yes. When we first heard about the Mo family incident, we thought of the tombs of the old Prime Minister and the eight masters there, afraid that the court would send someone to destroy them, so we decided to go and take a look first.","When we got there, we found that Eighth Master’s tomb had been dug open, the coffin lid was open, and there was nothing inside.","We patrolled there ten days ago and everything was fine then. So I can determine that Eighth Master’s tomb was dug open no more than ten days ago.\"","This news was shocking to Mo Jiuye.","It was already difficult to accept that his father and brothers died in service of the country. And now his eighth brother's tomb was dug up again. He couldn’t figure out why the grave robbers did this.","\"Did you guys continue investigating this matter later?\"","Liang Hao nodded: \"Since discovering that Eighth Master’s tomb had been dug up, we came back almost every day to check it out but found no clues. Until we left there, the tombs of the old Prime Minister and the other seven masters were still intact. \"","Mo Jiuye gasped. Some memories of his eighth brother appeared in his mind.","His eighth brother Mo Chuhan was with his sixth and seventh brothers when the incident happened. At that time, he was leading his troops to guard another city gate.","When the corpses of the three elder brothers were carried back, they were already mutilated beyond recognition. They could only be identified by their clothing.","Mo Jiuye was heartbroken at the time. But there were still new battles to face. After arranging the funeral, he buried his elder brothers.","If he remembered correctly, when Eighth Brother was encoffined, there was still blood flowing from his leg, which made Mo Jiuye suspect for a moment that Eighth Brother had not died.","However, after being diagnosed by many army doctors, it was determined that Eighth Brother was already dead, so Mo Jiuye dismissed his doubts.","Thinking of this, he asked Liang Hao: \"Did you see any bloodstains in Eighth Master's coffin?\"","Liang Hao shook his head: \"No, Eighth Master’s coffin was very clean. At that time I wondered why there was not even a rotten piece of clothing left in the coffin when Eighth Master had been buried for many years?\"","Mo Jiuye felt countless doubts arose in his mind.","According to Liang Hao's statement, that coffin should not be the one used to encoffin Eighth Brother back then.","Also, why did the tomb robbers only dig up Eighth Brother’s tomb?","What was the purpose of the tomb robbers taking away Eighth Brother and his original coffin?","One question after another appeared in Mo Jiuye's mind, making him feel breathless.","Mo Jiuye had made up his mind that after settling his family in the northwest, he would personally investigate this matter.","He looked up at the people: \"It's getting late, go back and rest early. Just follow along if needed tomorrow.\"","Liang Hao and the others didn’t know why Master was in such a hurry to urge them to leave, but they didn’t ask much.","\"Okay, we’ll wait for Master outside the city gate tomorrow.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded with a \"hmm\", and with lightness skill he jumped up and disappeared from their sight quickly.","In the inn.","He Zhiran thought that it was Nan Rui's men who had appeared, so Mo Jiuye chased them.","Seeing that he had been gone for so long without returning, He Zhiran was worried that he might be in danger, so she decided to go out and look for him.","Just as she pushed open the door, she bumped into Mo Jiuye who was rushing back.","Mo Jiuye instinctively put his arms around the person and said gently, \"Be careful.\"","He Zhiran dragged him into the room.","\"Where have you been? Was it Nan Rui who sent someone?\"","Mo Jiuye pressed He Zhiran onto a chair and stroked her head casually.","\"No, it was our own people ...\"","Next, Mo Jiuye told He Zhiran all the details about Liang Hao and the others appearing in Xiangyang County.","After listening, He Zhiran had the same questions in her mind as Mo Jiuye.","Unfortunately, when she had read history books before, she did not find more records about other people in the Mo family.","Especially after Mo Jiuye died on the way to exile, the history books did not mention anything related to the Mo family.","Therefore, she could not determine the real reason why Mo Chuhan's tomb was dug up.","Although this matter was puzzling, they both knew that there was nothing they could do about it at the moment.","As Mo Jiuye had thought, after arriving in the northwest, they could make a trip to the frontier after settling their family.","After talking for a while, the two went back to bed.","Early the next morning, He Zhiran went out with the officials to purchase supplies.","To guard against Nan Rui sending assassins, Mo Jiuye took the initiative to stay behind this time to protect the safety of the family, with only He Zhiran going out alone.","When they arrived at the market, the officials took the initiative to separate from He Zhiran.","He Zhiran felt it was still more cost-effective to buy supplies on Taobao, and she only went out with the officials this time to cover people’s eyes and ears.","Therefore, she led the mule cart directly to a deserted place and bought the corresponding supplies on Taobao.","Feeling it was about time, she led the mule cart to meet up with the officials."]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121: Meet Sister Phil","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye was in a hurry on the road. Seeing them come back, he prepared to set off again.","After leaving the city gate, He Zhiran saw the five tall figures standing by the roadside from afar.","Liang Hao and the others had already changed into ordinary people's outfits. Seeing Mo Jiuye, they nodded to him.","Then they pretended to be passersby and followed the exile team from afar.","The team kept walking along the official road. When they passed a village, suddenly a person rushed out from the roadside, stumbling towards the team.","The person was an old woman, holding a package in her arms. Seeing people coming, she shouted loudly: \"Help...robbery!\"","Peng Wang saw this and waved to signal the team to stop, then looked towards the old woman.","The old woman had white hair. Her silk clothes could no longer be seen the original color, and her eyes were full of panic.","At the same time, several burly men chased her from behind.","Seeing the people chasing her getting closer and closer, Fe Mama was so scared that she hurried to hide behind Peng Wang.","\"I can give you silver, please save me.\"","Peng Wang didn't intend to meddle at first. Hearing that he could get silver by saving people, he was moved.","So, when those burly men were about to get close to the old woman, he stopped them with his men.","\"Broad daylight, are you tired of living? How dare you commit robbery!\"","Those burly men looked sly. It was obvious they were not good people.","If they met ordinary passersby, they could easily scare people off and no one would dare to meddle.","But the people in front of them were different. They were all dressed as officers, which made the burly men instinctively deterred.","However, thinking of the package held by the old woman, they were still reluctant to leave just like that.","The leader of the burly men grinned, revealing a mouthful of yellow teeth.","\"My Lord, this old woman is a servant of my family who took away the family property and wanted to escape. We are here to retrieve what belongs to our family.\"","Before his voice fell, the old woman retorted: \"My Lord, don't listen to his nonsense. I don't know him at all. How could I have taken away their family property?","Besides, look at his outfit. Does he look like someone from a rich family? His family couldn't even afford servants.\"","While the old woman was talking, the gossipy He Zhiran also pulled Mo Jiuye over to watch the excitement.","Unexpectedly, Mo Jiuye recognized the old woman at first glance.","Considering there were many onlookers here, he did not call out her name.","Having met an acquaintance, he would certainly not stand idly by, especially since this person had a special identity.","Therefore, before Peng Wang could speak, Mo Jiuye went to the burly men and said, \"I advise you to give up your wicked ideas. Go back where you came from, lest you suffer.\"","Hearing the familiar voice, Fe Mama grabbed the package tighter, intending to slip away.","He Zhiran also noticed Mo Jiuye's abnormal behavior. He was not the kind of person who liked to meddle. There must be hidden reasons why he stood up for the old woman.","Therefore, after Mo Jiuye left, she kept an eye on the old woman.","Seeing her attempt to sneak away, He Zhiran stepped forward to stop her and whispered:","\"You can't leave yet.\"","Through the previous voice, Fe Mama confirmed that the one who helped her was Mo Jiuye. She suddenly felt guilty and wanted to take the chance to escape from here.","Unexpectedly, she was stopped by a beautiful woman she didn't know.","In this situation, she couldn’t get away anyway.","Fe Mama had to stand in her original position.","He Zhiran's eyes were still staring at her to prevent her from escaping.","On Mo Jiuye's side, as soon as his words fell, Peng Wang and several officers cooperated to reveal their whips.","Seeing this, the burly men turned around and fled.","Mo Jiuye saw the men run away. He turned around and said to Peng Wang: \"Brother Peng, this old lady is an acquaintance of mine. I want to have a private chat with her.\"","Peng Wang did not doubt him. Judging by Mo Jiuye's meddling attitude just now, he guessed what's going on.","\"Okay, chat while walking.\"","Mo Jiuye thanked Peng Wang and took Fe Mama with He Zhiran to one side of the team.","Fe Mama had evasive eyes and dared not look Mo Jiuye straight in the eye.","Not until they were some distance away from the exile team did Mo Jiuye ask, \"Why did Fe Mama appear here?\"","Fe Mama tried her best to control her emotions and lowered her head: \"The gentleman must have recognized the wrong person. I am not Fe Mama.\"","How could Mo Jiuye possibly mistaken her? He often saw this Fe Mama when he was a child.","\"Does Fe Mama have any difficulties to tell?\"","Fe Mama was still pretending: \"The old woman thanks the gentleman for saving her life. You really have recognized the wrong person.\"","As she spoke, she opened the package in her arms and took out some women's jewelry to offer up.","\"The old woman appreciates the gentleman's lifesaving grace. Take these as thanks. I still have urgent matters and will not disturb you.\"","After speaking, Fe Mama turned to leave.","Still, it was He Zhiran who blocked her way first.","Fe Mama knew clearly that she probably couldn't gloss over it today. She had to turn around and face Mo Jiuye, no longer disguising herself.","\"My Lord, this old slave escaped from the palace. It’s shameful for you to see me like this.\"","Mo Jiuye had always had a good impression on Concubine Yuan's palace servants, especially Concubine Yuan's two personal maidservants, who treated him no differently than Nan Qi.","What he thought now was that since Fe Mama said she escaped from the palace, it meant something must have happened to Concubine Yuan.","And this matter must be related to Nan Qi.","Therefore, no matter what today, he had to get to the bottom of it.","In order not to stray too far from the main group, Mo Jiuye took Fe Mama to walk while asking questions.","\"Fe Mama, did the Concubine run into difficulties?\"","On her way out of the palace, Fe Mama encountered countless difficulties and dangers, almost losing her life.","She even thought several times that the secrets she knew might be buried with her in the soil after her death.","Meeting Mo Jiuye now, Fe Mama seemed to see a glimmer of hope to survive. She gritted her teeth and decided to tell Mo Jiuye what she knew.","That way, even if she entered the ground, she would have no regrets.","Before revealing the secret in her heart, Fe Mama glanced at He Zhiran unconsciously.","Mo Jiuye explained: \"Don't worry Fe Mama, my wife is one of us.\"","Fe Mama looked He Zhiran up and down and then said,","\"The old slave did something wrong back then, and now I'm suffering the consequences.\"","Hearing this, the first thing Mo Jiuye thought of was Nan Qi being switched at childbirth.","\"Does what Fe Mama said have to do with Prince Qi?\"","Fe Mama was shocked.","\"Does My Lord know about this?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't intend to hide it either.","\"Nan Qi once sent someone to assassinate me. Later, when I was in Pingyuan County, he took the initiative to ask me to meet at a restaurant and poisoned the wine...\""]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122: Concubine Yuan's Own Son","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Fe Mama felt increasingly ashamed.","\"This is all my fault, this old servant's mistake.\"","After a pause, Fe Mama continued: \"In fact, Prince Qi is not Concubine Yuan's biological son, but my useless nephew.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's eyes widened at the same time.","This news was too shocking for them, and for a time they still had some trouble digesting it.","However, soon, the two's minds became clear, and the first thing they thought of was that the real Third Prince was likely Fei Nanyu.","Of course, this was just their guess, and they still had to listen to Fe Mama’s explanation for the specifics.","Fe Mama sighed, and continued: \"Twenty-one years ago, a master told Concubine Yuan that the child in her belly was a girl.","In order to consolidate her position, Concubine Yuan came up with the idea of ​​switching the baby. At that time, she ordered people to secretly find many pregnant women whose expected delivery times were close to hers.","She was thinking that when her little princess was born in her belly, she would find a family who had given birth to a boy and switch their babies.","Who knew that Concubine Yuan ended up having a premature birth due to some unexpected accidents, and those pregnant women who had been prepared in advance did not come in handy.","Coincidentally, on that day I received news that the Old Duke’s wife had given birth to a baby boy early in the morning, who is now you, Duke.","In a hurry, Concubine Yuan turned her attention to the Mo Family.","At that time, along with Xu Lady, I bribed the midwife who was helping Concubine Yuan give birth, and told her not to announce the good news after the Empress gave birth, but to hand the child directly to us.","Then I took the newborn young master and sneaked out of the palace with others, intending to go to the Mo Residence to switch the babies.\"","Speaking up to now, Fe Mama looked increasingly uneasy.","\"It was all because of my selfishness that I had crooked thoughts. I thought that my sister-in-law had just given birth to a boy the day before, so I could let my nephew become a prince and enjoy wealth and prosperity. I could also live up to the expectations of my Fe ancestors.","So after leaving the imperial palace, I sent those guards away and told them that I had my own way to get a baby from the Mo’s.","Perhaps those guards thought that with the tight security at the Mo Residence, it would be difficult to succeed, so when they heard me say that, they were relieved instead.","After the guards left, I took the young master back home. After explaining the situation to my brother and sister-in-law, I left the young master there and took away my nephew, who is now Prince Qi.","When I returned to Concubine Yuan's palace, I did not tell her the truth. She only thought that I had brought back a baby from the Mo’s.","After everything was properly arranged, I sent someone to inform His Majesty the Emperor that Concubine Yuan had given birth to a little prince.","Upon receiving the news, the Emperor came over immediately with the Empress and Grand Empress to see the little prince.","Concubine Yuan ordered me and Xu Lady to silence the midwife. Just as we covered her head with white silk, she laughed loudly and told us that what Concubine Yuan had given birth to was originally a little prince, and we were foolish to take such risks.","I thought the midwife was just saying that to taunt us, but to verify the truth of her words, I found an excuse to go back home the next day.","When I saw the baby in my sister-in-law's arms, I could completely confirm that what the midwife said was true - Concubine Yuan did indeed give birth to a little prince.","In order to make up for my guilt, I suggested that my brother give the Third Prince a name with the character “Nan”. My brother considered that the surname “Nan” was too alarming to others, so he replaced “Nan” with the homophone “Nanyu”, finally naming him “Fei Nanyu”.","Only me and my brother and sister-in-law know about this. We also discussed that we would not mention it to anyone in the future.","After finding out the truth, in order not to bring disaster upon myself, I hurriedly asked my brother and sister-in-law to take away the real Third Prince overnight. There has been no news until now.","Concubine Yuan later learned that the Ninth Young Master of the Mo Family was still a boy, so she knew that she had been deceived by that master.","However, the Emperor and others had already seen the Third Prince’s appearance with their own eyes, so at that point, it was impossible to switch him back.","Concubine Yuan has always believed that you are her biological son. The Duke must also be clear that Concubine Yuan's attitude towards you is particularly different.\"","What Fe Mama recounted was something that He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had never imagined before.","Now, in the light of the truth, Fei Nanyu was the real Third Prince, Concubine Yuan's biological son.","So a new question came again.","\"How did Nan Qi get to know about this?\" Mo Jiuye asked.","Since Fe Mama had revealed such a big secret, she had no intention of concealing anything else.","\"Earlier this year, when Concubine Yuan heard that the Duke had returned triumphantly, she called me and Xu Lady to discuss what excuses could be used to summon you into the palace to meet. It was then that our conversation was overheard by Prince Qi, who had come to pay his respects.","He threatened Concubine Yuan not to reveal a single word of this matter, otherwise even if he died, he would pull down Concubine Yuan's maternal clan with him as a cushion underneath.","What's worse is that Prince Qi took Xu Lady away for severe interrogation a few days later. Fortunately I came back late from going out of the palace to run errands that day, otherwise when I heard Xu Lady had been taken away by Prince Qi's people, I would have had a bad premonition right away.","So I packed some valuables and fled the imperial palace overnight.","For more than half a year after that, I was always on the run, evading pursuit by Prince Qi's men. It took a great effort for me to escape here, but I met those local ruffians who wanted to rob my belongings. \"","Speaking to here, Fe Mama was still a little scared in retrospect.","\"If the Duke hadn't saved me today, I'm afraid I would have lost my life to those people.\"","Regarding Fe Mama's deception and concealment, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran felt no sympathy for her at all.","However, they knew Fe Mama must stay alive.","Only with her alive would there be a day when Prince Qi’s identity could be exposed.","Now they were on the way to exile and could not take Fe Mama with them. Once discovered by Prince Qi's people, it would become a disaster.","They were not afraid of Nan Qi, but who wouldn’t want peaceful days?","Especially now that the Mo Family had nothing to do with the mountains and rivers of Da Shun, Mo Jiuye did not want to wade into these muddy waters.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye felt that the person who most wanted Fe Mama to survive was Fei Nanyu.","In that case, why not do him a favor?","Fe Mama would surely survive once she was in Fei Nanyu’s hands.","\"Fe Mama, do you want to see Fei Nanyu?\"","Fe Mama's eyes widened, and she asked uncertainly, \"Does the Duke know Nanyu?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. If I'm not mistaken, he should be in the Capital city now.","Then he saw Fe Mama solemnly kneel down before Mo Jiuye.","\"This old servant has told the Duke everything she knows. I trust the Duke's character not to spread this matter out, and since you know the whereabouts of the real Third Prince, this old servant intends to find him and make things clear.\"","After speaking, Fe Mama got up and was about to leave.","Mo Jiuye stopped her and said, \"Wait, it's not safe for you to go back to the capital alone. I can send people to escort you.\""]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: I'll try to kill him Tonight.","paragraphs":["Fe Mama was naturally willing to be escorted since someone offered. She had been on the run escaping pursuers ever since she fled from the Imperial Palace. If it hadn't been for her good fortune, her old bones would have long been done for.","\"Then I'll have to thank Sir Duke,\" said Fe Mama.","Mo Jiuye didn't have the mind to correct how Fe Mama addressed him. After all, they wouldn't have another chance to meet again in the future.","He made a gesture with his eyes towards Liang Hao and the others in the distance.","Liang Hao understood and quickly led his men over towards Mo Jiuye’s direction.","Mo Jiuye also deliberately slowed his pace to leave some distance between them and the exile convoy.","He Zhiran kept a close eye on the He family's movements all along.","Among the entire exile convoy right now, only the He family didn't get along well with the Mo family. Even though their conversation with Fe Mama was already far away from the convoy, they still had to be wary.","Just in case He Zhiyuan happened to overhear something and leaked word out about what would happen later, that would invite unnecessary trouble.","Sure enough, that evildoer He Zhiyuan kept sneaking glances back in their direction every so often.","Even knowing he wouldn't be able to obtain any news, it was still annoying.","It seemed that He Zhiyuan was not someone who could be left alive, or they had to find some other method to make him unable to speak nonsense to outsiders.","Just as He Zhiran was thinking about how to get He Zhiyuan to shut his mouth, Liang Hao and the others had already approached them.","The men bowed with clasped hands to Mo Jiuye, calling out “Ninth Master”, then stood there in an orderly manner awaiting orders.","Mo Jiuye pointed at Fe Mama and said, “This is Empress Yuan's personal maid. Some matters led her to be pursued for assassination by Nan Qi. I want to send two of your men to escort her back to the capital.”","“No problem. I’m willing to go,” Song Chao and Wang Dali said at once.","After all, there were many eyes here. Mo Jiuye also didn’t want Fe Mama to linger too long.","This was his first time asking He Zhiran for silver.","“I want them to carry some silver for traveling expenses along the road.”","He Zhiran didn't have a stingy personality to begin with. Moreover, half of the silver from the royal treasury was due to Mo Jiuye's contributions. Naturally he had the authority to allocate it.","Without a second word, He Zhiran fished out 200 silver bills from his interspatial ring through his sleeve to hand over to Song Chao.","“Use this on your journey. Also, buy a pack animal cart to make traveling more convenient.”","Song Chao returned the silver bills back.","“Master Ninth, we already carried silver when we left the border.”","Fe Mama also looked towards Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","“There are some valuables in this old servant's bundle that are enough for travel expenses to the capital. It’s reassuring for you to have some silver in this special situation.”","Seeing that they had rejected his offered silver, Mo Jiuye simply had He Zhiran put it away since they were currently exiled and stripped of their estates by His Majesty. Too high of a profile would easily attract others' speculation.","“Since this is the case, be careful on your journey.”","Glancing at Fe Mama’s head full of conspicuous white hair, it was far too eye-catching.","The assassins sent by Nan Qi to kill would definitely use her standout white hair as the first sign to identify their target.","For safety reasons, He Zhiran didn't have Fe Mama leave immediately.","Instead, she bought a hair dye product called “Wash Black” at Taobao Mall. This stuff could instantly turn hair black by simply washing it.","She took the “Wash Black” from her interspatial ring and exchanged it for a small porcelain bottle to give Fe Mama.","“Mama can use this to wash her hair. It will quickly become black. At that time, change your outfit again. It will definitely be much safer.”","Fe Mama accepted the little porcelain bottle gratefully and gave sincere thanks.","“Thank you, Madam. This old servant was worried this entire way about my conspicuous white hair. With this, I’m much safer now.”","After finishing the arrangements, Mo Jiuye glanced at the skies.","“It's getting late now. You should set off early.”","Song Chao and Wang Dali received their orders and escorted Fe Mama away.","Liang Hao led the other two men to continue keeping their distance from the convoy.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran quickened their pace, intending to catch up with the exile convoy faster.","On the way, He Zhiran said softly, “I just discovered He Zhiyuan staring in this direction.”","Mo Jiuye’s gaze darkened. “I was thinking that since he told me about Nan Rui’s matters, I would spare his life. Looks like this man really can’t remain alive.”","Seeing that he was thinking the same as her, He Zhiran asked, “How do you plan to do it?”","Mo Jiuye made a throat slitting gesture. “I’ll take his life tonight.”","Hearing Mo Jiuye speak this way, He Zhiran instinctively glanced towards Peng Wang’s direction.","“Doing this, wouldn’t it cause trouble for Big Brother Peng?”","This entire journey, Peng Wang had treated them fairly well. If they brought trouble to someone for their own selfish desires, it would be somewhat unjustifiable.","Mo Jiuye raised his brows. “Do you have a better way?”","He Zhiran nodded. “Remember that silver hoop snake that bit Big Brother Peng when we first left the capital?”","“I remember.” Mo Jiuye replied.","He Zhiran continued, “Not long ago when I was free, I extracted the silver hoop snake venom and created two poisons. One is called ‘Dazed’, this drug can temporarily numb one’s senses. With just adding a few other things inside, after ingesting it one would become a fool for the rest of their life like the Sun boy.”","Mo Jiuye’s eyes lit up. “Since that’s the case, I’ll make my move tonight.”","As they spoke, they had already caught up with the exile convoy. Both tacitly stopped mentioning the matter further.","That night’s resting spot was at the foot of a mountain. As always, after finishing dinner everyone squeezed into their tents early to rest.","He Zhiran thought of Liang Hao and the others. Although they still had some distance from the convoy, they also had to camp outside similarly.","She said to Mo Jiuye, “Why don’t I help them buy a tent in my interspatial space, using the excuse it was purchased from Foreigners as well?”","Mo Jiuye hadn’t ignored the issue of Liang Hao and the others resting outdoors either.","He just didn't have any good solutions in mind regarding it so far.","“That’s a good idea. Leave the tent’s origins to me to handle.”","Obtaining Mo Jiuye’s approval, He Zhiran quickly picked out a tent with an exterior resembling those used anciently for marching battles inside Taobao Mall.","Other than a smaller capacity compared to ancient military campaign tents, the biggest characteristic was its simple operation.","Mo Jiuye gave the tent a look then took advantage of the nighttime when others couldn't see to deliver it to Liang Hao’s group.","When he returned, he deliberately observed where the He family members were resting.","Most had already fallen asleep. Only He Zhiyuan sat under a tree, head lowered doing something.","Mo Jiuye stealthily leapt onto the big tree and looked down by the moonlight. He saw He Zhiyuan tearing off a corner of his own lapel. Then he bit open his finger and wrote something on it.","Mo Jiuye’s dark eyes narrowed slightly. He stared hard trying to see He Zhiyuan’s actions clearer by the moonlight.","But the dim lighting and distance made him completely unable to discern what was written.","Even so, Mo Jiuye didn’t immediately go stop him. He wanted to see if the finished content He Zhiyuan wrote out was truly related to the incident of running into Fe Mama today."]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: He Zhiyuan is Dead","paragraphs":["After about the time it takes to burn a stick of incense, He Zhiyuan finally stopped moving.","He licked the blood on his fingers, then carefully folded the piece of clothes and tucked it into his bosom.","Mo Jiuye looked around and saw that everyone else was resting. The two officers in charge of keeping watch were dozing off.","He quickly leapt down from the tree, chopped He Zhiyuan unconscious with a knifehand strike, grabbed him by the collar and swiftly disappeared from the spot.","After running for some distance, Mo Jiuye tossed He Zhiyuan onto the ground and took the piece of clothing from his embrace at the same time.","He lit a pile of hay with a firesteel and by the firelight, the words written in blood on the clothes were clearly visible.","The content was indeed as he and He Zhiran had expected.","It was nothing more than saying that he had discovered Mo Jiuye's abnormal behavior today, and had rescued an old woman who seemed familiar. The old woman did not look like an ordinary person.","If Prince Rui wanted to know more, he should rescue him from water and fire as soon as possible...","After reading the blood letter, Mo Jiuye decisively threw it into the fire to burn it up.","He had originally wanted to spare He Zhiyuan's life, but he was so ungrateful instead.","For his own selfish desires, he even wanted to sell him out.","Fortunately, he and He Zhiran were vigilant and had noticed something amiss early on, otherwise if this blood letter had reached Nan Rui’s hands, it would have been big trouble again.","Thinking of this, he might as well not use the poison He Zhiran gave him. Mo Jiuye directly drew his blade and took He Zhiyuan's life.","After doing all this, Mo Jiuye stealthily returned He Zhiyuan’s corpse to its original place.","In order not to arouse suspicion, he carefully went back and cleaned up the blood stains on the ground before returning to the tent.","The next morning at daybreak, a woman’s tragic wails rang out from the camp.","\"Officer, my master is dead...\"","The officer came over to take a look very impatiently and found that He Zhiyuan was indeed dead. He hurriedly ran to report to Peng Wang.","After looking at He Zhiyuan’s corpse, Peng Wang turned his head and glanced in the direction of Mo’s family.","He waved his hand at several officers: \"The man is dead, bury him!\"","He’s family disagreed and gathered around Peng Wang.","\"Officer, my master was obviously stabbed to death. He can't just be buried without knowing why!\"","Peng Wang looked coldly at He’s several women: \"According to what you mean, you expect me, an escort officer for exiles, to find out the murderer?\"","Speaking of the murderer, the first person Peng Wang thought of was Mo Jiuye.","Apart from Mo Jiuye, he couldn't think of anyone else who would make a move against He Zhiyuan.","However, this was just his guess and he could not completely determine that it was Mo Jiuye who did it.","Moreover, even if Mo Jiuye did it, he would not say it out...","Peng Wang just cursed inwardly: This guy, only knows how to stir up trouble for himself!","Seeing that Peng Wang was glowering, He’s family did not dare say anything more about justice for He Zhiyuan. They could only watch as the officers carried away his corpse.","With He Zhiyuan dead, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were no longer worried about the incident with Fe Mama being exposed.","Right now, the only thing they needed to guard against was Nan Rui’s assassination attempts.","However, the convoy had traveled smoothly for ten days and Nan Rui still did not show any movement.","Even so, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran did not dare to be careless in the slightest.","It was already September, and the temperature difference between day and night was gradually increasing.","Especially at midnight, even under cotton quilts in the tent, one did not feel very warm.","In the morning when He Zhiran was folding quilts in the tent, she suddenly sensed Mo Jiuye’s figure flash by the tent entrance as he quickly disappeared on the spot.","He Zhiran stopped minding her business at hand and rushed out swiftly.","She saw that Mo Jiuye had casually grabbed a ladle to block a few feathered arrows that were shot towards them.","Without hesitation, He Zhiran immediately took out a Swiss army knife from her space and threw it towards Mo Jiuye.","\"Catch it.\"","Mo Jiuye steadily caught the army knife and continued to block the arrows.","He Zhiran quickly hid behind a big tree and looked in the direction where the arrows were coming from.","She saw that in a slightly concealed place ahead, a few men in black were shooting arrows at Mo Jiuye.","Seeing that those people kept aiming at Mo Jiuye alone, He Zhiran quickly climbed up the tree, took out her sleeve arrows, and shot them at those men.","At the same time, the officers and other prisoners also noticed something wrong here.","The sisters-in-law had already warily grasped their mini pistols. If not for Jiu Ge and Jiu Mei telling them not to let these things see the light unless absolutely necessary, they would have already fired projectiles in the direction where the arrows came from...","Peng Wang’s side also shouted loudly that there were assassins and everyone should be careful.","Encountering such a situation, the first thing Peng Wang thought of was the two brothers who had died recently at Niujiao Mountain.","They couldn’t afford to have another accident happen after two officers had died.","The Fang’s and Xie’s men also found some things that could be used as weapons, intending to come over to help.","But the attackers only targeted Mo Jiuye alone, and they were also keeping their distance. The ‘weapons’ like ladles and bricks in these people’s hands were simply useless.","Liang Hao on his side also noticed something wrong. He came over with Xu Qingfeng and Li Mingrui to protect Mo Jiuye.","On the tree, He Zhiran had already shot three men in black dead with her sleeve arrows.","However, the number of men in black was replenished instantly.","This tactic was completely different from the people Nan Heng had previously sent. They did not even show their faces at all, always hiding from afar to shoot sneak arrows.","Not until Liang Hao and the other two joined in and continuously shot down many men in black with the bows on their backs did they change their tactics.","Seeing too many losses on their side, the men in black no longer shot arrows. Wielding sabers, they charged straight at Mo Jiuye to attack.","Seeing the large number of men in black, Mo Jiuye was worried that it would implicate his family, so he utilized lightness skill to run towards the distance.","The men in black chased relentlessly.","He Zhiran still followed behind, shooting arrows at the men in black.","Those men in black ignored the people behind them. They even automatically ignored He Zhiran’s attacks, only intent on taking Mo Jiuye’s life.","After running out several hundred meters in one breath, Mo Jiuye stopped. He raised his army knife to fight with the men in black.","Liang Hao and the others arrived right after Mo Jiuye. They quickly joined the melee.","When He Zhiran caught up, those men in black had been killed off a number already by them. At present, she estimated there were still twenty to thirty people left.","She saw that Mo Jiuye and the others were not struggling too much against them. He Zhiran then continued shooting arrows at the men in black from behind.","The remaining dozen men in black saw that things were not going well. They feigned a few moves and then fled towards one direction.","Liang Hao brought Xu Qingfeng and Li Mingrui to quickly chase.","Only one person still relentlessly unleashed moves at Mo Jiuye. From the looks of their fight, Mo Jiuye was already at a slight disadvantage.","He Zhiran hurriedly aimed her crossbow arrow at the back of that man in black’s head, preparing for a fatal blow.","Seeing her posture, Mo Jiuye shouted loudly: \"Don’t hurt him!\""]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: Puppets","paragraphs":["He Zhiran did not know the reason why Mo Jiuye stopped her from taking action, but she obediently did not move.","Mo Jiuye naturally wanted to keep that man in black alive.","She could also see that Mo Jiuye had been evading all along. Even though the other side's moves were lethal, he had no intention of fighting back.","In order not to put Mo Jiuye in danger, she decisively switched her crossbow arrow to a tranquilizer gun.","She aimed at the left shoulder of the man in black and fired with a \"bang\". The man in black swayed and fell backward.","Mo Jiuye dashed forward in a flash, grabbed the arms of the man in black, gently put him on the ground, and at the same time, reached out to uncover his mask.","Seeing this familiar face, the eyes of this strapping man began to well up.","\"Eighth Brother, it really is you, you are still alive...\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran hurriedly walked over, her eyes full of incredulity.","\"This person is your eighth brother?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded with difficulty: \"When I fought with him just now, I realized that his moves seemed familiar. So while fighting, I tried to probe, and I can completely confirm that the martial arts he used came from the Mo Family.","I don't know why, when I asked who he was, it was as if he didn't hear me at all. He kept attacking me like a puppet without any reaction.\"","Hearing this, He Zhiran reached out and took Mo Chuhan's pulse. Her frown grew tighter and tighter.","Mo Jiuye stared closely at He Zhiran's expression.","\"What exactly happened to Eighth Brother?\"","He Zhiran slowly stood up: \"His pulse is very strange. I can't determine the specifics now. I need to take him into the space and use those medical devices to check before I know more.\"","Mo Jiuye looked deeply into He Zhiran's eyes, his tone pleading,","\"I beg you, you must save Eighth Brother. Eighth Brother is upright and will not reveal the secrets of your space.\"","He Zhiran was not worried that the space would be exposed at all.","When she diagnosed Mo Chuhan's pulse just now, she could roughly determine one thing - this person should have lost his self-awareness.","Besides, she could completely use some drugs to control Mo Chuhan and prevent him from regaining consciousness before leaving the space.","\"That's no problem. As long as you want, I can take him into the space to check at any time.\" As she spoke, with a wave of He Zhiran's hand, Mo Chuhan instantly disappeared on the spot.","At this time, Liang Hao and the others had also returned. Seeing the corpses of the men in black on the ground, they knew Mo Jiuye was no longer in danger here.","\"Ninth Master, none of those men were kept alive.\"","\"Um, thanks for your hard work.\" Mo Jiyue just absentmindedly responded. Then he pulled He Zhiran toward the team.","Liang Hao and the others tactfully returned to their original positions.","The Mo Family women were worried about He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye's safety, and they still remained in position gripping their guns. They came over to greet them.","Seeing both of them return safely, they let out of sigh of relief.","The second sister-in-law angrily scolded: \"I really don't know what these people want to do. Our Mo Family has already declined to the point of exile, yet they still want to kill us.\"","This time, the other sister-in-laws didn't remain silent as usual. Following the second sister-in-law's words, they continued to curse those who wanted to harm Mo Jiuye.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye knew the sister-in-laws were upset in their hearts and did not stop their behavior.","On their way back, they had already discussed that He Zhiran would pretend to sprain her ankle, then use it as an excuse to ride in the mule cart, so she would have a chance to enter the space and help treat Mo Chuhan.","So after walking out several meters away, He Zhiran deliberately stepped on a rock.","\"Ow...\"","Mo Jiuye rushed forward to support her. \"What's wrong?\"","\"I sprained my ankle a little.\"","Just as the sister-in-laws were about to come over to show concern, Mo Jiuye suddenly picked He Zhiran up in his arms.","\"Go back and tell Peng Wang that you will ride in the mule cart to travel today.\"","Mo Jiuye strode away quickly, soon leaving the sister-in-laws behind.","Back at the camp, after Mo Jiuye explained the situation to Peng Wang, he carried He Zhiran onto the mule cart.","Peng Wang came over again to inquire about the situation. Knowing the matter was resolved, he began to arrange the journey to continue.","After He Zhiran entered the compartment, she immediately flashed into the space.","Even though Mo Jiuye was anxious about Eighth Brother's condition, he couldn't follow He Zhiran into the space. His current task was to drive the mule cart.","Upon entering the space, He Zhiran gave Mo Chuhan a full examination.","The result shocked her tremendously.","Mo Chuhan's condition was actually caused by Gu poison!","This was no trivial matter. She immediately came out of the space and told Mo Jiuye about the diagnosis results of Mo Chuhan.","Mo Jiuye was equally surprised. He had also heard about Gu poison, but it was rarely seen in the Da Shun Dynasty, so he had only heard about it and never seen it with his own eyes.","He couldn't figure out why Eighth Brother was poisoned by Gu.","\"Can you determine what kind of Gu poison is in his body?\"","In her previous life, He Zhiran had read some books about Gu poison in the Miao areas. Based on the scan just now, she could roughly make out the shape of the Gu worm.","\"According to Eighth Brother's symptoms and the shape of the Gu worm, I can preliminarily determine that he is infected with Puppet Gu.\"","\"Puppet Gu?\"","He Zhiran nodded, \"Yes, this is my initial judgment. To truly confirm it, I want to buy a related book for reference.\"","After speaking, she used her mind to purchase a book called The Compendium of Gu Poison.","The mule cart that Mo Jiuye was driving moved at the same speed as the rest of the team on foot. He Zhiran simply sat on the edge of the cart compartment, holding the book for Mo Jiuye to look over together.","Considering that Mo Jiuye couldn't recognize simplified Chinese characters, after flipping to the page describing Puppet Gu, He Zhiran read it out softly for him to listen, while taking out the images from the space scan of Mo Chuhan earlier for comparison.","Sure enough, the Gu worm in the images completely matched the picture in the book.","The book also introduced that Puppet Gu survives in the host's body at the axillary artery of the arm, relying on the host's blood to sustain its life.","There is one mother Gu worm and multiple child Gu worms.","There is only one mother Gu worm, held in the hands of the controller. The number of child Gu worms is unlimited. The one who carries the child Gu in the body loses autonomous consciousness, with all behaviors determined by the mother Gu controller.","Moreover, the controller obtains the survival status of the child Gu carrier based on the condition of the mother Gu in hand.","That is to say, once the child Gu carrier dies, the mother Gu will instinctively summon the child Gu back.","Mo Jiuye frowned.","\"As far as I know, Gu breeders are all in the southern border areas. To remove Eighth Brother's Gu worm, we still have to find a way when we go there.\"","He had already decided that as long as He Zhiran could preserve Eighth Brother's life for now, after arriving in the northwest as free people, he would immediately set off for the southern border with Eighth Brother to remove his Gu poison.","He Zhiran smiled faintly, \"Why haven't you asked if I can remove the Gu poison?\"","He was very clear about He Zhiran's superb medical skills. But after all, what was in Eighth Brother was a Gu worm, and there was no one in the entire Da Shun Dynasty who knew Gu techniques. Mo Jiuye hadn't thought of her at all.","Hearing this, he raised his eyebrows, somewhat uncertain as he asked, \"You can remove Gu poison?\"","He Zhiran nodded, \"I should be able to, but I need your cooperation.\"","\"That's no problem. If Eighth Brother has no major issues with his body, let's go into your space together tonight to operate.\""]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: Solution to Poison","paragraphs":["When He Zhiran heard that she could remove the gu worms from Mo Chuhan's body, Mo Jiuye was overjoyed, eagerly wishing it could be nightfall soon so he could treat Eighth Brother sooner.","To be safe, He Zhiran returned to her space and injected Mo Chuhan with a tranquilizer to keep him asleep for now.","Finally, after everyone else had returned to their tents to rest for the night, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye impatiently entered her space.","Mo Chuhan was still fast asleep.","Using her mind, He Zhiran sent him to the operating room.","When Mo Jiuye heard she was going to perform surgery to remove the gu worms from Eighth Brother, the first thing that came to mind was that Eighth Brother might also be stripped naked like he had been.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye hurriedly pushed He Zhiran towards the exit of the operating room.","\"I'll take off Eighth Brother's clothes. Call me when you're ready.\"","He Zhiran frowned.","\"The gu worm is in his arm. He doesn't need to be fully undressed.\"","Mo Jiuye suddenly realized his mistake and didn't continue pushing her out.","However, he still took the initiative to remove Mo Chuhan's shirt himself.","Seeing how emaciated Eighth Brother had become, nothing but skin and bones, Mo Jiuye felt a stabbing pain in his heart.","Eighth Brother was the strongest martial artist in the family and had also been the burliest. Who knows what he had experienced over these years to become so wasted away.","There was no time to think more about it. Removing the gu worm was most urgent.","After taking off Mo Chuhan's shirt, Mo Jiuye voluntarily stood in a corner out of the way.","Seeing Mo Jiuye dumbly standing in the corner, He Zhiran called him over to put on sterile surgical gowns together. She then handed him a sealed glass bottle.","\"Hold this tightly. As soon as the gu worm pokes its head out, quickly capture it in here. Don't let it get away.\"","Mo Jiuye took the glass bottle solemnly and nodded.","To prevent Mo Chuhan from waking due to pain, He Zhiran first administered some local anesthetic.","She then prepared a tray of surgical instruments at her side and began operating in earnest.","Mo Jiuye watched as a silver scalpel sliced open Eighth Brother's arm, blood flowing from the incision.","He Zhiran seemed oblivious to the blood, cautiously cutting deeper to prevent killing the gu worm outright.","About five minutes later, He Zhiran spoke solemnly.","\"Get ready to catch the gu worm.\"","Mo Jiuye's senses heightened, eyes fixed unblinkingly on the incision site.","Using forceps in one hand and hemostatic forceps in the other, He Zhiran gently peeled back Mo Chuhan's skin and flesh a little.","An eight to nine millimeter long black worm then entered their line of sight.","As if sensing the surrounding danger, the puppet gu spread its wings, preparing to escape its host's body.","With quick reflexes, Mo Jiuye positioned the bottle opening in the gu worm's path, guiding it directly inside. He then sealed the cap tightly.","Their great task accomplished, He Zhiran immediately stitched up Mo Chuhan's wound.","Only then did Mo Jiuye realize this was how He Zhiran had treated his wounds previously.","While the treatment method was unfamiliar to him, he knew such treated wounds would heal several times faster than conventional methods.","After treating Mo Chuhan’s wound, He Zhiran hooked him up to an IV drip with anti-inflammatory medication.","She wiped the sweat from her brow and took off the surgical gown, then opened the TaoBaoBao shopping app intending to buy some blood plasma.","Upon opening the TaoBaoBao app on her phone, the notice she saw gave her a huge, pleasant surprise.","Sales of goods from her store today were extremely impressive, earning 10.9 million yuan.","Checking further, the big buyer was none other than the small collector who hadn’t appeared for a long time.","The small collector had also left her a message, but He Zhiran was currently busy buying blood plasma and dealing with Mo Chuhan. She decided to reply when time allowed later.","Once separated from its host, the gu larva could survive at most ten days.","In other words, if the larva could not successfully return to the mother gu within those ten days, it would certainly perish.","Her reasoning behind going through such effort to keep the larva alive was the hope that, given the opportunity, she could use this clue to find the one who had used gu worms on Mo Chuhan.","The Gu Worm Compendium stated that to enable gu larvae expelled from a human body to live for an extended period, they needed nourishment from fresh human blood.","Therefore, He Zhiran intended to feed the larva blood as soon as it left the host, to avoid any accidents.","However, Mo Jiuye didn’t understand any of this. He had assumed they would remove and burn the larva outright.","Who would have thought He Zhiran would add so much blood to the bottle?","\"What is your intention in doing so?\"","He Zhiran explained her rationale.","Hearing her explanation, Mo Jiuye sincerely gave her a big thumbs up.","\"Fortunately your thinking is meticulous. Otherwise, even if Eighth Brother knew who used the gu on him, we still might not be able to find them.\"","Mo Jiuye had heard some legends about gu raisers in southern Xinjiang.","Elusive when seen by others, they appeared as ordinary people. But reveal their true nature, they were terrifying gu raisers who struck fear by reputation alone.","After filling half the plasma bottle, He Zhiran carefully stored away the bottle containing the larva.","Pointing at the still unconscious Mo Chuhan, Mo Jiuye asked,","\"Now that the gu worm has been removed, I wonder when Eighth Brother will awaken?\"","He Zhiran glanced at the large clock on the wall then said,","\"His vitals have all stabilized. He should regain consciousness within the hour. When that IV bag finishes, we need to take him out quickly.\"","Mo Jiuye’s mood was still somewhat low, but it didn’t affect his thinking.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye remained silent for some time, He Zhiran asked,","“Are you thinking about the one behind the scenes manipulating Eighth Brother?”","Mo Jiuye nodded.","“Eighth Brother being afflicted with gu worms can’t be unrelated to the southern Xinjiang people.","While it's understandable for the southern Xinjiang people to bitterly detest the Mo Family, over the years the Mo Family’s existence has thwarted their invasion attempts on Da Shun time and time again, forcing them to retreat defeated and suffer devastating losses each time.","However, those black clothed men’s martial arts were entirely from the Central Plains, bearing no traces of the southern Xinjiang people.”","Based on this point alone, Mo Jiuye could eliminate the possibility that those people had been sent by the southern Xinjiang side.","Both of them sank into contemplative silence at the same time.","Originally, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had believed the mastermind behind the assassination attempt was Nan Rui.","But judging from Mo Chuhan’s situation, that mastermind had clearly colluded with the southern Xinjiang people.","In that case, they could no longer pinpoint Nan Rui alone as the mastermind behind the scenes.","Especially He Zhiran, with her deeper historical knowledge, many ambitious people would choose to collude with foreign enemies to expand their own power.","In short, at present the two of them could not conclusively determine the true mastermind’s identity. They could only wait for Mo Chuhan to regain consciousness and inquire further, hoping to obtain useful information from him.","Unable to find the real answer for now, they both tacitly avoided continuing the topic."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: He's been apart from his family for three years.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran looked at Mo Chuhan who was still in a coma.","\"Have you thought about how to bring Eighth Brother to meet Mother and Sisters-in-law?\"","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment. They had brought Mo Chuhan into the space early in the morning, and now it was already late into the night.","If he told the truth that Eighth Brother was one of the black-clothed assassins who had tried to kill him, it would be hard to explain everything that had happened today.","After thinking for a bit, he said: \"Let's go farther away and say that I heard some noises in the mountains and went to check it out, and that's when I ran into Eighth Brother.\"","He Zhiran nodded: \"Okay, that works too.\"","In the time they were talking, half an hour had already passed.","Mo Chuhan's IV had also finished dripping. He Zhiran brought Mo Jiuye and vanished from the space without a sound.","The two of them noiselessly left the campsite and headed towards the distance.","When they felt they were somewhat far away from the camp, Mo Jiuye stopped in his tracks.","\"Let's do it here!\"","\"Alright.\" As He Zhiran's voice fell, Mo Chuhan had already appeared on the open ground in front of the two.","Seeing that Eighth Brother still hadn't woken up, Mo Jiuye went and gathered some firewood to make a bonfire.","About twenty minutes later, Mo Chuhan's fingers twitched, then he slowly opened his eyes.","Mo Chuhan stared at Mo Jiuye in disbelief for a long time, seeming unable to believe it.","His voice was somewhat hoarse and powerless. \"Ninth younger brother?\"","Tears once again welled up in Mo Jiuye's eyes. He grabbed Mo Chuhan's hand excitedly and said emotionally, \"Eighth Brother, it's me, it's Jiuye!\"","Mo Chuhan reached out a trembling hand, trying to touch Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye moved his body closer to help prop Mo Chuhan up into a sitting position.","\"Eighth Brother, we all thought you had died. What on earth happened?\"","Mo Chuhan's lips moved, but he seemed very weak.","\"I was with Sixth and Seventh Brother resisting the invasion from the Southern Borderlands when we were lured by the enemy to a mountain valley.","Just as I was battling the enemies, there suddenly appeared a pungent smell that I accidentally inhaled through my nose and mouth.","The next time I awoke, I was chained with iron shackles to a pillar in a dark, gloomy cave.","Not long after, an old man dressed like someone from the Southern Borderlands came before me. All I saw was him scattering some powder at me. Right after that, I didn't know anything anymore.\"","When Mo Chuhan finished speaking, he tightly grasped Mo Jiuye's arm.","\"Ninth younger brother, are Sixth and Seventh Brother okay? And where are we now?\"","Mo Jiuye wiped away the tears at the corner of his eyes, then said:","\"Eighth Brother, the incident you spoke of happened three years ago. Back then, I received the news that you, Sixth Brother and Seventh Brother had all died at the hands of the Southern Borderlands troops. I didn't expect that you were actually still alive, Eighth Brother!","The Mo family manor has now been ransacked and exiled by an imperial decree accusing us of treason and colluding with the enemy. Right now we're on the road during this exile.","This morning a group of black-clothed assassins tried to kill me, and you, Eighth Brother, were one of those black-clothed men.","Although you had your face covered, I immediately recognized your martial arts techniques, so I knocked you out and hid you away.\"","As Mo Jiuye spoke, he had already pulled He Zhiran over to stand in front of Mo Chuhan.","\"Eighth Brother, this is my wife, He Zhiran, the legitimate daughter of the He Chancellor's household. Thankfully she knows medicine and helped remove your puppet worm.\"","In just those few short sentences from Mo Jiuye, Mo Chuhan received a huge amount of shocking information.","He stared fixedly at the two people dressed in coarse hemp clothing standing before him, but was unable to respond for quite some time.","After a long pause, Mo Chuhan tentatively asked:","\"Ninth younger brother, did you say it's already been three years since that battle at the Southern Borderlands?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. \"That's right Eighth Brother, it's exactly three years now.\"","Mo Chuhan continued asking: \"Then what about Sixth Brother and Seventh Brother?\" He was hoping that if he could miraculously survive, then surely Sixth and Seventh Brother could also appear alive by some miracle.","Mo Jiuye tilted his head slightly to one side, forcefully blinking his eyes several times to hold back the tears that threatened to spill out.","\"Sixth Brother and Seventh Brother both lost their lives in that battle.\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Chuhan gripped Mo Jiuye's arms tightly as tears began streaming down his face.","\"Could it be that the only Mo men remaining now are just us two brothers?\"","Mo Jiuye answered with great difficulty, \"Yes.\"","When Mo Chuhan heard the affirmative answer, his eyes seemed to be those of a trapped beast stained with blood.","He struggled to sit up straight, gripping his hair tightly with both hands and yelling out in near despair.","\"No...I can't believe all this is real!\"","Seeing his state, Mo Jiuye suppressed the heart-wrenching pain he felt to go up and comfort him.","\"Eighth Brother, it's already been so long since it happened. Now that you're still alive, it's the heavens showing great benevolence to our Mo family.\"","Witnessing this scene also brought tears flowing freely down He Zhiran's face, but her reason was still sound.","She went up to the two brothers and gently reminded:","\"Eighth Brother, Mother and Eighth Sister-in-Law are at the campsite not far away.\"","Sure enough, upon hearing He Zhiran's words, Mo Chuhan's emotions calmed down quite a bit.","He looked at Mo Jiuye with bloodshot eyes.","\"Ninth younger brother, how are Mother and your Eighth sister-in-law? Are they well?\"","Mo Jiuye carefully helped prop Mo Chuhan up to his feet.","\"They're both doing fine. And from what I can see, Eighth Sister-in-Law seems to miss you a lot.\"","A mental image of his mother's loving countenance and his wife's charming figure instantly appeared in Mo Chuhan's mind.","He had married his wife Zhao Xianglan less than a month ago when they were still passionately in love. But then he immediately received the urgent news from the border pass and set off with Mo Jiuye through the night to rush there under imperial orders.","He remembered that the last time he left home, his mother had brought all the women of the household to see them off at the front gates.","By then his mother had already lost her husband and five sons.","Even so, she still admonished him and Ninth Younger Brother: the Mo Family's men cannot be cowards!","His wife Zhao Xianglan had held onto him reluctantly, her eyes full of heartache...","Who knew that this farewell would last three whole years.","And he had actually spent those three years unconscious and muddled.","Mo Chuhan gripped Mo Jiuye's hand tightly. \"Ninth younger brother, take me to see them.\"","Seeing Mo Chuhan stumbling with each step, Mo Jiuye felt anxious.","He was thinking that Eighth Brother had only gotten his arm cut open, there's no way he could be this feeble.","So he asked He Zhiran,","\"Ranran, what exactly is going on with Eighth Brother's body?\"","\"It's normal for Eighth Brother to be weak right now after the Puppet Worm had sucked out so much of his essence and blood over the past three years. And judging by his current state, it should also be because he hasn't eaten anything for a long time.","Coincidentally, I still happen to have some food in my package, so let's first get some food into Eighth Brother's stomach.\"","He Zhiran didn't actually have any package on her. She realized that Mo Chuhan hadn't been paying much attention to her this whole time, so taking out a random package from her space wouldn't be discovered.","As she finished speaking, her consciousness entered her space. She bought a large white steamed bun from Taobao, and took out some braised beef from her fridge.","Mo Chuhan really was starving. He gave a word of thanks before accepting the food from He Zhiran's hands and started wolfing it all down.","He Zhiran also took out a water bladder.","\"Eighth Brother, since it's likely been a very long time since you've last eaten, don't eat too quickly or you'll hurt your stomach and spleen.\"","Hearing this, Mo Chuhan's face flushed red.","He had actually forgotten his younger siblings were still here.","Mo Chuhan felt a little embarrassed as he accepted the water bladder. \"Thank you for the reminder, younger sister.\""]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: Mo Chu Han, You Bastard","paragraphs":["Mo Chuhan finally felt a bit of strength after devouring a large steamed bun and a packet of sauced beef.","He quickened his pace, hoping to reunite with his family as soon as possible.","When they reached the vicinity of the camp, Mo Jiuye deliberately didn't hide from the night watchmen.","In the future, Eighth Brother would be traveling with them to the northwest, so there was no need for concealment.","As for those who wanted them dead behind their backs, they would still make their move even if Eighth Brother wasn't present.","The sound of the three people walking was not quiet. Even though the night watchmen were a bit drowsy, they could still hear the noise.","The sky was too dark, and the watchmen couldn't see the faces of the approaching individuals, only three silhouettes.","\"Who's there?\" one of the watchmen asked loudly.","\"It's us, sir,\" He Zhiran replied.","He Zhiran's position was somewhat close to where Mo's family's tent was located.","When the Mo family women heard her voice, they thought something had happened and came out of the tent one by one to check.","\"He Zhiran, what happened?\" Old Lady Mo asked anxiously.","At this moment, the watchmen also came over to investigate, asking, \"He Zhiran, why are you all not resting in the middle of the night? What are you doing out here?\"","He Zhiran didn't immediately answer the watchmen because she saw Old Lady Mo stumbling towards Mo Chuhan's direction.","Old Lady Mo rubbed her eyes vigorously and carefully examined Mo Chuhan.","\"Chuhan?\"","Mo Chuhan knelt down in front of Old Lady Mo and said, \"Mother, it's your unfilial son, Chuhan.\"","At that moment, Eighth Sister-in-law also recognized Mo Chuhan's voice and came to him, bypassing several other sisters-in-law.","\"Husband, is it really you? You're really not dead?\"","Mo Chuhan, seeing his once plump wife who had now become thin, nodded with difficulty, \"Xianglan, it's me, I'm not dead.\"","Eighth Sister-in-law burst into tears and threw herself into Mo Chuhan's arms, ignoring the gazes around them.","At the same time, her little fists continued to pound on his chest.","\"Mo Chuhan, you jerk... Why didn't you come home if you weren't dead... Sob, sob, sob...","You know what? I was mocked by my two sisters-in-law from my natal family for three whole years. They said I brought bad luck to my husband as soon as we got married...","It's all your fault... Sob, sob, sob...\"","Seeing this scene, the other sisters-in-law also shed tears, but they had the discernment not to approach.","Mo Hanyue also came to Old Lady Mo's side and looked at the person in front of her who had become unrecognizably thin.","\"Mother, is this really Eighth Brother? How did he become like this?\"","At the moment when Mo Chuhan knelt down, Old Lady Mo intended to step forward and help him up to inquire further.","However, before she could make a move, Eighth Sister-in-law threw herself at him.","As someone who had gone through the pain of separation from her spouse, she naturally understood and restrained herself from approaching.","Upon hearing her sister-in-law's words, Eighth Sister-in-law realized that she had been a bit too impulsive just now.","She quickly got up from Mo Chuhan's embrace and turned to look at Old Lady Mo.","\"Mother, I'm sorry, it was an abrupt action on my part.\"","Old Lady Mo patted her shoulder and said, \"It's alright. Nowadays, we are no longer a wealthy family where rules need to be followed at every turn. We can let go of those formalities.\"","As they spoke, Old Lady Mo had already approached Mo Chuhan and reached out to help him up.","As Old Lady Mo's hand touched Mo Chuhan's arm, the tears she had just suppressed once again flowed uncontrollably.","\"Chuhan, what have you experienced in these three years? Why have you become so thin?\"","Mo Chuhan followed his mother's guidance and stood up.","\"Mother, I...\"","Just as Mo Chuhan was about to explain something, Mo Jiuye stepped forward.","\"Mother, Eighth Brother is injured and still very weak. It would be better to ask these questions later, slowly.\"","Old Lady Mo understood Mo Jiuye's meaning. It was simply that it was not appropriate to discuss these matters with so many people around.","She had been too concerned about Mo Chuhan earlier, which made her overlook this point.","At this moment, Peng Wang also arrived with a group of officials to assess the situation, and members of the Fang and Xie families were also nearby, watching.","From their earlier conversation, they had already learned about Mo Chuhan's identity.","Although they were puzzled by Mo Chuhan's resurrection, they genuinely felt happy for the Mo family.","Peng Wang was the most tactful and waved his hand towards the onlookers.","\"The Mo family is catching up on old times. It's none of your business. Everyone, disperse!\"","The crowd obediently dispersed.","Mo Jiuye glanced at the sky and realized it would still be some time before dawn.","\"Eighth Brother, you should rest in my tent for now. We can talk later.\"","At that, Fifth Sister-in-Law walked over.","\"Ninth Brother, Eighth Sister and I share a tent. I'll take my things and squeeze in with Mother and Hanyue. Let Eighth Brother go to Eighth Sister's tent.\"","Before Mo Jiuye could respond, Old Lady Mo agreed first, \"Yes, that's appropriate. Considering Chuhan's weak state, it's convenient for Zhao Shi to take care of him.\"","As they spoke, Fifth Sister-in-Law had already brought out her luggage from the tent, making space for Eighth Brother and Eighth Sister.","Eighth Sister-in-Law reached out and supported Mo Chuhan's arm.","\"Husband, I'll support you.\"","Mo Chuhan gently patted the hand wrapped around his arm.","\"Alright.\"","Eighth Sister-in-Law carefully supported Mo Chuhan as they entered the tent, but the curtain was not drawn.","She knew that Mother must have a lot to say to her husband.","Sure enough, Old Lady Mo followed them inside.","Mo Jiuye was worried that Eighth Brother might mistakenly reveal the explanations they had prepared, so he quickly stepped forward and held onto Old Lady Mo.","\"Mother, Eighth Brother is very weak. Let him rest for now. If you want to know something, let your son tell you tomorrow.\"","Old Lady Mo looked at Mo Chuhan, who was sitting inside the tent with a slightly tilted body, and said to Eighth Sister-in-Law, \"Zhao Shi, you should rest early. We can talk about it tomorrow.\"","After speaking, she left with Mo Jiuye.","Undoubtedly, she would carefully inquire about Mo Chuhan's situation.","The other sisters-in-law tacitly led Mo Hanyue back to their respective tents. They all understood that if there was something about Mo Chuhan they needed to know, Mother would inform them tomorrow. There was no urgency at this moment.","Mo Jiuye proceeded to recount Mo Chuhan's ordeal to his mother, as he had discussed with He Zhiran in advance.","\"Mother, Eighth Brother is one of those black-clad individuals who rise early. When I fought against him, I sensed something was amiss. So, I knocked him unconscious and secretly hid him in a nearby cave, leaving Liang Hao and the others to keep watch there.","After nightfall, I utilized my lightness skills to return to that cave with Ranran to treat Eighth Brother...\"","Old Lady Mo had already heard about Liang Hao and the others seeking refuge, and she didn't harbor any doubts about it.","Mo Jiuye used the excuse of saving Mo Chuhan to deflect attention from the matter, but he didn't conceal anything else.","Upon hearing this, Old Lady Mo once again burst into tears.","\"Who on earth is behind such persecution against our Mo family's children?\"","Seeing Old Lady Mo in distress, He Zhiran stepped forward to console her.","\"Mother, the situation has already passed. It's fortunate that Eighth Brother is able to come back alive.","You don't need to worry about his health; with me here, I guarantee his complete recovery.\"","Old Lady Mo nodded and then patted He Zhiran's hand.","\"He Shi, ever since you married into the Mo family, I've observed everything you've done. If it weren't for you, our entire family would have perished long ago.","And now, you have also lifted the puppetry curse from Eighth Brother. This act of kindness will remain in my heart.\""]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: Are you gonna Show me your Hand for Dinner","paragraphs":["\"Mother, we are all one family, saying these things makes you feel unwelcome.\" He Zhiran held Old Lady Mo's hand to comfort her.","Mo Jiuye chose to tell Old Lady Mo about the incident because he knew his mother's temperament well.","Old Lady Mo had seen all kinds of storms and her disposition was not as simple as ordinary women's.","If he had been vague about Mo Chuhan's experience, she probably could not have handled it at all.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye chose to lay all his cards on the table.","This way, although his mother would feel sad, it was still better than letting her worry all day.","In addition, Mo Jiuye repeated the excuses that he and He Zhiran had come up with, indicating that his mother should say the same thing to others.","Naturally, Old Lady Mo understood his intentions without needing further explanation.","While Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were comforting Old Lady Mo, Eighth Sister-in-law had helped Mo Chuhan lie back down in her original spot in the tent.","She still had tears running down her face.","\"Husband, do you know that when I first heard the news of your death, if not for thinking that I still had to serve your mother on your behalf, I really could not have gone on living...\"","As she spoke, Eighth Sister-in-law threw herself into Mo Chuhan's arms again, bawling.","\"Husband, do you know how much I missed you... woo woo woo...\"","Mo Chuhan raised his hand to hug his delicate wife tightly, gently stroking her somewhat withered hair, and said, \"It was I who wronged you. As long as I can still live, I will definitely make it up to you in the future...\"","Eighth Sister-in-law vigorously nuzzled her face against his chest.","\"You must live well. If anyone is to die, I will die first. I can't bear the pain of losing you again.\"","\"Alright, I promise you that I will live well.\"","...","For all the Mo family members, this was destined to be a sleepless night.","When everyone got up early in the morning, they almost all had huge dark circles under their eyes.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye came out from the tent and went to find Peng Wang first thing.","They felt that it was necessary to officially notify Peng Wang about Mo Chuhan's matter.","Peng Wang had anticipated that they would come to find him, so after getting up he did not hurry to urge the team to move on, but waited in place instead.","Mo Jiuye brought He Zhiran to sit next to him.","\"Big Brother Peng, as you saw last night, my eighth brother is not dead.\"","\"This is absolutely great news for your Mo family, worth celebrating.\" As Peng Wang spoke, he looked towards He Zhiran.","\"Little sister, I haven't tasted your cooking skills in a long time. You'll show off some skills for dinner tonight, right?\"","\"No problem, I guarantee Big Brother Peng and the other officials will be satisfied.\"","Clearly, Peng Wang was a smart man. He did not want to delve into the details of how Mo Chuhan was able to come back alive.","He always kept in mind one principle - the more you know, the faster you die!","With one look Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran realized Peng Wang's intention. Originally they had only wanted to inform Peng Wang that there was one more person in the team.","Now that was settled, they did not need to waste their breath finding all kinds of excuses to conceal things.","The exile team had a rule that unless under special circumstances, criminals were not allowed to ride in any vehicles.","Considering Mo Chuhan’s current state, he was too weak to keep up with the main group on the road.","Peng Wang would do people a favor - he understood that Mo Jiuye would bring this matter up, so he took the initiative to offer to let Mo Chuhan ride in a mule cart.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran naturally expressed their gratitude profusely.","The sisters-in-law had cooked soft rice porridge early in the morning, plus one white flour steamed bun and one tea egg for each person.","Everyone had just finished breakfast when Peng Wang's side started getting ready to move on.","Considering Mo Chuhan’s physical condition and severe malnutrition, He Zhiran had endless ways to replenish him.","At the moment, with so many people around, it was best to use some ginseng and lingzhi and other medicinal ingredients that people of this era would recognize to nourish Mo Chuhan’s body.","She just needed to find an opportunity to reveal these medicinal ingredients.","Fortunately, the troops passed through another city that day.","Originally they did not need to enter the city, but Peng Wang had a craving and said early in the morning that he wanted to eat the dishes cooked by He Zhiran, thinking about the taste all day.","Therefore, when they passed by, he ordered the main troops to wait in place. He brought He Zhiran and an official into the city to purchase supplies.","Knowing that the things He Zhiran would \"purchase\" on one trip into the city would definitely not be few, Mo Jiuye helped Mo Chuhan down and let her lead the mule cart.","Peng Wang no longer regarded the Mo family as criminals now and naturally would not extort He Zhiran.","\"Little sister, here are five taels of silver. I'll leave tonight’s dinner for my brothers in your hands.\" As he spoke, he was about to put the silver into He Zhiran's hands.","Considering Peng Wang’s care for her family over this period, He Zhiran did not take his silver.","\"Big Brother Peng, we agreed that this would be our treat, how can we let you take out silver?\"","He Zhiran directly pushed the silver back.","Seeing this, Peng Wang did not argue with her either.","\"Since this is the case, big brother will not stand on ceremony with you.\"","He knew that He Zhiran liked to shop alone. Peng Wang took the official to a roadside tea stall, where they drank tea while waiting.","He Zhiran's main goal in entering the city this time was to buy some nourishing products for Mo Chuhan.","After splitting up from Peng Wang, she led the mule cart into a deserted alley.","She went straight into the mule cart and bought two whole old mountain ginsengs and two lingzhi mushrooms in Taobao Treasure Mall.","There is a saying that medicinal supplements are not as good as food supplements. However, Mo Chuhan’s body was too weak.","He Zhiran decided to use both medicinal and food supplements at the same time.","So she also bought two meat pigeons and one black chicken in the space, and used these plus the lingzhi and ginseng to cook soup for Mo Chuhan.","In addition, she poured several types of medicinal potions extracted from the space pharmacy that promote human immune function into a small porcelain bottle for Mo Chuhan to take on time every day.","Having a rare purchasing opportunity, He Zhiran naturally would not let it pass.","She bought several kinds of seasonal fruits, vegetables, various meats and some smoked sauce foods.","When treating others to a meal, she had to go all out.","He Zhiran bought a case of Wuliangye liquor in Taobao Treasure Mall and poured it into a wine jar.","When the supplies were prepared and half the carriage was already filled, He Zhiran finally led the satisfied mule cart to the tea stall to reunite with Peng Wang.","Regarding He Zhiran’s efficiency in purchasing, Peng Wang had long been accustomed to it.","Considering returning earlier to have more time to prepare dinner, He Zhiran let Peng Wang and the official ride in the carriage while she drove the mule cart all the way back, as this would allow them to move faster.","The moment Peng Wang entered the carriage, he was completely dumbfounded.","The Hes were indeed wealthy and powerful, actually buying so much stuff.","Then he thought again of the five taels of silver he had taken out earlier - afraid that would not even buy half...","He Zhiran was unaware of Peng Wang's thoughts. She drove the mule cart quickly out of the city.","Seeing the sky, Peng Wang ordered them to hurry on for another hour before resting in place.","With a goal, the main group picked up the pace even more vigorously down the road.","An hour later, Peng Wang chose to spend the night by a river.","Knowing that they had to treat the officials to dinner tonight, the sisters-in-law came over to help process the ingredients after the team stopped."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: As Much As You Want","paragraphs":["The women of the Fang and Xie families heard that He Zhiran was treating the officials to dinner tonight and rushed over to help.","He Zhiran was in no hurry to start cooking. Instead, she first taught Eighth Sister-in-law how to cook medicinal soup to nourish Mo Chuhan's health.","When Eighth Sister-in-law saw how many valuable ingredients He Zhiran had bought for Mo Chuhan's health, she was so moved that her eyes reddened.","\"Sister-in-law, you must have spent a lot of silver on this?\"","He Zhiran casually smiled, \"It wasn't much, don't worry about it.\"","Indeed she hadn't spent much from Taobao. Though you could buy anything there, items like thousand-year ginseng and lingzhi described in novels didn't actually exist.","It was all cultivated by advanced methods.","And it wasn't expensive either.","Two ginsengs cost 1,500 yuan. She chose the best looking lingzhi, spending 1,400 yuan.","Add in the silkie chicken and meat pigeon, still less than half the money from selling one silver hairpin.","To He Zhiran now, this was pocket change.","Moreover, Emperor Shunwu was footing the bill so she felt no pressure.","Seeing the fine supplements her sister-in-law bought for her husband, Eighth Sister-in-law studied the soup carefully, afraid of ruining the precious ingredients.","After making sure Eighth Sister-in-law could handle it independently, He Zhiran went to prepare dinner.","The feast tonight was to satisfy Official Peng and the others while celebrating Mo Chuhan's homecoming.","With everyone's help, He Zhiran only needed to cook.","As before, Mo Jiuye squatted nearby, helping tend the fire.","He now had another use too.","That was to help He Zhiran sneak ingredients from her space.","Whenever she wanted to secretly take out seasonings, Mo Jiuye would look around before blocking people's line of sight.","The couple worked seamlessly together. By nightfall, eight dishes and one soup were finished.","Red braised pork ribs, He Zhiran’s favorite, were essential.","There was also ready-made crystal elbow pork she’d bought straight from Taobao, making everyone drool.","The perfectly roasted duck, Dongpo pork, radish stuffed meatballs soup and other colorfully prepared dishes had generous portions, even the Fang and Xie families got a share.","Only the woeful He family, who now cowered without He Zhizhuan, could merely watch from afar.","Outside, two large oilcloths were spread on the ground for the officials.","This was the first family reunion dinner since Mo Chuhan returned.","At Lady Mo’s invitation, everyone crowded around together, livelier this way.","Having just downed a huge bowl of medicinal chicken soup from his wife, Mo Chuhan wasn’t hungry now.","But thinking this celebrated his homecoming, he tried to eat more.","Afraid her husband might not get his fill, Eighth Sister-in-law continuously heaped food on his bowl.","After the meal Mo Chuhan had to walk around to help digestion...","He Zhiran gave Eighth Sister-in-law medicine to boost immunity, telling her to administer it to Mo Chuhan twice a day.","Exhausted from the busy day and lack of sleep last night over Mo Chuhan’s matter, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye returned to their tent early to rest up for traveling tomorrow.","Perhaps from drinking wine, Mo Jiuye’s hot body kept lightly touching hers tonight.","Feeling the heat emanating from him, her body reflexively tensed.","Strangely, she didn’t dislike the sensation at all, even feeling a trace of pleasure and excitement.","Her encroaching drowsiness was abruptly dispelled by these peculiar feelings.","Glancing over, Mo Jiuye had his eyes shut, breathing evenly, clearly already asleep.","To keep her mind from wandering, He Zhiran entered her space, wanting to check Taobao and reply to Little Collector.","This gave He Zhiran a huge surprise.","When she went to town for supplies earlier, there was no record of transactions in the shop.","But now the message box showed an income of 13 million!","In all the time her antique shop was open, today’s profits exceeded the total previously.","If not for worrying about waking Mo Jiuye, she could have jumped and shouted to express her elation.","Looking over the purchase record, it was all ‘Little Collector’ as expected.","She wondered what Little Collector did for a living to splurge like this.","Curious, she opened the chat with him.","Little Collector: Boss, I urgently need a batch of paintings and vases recently. Please list them as soon as possible if you have stock. Price is no object.","He sent the message at 3:05 pm, over five hours ago now.","Unsure if he was still online, she tentatively responded:","“I have countless paintings and vases for you. What price range do you want?”","Assuming no reply from Little Collector, she was about to browse other things when his avatar flashed - he astonishingly messaged back!","He Zhiran hurriedly opened the chat.","Little Collector: I have no requirements as long as they’re quality pieces from your shop.","He Zhiran: No problem, I'll provide as many as you need.","Little Collector: (╰(*°▽°*)╯) Really? Wonderful, please list them quickly boss, I can hardly wait.","To expedite listing, she flashed straight into her space.","Now that Mo Jiuye knew about it, she had nothing to worry about either.","Using her consciousness, she summoned a huge quantity of paintings and vases.","Snapping photos, pricing, uploading, all done swiftly.","These were so bulky that selling them online significantly freed up room.","This time, determined to go all out, she listed nearly a thousand pieces!","Opening Little Collector’s chat box, she messaged: Listing complete, please browse and purchase whatever you like!","Seeing the shop suddenly expanded with so many new listings, Little Collector couldn’t peel his eyes away, let alone respond right now!","Assuming he’d gone to rest already since it was so late, feeling tired herself, she decided to leave the space and visit the god of dreams too.","Anyway these were items Little Collector specially asked for and she’d uploaded tons, first thing after waking up tomorrow would be to check sales!"]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: Unexpected Surprise","paragraphs":["Individual, ten, hundred, thousand, ten thousand, one hundred thousand, million, ten million, one hundred million, billion!","Damn, incredible!","The number that appeared on the info box was actually nine digits.","He Zhiran felt her legs go soft.","She actually had the day to become a billionaire...","A moment after the excitement, He Zhiran wanted to close the info box and check the specific sales situation of the store.","Who knew, she had just closed the info box, and another one popped up immediately.","[Congratulations, you have successfully joined the ranks of billionaires. Taobao rewards you with a chance to participate in a lottery.]","Lottery?","This Taobao is too good at playing!","Just as He Zhiran was stunned, the dialog box disappeared automatically.","A large rotating lottery wheel appeared on the screen.","He Zhiran didn't take this lottery to heart at all.","The little trick officially made just to promote consumption, nothing more than some promotional coupons.","She casually clicked the \"Draw\" button in the middle of the screen.","The turntable started spinning rapidly.","A few seconds later, the pointer was fixed on the mystery surprise prize.","Subsequently, another dialog box appeared on the screen.","[The mystery surprise is divided into special, advanced and normal levels. Now is the time to test your luck.]","The dialog box disappeared automatically, and three cards appeared on the screen.","This was not unfamiliar to He Zhiran's previous life experience on various platforms.","She casually clicked on one of the middle cards.","The screen was suddenly filled with golden light.","[Congratulations, you have drawn a special surprise and are rewarded with a Transmigrator Farm Space.]","He Zhiran???","Planting space???","Isn't it what she thought it was?","Just as He Zhiran's mind was racing with various possibilities, a 3D image appeared on the screen.","In the picture, you could see fields full of crops, clear ponds, vast pastures, processing plants and huge warehouses, as well as fruit trees on the distant hillsides that were already full of fruits.","Thinking that she could have such a planting space, He Zhiran couldn't help swallowing.","Not to mention that such a space could create a lot of wealth for her, just using it to appreciate would make people feel refreshed.","Not only that, the farm was also set up very thoughtfully.","An omnipotent control panel was set up here for the owner of the farm space.","The control panel can choose to water all crops with one click, or choose regional irrigation, automatic feeding, automatic harvesting and other functions.","That is to say, the owner of the space can complete everything they want to do on the control panel without using any manpower.","He Zhiran thought that she could get such a space, and silently thanked the kindness of the transmigration father to her in her heart.","Just as He Zhiran was eagerly looking for the entrance to the farm space, the tightly closed door of the medical room suddenly opened, instantly leaving her with the urge to swear.","The small parking lot outside the medical room had disappeared, and what caught her eye was a piece of barren land and the bare hill in the distance.","He Zhiran suddenly felt cheated.","Ranch, fish pond, warehouse, fertile fields, orchards, none of these things existed at all. The only thing that made her feel a little real was that when she turned left out the door, there was an operating table identical to the one in the picture.","50 million had already been spent, even if she was cheated, He Zhiran had to figure it out.","So she quickly came to the operating table with her consciousness.","Based on experience, she decisively pressed a button similar to a switch.","Ten seconds later, the screen of the operating table lit up.","[Welcome master to the farm space, I, Steward 008, will serve you sincerely in the future.]","He Zhiran manipulated the screen with her consciousness and flipped down.","[The space is currently in its initial state and needs to be handled according to the master's preferences.]","[Question, do you want to plant the land?]","He Zhiran chose yes.","Another dialog box popped up on the screen.","[The land is currently in its original state. To turn it into fertile fields, 100 yuan per acre is required for development. Does the master want to reclaim fertile fields?]","Money again?","He Zhiran was really drunk.","She always felt cheated, suspecting that future investment in the farm space would probably increase.","Just as she hesitated, the operating system popped up another dialog box.","[Master, the space does require some capital investment in its original state. Once the scale is formed, you will get higher returns for it. Do you choose to reclaim fertile fields now?]","Although He Zhiran was a little angry, she still wanted to try.","She chose yes, and then paid only for the reclamation of one acre of fertile fields, intending to observe first whether she would continue to be cheated.","The fee was deducted directly from her Alipay account, and the operating table started working immediately.","On the land about fifty meters away from the operating table, it was as if countless pangolins were shuttling back and forth inside. In the blink of an eye, a square acre of land was turned over neatly.","Seeing the reclamation process with her own eyes, He Zhiran could confirm that she had not been cheated.","Even in the afterlife, hiring manpower to reclaim an acre of land would probably cost more than this price.","So He Zhiran decisively reclaimed the remaining 49 acres of land.","Due to the simultaneous work, it took almost the same time to reclaim the 49 acres of land as it did to reclaim the first acre.","Not only that, each acre of land was separated by a not too deep trench, which looked very tidy when viewed.","With all the land in the space reclaimed, countless types of crops appeared on the computer screen of the operating table for her to choose from.","Considering the future diet of the family, He Zhiran chose to plant half of the land with common crops such as rice, wheat and corn.","The other half of the land was used to plant all kinds of vegetables.","However, the seeds here also cost money to purchase, although the prices were higher than those in the Taobao store, they were within the acceptable range for He Zhiran.","The operating table had functions like one-click planting and watering. After He Zhiran set everything up, she went to check out the others.","The fish ponds, pastures, warehouses, orchards, etc. had the same operating methods.","That is to say, as long as there is money here, nothing is a problem."]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: The Reason why Mohism is poor is Here.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran had been busy at the control panel for over an hour, finally completing the construction of this farm space.","All the necessary facilities such as fish ponds and warehouses were fully equipped.","Moreover, she made an exciting discovery.","The seeds she had just planted in the soil had sprouted small green shoots.","At that moment, another dialog box appeared on the screen of the control panel.","The dialog box contained a lot of information, mainly introducing the features of the space.","[In the farm space, crops and vegetables mature in three days, fruit trees reach adulthood in ten days, and mature fruit trees yield a batch of fruit every ten days.","Various aquatic species in the fish pond take ten days to breed, poultry takes ten days to grow, and livestock takes half a month to mature.","The seeds produced in the space undergo genetic improvement and can be planted outside without being picky about the soil and climate.]","Seeing all this, He Zhiran was overjoyed. Not to mention the harvest time of living things, just the maturity time of crops alone was incredibly satisfying.","Furthermore, the seeds produced here were so amazing that she could completely disregard the climate and freely cultivate them when she arrived in the northwest.","He Zhiran began to yearn for a warm and prosperous life with her family in the northwest, living together as husband and wife, with the man tilling the land and the woman weaving.","Although it cost her hundreds of thousands to create this primitive space, seeing such a user-friendly environment, she felt it was all worth it.","He Zhiran hadn't felt so relaxed and content in a long time. She decided to wander around the newly arranged space.","She first went to the clear fish pond.","The newly purchased fish fry and small shrimps were swimming around, especially the plump-headed fish. She remembered that when she bought the fish fry, they were only the size of a little finger, but now they seemed to have grown a bit.","After inspecting the fish pond, she went to check the pasture and breeding area.","There were cows and sheep everywhere, and the breeding areas for various poultry and livestock in the breeding field were clearly marked.","The warehouse also appeared to be quite large. Just thinking about when Mo Jiuye took her to move the national treasury, having a warehouse like this would have been incredibly convenient.","With this in mind, He Zhiran used her mind to transfer all the medical supplies from the infirmary to the warehouse.","After casually touring around, considering that she had been lingering in the space for quite a while, she reluctantly left.","Seeing that she finally reacted, Mo Jiuye asked eagerly, \"Why did you look at the space for so long?\"","Mo Jiuye had just woken up and found her sitting there in a daze.","From this, it could be inferred that her consciousness must have entered the space to check on things, but today she had been in there for quite a long time, which made Mo Jiuye feel somewhat uneasy.","He Zhiran was still in the midst of her excitement. Not knowing how to explain, she said, \"Come, let me show you a surprise.\"","Before her words could fall, their figures appeared in the space.","They were still standing in the infirmary.","The first thing Mo Jiuye noticed was that all the wealth they had brought from the national treasury was gone.","Seeing his astonishment, He Zhiran didn't explain immediately but mysteriously pulled him along and pushed open the door of the infirmary.","Mo Jiuye was once again astonished. \"Can this door open?\"","Just as he was wondering, he was completely stunned by the scene before him.","He Zhiran, who had lived two lives, finally found a sense of satisfaction in sharing it with someone.","She pointed to the orderly farmland in front of her and said, \"This is the precious space I just acquired.\"","Then, she carefully explained the benefits and characteristics of this space to Mo Jiuye.","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye was indeed shocked at first, but when he turned his head and saw the familiar medical room, he quickly put his mind at ease.","If He Zhiran could possess such a magical medical room, having one more farm like this was not a big deal.","He Zhiran was extremely excited at the moment. She even took the initiative to hold Mo Jiuye's hand and took him to visit the farm space.","Just like her, Mo Jiuye also had a feeling of not wanting to leave when he arrived here.","There were no dangers like outside, no deceitful schemes, no right or wrong, only the girl he had already fallen in love with from the bottom of his heart...","Seeing Mo Jiuye sitting by the fish pond in a daze, He Zhiran nudged him.","\"How do you feel about this farm space?\"","Mo Jiuye wasn't very good at expressing himself.","\"It's naturally good.\"","Seeing his calm appearance, He Zhiran couldn't help but pout.","\"Don't think this space came for free.\"","Mo Jiuye asked in return, \"Then how did you get it?\"","He Zhiran held out her palm. \"Fifty million, I bought this space with fifty million.\"","Mo Jiuye frowned. \"Where did you get so much money?\" He clearly remembered that the wealth he obtained from the treasury, when converted to silver, would amount to at most eighteen million.","Seeing his expression, it seemed like he had forgotten about her earning money in the online marketplace.","\"It's not silver, it's money earned from the online marketplace.\"","Although Mo Jiuye was not unfamiliar with her opening a shop in the online marketplace, he didn't have a deep understanding of the concept of money.","\"Fifty million? How many valuable items did you have to sell?\"","He Zhiran calculated.","\"A few dozen calligraphy and paintings, as well as dozens of vases and ornaments, that's all.\"","Mo Jiuye simply couldn't believe his ears.","Although those calligraphy and paintings, as well as vases and ornaments, were all from the treasury, they were not the most valuable things.","With that in mind, Mo Jiuye couldn't help but sigh, \"It's too cheap.\"","\"You think fifty million is cheap?\"","For He Zhiran, who had relied on allowances to get by in her previous life, fifty million was definitely a huge sum of money.","Mo Jiuye answered seriously.","\"When I led the army to invade the enemy's palace, the emperor liked to collect those things, but I didn't really care about them at that time.\"","Listening to Mo Jiuye mention the treasures of the enemy country, He Zhiran instantly remembered the time they moved the treasury together.","She could still vividly feel that satisfying feeling at this moment.","She couldn't understand why Mo Jiuye didn't appreciate those things.","\"Why don't you appreciate them?\"","\"During years of war, the people of both countries were starving to death. Those things couldn't be eaten as food. In my opinion, they were just a pile of showy and useless junk.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye say this, He Zhiran couldn't help but sigh.","Thinking about the possible whereabouts of so many treasures, she asked, \"Don't tell me all the treasures in the enemy's palace have been surrendered to the court.\"","Mo Jiuye shook his head, \"Those treasures have been exchanged for silver. Part of it was distributed as rewards to the soldiers who fought alongside me, risking their lives. Another portion was given to the displaced people who lost their homes due to the turmoil of war.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran couldn't help but admire Mo Jiuye's disregard for wealth.","Originally, she had thought that as a martial family that had been engaged in battles for years, their storerooms would be filled with endless riches.","After all, they had plenty of opportunities to acquire spoils of war.","However, the storerooms of the Mo family were not just poor, they couldn't even be considered wealthy.","It turned out that the reason for the poverty of the Mo family lay here.","But when she thought about it, He Zhiran could understand Mo Jiuye's actions.","As a patriotic general, he risked his life and donned armor with the purpose of protecting the safety of the people.","If Mo Jiuye turned a blind eye to the plight of the people who had become homeless due to the war and claimed all those possessions for himself, it would contradict his original intention of fighting.","With these thoughts in mind, He Zhiran's admiration for Mo Jiuye's noble principles grew even stronger.","If all future officials could consider the well-being of the people like Mo Jiuye, surely the lives of the common folk would become more prosperous..."]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: In my eyes, you are the most different one.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran realized that her thoughts had unknowingly drifted from the joy of sharing space to contemplation of the complexities of the world.","She brought her wandering thoughts back to the agricultural space.","\"When we reach the northwest, shall we build a home like this? What do you think?\" she asked.","As she spoke, He Zhiran already envisioned the image of Mo Jiuye tilling the soil with a hoe.","Perhaps, this was the life she truly wanted.","Mo Jiuye replied without hesitation, \"Sure, I'll contribute my efforts. You just need to take care of our children at home.\"","Upon hearing the words \"our children,\" He Zhiran blushed.","\"Who said I want to have children with you?\"","Mo Jiuye, caught up in his good mood, couldn't control his words and blurted out his true feelings.","Initially, he didn't feel anything was amiss, but when He Zhiran asked that question, he too blushed and stumbled over his words.","\"You... you're my lawfully wedded wife... Who else would I have children with if not you?\"","After spending so much time with Mo Jiuye, this was the first time she saw a different side of him.","In the past, Mo Jiuye was always reserved and taciturn in front of others. Why did he seem like a changed person today?","Now, He Zhiran was truly speechless.","Her identity was undoubtedly that of Mo Jiuye's lawfully wedded wife.","Although she had already accepted Mo Jiuye in her heart, as a modern soul, even if she hadn't experienced love before, she didn't want to live her life in a haphazard manner without expressing her feelings.","Thinking about Mo Jiuye's character, he was indeed a closed-off person, an old-fashioned relic with deeply entrenched feudal ideas.","She didn't think it was likely that he would take the initiative to confess his feelings to her.","Since that was the case, she might as well ask him herself.","Once she knew the answer, she could determine her future direction.","\"Um... Do you like me?\" she asked.","\"I do,\" Mo Jiuye answered without hesitation.","She thought he would continue and say something else, but to her surprise, after answering with those two words, he fell silent and just gazed at her affectionately.","He Zhiran felt helpless and continued to guide him.","\"Then, tell me, what do you like about me?\"","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment and replied earnestly.","\"You are different from all the other women I've known. Beautiful, level-headed, wise, decisive...","In short, in my eyes, you are the most unique one.","No matter what you're doing, seeing you makes me extremely happy.","If you're not in my line of sight, I even feel a bit anxious.","When you fell off the cliff last time, the first thing I thought was that if you died, I would rather be dead.\"","This was the first time He Zhiran had heard Mo Jiuye say so much at once.","She knew in her heart that Mo Jiuye wasn't good at expressing himself.","And with his character, he wouldn't say insincere words just to please a woman.","It had to be said that He Zhiran was a little touched at this moment.","She had initially thought that coming from an ancient man, it was already good enough for him to say so much. But unexpectedly, he paused and continued:","\"Although I have now fallen into exile as a prisoner of the court, unable to give you the privileged status that all those women desire, I can assure you that I will only treat you well in this lifetime and never let you suffer any grievances.\"","Mo Jiuye had been struggling in his heart recently.","He had considered that he might not be able to provide He Zhiran with a life of luxury, and he even entertained thoughts of setting He Zhiran free.","But whenever he thought about her leaving him, a heart-wrenching pain would constantly remind him that he had deeply fallen for this woman.","Without her, he would not be happy.","Therefore, today Mo Jiuye took the opportunity to express his true feelings.","He hoped that He Zhiran had also developed feelings for him and willingly chose to be with him.","At this moment, He Zhiran was already certain of Mo Jiuye's intentions.","After questioning herself, she confirmed that she also liked Mo Jiuye.","Since they both had affection for each other, it was not in her nature to continue to be reserved.","\"A promise once spoken is difficult to retract, so you must keep your word.\"","Even if Mo Jiuye was usually slow to catch on, he understood He Zhiran's meaning at this moment.","Excitedly, he grabbed her hand and asked, \"Ranran, you accept me, right?\"","He Zhiran nodded, saying, \"Um, I'll have to see how you perform in the future.\"","Mo Jiuye, happy like a child, picked up He Zhiran and spun around in place.","\"Ranran, rest assured, I, Mo Jiuye, will keep my word. I will love only you in this lifetime.\"","Suddenly being lifted and spun around, He Zhiran felt a bit dizzy.","However, she didn't want to spoil Mo Jiuye's good mood.","Since they were leaving the capital city and he was rarely this happy, He Zhiran couldn't bring herself to stop him.","Fortunately, after a few spins, Mo Jiuye stopped, but he didn't let go of the hand that embraced her.","The two stood in place, leaning against each other, feeling each other's heartbeats...","Although He Zhiran possessed a modern soul, having lived two lives, this was her first time experiencing love. She still felt a bit hesitant.","After holding each other for a while, she felt a little embarrassed and pushed him away, casually making up an excuse, \"I'll go check my phone.\"","Watching his beloved woman quickly run off, Mo Jiuye helplessly shook his head and continued to sit in place, enjoying the scenery of the surroundings.","He Zhiran rushed into the medical room and took out her phone, casually browsing on Taobao Mall.","It was then that she noticed a flashing icon at the bottom of the screen.","It was from Little Collector.","\"Boss, you're really amazing. I love all the items in your shop. If it weren't for some financial difficulties I'm currently facing, I would definitely buy everything in your store.\"","He Zhiran: \"I have a wide variety of antiques here, and you're my first customer, also a big customer. Just let me know if you need anything in the future.\"","Her thought was that even if she didn't have what Little Collector wanted, she could go out and find it.","After all, she was in ancient times, so would it be difficult to obtain whatever she wanted?","Perhaps it was because it was late, but Little Collector didn't reply. He Zhiran glanced at the remaining hundreds of items in the store and decided that there was no need to restock. She closed her phone and left with Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye's heart was still fluttering from the sudden \"passive\" confession that had just taken place, leaving him feeling a bit overwhelmed and unsure of what to do next.","He Zhiran, too, was still caught up in the excitement of receiving the farm space and Mo Jiuye's confession.","However, at this moment, she was overcome with shyness and dared not make any movements, keeping her back turned to Mo Jiuye.","Taking note of the early hour, Mo Jiuye decided to remain lying in the tent, propping his head up with one hand as he gazed at her.","Then, tentatively, he reached out his arm towards her.","He Zhiran felt his touch and her body tensed up. Immediately, a tingling sensation spread throughout her entire body, like an electric shock.","However, she didn't dodge away.","Seeing her response, Mo Jiuye cautiously exerted more strength and pulled her into his embrace..."]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: Tang Mingrui","paragraphs":["He Zhiran still did not dodge.","Anyway, she had already worshipped Mo Jiuye here, and they were legitimate husband and wife.","Besides, they had just expressed their feelings to each other. If something happened at this time, it would be reasonable.","She drilled into Mo Jiuye's arms smoothly. Mo Jiuye was overjoyed, and his arms holding her tightened again.","He patted her back lightly.","\"It's still early, let's rest for a while longer. I have to make up a perfect bridal chamber candle night for you, so I will definitely wait until then.\"","He Zhiran was relieved at this point.","Because of the surprise of the space, He Zhiran had hardly slept all night, and she was really a little sleepy now.","She closed her eyes and felt the embrace that made her feel extremely at ease, and soon fell asleep.","Although she had only slept for half an hour, the way she woke up this time was also different from before. She was still lying in Mo Jiuye’s arms.","Mo Jiuye's voice sounded a little hoarse, \"Awake?\"","\"Well.\" He Zhiran responded, and was about to get up.","Unexpectedly, Mo Jiuye suddenly hugged her tightly and gently kissed her forehead.","He Zhiran was a little embarrassed and pushed him lightly, and was about to say something when she heard the voice of the eighth sister-in-law outside.","\"Ninth Sister-in-law, your medicine is really effective. My eighth brother felt much more flexible when he got up this morning.\"","Hearing the sound of footsteps approaching, He Zhiran seemed to have done something wrong, and quickly got out of Mo Jiuye's arms.","She casually tidied up a bit, lifted the tent curtain.","In fact, it was just that she had the feeling that she had done something shameful and was afraid of being seen.","The eighth sister-in-law was very aware of the rules and stood about five meters away from the tent.","Seeing He Zhiran come out, the eighth sister-in-law still stood in place.","\"Ninth Sister-in-law, the eighth sister-in-law doesn't know how to thank you enough.\"","He Zhiran smiled, \"Eighth Sister-in-law, we are all family, so there is no need to thank each other.\"","Seeing He Zhiran walking towards her, the eighth sister-in-law took a few steps forward and took her by the arm.","\"Since Ninth Sister-in-law said so, Eighth Sister-in-law won't be polite to you.\"","As they spoke, the other sisters-in-law had also prepared breakfast and came to call for the meal.","Mo Jiuye took the initiative to tidy up the tent and other items and went to eat breakfast with them.","Just after putting down his chopsticks, Peng Wang came over.","He first asked about Mo Chuhan's physical condition, then looked at their mule cart somewhat awkwardly.","\"Brother Mo, sister-in-law, in another two days, we will have to go through the salt lake section.","There is no bridge over the salt lake. To cross the river, you can only take a boat. I'm afraid your mule cart can't be kept.","After all, it was bought with money. It would be a pity to throw it away. When you pass through the town today, go to the livestock department to dispose of it yourself!\"","If it were before last night, He Zhiran would definitely dispose of the mule cart according to Peng Wang's proposal.","However, she now has such a large farm space that she can store the mule cart directly.","After all, this secret is only known to her and Mo Jiuye, so she readily agreed with Peng Wang's words.","\"Big Brother Peng, don't worry, we will dispose of the mule cart today.\"","Peng Wang came over just to remind them of this. After achieving his goal, he began to arrange to continue on their way.","In order to give them a chance to deal with the mule cart, the main force drove half a time longer today and rested directly in the town.","Early the next morning, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye took the mule cart out.","On the surface, it was to dispose of the mule cart, but in fact it was to put it into the space.","He Zhiran also took the opportunity to buy some replenishment products for Mo Chuhan in Taobao Treasure Mall, as well as some seasonal fruits for her family to eat.","When the two returned to the inn, Peng Wang and the others were ready to set off for Salt Lake.","According to Peng Wang's plan, the main force could arrive at the town near Salt Lake by nightfall.","This place is quite different from other places.","The water area of ​​Salt Lake is extremely large, covering three provinces, and it is also the most prosperous water transportation artery in Da Shun Dynasty.","As the name implies, Salt Lake is also a major producer of edible salt in the Da Shun Dynasty.","Therefore, the number of merchants and merchants coming and going here is quite considerable.","It is so prosperous here that I thought Peng Wang would take them to stay at an inn.","Unexpectedly, Peng Wang actually took them to a small grove.","The officials were obviously used to it and greeted everyone to find a place to rest.","He Zhiran was very puzzled by this, so she asked the official who was closest to her.","\"Sir, I just saw a lot of inns on the way, so why stay here?\"","The officer sighed.","\"You don't know because it's your first time here. Salt Lake is prosperous. Inns here are full every day, so prices are very high. A room that costs 100 wen to stay overnight in other places costs at least two taels of silver here.\"","To this, He Zhiran didn’t feel anything. It was just like the difference between big cities and small cities in her previous life. The prices were also different.","Although there was plenty of silver in her space, there was no need to show off here.","Therefore, she readily accepted Peng Wang's arrangement.","I thought the officer would be busy explaining it, but unexpectedly, he started talking about other things.","\"The last time we came, we heard people say that most of the inns and restaurants here were in the hands of a merchant named Tang.","Later, I don't know which character the Tang family offended that they shouldn't have offended. Overnight, their inns and restaurants changed hands, and the head of the Tang family also fell ill because of this and died after a few days.","After the new owner took over Tang's business, he gradually monopolized all the restaurants and inns here, and prices have been rising, resulting in the current situation where ordinary people can't afford to stay in an inn.\"","Regarding the officer's account, He Zhiran just listened to it as a story. After all, these were other people's affairs.","Just as everyone was having dinner and preparing to rest, there was a faint cry for help in the woods.","Mo Jiuye was the first to be vigilant.","Although Mo Chuhan's body was still a little weak, he did not slack off at all.","The two brothers faced the direction where the sound came from and had already taken a defensive posture.","Liang Hao and the others also hid in the dark, ready to take action with just one order from the two masters.","He Zhiran also walked quickly to the two’s side and listened carefully to the movement in the distance.","Soon, the cry for help grew closer and closer, accompanied by a messy sound of footsteps.","In the moonlight, you could see a few shadows flashing ahead.","The person running at the front was obviously lacking in strength, staggering.","The people behind him held a big knife in their hands and shouted loudly, \"Tang Mingrui, if you want to live, hand over the Tang family's business secrets obediently, otherwise, a year from today will be your memorial day.\"","\"Salt Gang robbers, even if I die, I won't hand over the secrets to you.\"","When they heard the name Tang Mingrui, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked at each other tacitly.","This name was not unfamiliar to them.","In order to find out the real reason why Nan Qi assassinated Mo Jiuye some time ago, they had carefully read the history of this period.","They had a deep memory of some famous people in history.","The historical records show that after Fei Nan established the Da Xing Dynasty, the merchant named Tang Mingrui gave him the greatest financial support in building the country."]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135: This guy looks pretty pathetic.","paragraphs":["Moreover, Fei Nanyu trusted Tang Mingrui to the utmost. Soon after he ascended to the throne, he bestowed Tang Family the sole imperial merchant status in Daxing Country.","As a result, during Fei Nanyu’s reign, Tang Family’s business thrived even more, becoming an existence as rich as a country.","Of course, this was not without the business acumen of Tang Family’s current head.","Moreover, historical books also mentioned that Tang Mingrui’s ancestors had run businesses for generations. Later, due to the Salt Gang’s plot, they almost suffered family ruin and death of their members.","To be able to revive Tang Family again, 17-year-old Tang Mingrui took his mother and two young brothers, and escaped his hometown using the little savings left in the family.","Afterwards, through many years of hard work and striving, he built up a business of no small size again. At the same time, he also secretly collected detailed information about the Salt Gang.","After Nan Qi ascended to the throne, Fei Nanyu brought men to crackdown on the Salt Gang. Tang Mingrui resolutely submitted the information he had collected over the years, and got acquainted with Fei Nanyu because of this.","At the same time, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye also immediately thought of the Tang Family the officer had just spoken of.","It was very likely that the Tang Family mentioned by the officer was Tang Mingrui’s original clan.","At this time, what He Zhiran was thinking was, first not considering whether Tang Mingrui had any connection with Fei Nanyu.","After arriving at the Northwest, in order to let her family live better, she would definitely have to run some profitable businesses on the surface to conceal her using the silver from the national treasury.","However, Da Shun Dynasty had a rule that exiled people who did not have a special pardon order from the Emperor would have to live in exile for the rest of their lives, and could not leave the city walls for half a step.","Thus, the best method was to find a clever businessman to cooperate with.","Thinking thus, He Zhiran felt the most suitable partner to cooperate with her business was Tang Mingrui.","“Husband, this person looks quite pitiful.”","Mo Jiuye naturally understood her meaning.","“Hmm, I’ll go over to take a look.”","Mo Chuhan did not think too much. He only thought his Ninth Sister’s womanly compassion had been aroused.","Thus, he also intended to follow Mo Jiuye.","However, Mo Jiuye stopped him.","“Eighth Brother, your health is weak. Leave this small matter to me.”","Seeing it was only a few men chasing with sabers, Mo Chuhan did not continue forcing himself as Mo Jiuye could totally handle it.","Since Mo Jiuye chose to take action, he would naturally not leave any living mouths.","Moreover, he never had any good impressions towards the Salt Gang’s men.","He might as well go all the way and directly take their dog lives.","He hid in the shadows, and aligned the mini sleeve arrows at several Salt Gang’s men.","With a few swoosh sounds, the Salt Gang’s men all had an arrow in their foreheads and died on the ground.","Seeing the death of the chasers, Tang Mingrui clearly realized he had been saved.","As he heaved a sigh of relief, he continued walking towards Mo Jiuye’s direction.","“I am Tang Mingrui. Much thanks to Sir for saving my life.”","Having purposefully saved the person, Mo Jiuye would naturally not continue hiding.","After scanning the surroundings and seeing no danger, he flashed out from the shadows.","At the same time, He Zhiran also rushed over.","Facing one man and one woman, Tang Mingrui had no doubt that he was the one they saved.","He bowed with clasped hands again, “Sir.”","Mo Jiuye helped him up slightly.","“I just couldn't ignore an injustice on the road. Young Master need not take it too seriously.”","Having been saved, the first thing Tang Mingrui thought of was how to express some gratitude.","His hand habitually reached into his pocket, only to find it completely empty.","He was apparently somewhat embarrassed.","“I originally wanted to give you some silver taels to thank you for saving my life, but my family has run into some thorny issues recently......”","Mo Jiuye thought that since historical books recorded that Tang Mingrui’s future business prospects were limitless, even if he did not take action to save him today, Tang Mingrui would not die here.","Therefore, he did not place too much emphasis on saving the person.","Just when he was about to say ‘no need to stand on ceremony’, He Zhiran seized the chance to speak first.","“We are criminals who were seized and exiled under the court’s decree. We are now rushing towards Du Cheng in the Northwest.","My husband is called Mo Jiuye. Young Master, if you are truly grateful for our lifesaving grace, when you have some silver on hand in the future, you can send it to Yun City in Northwest for us. Our future lives will indeed require some silver.”","He Zhiran thought that since her purpose of letting Mo Jiuye save Tang Mingrui was for their future business partnership.","Rather than ambiguously declining now and severing possible future connections, it would be more straightforward to directly state their names and address, so he could find them accurately when repaying their kindness.","Of course, He Zhiran was also gambling by doing this.","After all, no one was willing to set foot in the barren Northwest lands.","Whether Tang Mingrui would truly repay kindness and send silver to the Northwest in the future were unknown numbers.","She was doing this just to leave herself an additional pathway.","In case Tang Mingrui really had the heart to repay them, having him as a connection would benefit her future businesses.","Hearing Mo Jiuye’s name, Tang Mingrui froze for a moment.","Clearly, he was not unfamiliar with the name Mo Jiuye.","Tang Mingrui did not know why the Mo Family had declined to the point of being seized and exiled.","Since young, he often heard storytellers talk about the brave, enemy-slaying exploits of the Mo Family men. Hence, he had an extremely deep impression about them.","Especially a few years ago, the Third Young Master of the Mo Family had personally led men here to crackdown on the Salt Gang’s evildoers under decree.","He still clearly remembered the scene of the Third Young Master of the Mo Family pushing the Salt Gang’s boss at that time into the prisoner carriage.","This matter was praised by the commoners around the salt lakes for a very long time. Especially the Third Young Master of the Mo Family, the commoners spread tales of him even more exceptionally.","Who knew that after just a few short years, times had changed. The Mo Family men successively died on the battlefields. And today, they had even fallen to the extent of being seized and exiled.","He had assumed that after saying all these, Tang Mingrui would feel she was too realistic, politely decline on the surface then leave.","Unexpectedly, after hearing her words, Tang Mingrui's attitude became even more humble.","“Yesterday, my family had already taken a boat across the river. At this moment, they are waiting for me at Du Cheng pier to reunite.","That place is a necessary route heading Northwest. I have yet to decide where to bring my family, so why don’t I just follow Sir and Madam. Along the way, I can also think of ways to earn some silver.”","Hearing his words, He Zhiran did not hesitate at all and immediately agreed.","“It seems we really have an affinity with Young Master Tang. Let’s go together then! It’ll be safer with more people watching out for each other on the road.”","Tang Mingrui looked around and pointed at the few Salt Gang men’s corpses on the ground, then said:","“Sir had just taken their lives earlier in order to save me. I’m afraid people will discover them tomorrow morning.","The Salt Gang has great numbers. I cannot trouble you further. I won’t disturb you here. I will wait for you at Du Cheng pier tomorrow.”","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were not actually afraid of those Salt Gang fellows. But no one liked inviting trouble without reason.","Hence, they both agreed with Tang Mingrui’s decision.","“Alright, see you at Du Cheng tomorrow.”","After Mo Jiuye spoke, he pulled He Zhiran’s hand and left together to regroup with Mo Chuhan. Then, they returned to camp together.","He first gestured towards Liang Hao and others not far away. Very soon, Liang Hao brought men over."]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136: Someone Else is really in charge.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye knew that these three people had some silver on them and did not want them to sleep outdoors like himself.","So he casually found an excuse.","\"You guys can go into town and take a look around, while gathering some information on the Salt Gang.\"","\"Yes!\"","After responding, the three's figures disappeared.","Returning to the tent, Mo Jiuye told He Zhiran what he knew about the Salt Gang.","\"Four years ago, the Salt Gang bandits were rampant around the salt lakes, and their scale was growing.","When the Emperor heard about this, he decreed that Third Brother lead people here to suppress and eradicate the Salt Gang.","After more than a month of casting a wide net, Third Brother finally found the lair of the Salt Gang and captured the gang leader and some backbone elders.","As a result, there was peace here for a while. I didn't expect that in just a few years after Third Brother was ordered to eradicate the Salt Gang, the Salt Gang has developed and grown to such an extent again.\"","After listening to Mo Jiuye's account, the first thing He Zhiran thought of was that for the Salt Gang to reemerge in such a short time after being suppressed by the court, there must be someone manipulating all this behind the scenes.","\"Have you ever thought that on the surface the Salt Gang seems to be a spontaneous organization formed by people with financial interests, but in reality there are mysterious figures truly controlling everything behind the scenes?\"","This point was not He Zhiran's casual speculation. From ancient times to the present, which dynasty's Salt Gang did not have a mysterious figure supporting it behind the scenes?","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment and nodded: \"It's not impossible.\"","He just couldn't think of who the Salt Gang's real behind-the-scenes figure was.","Now that the Salt Gang has grown powerful again, it should be Emperor Shunwu who needs to worry about it.","Mo Jiuye was just chatting idly with He Zhiran about these things!","Anyway, they would be leaving this troublesome place tomorrow morning and the future of the Salt Gang had nothing to do with them.","Mo Jiuye looked at the sky and reminded: \"It's getting late, we still have to travel tomorrow, so let’s rest early!\"","He Zhiran was indeed a little tired. The two tidied up and then fell asleep.","In the middle of the night, they suddenly heard a clamoring noise.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran came out of the tent at the same time to check.","There were flames rising to the sky on the outskirts of the forest.","\"Hey! Officers, have you seen several men with knives?\"","Zhang Qing had just changed shifts and went to rest. At this moment he was woken up and his mood was a little bad.","\"Who are you, shouting here?\"","The leader of the Salt Gang raised the whip in his hand and lashed Zhang Qing over the head, annoyed.","\"How dare you be so arrogant on my Salt Gang territory, looks like you're tired of living!\"","Seeing that Zhang Qing was at a disadvantage, Peng Wang hurried over.","\"Don't fight, let's talk nicely, let's talk nicely.\"","When Peng Wang spoke, he clearly lacked confidence.","There is a saying, don’t press down the local snake. On the territory of the Salt Gang, he didn’t dare put on the airs of an official.","He had heard that the Salt Gang killed people without blinking, and they must have had someone backing them up. A small eighth-rank official like himself was definitely not someone he could afford to provoke.","Seeing that Peng Wang spoke softly, the Salt Gang boss snorted and put away his whip.","\"Humph! Consider yourselves self-aware. I won't settle accounts with you today.\"","The Salt Gang boss ordered his men to search the camp with torches. When they didn't find the people they were looking for, he ordered them to leave.","Seeing the Salt Gang people walk away, Peng Wang finally breathed a sigh of relief.","He turned his head to scold Zhang Qing, actually hinting at Mo Jiuye.","\"I've told you countless times not to cause trouble when going out, why don't you ever remember?\"","Zhang Qing scratched his head apprehensively.","\"Boss, I was wrong.\"","Peng Wang patted him on the back of his head.","\"If you know you’re wrong then you should change.\"","\"I will definitely change.\"","......","Seeing the matter settled, everyone returned to rest in the tents.","In order to leave this troublesome place early, as soon as dawn broke, the officials urged everyone to get up and continue on the road, even skipping breakfast time.","Carrying their packed belongings, they came to the pier, but were told that due to a senior official’s visit over the next few days, the pier was closed today.","At this point, even if Peng Wang wanted to leave, he couldn’t.","He had no choice but to grit his teeth and lead the people back, rest here for a day, then set off early tomorrow morning.","At this moment, both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were guessing who the senior official mentioned by the pier master might be.","However, this question was really difficult for them to answer.","Those who could be called senior officials were not few in number.","Many higher-ranking officials in the capital could be addressed like that.","Since they couldn’t figure out the answer, the two tacitly decided not to continue wasting brain cells.","Out of curiosity, they decided to scout around when night fell.","With the rare opportunity of not needing to rush on the road, He Zhiran planned to rest well for a day.","He would also build up his energy as there would likely be action at night.","They had failed to leave this place, and so had Tang Mingrui.","At this moment he was hiding in the cellar of the old Tang house, finding some rouge and cosmetics that the family's women had not had time to take away, as well as a few pieces of women’s clothing.","He spent a long time making up and dressing up. Feeling flawless after putting on a woman's hair bun and changing into women’s clothes, he finally left the cellar.","The first thing he thought of was that his benefactor would not be able to leave here today. If the Salt Gang found anything suspicious, it would be dangerous.","Therefore, he decided to go over to warn them.","As a result, when he arrived at the camp, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were resting in the tent, and Tang Mingrui did not see them.","However, seeing that this group of people still looked fairly composed, Tang Mingrui knew his benefactor should not be in danger, so he felt relieved and left.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye claimed to the outside that they were napping so that no one would bother them.","The two entered the space together, enjoying delicious food while experiencing a special kind of tranquility.","It had to be said that this farm space was truly magical. The grains and vegetables planted had grown very tall.","The fruit trees on the mountain had also grown much taller, forming a vast green scene from afar.","The cattle and sheep on the grasslands were grazing leisurely, and even the donkeys that had just been brought in quickly adapted to life here, rolling around lazily in open spaces.","Such scenery was like a paradise for He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye.","After spending a leisurely day in the space, they finally stayed up until late at night."]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137: Who Are They","paragraphs":["He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye changed into their night clothes separately, and left the tent.","Without any clear target, Mo Jiuye hugged He Zhiran by the waist using Qinggong to shuttle around randomly.","After a long time, their eyes were focused on a brightly lit painted boat on the lake surface.","From afar, the sound of singing and dancing on the painted boat could still be heard.","The painted boat slowly traveled on the lake, estimated to be at least a thousand meters away from the shore.","In order to determine if the adults they were curious about were on the ship, He Zhiran decisively bought a night vision telescope.","It had to be said that technological products like night vision telescopes were really overbearing.","He Zhiran just randomly looked around for a while, and her gaze stayed on the central location on the second floor of the painted boat, where two men were sitting.","One of them looked to be in his early thirties, with fair skin, upturned eyebrows, and gave off the first impression of being a little mean.","Judging from his luxurious clothing, this person was most likely the \"important person\" the dock foreman had mentioned.","This person was holding a scantily clad woman in his arms, holding a wine glass, and his eyes were still lecherously staring at those dancing maids.","While the man sitting on the other side had a full beard, a thin figure, and his hair seemed to be deliberately draped over both sides to cover half of his face.","Under the telescope, He Zhiran basically couldn't see the appearance of this person at all.","These two were very unfamiliar to He Zhiran.","Mo Jiuye looked at the thing in her hand and asked, \"What is this?\"","He Zhiran directly handed the telescope over to him.","\"Aim it at here, try it yourself.\"","She felt that actual practice was more convenient than her explaining, and it would also let Mo Jiuye see if he was familiar with those two people.","He Zhiran stared at Mo Jiuye closely, and saw his originally relaxed eyebrows instantly turn into a crease.","From Mo Jiuye's expression, it wasn't difficult to see that he must recognize those two men, or at least recognize one of them.","She eagerly asked,","\"Who are they?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't answer immediately, but continued to watch for a while before retrieving the telescope.","\"It's Nan Heng.\"","\"Nan Heng?\"","He Zhiran continued to ask, \"Do you recognize the other one?\"","Mo Jiuye frowned, \"Seeing the figure, it looks familiar, but I don't dare to confirm it now.\"","He Zhiran surveyed around, and said softly, \"Why don't we go check on the painted boat.\"","Even if she didn't say it, Mo Jiuye also had this intention.","Not to mention whether Nan Heng was related to the Salt Gang, just based on the point that he had sent so many assassins to assassinate himself, Mo Jiuye didn’t plan on easily letting him off.","And the bearded man, although he hadn't seen his appearance clearly, he felt a sense of familiarity in his heart for some unknown reason.","No matter what, he would have to take the risk and find out what's going on on that painted boat today.","\"There are Nan Heng’s guards all around the painted boat, I’ll swim over alone to check things out, you can just wait here for me.\"","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye was worried about her safety, however, waiting safely here was not her style at all.","\"You take me along, we’ll buy a rubber dinghy on Taobao and row over there, then we can take action as the opportunity arises. And in case those people find us, with me there, I can still bring you into space to hide temporarily. Besides, as you know clearly, I can take out some good stuff here anytime to deal with emergencies.\"","Through understanding over this period of time, Mo Jiuye also knew her temperament. Whatever she wanted to do, he simply couldn’t stop it.","\"You must follow me closely and cannot leave my side.”","\"Don’t worry!”","As the two spoke, they had already reached the lakeside.","He Zhiran carefully checked the surrounding movement again, and feeling that there was no abnormality, her consciousness swiftly entered the space and bought an inflatable rubber dinghy.","In order for the dinghy to not be noticed by people in the salt lake, she specifically selected a dark night black color.","He Zhiran quickly inflated the dinghy with an air pump, and then placed it into the lake.","Mo Jiuye held her hand and boarded it together.","In order not to startle the snake in the grass, the two didn’t dare to row too hard, for fear of raising splashes that would expose them.","When the distance to the painted boat was about a hundred meters, Mo Jiuye picked up the telescope again to check.","Then he handed the telescope to He Zhiran.","After He Zhiran took a look, she whispered, \"Are you going to shoot and kill the nearest few guards and board this ship from here?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"On the stern where we can see, there are a total of six people guarding, relatively sparse compared to other positions.”","\"Okay, I'll take the three on the left.\"","As He Zhiran spoke, she raised her arm at the same time as Mo Jiuye in tacit understanding, as the dinghy gradually approached the painted boat. The mini crossbow arrows had already aimed at the center of two guards' eyebrows.","It had to be said, the cooperation between the two was extremely tacit, with every arrow hitting its target.","In just an instant, after a few arrows were shot out, the six guards that could clearly be seen with the naked eye fell to the ground.","Without a doubt, Mo Jiuye hugged He Zhiran by the waist and directly leapt onto the deck using Qinggong, while at the same time, He Zhiran also put away the dinghy into the space.","On the deck, the six guards had completely lost their voice.","Looking ahead, there were also guards on patrol duty, and not only that, a group of on-duty guards had just passed by here.","He Zhiran whispered a suggestion, \"For convenience, let's change into the guards' clothes.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, first stripped off the clothes of a slightly smaller guard and threw them to He Zhiran, then found a guard uniform similar to his own stature and put them on.","Just as the two tidied up, a team of patrolling guards came straight towards their faces.","The guards saw that there were only two people here and asked, \"Where are your other men?\"","Mo Jiuye calmly replied, \"They ate something bad and all have upset stomachs, so they went to the toilet.\"","The guards did not doubt much further and routinely passed them to continue patrolling.","Seeing those guards walk away, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran went one after the other up the stairs leading to the second floor of the painted boat.","In comparison, the second floor was much livelier, with not only guards on duty, but also many people dressed in ordinary civilian clothes sitting at small tables drinking and playing dice.","Mo Jiuye judged that these people dressed in ordinary civilian clothes should all be members of the Salt Gang.","So obviously, even if Nan Heng was not the real person behind the Salt Gang, he was also inextricably linked with them.","Moreover, judging from the behaviour of those Salt Gang members, Nan Heng was very familiar with them.","Mo Jiuye observed for a while, then directly took He Zhiran and leapt onto the top of the painted boat.","He found a position close to Nan Heng and poked a small hole in the ceiling to look down.","Just then, they saw a small boat drifting over not far from the painted boat.","In the moonlight they could see someone standing with hands behind their back at the bow, judging by the figure, it seemed to be a woman.","Soon guards came to report,","\"Reporting to Prince Heng, the Imperial Tutor has arrived.\"","Nan Heng pushed away the woman in his arms to the side, got up to tidy his clothes of creases.","\"Take this prince to personally welcome her.\""]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138: The Mohist Spirit is Too Tough.","paragraphs":["Nan Heng walked towards the outside of the cabin, while the bearded man still sat upright, without even moving his head once.","This was somewhat similar to when Mo Chuhan was under the puppet gu spell, yet also different.","When Mo Chuhan was under the puppet gu, although he had no consciousness, he could still move. The man before them now not only seemed to have no consciousness, but his body also appeared rigid.","For now, they could only ignore the bearded man and observe Nan Heng's actions.","The small boat soon met up with the painted boat. Nan Heng ordered his men to lower the ladder to welcome the Imperial Tutor.","Unexpectedly, the Imperial Tutor did not climb up the ladder. Her body made a slight leap and landed right in front of Nan Heng.","Nan Heng laughed obsequiously.","\"This king has been respectfully awaiting the Imperial Tutor for a long time. Please come inside.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye carefully observed the Imperial Tutor from atop the cabin.","She was indeed a woman, appearing to be around forty years old. Her clothing was no different from those worn by people of Great Shun. Her face, bearing some traces left by the years, still retained its charm.","He Zhiran softly asked, \"Do you recognize this Imperial Tutor?\"","Killing intent brimmed in Mo Jiuye's dark eyes. \"Of course. Even in death I would not forget her.\"","From Mo Jiuye's expression, He Zhiran could see how much he hated the woman before them.","But now was not the time to inquire about the reasons behind this.","To avoid exposing themselves, the two tacitly held their breath and continued watching the situation below.","Nan Heng respectfully led the Imperial Tutor into the cabin and gestured invitingly towards the chief seat.","The Imperial Tutor sat down casually, one hand propping up her forehead, a somewhat indolent pose.","\"This Imperial Tutor has said it before. The Mohists' mindset is too stubborn and hard to control. Yet you refused to listen.\"","Upon hearing the words \"Mohist people\", He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye's hearts tightened at the same time.","Mo Jiuye instinctively glanced over at the bearded man.","In order to see more clearly, he shifted slightly to view from another angle.","But when he looked again, he couldn't help but gasp. If not for the rationality still left in him, he would have leapt down this instant to save the man.","Sensing his change in emotions, and already having her own guesses about the situation, He Zhiran took the initiative to grasp Mo Jiuye's hand.","The moment she held his hand, He Zhiran could clearly feel that his palm was already damp with sweat.","Mo Jiuye whispered, \"That man is my third brother.\"","He Zhiran had already speculated this possibility earlier, so she did not appear too shocked.","Like Mo Jiuye, countless questions had appeared in her mind.","But both understood clearly that now was not the time to seek answers to these questions. They continued observing the situation below.","Nan Heng gave an embarrassed laugh. Glancing at Mo Yunfeng, still sitting there motionless like a dead man, he continued, \"Imperial Tutor, as you know, back then I painstakingly built up my power and influence in the Salt Gang, only for it to be completely annihilated by Mo Yunfeng in one strike.","Over the past two years, I spent tremendous effort to restore the Salt Gang. You've witnessed this too.","Right now, the Salt Gang lacks an obedient leader of high martial prowess. I feel Mo Yunfeng is the most suitable candidate.","Just as he once brought my Salt Gang to ruin, in the future he must rebuild and expand it even more splendidly for me.","And if misfortune should strike the Salt Gang again, the blame would fall on the Mohists.\"","The Imperial Tutor gazed coldly at Mo Yunfeng. Then she said in a frosty tone, \"This Imperial Tutor captured Mo Yunfeng back then not for you to take revenge.\"","Nan Heng smiled obsequiously again. \"Naturally this king understands the Imperial Tutor's intentions. However, don't you think keeping Mo Yunfeng here would be of even greater use?\"","The Imperial Tutor looked down, eyes lowered. \"His willpower is too strong. This Imperial Tutor will make one final attempt. If it still fails, hand him to me to bring away.\"","As she spoke, the Imperial Tutor took out a small porcelain bottle from her bosom.","Right at the moment she was about to uncork it, two arrows simultaneously shot towards her from the cabin roof!","The Imperial Tutor reacted swiftly. Her body nimbly evaded the arrows, while rapidly putting the small bottle back into her bosom.","Nan Heng yelled, \"Men, there are assassins!\"","The cabin doors were quickly shoved open from outside. A group of armed guards swarmed noisily in, together with the Salt Gang members who were originally gambling and boxing in there.","Nan Heng pointed upwards. \"The assassins are up there! Search them out! Leave no survivors!\"","The Imperial Tutor also leapt upwards towards the cabin roof, drawing out her soft sword.","Seeing the situation turn dire, He Zhiran pulled Mo Jiuye along to enter the space right after shooting their arrows.","She was clear that there would likely be a fierce battle tonight. It even held an implication that either they died or their opponents perished.","Of course, He Zhiran only thought this way to psych herself up for their next move.","With such a heaven-defying space on their side, the dead ones would definitely be their opponents.","Inside the space, the two swiftly changed into dark clothes, masking their faces with scarves. After suffering through an agonizing wait of about ten minutes, sensing that the searchers still found nothing above the cabin and would start looking elsewhere, He Zhiran decided to exit first to investigate. If the danger had not receded, she would return here.","In any case, to her it was just a matter of thought. Even if those people discovered her, they would dismiss it as a trick of eyes.","Considering that Mo Jiuye might not let her take the risk alone, He Zhiran exited the space stealthily without informing him.","Sure enough, the instant Mo Jiuye saw her vanish abruptly before him, anxiety gripped his heart.","But right now, he was too powerless to do anything.","Just as Mo Jiuye was anxious and antsy, He Zhiran's figure reappeared before him.","\"They've started searching below. Let's get out now.\"","No sooner had she finished speaking than the two emerged atop the cabin roof. Indeed, all the guards were searching below them now, torches in hand.","Inside the cabin, Mo Yunfeng was still seated motionless as before, with two guards stationed at the doorway.","Exchanging a look, the two leapt down from the roof, swords flashing to dispose of the guards at the door.","Arriving before Mo Yunfeng, Mo Jiuye softly called out a couple of times, but Mo Yunfeng showed no reaction whatsoever.","With a wave of her hand, He Zhiran directly sent the man into her space.","From Mo Yunfeng's condition, he was likely under the puppet gu, same as Mo Chuhan previously.","Right now, he would retain no memory whatsoever of what occurred. As long as they removed him from the space after he regained consciousness, things would be fine.","Seeing He Zhiran successfully bring his third brother into the space, Mo Jiuye pulled her along to exit the cabin with him.","Just as they reached the doorway, they bumped right into the Imperial Tutor face-to-face.","\"Assassins are here!\" shouted the Imperial Tutor. Wielding her soft sword, she slashed towards the two.","Mo Jiuye wrapped his arm around He Zhiran's waist to shield her behind him, while raising the commando knife in his hand to block the Imperial Tutor's strike.","The two swiftly fell into battle.","At the same time, at the Imperial Tutor's loud shout, the summoned guards rushed over to join the melee.","After exchanging just a few moves with Mo Jiuye, the Imperial Tutor realized she was no match for him. Moreover, right before her eyes, his companion took out a packet of powder and sprinkled it. Her guards immediately collapsed in swathes."]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139: Painted Boat on Fire","paragraphs":["The Imperial Tutor saw that things were not going her way. She feigned a few moves with her hands and reached into her robe with one hand.","At this moment, He Zhiran had just finished spraying the second round of her homemade \"Grim Reaper's Descend\" toward those guards. When she turned her head and saw what the Imperial Tutor was doing, she realized something was wrong.","If her guess was correct, the Imperial Tutor was either trying to pull out some hidden weapons or was planning to use poison against them.","How could He Zhiran give her such a chance? She immediately took out a tranquilizer gun from her space and shot it at the Imperial Tutor's calves.","With a muffled bang, the Imperial Tutor's whole body collapsed limply.","He Zhiran went up and quickly sent her into her space. She and Mo Jiuye headed toward the first floor of the Painted Boat.","At the stairwell, they happened to run into Nan Heng, who was being escorted up by a group of guards and Salt Gang members.","He Zhiran whispered to Mo Jiuye, \"You take care of Nan Heng. I'll handle the others.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded lightly. He also raised a tranquilizer gun and fired it at Nan Heng's shoulder.","The moment Nan Heng fell to the ground, He Zhiran sprayed a handful of powder at those guards and Salt Gang members.","Before the guards and gang members could react to what was happening, they collapsed in piles with a swoosh.","He Zhiran took the opportunity to rush forward and grabbed one of Nan Heng's arms before sending him into her space too.","Today, they had only come out of curiosity, wanting to find out who was behind the Salt Gang. But they never expected to gain such a great harvest.","Looking at the dead guards and gang members now, the two still did not dare to underestimate the situation. They knew they could not leave anyone alive regarding what happened today with Prince Nan Heng.","So the two went through the entire Painted Boat with torches in hand, not leaving a single living soul other than those singing and dancing girls.","Neither Mo Jiuye nor He Zhiran were the sort to kill innocents.","They both knew clearly that those female performers made their living in the Painted Boat.","Even so, they did not dare be too careless either, not sure if some of those performers might be Nan Heng’s people.","Left with no choice, He Zhiran could only take out a drug from her space that paralyzed nerves and made the girls take it, erasing all their memories.","In order to survive, none of the singing and dancing girls dared resist ingesting the medicine she gave them.","With everything taken care of, He Zhiran sent all the girls onto the small boat that the Imperial Tutor had arrived on.","Next, He Zhiran took out several bottles of alcohol from her space, pouring them around the Painted Boat with Mo Jiuye.","At the same time, any items in the Painted Boat that He Zhiran felt were worth taking were stored away into her space one by one.","Whether these items were good or bad, they could still be sold as antiques in her shop.","After handling everything, He Zhiran took an inflatable boat from her space and threw it into the lake. Mo Jiuye wrapped his arm around her waist and leapt lightly onto the boat.","Mo Jiuye casually flung the torch in his hand onto the Painted Boat.","In the pitch dark night sky, flames burst forth into the heavens...","The light here was too bright. To avoid discovery from people on shore, Mo Jiuye utilized his inner strength while rowing to propel their inflatable boat to extreme speeds.","In the blink of an eye, the two returned to shore.","They could hear footsteps approaching not too far off. This meant the raging fire from the Painted Boat had already attracted the attention of those on land.","Luckily their speed to shore was fast, and no one discovered them.","He Zhiran stored away the inflatable boat. Mo Jiuye used his lightness skill to carry her up and swiftly left the area.","When they were about a hundred meters from their camp, Mo Jiuye spotted a swaying black shadow up ahead.","Unable to clearly see the other person in the dark windy night, they could only carefully approach the shadow to investigate.","Before Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran even got close, Mo Chuhan called out, “Is that Ninth Younger Brother and Sister-in-Law?\"","\"Eighth elder brother? What are you doing here?\" The two were clearly very shocked.","When they had left earlier, they had specifically observed things carefully and did not notice anything out of the ordinary.","\"I saw you two secretly leaving and was worried you’d run into danger, so I've been standing guard here waiting for you.”","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked at each other.","Without needing to say it aloud, they both thought the same thing – should they tell Mo Chuhan what just happened?","If they said nothing, they would still have to make up all kinds of excuses to Mo Yunfeng later when he returned home.","If they told him the truth, how would they explain Mo Yunfeng's current whereabouts?","Moreover, He Zhiran did not want to contribute her own opinion on the matter. After all, it was something between the Mo brothers.","After contemplating for a bit, Mo Jiuye spoke, “Eighth elder brother, we just went to check out the Painted Boat on Salt Lake a moment ago and ran into Nan Heng there...”","Mo Jiuye did not conceal anything and truthfully recounted to his brother all that had occurred on the Painted Boat, including the news that Mo Yunfeng was still alive.","Of course, the cheating methods they employed could definitely not be mentioned.","Upon hearing this, Mo Chuhan's expression was almost identical to when Mo Jiuye had discovered him alive back then.","\"Ninth younger brother, you're saying third elder brother isn't dead either? Where is he? Hurry and take me to see him!\"","At the moment, Mo Yunfeng was inside He Zhiran's space. How could Mo Jiuye take Mo Chuhan to find him?","Left with no alternative, he could only lie.","\"Eighth elder brother, we set the Painted Boat on fire and it drew many onlookers. Considering that bringing third elder brother along would easily attract unwanted attention, we hid him somewhere secluded for now.","Tomorrow when it is safer, I will go with Sister-in-Law to remove his Gu curse and bring him back.\"","Mo Chuhan did not doubt his explanation at all. He could only suppress the anxiousness in his heart and nodded, \"That works too. I will accompany you guys tomorrow to bring third elder brother back.\"","Mo Jiuye quickly dissuaded, \"No, the Salt Lake area has been unstable lately. I'm worried about everyone's safety, so one of us brothers must stay behind to protect our family.\"","There was no argument - nowadays, Mo Jiuye's ability to bluff people left nothing to be desired. Although somewhat reluctantly, Mo Chuhan had no choice but to concede that the Ninth Younger Brother made sense.","\"Since that is the case, eighth elder brother shall remain to protect our family. Ninth younger brother and sister-in-law must be extra careful when you head out.\"","Seeing that Mo Chuhan had already turned to walk back, He Zhiran spoke up to remind him.","“Eighth elder brother, don’t mention any of this to Mother and my sister-in-laws before we bring back third elder brother. Otherwise they may worry too much.\"","In fact, He Zhiran was being cautious. With such a huge incident regarding Nan Heng's disappearance, there would definitely be officials searching everywhere. If the women became too anxious and the officers detected something off, it would render things not worth the gain.","Mo Chuhan nodded. \"Mm, I understand.\"","The three silently returned to their own tents. Just as He Zhiran was about to take Mo Jiuye to enter her space together, Liang Hao’s voice sounded from outside the tent.","“Ninth master, your subordinate has an urgent report.\"","Mo Jiuye knew exactly what matter Liang Hao was referring to, except that he could not admit what they had done.","Mo Jiuye feigned having just woken up from his sleep and walked out of the tent.","“What is it?”","Liang Hao glanced around before lowering his voice. “Ninth master, the largest Painted Boat on Salt Lake caught fire. Your subordinate personally witnessed Prince Heng bring people onto that Painted Boat.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. “Mm, continue keeping watch. Report immediately if there is any new development.\"","This time, Mo Jiuye was not merely perfunctorily appeasing Liang Hao. He truly wanted to understand what would happen following the Painted Boat fire and Prince Heng’s disappearance.","Liang Hao took his leave once more. Only then did Mo Jiuye return into the tent.","He Zhiran brought him into her space with a flash."]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140: If I die, he dies with me.","paragraphs":["Mo Yunfeng still looked like a puppet, standing there with a blank expression, giving off a terracotta warrior vibe at first glance.","Nan Heng and the National Teacher were still in a coma.","The two tacitly walked up, He Zhiran went to search the National Teacher's body while Mo Jiuye went to search Nan Heng's body.","He Zhiran's harvest was considerable.","Apart from over ten thousand taels of silver bills on the National Teacher's body, there was also the small porcelain bottle she had just taken out.","In addition, there were a few packs of medicinal powder.","After examining for a while, He Zhiran knew these were all poisons used for self-defense, basically similar to the “Death Descends” she had just used.","On Nan Heng’s side, Mo Jiuye also searched out a few thousand taels of silver bills on his body, as well as a high-quality jade pendant.","Apart from that, Nan Heng had nothing else on him.","He Zhiran was very curious about the small porcelain bottle on the National Teacher’s body.","If her guess was correct, what was most likely inside was the mother Gu worm of the puppet Gu.","However, considering the mother Gu's ability to recognize its host, she did not dare to rashly open the bottle stopper without complete assurance.","After searching, Mo Jiuye tied the person up with ropes before walking towards He Zhiran’s direction.","He Zhiran could see that the hatred Mo Jiuye showed towards that National Teacher was by no means ordinary.","Without waiting for her to ask, Mo Jiuye took the initiative to say, \"My Mo Family has a blood feud with this person. My big brother and second brother died at her hands at the same time.","Moreover, her identity is very special. She is not only the National Teacher of the Southern Border, but also the Queen of the Southern Border.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran gasped.","If Mo Jiuye had not mentioned it, she would never have imagined that the big brother and second brother of the Mo Family would have died at the hands of a woman.","After all, the history books only briefly recorded the deaths of the Mo Family people without explaining it in too much detail.","Mo Jiuye paused for a moment before continuing, \"This person is proficient in using poison. Back then, my big brother and second brother had already killed the local commander-in-chief. Just as they were about to attack the city, this woman used poison on them.","My two brothers were caught off guard by her sinister move and died on the spot as a result.","That vicious woman even ordered people to cut off my brothers' heads and hang them on the city tower to show the public.\"","At this moment, Mo Jiuye's eyes were already filled with killing intent. If he didn't still have questions to ask, he would have already taken this woman's life.","He Zhiran could understand his mood at the moment. She walked up and tied up the National Teacher tightly before taking out a syringe to inject her to quickly wake her up.","The National Teacher was still a little confused, but she was soon shocked by the scene in front of her.","Without thinking too much, Mo Jiuye's military knife was already against her throat.","\"Witch, tell me, was the puppet Gu on Mo Yunfeng's body cast by you?\"","The National Teacher was instantly stung by the cold blade and gasped before looking at the speaker.","She saw a man and a woman in front of her.","Although the woman was wearing a black night walk outfit, she still couldn't hide her breathtaking beauty. However, this person was completely unfamiliar to her.","As for the man who spoke, she was no stranger.","\"Mo Jiuye?\"","\"Yun Li, now that you have fallen into my hands, it is impossible for you to have a chance to live. If you don't want to suffer too much physical pain, tell me what you know truthfully.\" There was a piercing chill in Mo Jiuye's voice.","Yun Li sneered, \"Hehe... How do you know I must die?\"","As she spoke, Yun Li seemed to use some secret technique to shrink her body slightly, and the ropes tied to her body instantly slipped off.","Regaining her freedom, Yun Li instinctively reached into her bosom to take her life-saving medicinal powder.","Mo Jiuye was also quick to act. Just as her fingers had just probed a little into her bosom, his hand rose and the knife fell directly chopping off one of her hands.","Yun Li screamed in pain, then her upper body tilted back, and she nimbly stood up with a carp flip.","At the same time, the tip of Mo Jiuye's knife was once again pressed against her throat.","As if unaware of the pain, Yun Li lowered her eyes to glance at the chilling sharp blade, and her tone also showed signs of softening.","\"Mo Jiuye, Mo Yunfeng's life is in my hands. Once I die, he will accompany me in death.\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye became more certain of one problem.","The puppet Gu in third brother's body was indeed Yun Li's handiwork.","This was also another reason why he had forcibly endured not killing Yun Li on the spot just now.","Seeing the situation, He Zhiran took out the tranquilizer gun again and knocked Yun Li unconscious.","In order not to let Yun Li die immediately from excessive blood loss, He Zhiran simply treated her wound before telling Mo Jiuye, \"First remove the Gu from third brother.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, and the two tacitly went to the operating room.","With the experience of removing Gu for Mo Chuhan last time, their speed this time was very fast. It was completed in less than an hour.","The larva Gu worm was put into a glass bottle in the same way.","However, He Zhiran did not immediately add plasma to the bottle like last time.","Mo Yunfeng was still unconscious at the moment. In order to prevent him from waking up prematurely and discovering the space's secret, He Zhiran gave him another dose of tranquilizer before leaving, thus ensuring foolproofness.","Mo Jiuye stared at the two bottles containing the puppet Gu offspring for a while, and spoke of the doubts in his heart.","\"Just now, Yun Li only mentioned that third brother's life was in her hands. Could it be that the puppet Gu in eighth brother has nothing to do with her?\"","He Zhiran picked up the bottle containing the larva Gu worm taken from Mo Chuhan's body.","\"Whether it has anything to do with her or not, we'll know after trying.\"","As they spoke, the two had already taken the glass bottle containing the larva from Mo Chuhan's body to the farm. They also took out the small porcelain bottle found on Yun Li's body.","The two bottles containing the mother and offspring of the puppet Gu were placed on the open space about ten meters apart.","According to the records in the Gu Insects Compendium, once the offspring Gu of the puppet Gu leaves the host body, it will immediately rush towards the mother Gu.","Puppet Gu fears fire. In order to truly kill the puppet Gu, strong firepower is required.","For this purpose, He Zhiran directly bought a flamethrower from Taobao Treasure Mall and set the flame to maximum before handing it to Mo Jiuye.","Once the offspring Gu rushes towards the mother Gu, it means that the person who used the puppet Gu on the eighth brother is Yun Li.","Finding the mastermind, then that offspring Gu worm would be of no use.","On the other hand, if that doesn't happen, they would have to continue raising this offspring Gu to find the true caster.","Mo Jiuye nodded to indicate that he understood.","With one hand holding the flamethrower and the other hand holding the glass bottle tightly, he was ready to deal with it.","The two tacitly looked at each other and then He Zhiran slowly opened the bottle stopper.","I saw the larva Gu desperately flying out of the glass bottle as if escaping and did not rush towards the porcelain bottle at the other end of the open space.","Perhaps due to being in the space, the larva Gu was unable to discern directions.","It thrashed around chaotically like a frightened fly.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye’s body made a graceful leap and he quickly collected the larva Gu back into the glass bottle.","The two of them looked at each other and the answer was self-evident.","The controller of this larva Gu was not Yun Li!","With the same method, they took the larva Gu worm removed from Mo Yunfeng's body to conduct an experiment."]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141: Hypnotic Cloudplough","paragraphs":["This time was completely different from the last.","As soon as Mo Yunfeng's puppet worm regained its freedom, it flew straight towards the porcelain bottle containing the mother worm.","However, the mother worm was not released. The puppet worm could only circle around the porcelain bottle.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye immediately went forward and pressed the switch of the flamethrower, burning it alive.","At the same time, he could clearly see that the porcelain bottle containing the mother worm shook a few times.","Without a doubt, the puppet worm in Mo Yunfeng was indeed Yun Li's doing.","Now that Mo Yunfeng's puppet worm was removed, there was no need to worry about Yun Li using his life to threaten them.","The two returned to Yun Li.","He Zhiran was now uncertain whether Yun Li still had puppet worms that had dispersed, and even more unsure whether there were people related to the Mo family among those controlled by the puppet worms.","Therefore, she did not dare to be too careless when interrogating Yun Li.","She considered that Yun Li had been tranquilized twice, equivalent to being fully anesthetized twice.","In her previous life as a military doctor, she knew this best.","No matter how strong one's will usually was, after going through full body anesthesia twice in a row, one's mind would become much weaker.","She intended to take advantage of this time to hypnotize Yun Li.","Once successful, it would also save a lot of trouble.","In order to increase the success rate of hypnosis, He Zhiran directly bought a pocket watch and a professional hypnotic music player.","She placed the music player next to Yun Li, and selected a piece of music that she felt had the best hypnotic effect to play on repeat.","After preparing all this, He Zhiran woke Yun Li up.","As soon as Yun Li opened her eyes, she saw a strange thing swinging in front of her.","\"Mo Jiuye, I advise you not to play any tricks. If you want Mo Yunfeng's life, release me immediately, otherwise I don't mind taking it now...\"","Her voice got smaller and smaller, to the point that she didn't finish her sentence before her eyes became dull.","Seeing this, He Zhiran first tentatively asked, \"What is your name and identity?\"","\"My name is Yun Li. I am the Queen of Southern Borderland and the respected National Teacher of Southern Borderland.\"","Yun Li's voice was somewhat low, and He Zhiran could feel that there was no emotion mixed in it.","He Zhiran could determine that she had entered a hypnotized state.","She continued to ask, \"When did you start using puppet worms to control Mo Yunfeng?\"","Yun Li: \"Four years ago, during the battle with Southern Borderland, he was knocked unconscious by my means and then captured. At that time, my mother worm had just matured, so I used him for experiments.\"","He Zhiran: \"There are many people who can be used for experiments. Why choose Mo Yunfeng?\"","Yun Li: \"My master told me that the Mo family are extremely tenacious. If my puppet worms can successfully control a Mo family member, it can prove that my worm-rearing skills have reached graduation level.\"","He Zhiran: \"Besides controlling Mo Yunfeng, who else have you controlled?\"","Yun Li: \"Only Mo Yunfeng.\"","He Zhiran: \"Why only one person?\"","Yun Li: \"I still couldn't completely control Mo Yunfeng's will, so the mother worm couldn't continue producing puppet worms to control others.\"","He Zhiran: \"Do you know Mo Chuhan?\"","Yun Li: \"Of course I know him. Mo Chuhan was the strongest Mo family warrior. It's a pity that he's already dead.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked at each other. They both knew that at this time, Yun Li could not be lying.","So they could confirm one thing - that Yun Li did not know that Mo Chuhan was still alive.","This also explained another problem: Yun Li was even more unaware of the person who had given Mo Chuhan a puppet worm.","After exchanging looks, He Zhiran waved the pocket watch and continued to ask:","\"How many Mo men have died at your hands?\"","Hearing this question, Mo Jiuye's eyes had already turned red as he stared fiercely at Yun Li.","Yun Li: \"No Mo family members have died at my hands.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran reflexively turned to look at Mo Jiuye.","\"That's impossible,\" Mo Jiuye retorted.","In order not to let Mo Jiuye's emotions affect Yun Li too much, He Zhiran quickly made a \"shush\" gesture at him.","Mo Jiuye hurriedly closed his mouth.","He Zhiran knew that her hypnosis skills were not good enough to control the other party for long. She had to hurry up and ask more things.","\"Didn't Mo Junrui and Mo Jiacheng die at your hands back then?\"","Yun Li: \"They didn't die. I only gave them sleeping drugs.\"","He Zhiran: \"Then whose heads were those hung on the city tower?\"","Yun Li: \"Those were two random heads we found. Their faces were covered in blood, and they were hung so high up that we could say they were anyone.\"","He Zhiran: \"Since they're not dead, where are those two now?\"","Yun Li: \"They were taken away by my master.\"","He Zhiran: \"Who is your master?\"","Yun Li: \"My master... My master is...\"","She didn't finish her sentence before her head started shaking violently.","\"I can't say, I can't say... Ah... My head hurts so much...\"","Seeing Yun Li's state, so different from after she had woken up from hypnosis, He Zhiran was somewhat confused.","So she tried to adjust the swinging frequency of the pocket watch slightly.","\"Look here, don't be afraid. You are safe here.\"","Soon, Yun Li's emotions gradually stabilized.","He Zhiran: \"According to your understanding, how many Mo men are still alive in this world?\"","Yun Li: \"Mo Junrui and Mo Jiacheng are with my master, Mo Yunfeng is under my control, and there is the lucky Mo Jiuye. I tried to make a move on him several times but he always managed to escape.\"","He Zhiran: \"Does the Mo family banishment have anything to do with you?\"","Yun Li: \"That was because Emperor Shunwu was arrogant and suspicious. That was why the Mo family ended up like that.\"","He Zhiran: \"What is your relationship with Nan Heng?\"","Yun Li: \"A relationship of mutual use.\"","He Zhiran: \"Explain in detail how you make use of each other.\"","Yun Li: \"Nan Heng wants to compete for the position of Crown Prince. He needs my help from Southern Borderland. He promised me that after he ascended the throne, he would cede three cities to Southern Borderland, and supply Southern Borderland with 200,000 catties of grain every year.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran gasped.","How was Nan Heng's actions any different from selling out his country?","Mo Jiuye also clenched his fists tightly.","At this moment, he deeply realized how little the Mo family's decades of sacrifice to protect the Da Shun Dynasty had been worth.","With just a light sentence from Nan Heng, he could hand over the territory they had guarded for decades.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye glared fiercely at the still unconscious Nan Heng.","He hated that he could not kill this traitorous profiteer right now and feed his body to the dogs.","However, reason told him that Nan Heng was going to die, but definitely not now.","He Zhiran gently tugged Mo Jiuye's arm to signal him not to get agitated.","Seeing Mo Jiuye's emotions recover a little, she softly asked, \"Time's almost up. Is there anything else you want to ask?\"","Following He Zhiran's example, Mo Jiuye carefully approached Yun Li.","\"Why did Mo Yunfeng appear at the Salt Gang headquarters?\""]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142: Do You Want to Rebel","paragraphs":["Yun Li: \"Nan Heng accidentally saw me controlling Mo Yunfeng. He used 100 bags of salt to exchange for Mo Yunfeng to go work for him.\"","Mo Jiuye: \"What did Nan Heng ask Mo Yunfeng to do?\"","Yun Li: \"He said Mo Yunfeng brought people to wipe out the Salt Gang that he had put years of effort to support. Now there is no one by his side with high martial arts skills and obedience to be the head of the Salt Gang. He felt that Mo Yunfeng was the most suitable.","Not only can I control his will, but I can also make him fight one against a hundred with a wave of my hand.\"","Mo Jiuye: \"Why did you meet with Nan Heng today?\"","Yun Li: \"Mo Yunfeng often breaks free of my control by the witch insect. As a last resort, I can only manipulate the mother witch insect to make him lose consciousness for a short period of time.","During this period, I will also rush to Mo Yunfeng's side immediately and let the mother witch insect take control at close range.","A few days ago, I found that something was wrong with the mother witch insect. I knew there was a problem with Mo Yunfeng, so I rushed over to help.\"","Mo Jiuye felt that he had understood most of what he wanted to know. The next step was to kill this enemy he had hated for years.","However, before that, he still wanted to ask Yun Li who her master was again. Considering that Yun Li had an abnormal reaction just now when He Zhiran asked who her master was.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye decided to ask in a different way. \"Where is your master now?\"","Sure enough, as long as he didn't ask who her master was, Yun Li would not get too excited.","\"My master travels around the year. His whereabouts are unpredictable. I haven't seen him for three years.\"","Mo Jiuye frowned: \"What are the characteristics of your master?\"","Yun Li: \"My master looks young despite his white hair. When he travels outside, he often wears a black cloak. Also, he likes to dress up as a woman. That's all I know.\"","Mo Jiuye: \"Who exactly is your master?\"","As soon as his voice fell, Yun Li screamed in pain again holding her head.","\"I can't say...I can't say...\"","He Zhiran adjusted the shaking frequency of the pocket watch again, but this time it didn't work at all.","After Yun Li's cries for a few times, her eyes became clearer.","He Zhiran knew clearly that her hypnosis on Yun Li had failed.","After Yun Li regained consciousness, she was ignorant of what had just happened.","She still stared at Mo Jiuye mockingly.","\"I can tell you openly that Mo Yunfeng is controlled by my puppet witch insect. Once I die, the mother witch insect I raise will die with me.","You are also a well-informed person. I guess you can understand without me explaining further what is going to happen next, right?\"","Of course Mo Jiuye knew what would happen after Yun Li died.","All that would happen was that she and the mother witch insect would die together, and the offspring witch insects inhabiting the body would also die with the death of the mother witch insect, and the body hosting the offspring witch insects would perish together.","However, what Yun Li didn't know was that the offspring witch insect in Mo Yunfeng's body had been successfully removed. Even if she died, she would only perish together with the mother witch insect she raised, and would not affect Mo Yunfeng at all.","Seeing Mo Jiuye keeping silent, she sneered, \"Hehe... How is it, Mo Jiuye? Are you scared?","If you let me go now, maybe I'll be so happy that I'll consider letting Mo Yunfeng off the hook.","If you are still stubborn...\"","Yun Li glanced down at her arm that had been severed.","\"Anyway, I have become a cripple now. What's the fear of death?\"","Mo Jiuye was too lazy to continue talking nonsense with her. His hand rose with the knife and cut off Yun Li's other arm again.","A bloody, fair-skinned jade arm fell to the ground. He Zhiran walked over indifferently to wipe the sweat from Mo Jiuye's forehead that had oozed out due to his extremely agitated mood.","She could understand the hatred in Mo Jiuye's heart.","If it were her, not to mention chopping off her arms with one slash, even cutting Yun Li into thousands of pieces would not relieve the hatred in her heart.","Raising such vicious puppet witch insects to harm people was simply unforgivable.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran turned around and walked back to the medical room.","She had a vial there specially made to torture prisoners of war by people of a certain country .","Using this on someone like Yun Li was most suitable.","He Zhiran picked up a small vial and returned. She suddenly opened the bottle in front of Yun Li and poured all the liquid in the bottle onto her face.","At first Yun Li didn't feel anything and continued to threaten Mo Jiuye with Mo Yunfeng's life. However, just after a few seconds, her face began to feel burnt.","She instinctively wanted to grab her face with her hands before realizing that she had just lost both hands.","\"Mo Jiuye, what have you done to me? Ah...it hurts so much...\"","Yun Li screamed in an almost frenzied manner.","Although Mo Jiuye didn't know what He Zhiran poured on Yun Li's face, he was very clear that the stuff she took out must be something good. Therefore, he stopped attacking Yun Li and just stood not far away, staring at her quietly with his deep eyes.","Yun Li's face began to fester gradually, and her former beautiful face vanished instantly.","The only way to identify her now was her increasingly hoarse voice.","Tied up with ropes and lying not far away, Nan Heng seemed to be awakened by these jarring screams.","He looked towards the sound and saw a bloodied woman twisting in pain on the ground. When he recognized the woman's face clearly, he was almost scared to death.","However, he soon judged from the painful screams and her outfit that this person was Yun Li.","\"National Teacher, what happened to you?\"","While asking, Nan Heng instinctively tried to get up and run away, before realizing that his hands and feet were tied up tightly and he was completely immobilized.","He looked around subconsciously.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye had already changed into the coarse linen clothes he wore during his exile.","Nan Heng recognized him at a glance.","\"Mo Jiuye, do you want to rebel? How dare you kidnap me.\"","Mo Jiuye sneered coldly, \"Didn't you and your father already determine that I was rebelling and colluding with foreign enemies?\"","Hearing this, Nan Heng panicked somewhat.","Mo Jiuye's words were very clear that he no longer cared about the alleged rebellion. If so, what leverage did he have left to threaten him?","\"Mo Jiuye, you...you're bold...let me go quickly. I can pardon you from your crimes!\"","At this moment Mo Jiuye was too lazy to play word games with him. He walked over and picked Nan Heng up like a chicken, throwing him directly about five meters away from Yun Li.","He Zhiran seized the opportunity to kick Nan Heng viciously several times.","\"Watch closely. If you don't want to end up like her, confess all the nasty things you've done against the Mo family.\"","At that moment, Yun Li's body just happened to roll right in front of him. Up close, Nan Heng could see clearly that pus was constantly oozing from Yun Li's face.","There were even places where the rot was so severe that the bare white bones were exposed.","Nan Heng was scared pale. At the same time, he felt a stream of heat spreading down from the base of his thighs..."]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143: Gross as Hell","paragraphs":["He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye saw the situation and both turned their heads away at the same time, simply not wanting to look directly.","He Zhiran couldn't help but say: \"It's really f**king disgusting, disgusting to open the door to disgusting, disgusting to the extreme.\"","It seemed that after dealing with these two people, she would have to carefully clean the space...","Mo Jiuye gave a cold laugh and mocked: \"A prince of the country, yet so cowardly, truly disgraceful.\"","Nan Heng himself didn't want to do such a disgraceful thing, but was frightened by the scene just now and simply unable to control himself.","Now being mocked by the two people like this, he wished he could immediately find a hole to drill into and never come out for the rest of his life.","At this time, Yun Li used all his strength to roar:","\"Mo Jiuye, even if I die I will take Mo Yunfeng down with me as a mat under me, you will regret it!\"","Nan Heng clearly understood the meaning in Yun Li's words.","In his impression, the feelings between the Mo brothers could be said to be unbreakable.","However, looking at Mo Jiuye's performance now, it was as if he did not care about Mo Yunfeng's life and death at all.","Thinking of this, the feeling of fear in Nan Heng's heart became even stronger.","A person who did not even care about his brother's life and death, it can be seen how vicious he was.","I'm afraid that no matter how he pleaded today, Mo Jiuye would not let him go.","However, at this point, Nan Heng would rather deceive himself than face reality.","\"Mo...Mo Jiuye, as long as you are willing to let this prince go, this prince can assure you that in the future when this prince successfully ascends the throne, he will definitely redress the grievances of the Mo family, and will also restore your position as Duke of Protector... No... This prince can even make you a prince of a different surname...\"","It would be strange if Mo Jiuye believed this bullshit of his.","The Mo family did need to clear their grievances, however, they did not need a cowardly drunkard to help.","Moreover, he was completely disillusioned with the court, so the temptations Nan Heng spoke out held no attraction at all to Mo Jiuye.","He glanced coldly at Nan Heng without responding.","At this moment, his and He Zhiran's goal was the same, which was to completely destroy Nan Heng's remaining will with Yun Li's miserable state.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye did not refute, Nan Heng thought he was moved by the temptations he had spoken out, so he was going to try to continue to beguile him.","Just as Nan Heng was about to open his mouth, Yun Li's constantly struggling body rolled over to his vicinity again.","Nan Heng didn't dodge fast enough and was contaminated by Yun Li's pus that just looking at made one want to vomit.","\"Yun Li, roll away from me, don't touch me.\"","Hearing Nan Heng's voice, Yun Li tried hard to control the discomfort in his body and roared:","\"Nan Heng, having fallen into Mo Jiuye's hands, what qualifications do you have to mock me?","The torture I'm undergoing now, I believe will soon fall upon you too!\"","Upon hearing this, Nan Heng's body instinctively shuddered.","He was a prince of Da Shun, he did not believe that Mo Jiuye dared to treat him like that.","\"No...that's impossible, our identities are different, Mo Jiuye doesn't dare do anything to me.\"","Seeing that Nan Heng still couldn't accept reality even when he was about to die, Yun Li mocked: \"Then just wait and see!\"","After insisting on saying so much, Yun Li's state became frenzied again.","His body rolled back and forth on the ground, and soon there was no sound.","In front of Nan Heng, He Zhiran deliberately used her mind to send Yun Li's corpse to an inconspicuous corner.","Nan Heng watched with his own eyes as the unfamiliar woman waved her little hand, and Yun Li's corpse quickly floated up and then fell to the ground.","This scene looked extremely strange in Nan Heng's eyes, and even made him think of witchcraft.","He didn't know who the beautiful woman following Mo Jiuye was, and under such special circumstances, he didn't have much energy to speculate either.","Who knew that this woman he ignored turned out to know witchcraft.","He stared at He Zhiran in frightened eyes, and his body instinctively shrank back.","\"You...who on earth are you?\"","He Zhiran, with her two lifetimes added up, looked down the most on such cowardly men.","\"You don't have the qualifications to know who I am. If you don't want the same fate as Yun Li, then honestly answer our questions.\"","At the same time, Mo Jiuye strode forward, grabbed Nan Heng's hair and lifted him up.","\"Did you hear that? If you don't want to die so miserably, confess everything you've done to the Mo family.\"","Facing Mo Jiuye's question, Nan Heng's eyes dodged a little, first looking at He Zhiran, then at the corpse thrown over there in the distance, and finally at what he had done to the Mo family.","At this time, Nan Heng's forehead was already covered in beads of sweat.","Mo Jiuye reminded him coldly again: \"Thought about what to say?\"","Nan Heng felt that he was on the verge of collapse. He shouted: \"No...Mo Jiuye, I am a prince of the Da Shun Dynasty, you cannot treat me like this...\"","Mo Jiuye had long since lost his patience with Nan Heng.","He was seen stabbing downward with the tip of the military knife in his hand toward Nan Heng's instep.","\"Are you going to say it or not?\"","Nan Heng was so pained that he immediately let out a pig-like scream.","\"Ah...Mo Jiuye, you cannot treat me like this...\"","He Zhiran glanced at the clock in the infirmary. She and Mo Jiuye had been in this space for more than two hours.","If this dragged on, it would be dawn outside.","Originally, seeing Nan Heng's cowardly appearance, she did not intend to use hypnotic methods to inquire about the situation anymore.","After all, her mastery of hypnosis was just the tip of the iceberg, and she couldn't guarantee success every time she used it.","Not to mention she had already exhausted a lot of energy when using hypnosis on Yun Li earlier. If she performed it on Nan Heng again, she was afraid the success rate would not be very high.","But under the current circumstances, they could not afford to delay any longer.","Therefore, He Zhiran decided to try to hypnotize Nan Heng again.","Just as she was about to take action, she saw that Mo Jiuye had already forced Nan Heng to open his mouth over there.","\"I'll tell you, I'll tell you everything I know, as long as you let me go.\" He was so scared by Mo Jiuye that he changed his form of address from \"this prince\" to \"me\".","Mo Jiuye did not make any promises. He shook the knife in front of Nan Heng.","\"Speak!\"","Seeing this, He Zhiran had a flash of inspiration and quickly purchased a voice recorder from Taobao Treasury.","Before Nan Heng could open his mouth, she turned on the voice recorder and switched it to the recording function, then stood by Mo Jiuye's side.","No matter if this voice recorder would come in handy in the future, it was better to be safe than sorry.","Nan Heng stared at them timidly and said, \"Some of the evidence of the Mo family's rebellion was forged by me asking the National Teacher of the Southern Border to fabricate it, and there's also... there's also...\"","Seeing Nan Heng hem and haw, Mo Jiuye urged harshly: \"What else?\"","\"There's also... also Mo Xiuyan's death...\"","Hearing Mo Xiuyan's name, the corrosive killing intent flashed through Mo Jiuye's eyes again.","He grabbed Nan Heng by the collar, interrogating: \"It was you who killed my fourth brother?\"","Recalling that in the past, his eldest brother, second brother, and third brother died on the battlefield one after another, and his fourth brother Mo Xiuyan resolutely took on the responsibility of guarding the border."]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144: Just because Mo Jiuye can't do it doesn't mean she can't do it.","paragraphs":["Unexpectedly, Nan Heng took the initiative to volunteer to Emperor Shunwu, wanting to follow Mo Xiuyan to the border pass, intending to temper himself. Six months after the Fourth Master went into battle in armor, the capital received the tragic news of his death on the battlefield.","And the person who brought back this news in person was Nan Heng.","When Nan Heng described Mo Xiuyan's death in the main hall at that time, he was extremely sad. He even claimed that he had personally led people to bury Mo Xiuyan's corpse.","At first, the Mo family was suspicious of Nan Heng, but later someone went to the border to investigate, and heard that when Mo Xiuyan died, Nan Heng was also injured because he led people to meet him.","And through some detailed analysis, Nan Heng had no reason to make a move against Mo Xiuyan, so gradually, the Mo family's suspicion of Nan Heng dissipated.","Mo Jiuye heard Nan Heng mention this with his own ears, and he was clearly aware that the Mo family had been deceived by Nan Heng's methods at that time.","Seeing Mo Jiuye's emotional excitement, Nan Heng quickly defended himself.","\"I didn't kill Mo Xiuyan, he died under the knife of the enemy.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't believe his nonsense at all. His hand grabbing his collar tightened again, making it somewhat difficult for Nan Heng to breathe at this moment.","Nan Heng's face flushed red, and he coughed violently several times.","\"Let go of this king, let go... cough cough...\"","According to Mo Jiuye's heart, he wished he could swallow Nan Heng alive now, but reason told him that he still had a lot to ask, and Nan Heng couldn't die at this time.","Seeing this, He Zhiran gently patted Mo Jiuye's body, hinting him to calm down a little, and reminded at the same time: \"Let him speak.\"","Mo Jiuye gradually relaxed his grip.","\"Speak. If you dare to have one false sentence, I will make you regret coming to this world.\"","With smooth breathing, Nan Heng coughed violently several more times. He stared at Mo Jiuye in horror, with an unspeakable posture.","The things he had done to the Mo family, no matter which one was brought out, could arouse Mo Jiuye's anger.","At this moment, Nan Heng had a dilemma.","He was even afraid that before he had finished speaking of one thing, he would die under Mo Jiuye's knife.","It seemed that He Zhiran saw his thoughts, stepped forward and persuaded:","\"I know what you are thinking. You are just worried about your life.","I assure you now that as long as you honestly tell everything you have done, I will help you persuade my husband to spare your life.\"","It was then that Nan Heng realized that this beautiful woman who knew witchcraft was actually Mo Jiuye's new wife, the legitimate daughter of He the minister.","It's just that no matter what, he couldn't imagine how the He minister's family could raise such a powerful daughter.","Seeing that he hesitated for a long time without responding, He Zhiran urged, \"The only way to survive is right in front of you. It depends on your own choice.\"","Nan Heng collected his thoughts and looked at He Zhiran.","\"Why should I believe your words?\"","He Zhiran's lips curled into a smile as she looked at Mo Jiuye, \"My husband, do you listen to me or not?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded without thinking: \"Of course I listen.\"","He Zhiran shrugged at Nan Heng: \"Did you hear that? My husband admitted in person that he would listen to me.\"","At this moment, Nan Heng seemed to have grasped the last straw to save his life.","\"Then you have to promise this king that no matter what I say, Mo Jiuye will not touch me.\"","\"Okay, I promise you on behalf of my husband.\"","Before Mo Jiuye could answer, He Zhiran took the lead.","Mo Jiuye could not take action, but that did not mean she could not take action...","Seeing this, Nan Heng's fear in his heart dissipated a little.","\"That year at the border pass, I went to resist the enemy with Mo Xiuyan on the battlefield. Seeing that the enemy troops were defeated and scattered, I rose with the idea of chasing them.","Mo Xiuyan advised me not to pursue the bandits to their lair, but I was young and arrogant at the time, wanting to gain credit so that my father the emperor would appreciate me, so I did not listen to Mo Xiuyan's dissuasion.","Not long after I led a team to chase them out, I fell into the enemy's trap.","At the critical moment, it was Mo Xiuyan who led people to meet me. He killed a bloody path for me to escape, while he and those soldiers died there.","Mo Xiuyan died to save me. He didn't have much to do with me. It was because I was grateful for his kindness that I personally led people to bury him...\"","\"Bastard! My fourth brother was such a good person, yet he died to save a beast inferior to a pig and a dog like you... Nan Heng, you bastard...\"","When Mo Jiuye heard the real reason why the fourth master died in vain to save him, he was so angry that he even cursed.","At the same time, the knife in his hand had been raised, aiming at Nan Heng, preparing to chop down.","\"Mo Jiuye, you have already promised this king that you will not touch me...\"","Seeing this, He Zhiran stepped forward and took the knife from Mo Jiuye's hand.","\"My husband, you just promised him in person that you would not touch him.\"","Facing Mo Jiuye's loss of control, she had to remind him.","It wasn't that He Zhiran was merciful. Judging from Nan Heng's current state, if Mo Jiuye acted against him again, I'm afraid it would be difficult for them to ask him anything later.","In He Zhiran's heart, revenge must be reported, but there is no need to be anxious at this moment.","After they had completely squeezed out everything Nan Heng knew, they could torture him however they wanted.","Mo Jiuye also deeply understood this truth. It was just that there was too much depression in his heart, which caused his behavior to be somewhat out of control.","After He Zhiran's reminder, his reason returned quickly. He cooperated and said, \"Okay, listen to Ranan.\"","Nan Heng had just been scared by Mo Jiuye's actions. At this moment, seeing that this woman could really restrain his temper, Nan Heng felt a little relieved in his heart.","This time, it was He Zhiran who came forward to inquire.","\"Nan Heng, I ask you, why didn't you tell the truth when my fourth brother died to save you back then?\"","At these words, Nan Heng's eyes were a little evasive, mainly avoiding Mo Jiuye.","\"You Mo family people were biased towards Nan Qi's side to begin with. If I said Mo Xiuyan's true cause of death, I was afraid you Mo family members would immediately openly defect to Nan Qi.\"","He Zhiran looked at Mo Jiuye. Mo Jiuye nodded, indicating that he had no objection to Nan Heng's answer.","She continued to ask, \"Apart from my fourth brother's affairs, what else have you done to the Mo family?\"","Nan Heng still looked at Mo Jiuye timidly: \"There is also, before the Mo family was exiled, I bribed the servants in the Duke's mansion to poison the well.\"","For Mo Jiuye, there was no dispute about this either.","At that time, the first person he thought of who might poison was Nan Heng.","Fortunately, with He Zhiran there, the Mo family escaped this disaster.","He Zhiran continued to ask, \"What else?\"","Nan Heng thought about it and continued: “Also, I accidentally discovered that Mo Yunfeng was still alive, and was under Yun Li's puppet Gu.","Thinking that he had led people to wipe out the salt gang I had painstakingly built to a certain scale, I rose with the idea of letting him work for me.\"","\"Why did you do that?\" He Zhiran asked.","\"Only by doing this can my heart's hatred be resolved.\"","It was obvious that the Mo family member Nan Heng hated the most was undoubtedly Mo Yunfeng.","They had already learned about this when hypnotizing Yun Li, and the answers of the two people were almost the same. Therefore, He Zhiran did not continue to pursue this topic."]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145: I Know Why Mohism has no Descendants.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye saw that what he had said did not anger He Zhiran again. After thinking for a while, he spoke of another matter.","\"I also sent people to ambush at Niujiaoshan, intending to take Mo Jiuye's life.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had already learned about this from the man in black earlier, so hearing Nan Heng admit it now was merely confirmation.","\"I have only done this much against the Mo family, nothing else.\"","With his hands and feet tied up by ropes, Nan Heng would have definitely raised his hand to swear an oath to make the people in front of him believe his words.","Mo Jiuye walked step by step to stand in front of him and said heavily, \"Think carefully. Have you done anything else?\"","Nan Heng shook his head vigorously: \"Really nothing else. I have only done these things.","Not only that, after I heard the news that you and Nan Qi had a falling out, I have already called back the second batch of assassins that I was going to send out.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked at each other. By instinct, they felt that Nan Heng was not lying.","Since this was the case, he no longer had any need to live.","He Zhiran picked up the knife and aimed it at Nan Heng's throat, intending to give him a quick death.","Nan Heng thought this woman did not believe his words and was going to interrogate him further.","Trembling, he shouted loudly: \"I have already told you everything I have done. You can't go back on your word...\"","Facing such a coward, He Zhiran sneered inwardly while stopping her movement.","She was somewhat curious what else Nan Heng would do to beg for his life.","Nan Heng had already been scared out of his wits.","In order to live, he spoke to He Zhiran about conditions again.","\"I also know a big secret of the Mo family. If you agree to let me leave alive, I will tell you.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran did not know what the \"big matter\" of the Mo family Nan Heng was talking about.","They were indeed very interested.","He Zhiran put away her knife and revealed a harmless smile.","\"Since this is the case, go ahead and speak. Let's see if the importance of this matter is enough to spare your life.\"","Seeing her put down the knife, Nan Heng heaved a sigh of relief. At the same time, he spoke very quickly:","\"I know the reason why the Mo family has no descendants.\"","When it came to the Mo family's descendants, He Zhiran was very curious indeed.","It was understandable that Mo Jiuye's brothers were few. Added up there were only nine of them, and they were all married.","The sisters-in-law also looked quite healthy. Why hadn't any of them given birth for the Mo family?","Thinking of this, He Zhiran asked eagerly: \"What is the reason?\"","Seeing her interest, Nan Heng hurried to state his condition again.","\"If you want to know the real reason for this, you must send me to my people. As long as I'm safe, I will definitely tell you.\"","He Zhiran would have to be a fool to believe his nonsense.","\"Since you don't want to say, don't blame me for being ruthless.\"","As she spoke, she deliberately glanced at Yun Li's corpse, the implication obvious.","Thinking of Yun Li's painful appearance, Nan Heng shuddered instantly.","\"No, although I have done the Mo family wrong, I have never personally taken the life of any Mo family member. You cannot treat me like this.\"","At this time, Mo Jiuye sneered coldly.","\"You're good at exonerating yourself. Although the fourth brother did not die by your hand, the fact that he died because of you is indisputable. As for the third brother, he was alive as the Prince of Dashun, but seeing his subject suffer harm, he not only remained indifferent, but even took advantage of it.","Also, you instructed people to poison the well. If it weren't for the Mo family's tenacity, even banishment would have been avoided.\"","As for his own encounter with the black-clothed assassins lying in ambush at Niujiaoshan and falling off the cliff with He Zhiran, Mo Jiuye did not mention it.","Just those few things earlier would have been enough for Nan Heng to die several times over.","At this point, He Zhiran had already used her mind to take out a vial of liquid in front of Nan Heng and swayed it before him a few times.","\"It was from pouring this thing on Yun Li's face that made her become like that. Do you want to try it too?\"","\"No... you can't...\" Nan Heng shook his head desperately.","He Zhiran sneered coldly. \"Since you don't want to try it, I suppose you should know what to do.\"","Nan Heng nodded forcefully again. \"I know... I know... I'll say it.\"","After a pause, Nan Heng gritted his teeth and finally revealed the reason why the Mo family had no offspring.","\"It was my mother, my mother said that sooner or later the Mo family would become Nan Qi's faction. In order not to let the Mo family grow stronger, their lineage had to be severed.\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye could no longer control his emotions. He strode past He Zhiran and came up to Nan Heng, grasping his neck fiercely with his big hand.","\"What exactly did she do to the Mo family?\"","Afraid that Mo Jiuye would take his life on the spot, Nan Heng hurriedly explained, \"My mother... she bribed Granny Liu from Old Lady Mo's manor. Whenever there was a new bride, she would slip something into their tea on the first opportunity, causing the Mo daughters-in-law to be barren for life...\"","As Nan Heng's voice fell, a crisp cracking sound was heard in the silent space.","Mo Jiuye used some force and directly snapped Nan Heng's neck.","Nan Heng's eyes bulged wide open and he lost his breath instantly...","He Zhiran looked at the clock in the infirmary again. It was already past three in the morning.","Time did not allow them to discuss the matter of the Mo family women being secretly fed contraceptives any further. The most important thing now was to dispose of the two corpses before dawn.","Also, Mo Yunfeng was probably about to wake up soon. They had to send him out of space in time.","Seeing Mo Jiuye still standing in place, somewhat angry, He Zhiran reminded him: \"It's late, let's go out first.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. \"Alright.\"","The two briefly tidied themselves up and left the space together.","First, Mo Jiuye observed the surroundings outside the tent for a while before sweeping He Zhiran into his arms and disappearing instantly.","The two sped into the depths of the jungle and stopped in front of a deep pool.","He Zhiran glanced at the dark and bottomless pool.","Without further thought, she directly used her mind to take out the two corpses from space and threw them into the deep pool.","Such a place, such a deep pool, was indeed the right place to dispose of corpses.","The two corpses would probably never be found...","Having dealt with these matters, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran checked each other's attire to make sure there were no omissions or traces before leaving together.","Once again, Mo Jiuye carried He Zhiran as he exhibited his lightness skill, stopping a few miles away from the camp in the jungle.","With a movement of her mind, He Zhiran made Mo Yunfeng appear in the clearing in front of them.","Mo Jiuye stepped forward and gently patted Mo Yunfeng's cheeks.","\"Third brother, wake up, it's Jiuye. Can you hear me speak?\"","After Mo Jiuye called out for a few minutes, Mo Yunfeng finally stirred awake slowly.","Mo Yunfeng recognized the person in front of him with one glance.","\"Ninth younger brother?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded vigorously. \"Third brother, it's me!\""]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146: I have a husband, Too.","paragraphs":["Mo Yunfeng looked around, then looked at He Zhiran with a bewildered expression on his face.","\"Who is this?","And why are you dressed like this, Ninth Brother?\"","In Mo Yunfeng's impression, Ninth Brother had a clean personality.","However, at this moment, Mo Jiuye was wearing rough linen clothes covered in dust.","In addition to that, there had never been any maids around Ninth Brother, so why would this woman be following him?","Mo Yunfeng was totally confused.","Mo Jiuye knew they were pressed for time and understood Mo Yunfeng's puzzlement.","He spoke again, explaining everything to Mo Yunfeng from the beginning.","After listening to Ninth Brother recount what had happened in the Mo family over the past few years, Mo Yunfeng knelt on the ground and cried bitterly.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran knew that it would be difficult for Mo Yunfeng to accept all these facts at once, so crying was a way for him to vent his emotions. Therefore, neither of them went up to try and stop his behavior.","After Mo Yunfeng had cried enough, he looked towards Mo Jiuye.","“Ninth Brother, for now Third Brother will not reveal himself publicly.”","“Third Brother, what do you plan on...” Before Mo Jiuye could finish speaking, he was interrupted by Mo Yunfeng.","“Anyway, everyone thinks I’m dead, and I'm not on the exile list for the Mo family, so I might as well take this chance to go out and look for news on Eldest Brother and Second Brother.”","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran looked at each other, both feeling that what Mo Yunfeng said made sense.","Right now, not only was their current status unable to allow them to go out and search for Eldest Brother and Second Brother, but even after arriving in the northwest, they would first have to register with the local government office. Plus, the court had stipulated that exile criminals could not leave their place of exile for the rest of their lives without an imperial edict from the Emperor.","Local officials would come and check the households of exiled people from time to time. If they discovered someone had left, they would definitely report it to the imperial court.","That would bring unnecessary trouble to the family.","Therefore, it was best for Mo Yunfeng to not participate in the exile for now and directly go out to search for news instead.","Mo Jiuye nodded, “That’s reasonable. I’ll find an opportunity for Mother and Third Sister-in-law to secretly meet with Third Brother, which will reassure them as well.”","“Good, just make arrangements as you see fit, Ninth Brother.”","On the surface Mo Yunfeng looked calm and unruffled, but when Ninth Brother mentioned Mother and his wife, he was already impatient to see them.","Mo Jiuye looked up at the color of the sky, “Third Brother, it’s getting late. Just wait for me here while I go back and think of a way to bring Mother and Third Sister-in-law over to see you. Time is of the essence.”","He Zhiran secretly took out some rations from her space again for Mo Yunfeng before following Mo Jiuye back to the camp.","With Mo Chuhan’s high martial arts prowess, he had already noticed when Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister-in-law left the campsite.","He knew that the reason Ninth Brother and Ninth Sister-in-law had gone out was related to Third Brother’s matters. Worried that something might happen, he waited at the direction they had left, ready to meet them at any time.","Seeing them return from afar, Mo Chuhan hurriedly went up to greet them.","“Ninth Brother, Ninth Sister-in-law, where is Third Brother?”","“Eighth Brother, I and Ranran have obtained some new information. I’ll slowly tell you about this matter later. Right now I have to take Mother and Third Sister-in-law to see Third Brother as time is of the essence. If necessary, I’ll need your help to deal with Eldest Brother Peng here.”","Although Mo Chuhan was confused, he could see that Ninth Brother was very anxious.","“Alright, feel free to take Mother and Third Sister-in-law away. Leave things here to me.”","The tent where Old Lady Mo and Third Sister-in-law lived housed the female relatives, so Mo Jiuye was not convenient to come forward. He Zhiran took the initiative to go call them.","Soon, she brought the two puzzled women away, avoiding the officials’ line of sight to meet up with Mo Jiuye.","Pressed for time, Mo Jiuye supported Old Lady Mo while He Zhiran pulled Third Sister-in-law as they walked towards the woods.","On the way there, they told the two women that Mo Yunfeng was still alive and that they would soon be able to see him.","If it wasn’t for Mo Chuhan having died and come back to life beforehand, the two women would have found it hard to believe their own ears.","Especially Third Sister-in-law. Over the past few days, when she saw Mo Chuhan return alive, she didn’t know how envious she was of Eighth Sister-in-law. She never expected that her own husband could return from the dead as well...","Overjoyed, Third Sister-in-law burst into happy tears. In order to confirm that this was not false, she forcefully grabbed He Zhiran’s arm, continuously asking all sorts of questions.","“Ninth Sister-in-law, will my husband have become very thin as well?”","“Ninth Sister-in-law, do you think my husband will still remember me?”","“Ninth Sister-in-law, help check if my hair is very messy?”","“Ninth Sister-in-law...”","He Zhiran understood Third Sister-in-law’s feelings and patiently answered all her various questions.","Old Lady Mo was similarly agitated, with tears flowing like rain upon hearing her third son was still alive.","She kept softly murmuring, “Heaven blessings, my Mo family has gained another descendant... Amitabha... Amitabha...”","With two additional people, Mo Jiuye was unable to use lightness skills to hurry on the road, thus their speed naturally became much slower.","After walking for about half an hour, the group of people finally saw a tall figure standing up ahead.","Seeing the few people approaching, Mo Yunfeng strode forward to meet them.","He knelt on both knees in front of Old Lady Mo.","“Yunfeng has been unfilial and caused Mother to worry.”","If it wasn’t for the familiar voice, Old Lady Mo wouldn’t have recognized the bearded man with half his face covered by messy hair before her eyes as her third son, Mo Yunfeng.","She reached out a trembling hand and lightly touched Mo Yunfeng’s disheveled hair.","“Are you really my Yunfeng?”","Mo Yunfeng smoothed back his bangs to the back of his head, then lifted his head.","“Mother, your unfilial son Yunfeng is here.”","With his hair no longer blocking his face, even though stubble covered his cheeks, Old Lady Mo recognized her son at a glance.","“Yunfeng...It really is Yunfeng...Mother’s Yunfeng isn’t dead...That’s wonderful...”","Old Lady Mo excitedly grabbed Mo Yunfeng and bawled loudly.","Third Sister-in-law also wanted to ask about her husband’s circumstances, but upon seeing the interaction between mother-in-law and husband, she held herself back from immediately going forward.","She was still holding onto He Zhiran’s arm, ceaselessly shedding tears.","After crying for a while, Old Lady Mo gently patted Mo Yunfeng’s shoulder and helped pull him to his feet.","“Ever since you left home these years, Feng has shed who knows how many tears for you.”","As she spoke, Old Lady Mo was already leading Mo Yunfeng to stand before Third Sister-in-law.","Third Sister-in-law’s eyes were blurred by her tears.","“Husband, now I won’t have to be envious of Eighth Sister-in-law anymore...sob...I also have a husband now...sob...it’s all my fault for making you sad for so many years...”","Mo Yunfeng strode forward and engulfed Third Sister-in-law in his embrace.","“I’m sorry, Cui Lian, for making you heartbroken and grieved for so many years. It was all my fault.”"]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147: Where the troops Are","paragraphs":["Old Lady Mo was very tactful. Thinking that Mo Yunfeng and his wife hadn't seen each other for many years and must have a lot of intimate words to say, she pulled Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran to go a little further away.","After finding a suitable place to stand, Old Lady Mo wiped the tears from the corners of her eyes and asked, \"Jiuye, how did you find your third brother?\"","Mo Jiuye told the whole story of how he found Mo Yunfeng from beginning to end.","For Old Lady Mo, the amount of information in Mo Jiuye's words was too much.","Her fourth son Mo Xiuyan died because of Nan Heng. Her third son Mo Yunfeng was controlled by Nan Heng and the national teacher of Nanjiang for four years.","Her eldest son Mo Junrui and second son Mo Jiacheng were not dead after all, but their whereabouts were currently unknown.","Also, Mo Jiuye killed Nan Heng and the national teacher of Nanjiang with his own hands...","As for the matter of the Empress bribing Granny Liu to make infertility potions for her sisters-in-law, Mo Jiuye decided to keep his opinions for the time being until He Zhiran helped his sisters-in-law get checked.","Fortunately, Old Lady Mo was a woman who had seen storms. Although she was shocked by the news, she accepted it very quickly.","She grabbed Mo Jiuye's sleeve, \"Jiuye, your third brother chose to meet your mother here. Does this mean he doesn't intend to go northwest with us?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"Third brother said that the fact that he is alive is not yet known to outsiders. He wants to take this opportunity to change his name and lay low to find out about eldest brother and second brother.\"","Old Lady Mo turned her head to look at Mo Yunfeng, with reluctant colors flowing in her eyes.","But she knew clearly in her heart that what Mo Yunfeng was doing was right.","Once they arrived in the northwest, it would be difficult for him to come out to find someone.","At this moment, Mo Yunfeng walked over with his wife.","\"Mother, ninth brother should have told you, right? Your son is going out to find out about eldest brother and second brother.\"","\"Well, your ninth brother just said it. You have to be careful when you are alone outside. Your mother is old now and can no longer endure the pain of losing her son.\"","As Old Lady Mo spoke, tears flowed unconsciously again.","Mo Yunfeng stepped forward and took Old Lady Mo's hand.","\"Mother, don't worry. No matter what the result of this search is, your son will definitely be by your side next year for the New Year.\"","With Mo Yunfeng's guarantee, Old Lady Mo felt much more at ease.","\"Okay, remember your family is waiting for you in the northwest.\"","After comforting his mother, Mo Yunfeng exhorted his wife a few more words before preparing to leave.","Seeing this, He Zhiran hurriedly took out a stack of silver bills from her space and handed them to him.","\"Third brother will need money in many places when he is outside. Take these with you.\"","Mo Yunfeng was just thinking that the family didn't have any silver. They must have suffered a lot on the road. He was going to take the opportunity to get some silver from the Salt Gang to make up for the family.","Seeing so many silver bills taken out by his ninth brother and sister-in-law, Mo Yunfeng instinctively refused.","\"Ninth brother and sister-in-law must not give me this. There are many people in the family and they need more money on the road. Third brother can figure it out by himself.\"","In Old Lady Mo's heart, the silver He Zhiran took out was all given by her parents before they left. It was already very thoughtful of them to feed their large family. So Old Lady Mo also helped Mo Yunfeng refuse.","\"He Zhi, your third brother is a grown man. He won't starve to death outside. Take the silver back!\"","At this moment, the third sister-in-law took out a purse and stuffed it into Mo Yunfeng's hand.","\"Husband, if you don't want to use ninth brother and sister-in-law's silver, you can use mine, right?\"","Mo Yunfeng still did not take it. He put the purse back into the third sister-in-law's hand.","\"I will figure it out by myself. You guys keep the silver for emergencies.\"","Seeing that Mo Yunfeng insisted, the third sister-in-law could only take back the purse.","She exhorted him a few more words before reluctantly parting with her husband.","Mo Yunfeng quickly disappeared using his lightness skill.","The third sister-in-law's tears flowed uncontrolled again.","He Zhiran comforted her for a few sentences before everyone walked towards the camp.","On the way, Old Lady Mo told the third sister-in-law not to tell anyone else about today's events for the time being.","Although the Mo family didn't have any wicked people, still, too many people would inevitably leak something by accident.","Back at the camp, Old Lady Mo behaved as if nothing had happened at all, urging Mo Hanyue to get up and wash up.","Mo Chuhan saw them come back and anxiously pulled Mo Jiuye aside to ask.","Fortunately, at this time, the officials had just gotten up and there was still some time before departure.","He Zhiran, who had been sleepless all night, drilled into the tent to rest.","She had just begun to feel sleepy when she suddenly heard the sound of chaotic horse hoofs not far away.","The sound of horse hoofs grew louder and louder from afar, and soon stopped near the camp.","Everyone came out of the tents to see what was going on.","I saw a man in official clothes riding a horse, holding a portrait of Nan Heng in his hand.","\"Have you seen Prince Heng?\"","Peng Wang walked over first.","\"Sir, we have never seen Prince Heng.\"","Seeing Peng Wang's perfunctory reply, the man immediately frowned.","\"Look carefully. This is Prince Heng. You can't just gloss over it in one sentence.\"","Peng Wang was intimidated by the momentum of the man on horseback and broke out in a cold sweat.","But he didn't lie at all...","\"Sir, I am just a petty eighth-rank official. How could I have the qualifications to see Prince Heng?\"","The man on horseback thought it made sense. Prince Heng was not someone just anyone could see.","So after scanning the camp, he waved his hand behind him and left with a swoosh of people.","Peng Wang wiped the sweat from his forehead and led the people back to camp.","He didn't know what had happened. He immediately sent an official to find out the news.","It wasn’t for anything else. He was worried that something might have happened to Prince Heng here, and the pier would be blocked again.","It had to be said that Peng Wang was right.","The official who went out to investigate reported back:","Last night, the flower boat Prince Heng was riding caught fire, and Prince Heng's life and death was unknown.","Not only was the pier blocked, but the city gates were also closed. No one could enter or leave before Prince Heng was found.","Peng Wang was dumbfounded by this.","It would be fine if Prince Heng was found soon, but if he couldn't be found, wouldn't they have to stay here forever?","Thinking of this, Peng Wang's heart was extremely depressed.","He had been an escort official for so many years, and it was the first time things had gone so wrong. He could still accept natural disasters, but there was also man-made harm...","Helplessly, since things had come to this point, he could only admit his fate.","\"Order to station the team on the spot until passage is possible.\"","This news didn't mean anything to He Zhiran. After all, she had plenty of silver. There was no difference in living anywhere.","But it was different for the Fang and Xie families.","After hurrying for so long, the twenty or so taels of silver they had were almost gone.","If they still couldn't reach the northwest soon, they would probably have to starve like the He family in the future.","He Zhiran did not notice the reactions of the Xie and Fang families. At this time, she was extremely sleepy.","Hearing that they didn't need to hurry anymore, she immediately drilled into the tent, intending to make up for her sleep.","Old Lady Mo knew that she and Mo Jiuye had done so much last night that she told the family not to disturb her."]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148: Space Harvest","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye also saw the officials who were searching for people just now. After explaining the matter clearly to Mo Chuhan, he deliberately pretended not to know anything and came to Peng Wang's side.","\"Big Brother Peng, what on earth happened?\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye, Peng Wang immediately associated the incident that happened last night with him.","However, looking at Mo Jiuye's expression, it didn't seem to be him either.","Peng Wang asked doubtfully, \"Do you really not know?\"","Mo Jiuye was a little confused.","\"Why is Big Brother Peng asking this? What exactly happened?\"","Peng Wang saw that Mo Jiuye's eyes were clear and he didn't look like he was lying. He sighed and said,","\"I just sent someone to investigate. They said that the barge that Prince Heng was riding on caught fire on the lake last night, and Prince Heng is also missing. The government ordered people to seal off the pier and city gates until Prince Heng is found, and no one is allowed to enter or leave.\"","Mo Jiuye knew that Peng Wang was shrewd and would likely suspect him, so his main purpose in coming here was to dispel Peng Wang's doubts.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye's expression was even more exaggerated.","\"So you mean we weren't able to leave here yesterday because of Prince Heng's arrival?\"","Peng Wang observed Mo Jiuye's expression carefully and could now determine that Prince Heng's disappearance had nothing to do with Mo Jiuye.","He patted Mo Jiuye on the shoulder, \"Alas... I hope those people can find Prince Heng soon so we can be on our way.\"","Seeing Peng Wang's grieved appearance, Mo Jiuye comforted him with a few words before leaving.","After a simple breakfast, Mo Jiuye also sneaked into the tent to catch up on sleep.","It wasn't until the afternoon that the two were fully energized again.","Hearing the movement outside the tent, it seemed like the sisters-in-law were all chatting idly.","He Zhiran thought of the filth on the ground in her dimension space that she hadn't had a chance to clean up yet. She might as well go tidy up now.","She took Mo Jiuye with her into the space.","Mo Jiuye also thought of this point and went straight to the bathroom, taking a broom, mop and a large bucket to the farm.","As soon as he entered the farm, he was shocked by the scene in front of him.","The crops planted in the soil had all ripened.","He Zhiran was standing in front of the control panel harvesting them.","He saw the cucumbers on the vines float up in the blink of an eye and then fall into the bamboo basket on the ground.","And they were all very orderly, automatically arranging themselves neatly...","The other crops were the same, regardless of their shape or color, they were all placed in the bamboo baskets in the same way.","What was even more magical was that the rice grains went straight into bags after being hulled...","Although he had already heard He Zhiran mention the magical nature of the space before, seeing it with his own eyes still made him feel that this was all too unbelievable.","He Zhiran was also the same. As she stood in front of the control panel watching all this, it was as if she was watching a large anime performance.","At this moment, He Zhiran was as excited as a child.","The corners of her lips turned up in a big smile, and her shallow dimples seemed to be filled with happiness.","Mo Jiuye turned his head and saw her smiling face that was as beautiful as a flower.","In all the time they had been together, this was the first time he had seen her smile so happily. Mo Jiuye was actually stunned.","He Zhiran's attention was completely focused on the harvesting process and she didn't notice Mo Jiuye.","After finishing her operations, looking at the neatly arranged food in front of her, she couldn't wait to take it out immediately for her family to enjoy.","It was a pity that it was not easy for these things to see the light of day.","Mo Jiuye saw her suddenly falling into a daze and went up to ask her,","\"What are you thinking about?\"","He Zhiran pointed at the food and said, \"I was thinking about how I could let my family taste these things too.\"","Mo Jiuye was a little bolder.","\"The officials couldn't find Prince Heng, so I guess they won't let anyone leave in a short time. Let's tell Big Brother Peng tomorrow that we want to go into the woods for a walk.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran's eyes lit up immediately.","\"That's a good idea of yours. I'll pick out some suitable food to take out then.\"","Anyway, with Mo Jiuye, the scapegoat, around, she had nothing to worry about.","He Zhiran used her mind to send the food she had just harvested into the space. When she turned around after finishing up, she saw Mo Jiuye seriously cleaning the bloodstains on the ground.","She could have manipulated all this with her mind originally.","But when she saw Mo Jiuye working hard, she suddenly felt a sense of home.","At the same time, a harmonious picture also flashed through her mind.","Waking up early, she was busy preparing breakfast in the kitchen, while the man was sweeping the yard with a broom...","Although these were just some ordinary days that couldn't get any more ordinary, for He Zhiran, who had never felt the warmth of family since she was a child, it was the life she yearned for most.","She couldn't bear to destroy this picture, so she gave up the idea of mind manipulation.","Mo Jiuye worked very carefully, washing the places with bloodstains and dirt several times before putting away the tools when he was sure there were no more contaminants.","Looking at the time, it was almost evening. The two were afraid that their family would come to call them for dinner and discover something wrong if they stayed in the space for too long.","The two had just appeared in the tent when they heard Fourth Sister-in-law's voice calling for dinner from outside.","He Zhiran hurriedly responded and went out of the tent with Mo Jiuye.","After dinner, while chatting leisurely, He Zhiran saw Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai seem to have made an appointment to go find Peng Wang together.","It was some distance away, so she didn't hear clearly what the two said to Peng Wang.","She only saw Peng Wang waving his hands again and again, and finally yelled loudly,","\"Don't forget your identities.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked at each other, neither knowing what had happened.","Not long after, Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai came back with drooping heads.","Second Sister-in-law was also at Xie Family's place. Seeing her father come back, she asked a few questions with a worried look on her face before walking back.","They might not care about other people’s affairs, but Second Sister-in-law was obviously very disappointed. He Zhiran had to ask her about it.","\"Second Sister-in-law, what happened?\"","Second Sister-in-law sighed.","\"The silver of Xie Family and Fang Family is almost used up. My father and Uncle Fang wanted to discuss with Officer Peng to see if the team could continue staying for a period of time. They wanted to take the men in their families out to find work tomorrow, to earn some silver to supplement their income.","You saw the result of the discussion, it was fruitless. Officer Peng simply refused.\"","A lot had happened recently, and He Zhiran really hadn't paid much attention to the Fang and Xie families before.","After Second Sister-in-law's words, she thought about it and realized it was true.","Not to mention the food and drink of the two families, just staying at the inns along the way had cost a lot.","Even if they used it sparingly, the twenty taels of silver were probably almost gone.","The Fang Family was still alright since Mrs. Zhao's ring was still with her.","With the incident of her and Mo Jiuye falling off the cliff, and the two families helping Mo Family deal with the officials together, she was fully justified in returning the ring to Mrs. Zhao.","But what about Xie Family?","She couldn't just directly give them silver for no reason, that would change her original intention."]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149: Return the Ring","paragraphs":["As she was thinking, He Zhiran realized her consciousness had already entered the space.","She wanted to check the value of Mrs. Zhao's ring.","She had thought that a small ring would have a similar valuation to those silver hairpins on Taobao.","Unexpectedly, the guided price given for that ring turned out to be 800,000 yuan.","He Zhiran did not understand such jewelry items, but she believed Taobao's valuation would not be wrong.","She did not know how Mrs. Zhao had managed to keep this ring when her home was raided, but judging from its value, this ring must have been very meaningful to Mrs. Zhao.","He Zhiran decided to return the ring to Mrs. Zhao first.","As her consciousness withdrew from the space, she saw her sister-in-law staring at her.","\"Sister-in-law, when I went to relieve myself in the woods, I saw a lot of herbs. You also recognize some of them. Why don't we discuss with Big Brother Peng tomorrow and take everyone to gather herbs? We could also exchange some silver that way.\"","She had thought her sister-in-law would be very happy that she had come up with a way to earn money. Unexpectedly, her sister-in-law still had a bitter look on her face.","\"Sister-in-law, this is indeed a good idea, but the officers simply won't let anyone leave here. How can we gather herbs?\"","He Zhiran had to admit her idea was too simple.","Peng Wang trusted her and Mo Jiuye. This trust was earned through some experiences.","She really shouldn't ask him for favors without reason.","After thinking it over, He Zhiran did not have any ideas for the moment.","Seeing He Zhiran's difficulty, her sister-in-law said, \"Sister-in-law, there's nothing we can do to help with this matter. We shouldn't add to our troubles.\"","\"You're right, sister-in-law. After all, we have special identities. It's best to know our limits.\"","The two chatted for a while longer before the sister-in-law yawned and went to rest.","Seeing the Fang family had not rested yet, He Zhiran took out the ring from her space and brought it over to Mrs. Zhao.","\"Auntie, this ring must be very important to you. I was thinking of returning it.\"","When Mrs. Zhao saw the ring, her eyes instantly turned red, but she did not reach for it.","\"No, this is the ring I exchanged with you for the fish. I can't take it back.\"","He Zhiran directly put the ring into Mrs. Zhao's hand.","\"Auntie, with one look I can tell this ring is valuable. My few fish can't match up to it.\"","Mrs. Zhao took the ring, choking up, \"I won't hide it from my niece. This ring was passed down to me from my mother. When our home was raided, I wanted something to remember her by, so I hid the ring in my hair bun and brought it out with me. If not for seeing the children so pitifully hungry, I would never have taken it out no matter what.\"","\"Auntie, since the ring is so precious to you, keep it safe from now on. Don't take it out to exchange for things unless absolutely necessary.\"","He Zhiran was not good at persuading people, so she left after saying a few sentences.","With no foresight of danger, He Zhiran entered the space with Mo Jiuye to rest.","The two had slept quite a bit during the day, so they were not sleepy now.","He Zhiran thought of the crops harvested from the space that she had not tasted yet. It would be good to have them as a midnight snack.","Although the midnight snacks were mainly vegetables, He Zhiran was pleasantly surprised to find the taste of the space's vegetables was superb, not just their looks.","For example, the tomatoes were sweet and sour, more delicious than fruit.","The cucumbers were also sweet, and the cilantro was much more aromatic than any she had eaten before...","In short, everything produced in the space was top quality.","It was not until late into the night before the two were fully satisfied and lying in bed to rest.","The next day at dawn, after Mo Jiuye bid Peng Wang farewell, he took He Zhiran out.","Originally he had planned to go to the woods, but He Zhiran considered that the mature crops from the space were mainly vegetables and grains. So the two decided on the spot to go into the city instead.","The grains could be directly said to have been purchased at the market. They would try to choose suitable vegetables to bring back.","Perhaps because the entire city was searching for Nan Heng's whereabouts, there were not many pedestrians on the streets.","Although the shops on both sides of the roads were open for business as usual, there was little traffic.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were just randomly strolling about with no destination in mind.","As the two walked to the front of an embroidery house, first, a girl who looked thirteen or fourteen walked out, followed by two servant girls.","A middle-aged woman came rushing out behind them.","The woman was holding some doll-like objects in her hands.","\"Miss Li, I run a small business here. You don't want the dolls you ordered anymore. Who am I supposed to sell them to?\"","Miss Li turned around and said angrily, \"The things you made don't meet this young lady's preferences, so this young lady will not take them.\"","\"But Miss Li, these dolls were all made according to the samples you provided. How can you say they don't meet your preferences and refuse to take them?","Look, these dolls are all made with high-quality materials. Just buying these materials cost me several taels of silver, plus I pre-paid the labor costs. If you don't take them, I will suffer losses...\"","Miss Li disdainfully glanced at the dolls in the woman's hands and walked away without looking back.","He Zhiran took a careful look at the dolls the woman was holding.","Judging from the materials, they did seem quite expensive, comparable to the material of Miss Li's clothing.","But in that case...","No wonder Miss Li refused to buy them. Indeed, they were somewhat unsightly.","He Zhiran suddenly had an inspiration.","In her previous life, she had a good friend who liked to handmake dolls and crafts.","After making them, her friend had gifted her several pieces which were now placed on her bedside table in her space.","He Zhiran squeezed close in front of Mo Jiuye's body and stood right in front of him.","At first, Mo Jiuye was somewhat baffled by her intimate gesture.","However, very soon he felt a few small hands suddenly holding an object in front of him.","Glancing down, he saw it was actually the doll placed on her bedside table.","So he had misunderstood. She had only used him as a shield...","He Zhiran briskly walked a few steps and came before Miss Li, displaying a white fluffy long-eared rabbit crafted from fleece in front of her.","\"Miss, what do you think of this doll?\"","Having her path suddenly blocked, Miss Li instinctively wanted to get angry. But the moment she saw that snowy white and fluffy long-eared rabbit, her expression instantly changed - from anger to delight in less than a second.","\"Is this rabbit for sale? I can pay a high price to buy it.\"","Seeing the long-eared rabbit doll, the embroidery house owner had already forgotten about continuing to persuade Miss Li to purchase his dolls. He hurried over, eyes shining with pleasant surprise.","\"Little lady, did you make this doll yourself?\"","He Zhiran looked at both of them and resolved their problem in one sentence:","\"I made the rabbit doll myself, it's not for sale.\"","Hearing this, Miss Li became anxious, \"As long as you agree to sell this doll to me, I'll pay ten taels. How about it?\"","He Zhiran still calmly shook her head.","She had not taken out the rabbit doll to exchange it for these ten taels of silver.","Stepping past Miss Li, He Zhiran went straight to the embroidery shop owner.","\"Shopkeeper, given that I can produce such quality, would your embroidery house be willing to purchase my products?\""]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150: I hope the little Lady delivers soon.","paragraphs":["The shop owner nodded again and again without even thinking: \"Willing, of course willing!\"","\"In that case, shall we talk about cooperation?\"","\"Good good good, young lady please come inside, let's discuss properly.\" The shop owner made a \"please\" gesture and led He Zhiran into the embroidery room.","Miss Li saw that she was completely ignored, and unwillingly followed them inside.","\"Hey! Are you selling it for 20 taels of silver or not?\"","20 taels for a plush rabbit toy, if He Zhiran still didn't sell it, she was really overdoing it.","\"In that case, I can only reluctantly give up.\"","Miss Li was afraid things would change, so she hurriedly instructed the maid beside her to pay the silver.","The shop owner saw that He Zhiran had obtained 20 taels of silver so quickly, and it was false to say that she was not envious.","But she thought that if she could negotiate this business deal, she would have countless opportunities to earn 20 taels, and she was exceptionally excited.","Miss Li took the long-eared rabbit plush toy happily in her arms. It looked like she had no intention of leaving.","The anxious shop owner asked He Zhiran about the price to deliver the plush toys to her shop, but with Miss Li present, she didn't dare ask outright, pacing around anxiously.","Seeing that the person selling her rabbit plush toys was unhurried, Miss Li hurried over.","\"I don't know if you have any more similar quality plush toys, I want them all.\"","Similar quality plush toys?","She had as many as Miss Li wanted.","If there weren't any, she could still purchase them on Taobao Mall.","It was just that He Zhiran had not been blinded by the little profit in front of her.","Her goal was to talk business with the shop owner. Although this Miss Li was not lacking money, she wouldn't be able to buy too many.","He Zhiran was not lacking money. She suddenly started a plush toy business to help the Xie and Fang families so they could become self-sufficient. This was better than her helping them for no reason.","She didn't want to take out too many types of plush toys at once. Although she didn't know much about doing business, she understood the principle of making gradual progress.","\"I'm sorry Miss, currently there is only this one plush toy style.\"","Miss Li was clearly somewhat disappointed when she heard her words and waved to her two maids to leave.","The shop owner, seeing that the person had left, hurriedly said with a smile: \"Young lady, may I ask how many such plush toys can you provide to my embroidery shop?\"","He Zhiran could not guarantee the quantity of plush toys provided.","After all, she was not clear how long they could stay here.","\"Shop owner, I don't have any stock of these plush toys on hand. If you need them here, you can only have my family make them on a temporary basis.","I'm just passing through here, and now the pier and city gates are closed. I don't know how long I can stay here, so I can't guarantee the quantity.\"","The shop owner was somewhat disappointed to hear her words, but now that there was an opportunity to make money, she absolutely could not give it up.","\"That's fine too. Have your family make as many plush toys as possible recently, and I can take them all here. But the price...\"","He Zhiran didn't feel that a rabbit plush toy could be worth much silver in the first place.","The 20 taels previously was a price Miss Li took the initiative to offer, not her aggressively overpricing.","On the surface she was deliberating over the price, when in fact her consciousness had already entered her personal space. She planned to take a look - how much would the synthetic fur fabric, cotton stuffing and other materials needed to make the rabbit plush toys cost, so she could easily calculate a cost price.","In Taobao Mall there was fabric specifically for making plush toys. 50cm square pieces cost 10 yuan. Filling cotton cost 15 yuan per jin.","Decorative eyes and noses only needed 1 yuan per set.","He Zhiran roughly estimated that to make a rabbit plush toy the same size as the previous one, the cost would be around 15 yuan. Of course, labor costs needed to be calculated separately.","She also simply calculated the purchasing power of silver during this period, which was equivalent to about 1,000 yuan in modern times.","With 1 tael of silver, she could make over sixty something rabbit plush toys. To He Zhiran, this could hardly be considered a cost...","After calculating the cost, He Zhiran said: \"Shop owner, for long-eared rabbit plush toys the same size as before, I will provide them to you for at least 1 tael of silver each.\"","\"What? Young lady, don't make unreasonable demands! With a purchase price of 1 tael, who could I sell them to?\"","The shop owner also knew clearly that Miss Li could just spend 20 taels to buy a plush toy rabbit earlier because she was extravagant and impatient.","Moreover, such plush toys only needed to be owned once, no matter how silly and rich Miss Li was, she wouldn't spend 20 taels to buy another identical one.","She worried that with such a high purchase price, if she couldn't sell them, all that silver would be wasted.","He Zhiran smiled: \"The quality of my long-eared rabbit plush toys speaks for itself. That material is definitely unavailable to you. Such unique plush toys, the shop owner doesn't need to worry about selling them at all.\"","The shop owner did not deny this at all.","The material used to make the plush toys was indeed something she had never seen before, and it felt fluffy to the touch, with a very nice hand feel.","Seeing that the shop owner had not responded, He Zhiran continued persuading her.","\"I won't hide this from the shop owner, I happened to buy that material from a foreigner unintentionally. I don't have much left now. If the shop owner feels my asking price is too high, then I will look for another partner, I believe there will be people who can discern quality.\"","Having said this, He Zhiran made the motion of getting up to leave.","Upon seeing this, the shop owner immediately became anxious.","\"Young lady, don't rush to leave! 1 tael it is. I guarantee I will take all the plush toys you make.\"","The 1 tael price He Zhiran gave was already very reasonable. If she didn't want to go for thin profits but quick turnover to let the Fang and Xie family members earn some money, she could probably ask for 5 taels each and there would still be buyers.","She wasn't truly wanting to leave either, and sat back down in response to what the shop owner said.","\"As expected, the shop owner is refreshingly straightforward. Since this is the case, let us sign a contract on the spot to prevent future changes.\"","\"Good, as the young lady said, we'll sign a contract.\"","As the shop owner spoke, she had already brought over paper and brush.","She sized up He Zhiran's outfit, assuming she was just some poor family's daughter-in-law who probably couldn't write.","\"Young lady, shall I write the contract?\"","He Zhiran made a \"please\" gesture: \"Very well, I'll have to trouble the shop owner.\"","The shop owner also hadn't received much education. She only temporarily learned how to write to facilitate running the shop.","Therefore, her writing speed was not very fast.","It took about the time to brew a cup of tea before she finished writing two identical copies of the contract according to what they discussed.","The shop owner signed her name first, then handed both copies of the contract to He Zhiran.","\"If the young lady doesn't know how to write, just press your fingerprint.\"","He Zhiran smiled without replying, took the brush from the shop owner's hand, and signed her own name.","Seeing that the words she wrote were countless times better looking than her own, the shop owner's old face turned red.","She really shouldn't judge people by their appearances. She had assumed the other party couldn't write, but as it turned out, her writing was so beautiful...","He Zhiran pretended not to notice the shop owner's embarrassment and tucked away one copy of the contract before standing up by herself.","\"Shop owner, I shall stop disturbing your business. I will now return to have my family start working as soon as possible.\"","\"Good, I hope the young lady can deliver the goods soon.\"","He Zhiran responded and walked out of the embroidery room.","Mo Jiuye had been waiting at the door the whole time. Seeing her come out, he walked over and asked, \"You're not lacking money, so why take on this business?\"","The two continued walking forward aimlessly as He Zhiran explained while walking.","\"Yesterday when I saw the Fang and Xie family members looking miserable because they were lacking money, I suddenly noticed this business opportunity and thought to have them earn some travel expenses. My sisters-in-law and Han Yue are also bored with nothing to do recently. This is just right to give them something to do to pass the time.\""]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: I got us a lucrative business today.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye lovingly stroked her head, feeling happy that he was able to marry such a sensible and kind wife.","The two continued strolling for a while. Feeling that the time was almost up, they finally found a secluded place to flash into the space.","They had originally thought that going out this time and bringing back some food produced in the space would be enough.","They didn't expect to accidentally strike a small business deal.","He Zhiran opened the Taobao Treasure Mall and purchased materials that could make two hundred long-eared rabbit dolls.","When the items were purchased, she and Mo Jiuye were no longer calm.","Although these materials didn't weigh much, when piled together, they were like a small mountain...","It looked like they would have to hire a car to get back.","The two worked together to tightly pack those materials into five large sacks.","He Zhiran also carefully selected several bags of food, as well as her favorite fresh corn. Finally, at the Taobao Treasure Mall, she bought some meat.","In addition to that, she also brought a little of every kind of vegetable.","After getting everything ready, He Zhiran used her mind to bring these things out of the space. She stayed here to keep watch, while Mo Jiuye ran off to hire a car.","Not long after, Mo Jiuye hired an ox cart and came back with the driver to load the goods onto the cart.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye each found an empty spot on the cart and sat down before the ox slowly started pulling.","The people waiting at the camp didn't expect that the two of them had purchased so many things after just one trip out. Everyone came over to help unload the cart.","After moving everything back to where their family members were staying, the Fang and Xie families were curious and wanted to see what they had bought.","He Zhiran was in no hurry to open the sacks containing the food. Instead, she first took out a long-eared rabbit doll that had been regenerated in the space.","Seeing the doll, the sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue crowded around.","Mo Hanyue's love for the long-eared rabbit was impossible to hide in her eyes.","\"Sister-in-law Mo, this doll is so beautiful!\"","He Zhiran took this opportunity to talk about making the long-eared rabbits.","\"Today I helped everyone solicit a money-making business.\"","Hearing that there was money-making business, everyone's eyes lit up.","The Second Sister-in-Law was the first to volunteer: \"Sister-in-law Mo, I've been exercising on the road lately and have good arm strength. Washing clothes and the like is no problem for me.\"","The Seventh Sister-in-Law also stepped forward: \"Sister-in-law Mo, I'm best at sewing and mending.\"","Mo Hanyue pulled He Zhiran’s arm: \"Sister-in-law, whatever my sisters-in-law can do, Hanyue can do too. Hanyue can endure hardships.\"","Seeing this, the Fang and Xie family members also gathered around.","Mrs. Zhao was the first to speak: \"Niece-in-law, if there is any extra work suitable for us to do, we can do it too.\"","He Zhiran smiled and looked around, then raised the long-eared rabbit in her hand.","\"If I provide the materials, can you make this doll?\"","No one responded immediately. After all, the doll looked quite advanced, and they didn't dare guarantee that they could make it without carefully studying it first.","He Zhiran had already thought about this point.","The range of books available at Taobao Treasure Mall was quite comprehensive. She could directly purchase a tutorial book on making dolls.","As long as they learned the method, she believed that even she, who never touched needles and threads, could make it successfully.","If that didn’t work, she could still simply and crudely take apart a finished long-eared rabbit doll in the space, and cut according to the original size. She believed that as long as the women studied it a little, they would be able to learn how to make it.","The Eldest Sister-in-law walked forward a few steps: \"Sister-in-law, may I take a look at this doll?\"","He Zhiran handed the long-eared rabbit directly to her: \"Sister-in-law, feel free.\"","The Eldest Sister-in-law carefully examined the long-eared rabbit, and then her questions came.","\"Sister-in-law, it shouldn't be difficult to make this doll. And the biggest reason why the doll looks good is because of this material. If we don't have material like this, I'm afraid that even if we make it, we can’t achieve this kind of effect.\"","He Zhiran smiled and pulled over a large sack. She opened the sack, revealing the white fluffy fabric inside to everyone.","As soon as the fabric saw daylight, it immediately drew a cry of surprise from the women present.","\"My goodness, there really is such fabric!\"","\"This fabric must be very expensive, right?\"","\"This is the first time I've seen fabric that looks like animal fur.\"","The women unconsciously looked at their hands. If they weren't feeling a little dirty at the moment, they would hate to not reach out and touch the fluffy fabric.","Mo Hanyue excitedly hugged He Zhiran.","\"Sister-in-law, you're so awesome to be able to buy such fabric!\"","He Zhiran felt it necessary to explain this point. After all, such futuristic things were too likely to arouse suspicion.","\"We just met a foreigner near the pier promoting this fabric. I thought everyone could earn some money from it, so I bought some to bring back.","That foreigner said he still had a lot of such fabric, but our Dashun people simply didn't know the goods and hadn't been able to sell it out.","I was thinking that if our business is successful this time, we’ll find him again to buy more such fabric and earn more silver.\"","The reason why He Zhiran would say so was also for a reason.","She considered it more far-reaching. In case this business could continue for a long time, there must be a reasonable explanation for the source of goods.","After all, these exiled women used to see the world in the capital city. Even if they hadn’t seen foreigners with their own eyes, they must have heard about them from others.","They knew that the things in the hands of those foreigners were all exotic, so it was not strange that they had not seen such fabric before.","Seeing that her explanation was not questioned by anyone, He Zhiran continued:","\"I had already talked with an embroidery house in the market just now. For every doll we make, the embroidery house will purchase it for one or two taels of silver.\"","\"Sister-in-law, are you serious? As long as we can make dolls like these, we can sell them for one or two taels of silver each?\" The Second Sister-in-law was clearly incredulous.","He Zhiran nodded vigorously: \"Absolutely true!\"","Seeing this, Mrs. Zhao hurriedly inquired: \"Can we outsiders also participate?\"","\"Of course, the materials I brought back today can make two hundred such dolls. I need everyone's effort!\"","Mrs. Zhao added: \"The women of my family are all good at needlework. As long as the niece doesn’t look down on us, we can all help.\"","Seeing this, the Xie family members also expressed their desire to participate in making the long-eared rabbits.","Seeing the scene becoming noisy again, He Zhiran quickly waved at everyone.","\"Listen to me, everyone. The quality must pass inspection for these dolls. The materials are precious, there can be no cutting corners.","Also, as long as everyone's dolls meet the standards, I will pay five hundred wen per doll for the labor.\"","Although for He Zhiran these production materials were basically costless.","But she had just said that the materials purchased from foreigners, if she said the cost was too low, no one would believe it.","Rather than that, it would be better to quote a price that everyone felt reasonable to avoid unnecessary suspicion."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: If only their husband were alive.","paragraphs":["As He Zhiran's words fell, the scene boiled again.","Making a doll can earn five hundred wen for wages, and both the Xie family and Fang family feel a little unbelievable.","Even Old Lady Mo behind the crowd was moved.","Making two dolls a day can earn one or two silver coins. This money is really easy to earn.","She also wanted to participate and earn more silver to make up for family expenses.","Mrs. Zhao came forward again and said sincerely, \"Niece, this material looks expensive at first glance. Don't lose money for yourself to help us.\"","He Zhiran knew it would be like this.","She originally intended to make a rabbit doll for eight hundred wen wages. Fortunately, she said five hundred wen, otherwise it would definitely arouse suspicion.","\"Auntie doesn't have to worry. The foreigner saw that I bought a lot of fabrics and didn't give me a high price.\"","\"But you've done so much for everyone, you have to make some money!\"","Seeing what Mrs. Zhao said, Xie’s Mother also came forward to help out.","\"That's right, niece, don't lose money for everyone.\"","He Zhiran knew that these two people were sincerely considering herself.","She smiled and explained to them, \"Two aunties don't have to worry, I won't lose money.\"","In order not to entangle this issue again, He Zhiran hurriedly took out the fabrics for distribution.","Whoever wanted to participate in making dolls, each person was temporarily issued a portion of the material first to see how their skills were.","At this moment, Eldest Sister-in-law walked over holding the long-eared rabbit that she had been fiddling with in her hand for a long time.","\"Younger sister, Eldest Sister-in-law feels that this thing is not difficult to make. As long as it is tailored well, it can be sewn by hand.","Eldest Sister-in-law wants to ask you, can the doll be dismantled and tailored according to this size?\"","\"Of course, Eldest Sister-in-law will dismantle this doll.\" She had this plan in mind anyway, and it was just right that her eldest sister-in-law thought of this point too, which saved He Zhiran some trouble.","With He Zhiran’s words, Eldest Sister-in-law happily hugged the long-eared rabbit and materials to prepare.","Seeing this, others also followed one after another. He Zhiran was temporarily quiet here.","Mo Jiuye saw the women leave and came over to help He Zhiran tidy up the space food together.","The men from several families and the yamen runners also came over to help when they were free.","When they saw the food in the bag that they had never seen before, they asked curiously.","\"Brother Mo, are all these vegetables?\" Peng Wang picked up an unfamiliar green vegetable and flipped it back and forth in his hand.","He thought to himself that he had also gone out for a walk. How come he didn't see anyone selling these things?","Could it also have been bought from the foreigners?","Also, it's already October, although it's not particularly cold here yet, can such fresh vegetables still be grown in the fields?","Mo Jiuye has now also learned He Zhiran's tricks.","\"Brother Peng, many of these things were sold by a farmer carrying a shoulder pole. We didn't care if they were fresh vegetables or not when we saw them, so we took them all.\"","Peng Wang didn’t doubt it. No matter how peculiar these things were, he believed that the two had bought them back when they went out.","It's just that he was a little jealous of Mo Jiuye's luck.","Why didn't he run into farmers carrying shoulder poles selling these things when he went out?","Mo Jiuye felt that his previous explanation was very adequate. In order to prevent Peng Wang from continuing to ask questions, he hurriedly stuffed a tomato into Peng Wang’s hand.","\"Brother Peng, I just tasted this one, it's sour and sweet, more delicious than fruit.\"","Without any doubt, Peng Wang took the tomato and took a big bite.","\"Well, it's really delicious, more delicious than fruit,\" said Peng Wang, taking another bite.","His actions made the people around him salivate.","Mo Jiuye would not favor one over the other. When you see it, you get a share. He gave everyone a tomato.","After eating, everyone unanimously agreed that it was delicious, and from their appearance, they seemed to still crave more.","Even so, no one had the cheek to ask Mo Jiuye for more.","Mo Jiuye took the initiative to give some vegetables to the Fang family and Xie family. As for the yamen runners, he knew Peng Wang's temper too well.","When there was something delicious, they would always come to their home to mooch food, and would never make it themselves. So Mo Jiuye gave up the idea of giving them some food.","He Zhiran was ignorant of women's hobbies and had no interest in them. After arranging these foods properly, she went back to the tent to rest.","It was still quiet outside when it was almost time to make dinner.","When she walked out of the tent to check, she realized that she had inadvertently made trouble for herself.","All the women in the family, including Old Lady Mo, were gathered together, concentrating on making dolls there.","It seemed that she would have to make dinner with her own hands today.","It was also good. Anyway, with so many fresh foods, the sisters-in-law might not be able to cook them.","Seeing He Zhiran cooking, Mo Jiuye took the initiative to help set the fire.","He loved the taste of his wife's cooking the most. Usually he was reluctant to let her work too hard and had never mentioned it before.","Today, with so many good ingredients, and being able to eat the homemade delicacies made by his wife, just thinking about it made him feel comfortable.","Besides, he really enjoyed this plain and peaceful little life now.","Although Mo Chuhan's body had not completely recovered, after He Zhiran's careful conditioning, he was no longer restricted in his actions now.","Seeing that his ninth younger brother was distressed about his wife and went to help set fire, Mo Chuhan also thought of his own silly wife who would be happy just seeing delicious food.","With this thought, Mo Chuhan also intended to go see if his wife needed any help.","After more than two hours of research, the women finally figured out how to make the long-eared rabbit.","At present, they had already made a semi-finished product in their hands.","Although it was called a semi-finished product, the only difference was that the body of the long-eared rabbit was not yet completed, but the contours on its head were clearly visible.","When Mo Chuhan walked over, he saw his wife sewing the rabbit's tail there.","Seeing her serious appearance made people feel tender-hearted when they looked at her.","So he sat down quietly beside his wife without making a sound.","Eighth Sister-in-law was concentrating so hard that she did not notice the arrival of her husband.","Seeing that he was completely ignored, Mo Chuhan deliberately coughed.","Eighth Sister-in-law heard the sound, turned her head to look at him, and smiled: \"Why did you come over?\"","Mo Chuhan took the semi-finished doll from his wife's hand and took a look, praised: “It looks really good.”","Seeing that her labor achievements were affirmed, Eighth Sister-in-law immediately smiled with joy.","\"I think it looks very good too.\"","The interaction between the two attracted the eyes of the other women.","Everyone was envious of the Eighth Brother and Sister-in-law that the dead husband could come back alive. If their husbands were still alive, that would be great.","In the future, even if they could only live a humble life, it would be good to have someone to share the joys with.","Just like the Eighth Brother and Sister-in-law...","Because of Mo Chuhan's arrival, the attention of the women making dolls was divided, and they noticed that the Ninth Sister-in-law had already started preparing dinner in the distance.","Eldest Sister-in-law stood up first and called everyone over to help.","With the help of the sisters-in-law, He Zhiran was able to cook dinner much faster."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: Six Wives Suddenly Fainted","paragraphs":["The dinner tonight would certainly be very sumptuous. The clerks saw that the Mohists had finished cooking and Peng Wang brought them to eat without being invited.","After enjoying the delicious food, the women simply couldn't bear to rest. They set up a fire and continued making dolls by the light.","Practice makes perfect. When they successfully made qualified products, making the next one became easy.","When He Zhiran got up early in the morning, her sisters-in-law pulled her over to look at the dolls they made last night.","After an inspection, He Zhiran sincerely admired the craftsmanship of these ancients.","They were much better than the original version made by her girlfriends in her space, and could be said to have no flaws at all.","Eldest Sister-in-law and Sixth Sister-in-law each made three, and the other sisters-in-law and Mo Han Yue each made two dolls. Adding the one made by Old Lady Mo, the Mohists made 21 yesterday.","There were also twenty each from the Fang family and the Xie family.","He Zhiran felt that the number of dolls was worth her delivering. So after breakfast, accompanied by Mo Jiuye, she brought these finished long-eared rabbit dolls to the embroidery shop.","From afar, she saw the door of the embroidery shop surrounded by people.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye didn't know what had happened. They walked over quickly, intending to take a look.","They saw that Miss Li, who had spent twenty taels yesterday to buy the long-eared rabbit, had brought more than a dozen people to wait outside the door.","\"Boss, when will you have dolls like this for sale? We've been waiting since early morning.\"","The boss stood at the door, rather helpless, \"I'm not sure about this now. It depends on when they come to deliver the goods.\"","After watching for a while, He Zhiran walked over with the sixty-one finished long-eared rabbit dolls, accompanied by Mo Jiuye.","Seeing He Zhiran, the boss immediately became all smiles.","\"Little lady, you finally came. Look at these young ladies waiting at my door, they all came for the dolls.\"","Miss Li also saw He Zhiran.","\"Hurry, the dolls have arrived!\"","The ladies followed her like a swarm of bees into the embroidery shop.","Mo Jiuye put a bag of long-eared rabbit dolls directly on the counter.","He Zhiran walked forward, \"Boss, I brought 61 dolls today.\"","After checking the goods, the boss was very satisfied with this batch of dolls. He took He Zhiran inside to settle the silver.","Sixty-one taels of silver looked quite a lot, unlike banknotes. With outsiders present, she couldn't put them directly into her space, so she temporarily let Mo Jiuye keep them.","As she and the boss came to the counter, the customers who were waiting to buy the dolls had already surrounded it closely.","Seeing the boss come out, Miss Li walked up and said:","\"Boss, I was willing to spend twenty taels to buy a doll yesterday because I liked it too much. In fact, the doll is not worth that much at all. Don't raise the price just because you see more customers today!\"","Hearing this, the boss' face suddenly stiffened.","She had just seen so many customers brought by Miss Li, and had considered this issue.","These customers were all young ladies from wealthy families. Since Miss Li was willing to spend twenty taels to buy a doll, the others should be able to as well.","Moreover, this kind of doll was currently exclusive to her shop, and looked so cute. It must sell well.","Even if it couldn't sell for twenty taels, ten taels should be no problem.","Who knew Miss Li would undermine her like this as soon as she opened her mouth?","\"Miss Li, don't say that. You spent twenty taels to buy the doll. If I sell it to others for two taels, wouldn't that upset you?\" said the boss.","Miss Li didn't listen to her excuses at all.","\"I wouldn't feel upset at all. Two taels each would be just right.\"","Immediately, several of her lady friends chimed in to help.","\"Boss, if not for these special dolls, two taels would not be worth it. If you don't sell at this price, none of us will buy.\"","Hearing the news, other people who had come to watch the fun also joined in yelling.","\"That's right, two taels is already expensive.\"","The boss suddenly felt a big headache. She looked at He Zhiran instinctively.","He Zhiran just smiled to indicate she wouldn’t get involved.","Customers were not stupid. What Miss Li said made sense. There were two reasons why she was willing to pay twenty taels yesterday for the long-eared rabbit doll. First, this kind of doll was appearing for the first time, and she might have worried about not encountering it again in the future.","More importantly, she had money to spare.","Although the ladies who had come with Miss Li today looked like they were from wealthy families too, twenty taels was still not a small sum at this time.","Truly few would be willing to spend twenty taels to buy a doll.","She didn't expect the boss to be so greedy. For a business where she earned half the profit, she still wasn't willing to sell.","Fortunately she wouldn't stay here long-term. Otherwise she would definitely consider changing business partners.","Seeing that He Zhiran wasn't speaking for her, the boss also realized she probably couldn't sell the dolls for high prices.","So she smiled awkwardly.","\"Ladies, I did spend a lot to make these dolls. What do you think, sell at five taels each? Five taels a doll?\"","\"Two taels, will you sell or not? If not we're leaving.\" Miss Li spoke and prepared to leave with everyone.","Panicked, the boss quickly rushed up to stop them.","\"Three taels, three taels each, can't go lower.\"","Miss Li stopped and exchanged glances with the ladies before turning around again.","\"Fine, three taels each, and no more price increases.\"","\"No more increases, I promise.\" said the boss as she led them to the counter to select dolls.","After watching for a while, He Zhiran felt there was no point to keep watching. She pulled Mo Jiuye to leave together.","Just as they entered the small path leading back to the campsite, they ran right into the rather anxious Mo Chuhan.","Mo Chuhan hurried up to them.","\"Younger brother, younger sister-in-law, you're finally back.\"","Mo Jiuye raised his brows, \"Eighth elder brother, what happened?\"","\"Just now Sixth Sister-in-Law suddenly fainted. Mother said she was burning hot all over.\"","Upon hearing this Mo Jiuye handed all the food he was carrying to Mo Chuhan, then pulled He Zhiran to run towards the campsite.","Returning to the campsite, she saw a tent surrounded by people.","Pushing her way through the crowd, she walked in.","Eldest Sister-in-Law and Second Sister-in-Law were using handkerchiefs to wipe Sixth Sister-in-law’s forehead.","Seeing He Zhiran back, Eldest Sister-In-Law immediately got up and gave her seat to her.","\"Ninth younger sister-in-law, you're back just in time. Quickly take a look, why did Sixth sister-in-law suddenly faint?\"","He Zhiran walked up and first felt Sixth Sister-in-Law's forehead. Sure enough it was very hot.","By now, Sixth Sister-In-Law had regained some consciousness, her voice weak.","\"I'm fine, just caught a chill.\"","Without confirming what exactly happened to Sixth Sister-In-Law, He Zhiran would not be careless.","She took Sixth Sister-In-Law's pulse. Graudally, her frown grew deeper.","It was true Sixth Sister-In-Law had caught a chill, but from her pulse, it was clearly not just a simple chill.","She had a feeling that there seemed to be some force in Sixth Sister-In-Law's body causing her chill to become severe."]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: The Same abnormality in the pulse of three Sister-in-law.","paragraphs":["When Eldest Sister-in-law saw He Zhiran had a thoughtful look, she said, \"Ninth younger sister-in-law, Sixth younger sister-in-law may have really caught a cold.\"","Ever since I married into the Mo family, whenever I catch a cold, it's much more severe than before, and I've had experiences of fainting like Sixth younger sister-in-law.","Second Sister-in-law also said, \"Listening to Eldest sister-in-law's words, it seems to be the case. After I married into the Mo family, I also caught a cold once. Although I didn't faint, it was more severe than any previous colds I've had.\"","Their words made He Zhiran realize a problem first.","That is, both sisters-in-law said that after marrying into the Mo family, catching a cold would be more severe than before.","This reminded He Zhiran of something Nan Heng had confessed.","The Queen bribed servants of the Mo family that Liu Auntie would slip something into the tea of any new daughter-in-law who entered, which was to make the Mo family daughters-in-law unable to get pregnant.","In other words, it was adding contraceptive medicine into the tea.","He Zhiran frowned in thought.","Could the unusually severe cold Sisters-in-law had be related to the contraceptives they had taken?","This was only her initial suspicion. To further confirm, she would need to draw blood for testing, as that would allow a more accurate diagnosis.","With so many people gathered outside Sixth Sister-in-law's tent now, it was not convenient to immediately draw her blood.","So He Zhiran wanted to take this opportunity to first check the condition of the other Sisters-in-law.","She held Eldest Sister-in-law's wrist first to feel her pulse.","Although Eldest Sister-in-law did not have a cold, the slight abnormality in her pulse let He Zhiran confirm that her pulse was similar to Sixth Sister-in-law's.","Second Sister-in-law did not know why Ninth younger sister-in-law wanted to check Eldest Sister-in-law's pulse. Thinking she was making some comparison, Second Sister-in-law took the initiative to offer her own wrist.","Sure enough, the abnormal condition in all three Sisters-in-laws pulses were similar.","If she had not heard from Nan Heng that medicine had been given to the Sisters-in-law, she might not have noticed such subtle abnormalities.","This could also explain why no one in the Mo family had discovered the crux of why they were infertile.","Since this matter was not trivial, He Zhiran did not plan to speak openly before fully confirming it.","Seeing her check the pulse without saying anything afterwards, Second Sister-in-law asked,","\"Ninth younger sister-in-law, is there something wrong with our health?\"","\"Don't worry, Second Sister-in-law. You and Eldest Sister-in-law are very healthy. I was just comparing your pulses with Sixth Sister-in-law's.\"","Second Sister-in-law was relieved to hear this.","\"Oh, that's how it is. I thought there was also something wrong with our health.\"","Sixth Sister-in-law's cold was not difficult to deal with for He Zhiran. Eating some medicine from her space would be able to alleviate it.","What was most important now was to first draw Sixth Sister-in-law's blood for testing.","\"Eldest Sister-in-law and Second Sister-in-law, I want to give Sixth Sister-in-law acupuncture. Sixth Sister-in-law has caught a cold and is afraid of wind. Please stand guard outside and don't let anyone come and go around during my treatment.\"","The two sisters-in-law did not doubt He Zhiran's words at all and went out of the tent after acknowledging.","He Zhiran quickly took out silver needles.","In fact, it was not definitely necessary to treat Sixth Sister-in-law's cold with acupuncture. She wanted to use acupuncture as a cover to draw some of Sixth Sister-in-law's blood for testing.","\"Sixth Sister-in-law, let me give you acupuncture first. It might hurt a little, please bear with it.\"","Sixth Sister-in-law nodded slightly. \"It's hard on Ninth younger sister-in-law. Sixth Sister-in-law is not afraid of pain.\"","He Zhiran needled a few acupoints, and when she saw Sixth Sister-in-law start to become drowsy, she took out the blood draw equipment from her space and drew a tube of blood.","After dealing with this, He Zhiran removed the needles and Sixth Sister-in-law gradually awoke.","He Zhiran stood up, \"Sixth Sister-in-law, your body is weak. Just rest in the tent and I'll go prepare medicine.\"","Seeing He Zhiran come out, the Mo family's women all gathered around to ask about Sixth Sister-in-law's condition.","He Zhiran told everyone that Sixth Sister-in-law had likely caught a chill from staying up late making dolls last night, which led to today's cold.","No one objected to this. It was indeed a bit cold when they were surrounding the fire making dolls last night.","Considering Sixth Sister-in-law's originally weak constitution, it was not surprising she caught a cold.","Knowing that Sixth Sister-in-law had suddenly fainted not because of any major illness, everyone felt somewhat more at ease.","After explaining Sixth Sister-in-law's condition clearly, He Zhiran went into her own tent to prepare medicine.","The herbs gathered on the road could indeed be made into medicine to treat colds, but compared to Western medicine, the efficacy would be slower.","Right now Sixth Sister-in-law had a high fever. The first priority was to lower her temperature.","So she took out fever reducers, anti-inflammatories and cold medicine from her space.","After changing all the medicine into oil paper packaging, she returned to Sixth Sister-in-law's tent.","Eldest Sister-in-law brought a bowl of water. He Zhiran propped up Sixth Sister-in-law to sit up and take the medicine.","\"Sixth Sister-in-law, these medicines were all gifted by a master to me. They are very effective in treating colds. Please take this one first.\"","The first medicine He Zhiran gave Sixth Sister-in-law was the fever reducer. As for the other two, they needed to be taken at intervals.","Hearing that these oddly shaped pills were made by a master's hands, they must be precious indeed. Sixth Sister-in-law hesitated a bit.","\"Ninth younger sister-in-law, this is too precious.\"","He Zhiran smiled reassuringly. \"Don't worry Sixth Sister-in-law. I've already learned how to make these pills. As long as there are medicinal ingredients, I can produce them. So you don't need to feel burdened.\"","Hearing her say this, Sixth Sister-in-law indeed felt less burdened.","She followed He Zhiran's instructions, putting the pill in her mouth and washing it down with a big gulp of water.","Mo Hanyue stared at the pills in He Zhiran's hands, increasingly intrigued.","When she walked out of the tent, Mo Hanyue squeezed over.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, I've been following you to gather herbs recently and can now recognize many types. Could you teach me to produce these pills too? If I succeed, I can also earn some silver for the family.\"","He Zhiran had noticed for a while that this girl was very interested in medicine.","But learning medicine was not something that could be accomplished overnight.","Besides, in her past life she had specialized in Western surgery, and was not the most proficient in Chinese medicine.","She was able to check pulses and perform acupuncture for others after learning the basics from the old director at the military hospital.","Although her level in Chinese medicine had not reached mastery, she was quite familiar with pharmacology. And she also had prescriptions for many Chinese patent medicines.","Rather than slowly teaching Mo Hanyue Chinese medicine theory, it would be better to teach her how to produce Chinese patent medicine.","Being able to produce effective Chinese patent medicines in this era would definitely be a lucrative business.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran patted Mo Hanyue's head. \"If Hanyue likes learning medicine, let's start with pharmacology! I'll find a book on Chinese materia medica for you later. Get familiar with the medicinal properties of various Chinese medicines first.\"","Mo Hanyue nodded excitedly. \"Alright, Hanyue will study diligently!\"","He Zhiran was anxious to distribute wages for making the dolls and also concerned about testing Sixth Sister-in-law's blood sample. After saying a few words to Mo Hanyue, she gathered the women on the open grounds.","The women were all aware that He Zhiran gathering them was probably to distribute wages. The excitement in their eyes could not be concealed."]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: Graspskin","paragraphs":["Before this, Mo Jiuye had already helped divide those sixty-one taels of silver into two parts.","Seeing He Zhiran wanting to distribute the silver to everyone, he quickly brought over half of the divided silver.","Before making the dolls, He Zhiran had already talked about the details of the allocation of wages, so she didn’t plan on saying much more. She gave ten taels of silver to each the Fang family and the Xie family, and handed over what remained of her own portion to Eldest Sister-in-law to allocate.","The moment everyone received the silver, they thanked He Zhiran profusely.","Especially the Fang and Xie families. The silver He Zhiran brought them was literally timely rain.","If they didn’t have these taels of silver, they were afraid they would have to gnaw on black steamed buns to get through the days like the He family.","The He family people watched all of this from afar, with flames continuously spewing from their eyes.","But there was nothing they could do, as the others simply didn’t care about their mood...","After He Zhiran finished allocating the silver, she gave everyone a few reminders before returning to her own tent.","She pulled Mo Jiuye along with her as she slipped inside her space.","Earlier, when she was helping treat Sixth Sister-in-Law's illness, Mo Jiuye had held back since it was all women. Now seeing He Zhiran impatiently pulling him into her space, there must be some major problem with Sixth Sister-in-Law's health.","\"How is Sixth Sister-in-Law's illness exactly?\"","\"Sixth Sister-in-Law likely caught a chill from staying up late making dolls outside. However, her pulse condition is more complicated than a simple cold.","Later I helped check Eldest Sister-in-Law and Second Sister-in-Law's pulses as well, and discovered irregular phenomena in their pulses too. I now suspect this very possibly has to do with the queen sending someone to poison them.\"","Mo Jiuye was clearly somewhat worried.","\"The sisters-in-law won't be in danger, right?\"","On this point, He Zhiran currently also couldn't make an accurate judgment.","\"I just took the chance to draw some of Sixth Sister-in-Law's blood to test. I still don't know the exact details until after examination.\"","Concepts like examination were still somewhat unfamiliar to Mo Jiuye, but he didn't choose to inquire in this moment.","He Zhiran brought Sixth Sister-in-Law's blood sample to the lab, and after turning on the equipment, she started carefully operating it.","After about twenty minutes, the results for all the testing projects came out. Judging from the blood test, Sixth Sister-in-Law was still relatively healthy.","Only one index was abnormally high, already exceeding the detection range of the testing equipment.","That is to say, the equipment couldn't determine how high that index was rising.","Combing through various analyses to confirm, Sixth Sister-in-Law was indeed poisoned.","This poison wouldn't be fatal. Once the person caught a cold, it would stimulate white blood cells to quickly increase, leading to large scale inflammations in the body and causing high fever that wouldn't recede.","It was very easy for people to mistakenly diagnose this as leukemia symptoms.","Seeing He Zhiran continuously knitting her brows without saying a word, Mo Jiuye anxiously asked, \"So what exactly is the situation?\"","He Zhiran let out a sigh.","\"Based on the results of Sixth Sister-in-Law's blood tests, I suspect the medicine the queen gave them spreads toxins through the blood, causing her to be unable to get pregnant.","Right now I still don't know the specifics of this medicine, so I need to carefully research it.\"","After He Zhiran spoke, she brought the remaining blood sample to extract it, then placed it under a microscope to observe.","The results seen through the microscope made He Zhiran suddenly understand.","These cell forms were hexagonal. She had previously seen them in a medical journal.","The expert who published that article said it was highly possible that the reason for hexagonal cells appearing in blood was due to being induced by medicine.","And once a woman had cells of this shape appear in their blood, they would be incapable of conceiving a child for the rest of their lives.","In other words, the medicine Sixth Sister-in-Law had been given operated under just this principle, to cause her to be unable to get pregnant.","Unfortunately, He Zhiran didn't know the formulation principles for this medicine.","However, she could confirm that there was one type of antivenom that could clear the toxins in the blood.","This serum had been newly developed not long before she transmigrated, so it hadn't fully made its way into clinical application in the current day and age. Not only was there none available in her space, you also couldn't buy it on Taobao Treasure Mall.","Right now, if she wanted to help clear the toxins for the sisters-in-law, she first had to figure out exactly what poison the sisters-in-law had taken, so that she could conveniently formulate an antidote.","He Zhiran told Mo Jiuye of the final test results.","Mo Jiuye clenched his fists tightly in anger.","\"The queen... actually harmed so many innocent women for her own selfish desires.\"","He Zhiran was also angry, but she understood clearly in her heart that getting angry wouldn't solve anything. So she advised,","\"The queen has already lost her only son, and paid the price for everything she's done. In the future when we have the chance, we will definitely help the sisters-in-law get revenge. Right now, the most urgent thing is to first develop an antidote.\"","Especially for Third Sister-in-Law and Eighth Sister-in-Law. Third Brother and Eighth Brother were still alive. In the future, they would definitely want to have children of their own.","Mo Jiuye also understood this principle. Just now he was simply venting in anger.","\"If there's anything you need my help with when making the antidote, just speak up.\"","\"Mm, if I need your help I certainly won't stand on ceremony.\"","After He Zhiran spoke, she brought out her phone to open Taobao Treasure Mall, where she purchased a book called A Collection of Ancient and Modern Poisons.","Glancing through the table of contents, there really was an introduction about fertility medicines and such.","The contents combined modern medical theory as it was written. Although it didn't give precise formulas for these medicines, it did record methods for detoxification.","He Zhiran carefully looked through the operating principles and symptoms for several fertility drugs.","Finally, she could now fully confirm the medicine the sisters-in-law had taken was a drug with an extremely simple and direct name—Wu Zi.","Perhaps the medicinal materials for making Wu Zi had already gone extinct in later ages. And so the editor was unafraid of people being able to formulate this medicine from the formula, and thus recorded the prescription clearly in the book.","This allowed He Zhiran to luckily understand the formula for this ‘Wu Zi’ medicine.","Indeed, there were two medicinal ingredients she hadn’t heard of before. These materials must not have appeared in later ages.","In any case, she wasn’t interested in formulating these kinds of harmful things. Whether the materials existed or not didn’t matter, as long as the materials for the antidote weren’t scarce.","The prescription for the antidote was written at the very bottom. He Zhiran looked it over carefully; it consisted of a total of sixteen medicinal ingredients.","Fifteen of those were common medicinal materials.","However, one material called Dan Pi was extremely rare.","She had heard the former hospital president mention before that this medicinal material came from the eggshells of Dan birds.","Dan birds existed in snowy mountains. Due to the special environment, their eggshells had a certain thickness, and extremely strong insulation.","It was just a pity that Dan birds had extremely low numbers, and after laying their eggs they would bury them in heavy snow, causing few people to be able to find their eggs. This resulted in medicinal materials like Dan Pi being rarely seen.","He Zhiran tried doing a search on Taobao Treasure, thinking about this issue.","As expected, there were no listings for sale, as she had anticipated.","It seemed she could only take the chance when she went antiquing to ask about it."]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: Little Lady, here you are at last.","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye couldn't understand the simplified characters in the book. Seeing He Zhiran's serious expression for a long time, he asked with concern, \"Couldn't find an antidote?\"","\"I've found the formula for the antidote, but there's a very rare medicinal herb that I'm worried we won't be able to obtain,\" He Zhiran replied.","Mo Jiuye pressed further, \"What herb is it?\"","\"Dan Pi. Have you heard of it?\" He Zhiran asked.","\"You mean Dan Pi?\" Mo Jiuye's tone indicated that he was familiar with it.","\"You know about Dan Pi?\" He Zhiran seemed to glimpse a glimmer of hope.","\"Two years ago, I was ordered to escort the Fourth Princess to the southern border for a marriage alliance, and there was a medicinal herb called Dan Pi among her dowry.\"","Upon hearing that it was part of the Fourth Princess's dowry, He Zhiran immediately thought of the Empress.","The Fourth Princess was the Empress's biological daughter, so it was reasonable for her dowry to include medicinal herbs. However, the fact that the Empress was willing to let her bring such a precious and singularly effective herb raised suspicions.","Mo Jiuye suddenly understood this reasoning as well.","The two exchanged a meaningful glance, but neither spoke a word.","The Empress was undoubtedly worried that the Mo family would discover the clues and find the formula for the antidote. If they did, all her efforts would be in vain. That's why she made Dan Pi part of the Fourth Princess's dowry, to completely extinguish any hope the Mo family might have.","Thinking about all this, Mo Jiuye's veins bulged with anger. He wished he could storm into the palace right now and kill that wicked woman without delay.","Mo Jiuye himself didn't realize that his desire for revenge had reached an uncontrollable level.","He Zhiran understood the value of Dan Pi, and since Mo Jiuye knew the whereabouts of the herb, their target could only be in the southern border.","The fact that their sisters-in-law had been poisoned didn't pose an immediate threat to their lives, so finding the antidote wasn't urgent at the moment.","After settling in the northwest, they would definitely have to make a trip to the southern border to find the whereabouts of their eldest and second brother. That would be an opportunity to search for Dan Pi.","It must be said that the two of them were in sync with their thoughts, and Mo Jiuye was also considering this.","Therefore, the search for Dan Pi would be temporarily put on hold until they reached the southern border, at which point they would figure out a way.","Of course, He Zhiran would also keep an eye on Taobao's movements. If that special serum were to be widely used, there might be a link to purchase it on Taobao.","In any case, He Zhiran would keep both directions for the antidote in mind.","Since it was broad daylight, and they couldn't linger in the space for too long, He Zhiran took Mo Jiuye and left together.","She went to check on Sixth Sister-in-law's condition.","After taking the medicine, Sixth Sister-in-law broke out in a sweat and was now fine.","She heard that she had earned some silver by making dolls yesterday, and feeling slightly better, she wanted to continue making them.","He Zhiran stopped her, as it was understandable to want to make money, but her health was the most important thing.","Helpless, Sixth Sister-in-law could only continue resting in the tent.","Three days passed unnoticed.","There was still no notification for them to be allowed through, and the number of soldiers searching for someone here was increasing.","The streets of the city were filled with armed soldiers, asking everyone if they had seen the whereabouts of Prince Heng.","As a result, the common people hardly ventured out unless it was absolutely necessary, and business in the shops on both sides of the street plummeted.","However, this situation did not affect the business of the embroidery house.","Not only did it not affect it, but the number of customers coming to the embroidery house kept increasing.","The reason was none other than the credit of the long-eared rabbit dolls.","Three days later, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye arrived at the embroidery house again, carrying a hundred and thirty-one dolls. They were greeted by a crowded room filled with people.","Everyone urged the shopkeeper, asking when the long-eared rabbit dolls would arrive.","The shopkeeper couldn't produce the dolls and didn't want to lose so much business, so she continuously reassured the customers.","Just as she was getting tired of talking and was about to go get some water, she looked up and saw He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye walking in with a large package.","The shopkeeper was instantly delighted and hurriedly went to greet them.","\"Young lady, you finally came. If you didn't show up, my little shop would have been torn down by now.\"","He Zhiran didn't have a good impression of the shopkeeper. She handed the long-eared rabbit dolls to her and, after the shopkeeper inspected them, took the money and left with Mo Jiuye.","Just as they walked out of the embroidery house's door, they saw Tang Mingrui standing across the road.","Due to the city being closed off, Tang Mingrui had not left either.","At the same time, he noticed that the troublemakers from the Salt Gang had disappeared without a trace in the past few days, so he thought of coming out for some fresh air.","Little did he expect that when he passed by the embroidery house, he would notice something unusual here.","Unlike other shops that were empty, this place was overcrowded.","Out of curiosity, he stood there to see what was going on.","To his surprise, he saw Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran coming out from inside.","Tang Mingrui quickly walked up to them.","\"Sir, are you out shopping?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't hide anything and explained about selling the long-eared rabbit dolls to the embroidery house.","Tang Mingrui seemed somewhat incredulous.","\"Sir, are you saying that those fluffy plush dolls carried by the rich young ladies on the street are made by you?\"","Mo Jiuye smiled and looked at He Zhiran.","\"My wife came up with a way to earn some money when she saw that everyone was tight on funds.\"","When it came to making money, no one was more interested than Tang Mingrui.","He pointed to a teahouse nearby and said, \"Sir, it's fate that we meet on the street. How about we have some tea together and catch up?\"","Mo Jiuye instinctively glanced at He Zhiran and, seeing that she didn't object, readily agreed.","The three of them went to the teahouse and found a seat by the window.","When the waiter brought the tea, Tang Mingrui personally poured it for them, making a polite gesture.","\"Sir and Madam, please enjoy the tea.\"","Mo Jiuye picked up his teacup and politely said, \"Tang Young Master, there's no need to always refer to us as 'sir and madam.' If you don't mind, just call me Brother Mo.\"","Upon hearing this, Tang Mingrui stood up solemnly and bowed to both of them. \"In that case, I won't stand on ceremony. Brother Mo, Sister-in-law Mo.\"","After exchanging pleasantries, Tang Mingrui finally got to the point.","\"Sister-in-law Mo, do you know that the dolls you make are quite rare, especially the fabric used. I've been in business for years and have never seen anything like it.\"","He Zhiran stuck to her usual explanation.","\"I was strolling around with my husband when we happened to come across a foreigner selling this kind of fabric. We had a sudden idea to use it to make dolls, and surprisingly, they became quite popular.\"","It wasn't unusual to see one or two foreigners in the area around the Salt Lake, which was a major waterway for transportation.","Moreover, those foreigners had some interesting things in their hands. If it weren't for the language barrier and communication difficulties, Tang Mingrui would have wanted to trade with them.","At this moment, he admired He Zhiran's vision and courage.","The fabric used for making the dolls was obviously not cheap, and now that they were on their way to exile in the northwest with a guilty conscience, it was the time to use their money wisely. Yet she dared to purchase so much fabric to make dolls.","If they ended up losing, it would be a huge loss for people like them, who were exiled."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: Maximizing Profit","paragraphs":["Tang Mingrui did not hide his admiration at all, held his fists and said, \"Sister-in-law Mo really has vision, dare to do business with foreigners, and can make such unique dolls.\"","He Zhiran smiled and answered very modestly.","\"Life forced me, I had no choice.\"","After exchanging greetings for a few more sentences, Tang Mingrui finally spoke about his purpose.","“Sister-in-law Mo's dolls are special. It would be great if there were more varieties. After leaving here, I can sell them all the way to various cities, and the income must be considerable.\"","Making rabbit dolls was just a momentary intention for He Zhiran to help the Xie family and Fang family.","She did not expect Tang Mingrui to see unlimited business opportunities here.","From He Zhiran’s understanding of him, Tang Mingrui had a unique business mind. If he said the income was considerable, it must be true.","Thinking that a long-term business could be developed, not only could she earn some money for herself, but also the women of her family and the Fang and Xie families could earn money together. He Zhiran simply could not resist such a good thing.","\"If I cooperate with Young Master Tang, I am naturally willing. It just so happens that I bought a lot of fabrics that can be used to make dolls from foreigners, and I can come up with several other doll styles when I go back.\"","He Zhiran also saw that using foreigners as an excuse was not questioned by Tang Mingrui, and decided to use this unfounded scapegoat again.","At the moment, Tang Mingrui was thinking about making the first pot of gold from the doll business, and indeed did not doubt the existence of foreigners.","Seeing He Zhiran say that she could come up with several other doll styles, he was already looking forward to it.","\"In that case, I’ll wait for Sister-in-law Mo’s good news.\"","\"There is no problem making dolls, but does Young Master Tang plan to sell them around here?\"","He Zhiran felt that if Tang Mingrui was really as talented in business as recorded in the history books, it would be impossible for him to choose to sell dolls locally immediately.","The best way to make more money is to wait until the two hundred dolls in the embroidery room are sold out. People who didn't get to buy them will definitely feel regretful.","By then, Tang Mingrui could sell the dolls in his hands at high prices and limited quantities, which would definitely arouse customers' appetite.","At the same time, with the addition of new styles of dolls, Tang Mingrui's business would definitely make a fortune.","Tang Mingrui's answer did not disappoint her.","\"Sister-in-law Mo, if we still have to stay here for a long time, I plan to observe the customers' desire for dolls after the embroidery room dolls are sold out before making plans.\"","He Zhiran was very satisfied with such an answer.","\"In that case, I won't rush to work here either. I will definitely make some exquisite dolls to maximize benefits.\"","\"That’s great. I’ll wait for Sister-in-law Mo’s exquisite dolls.\"","The two talked a lot about the details of the doll business. Before they parted, they agreed that if they still could not leave here three days later, they would meet again at noon in this teahouse.","Mo Jiuye knew that He Zhiran would definitely take some plush fabrics back, so he arranged to hire an ox cart.","He Zhiran found a secluded place to prepare.","This time, she bought plush fabrics in various colors, as well as a large amount of cotton padding.","In addition, some of the food in her space also had to be taken away, as well as eggs and meat. The poultry and livestock raised in the space had not been harvested yet, so she bought some on Taobao Mall.","In addition, He Zhiran also carefully bought Mo Hanyue a book about traditional Chinese medicine in traditional Chinese characters.","She had just prepared the items to take back when Mo Jiuye came back with an ox cart.","This time He Zhiran bought a lot of plush fabrics, and a single ox cart simply couldn’t fit everything.","The driver went to call another companion, and the two ox carts carried the goods back to the camp.","When He Zhiran left with the finished dolls, the women felt regretful.","The reason was that He Zhiran had used up all the doll-making fabrics she bought from foreigners, and could no longer earn money so easily in the future.","Unexpectedly, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye went out for a while and brought back two carts of fabrics.","This made the women extremely happy, and they all came forward to help unload.","The second sister-in-law kept asking around He Zhiran.","\"Sister-in-law, did you and brother run into foreigners again?\"","\"Yeah, the foreigner was also unable to leave here. We went to look for them specially today, and happened to find that there were still such fabrics there, so I bought more.\"","He Zhiran lied without revealing anything.","Mo Jiuye next to him did not forget to win favor for his wife: \"It took Ranran a lot of effort to find that foreigner. It really wasn't easy to get these fabrics.\"","Sure enough, when the women heard that He Zhiran had taken great pains to find foreigners to buy fabrics, they came forward to express their gratitude.","Following Mo Jiuye's words, He Zhiran said a few words, just to let everyone know how hard it was to get the fabrics, so that they would make dolls more carefully.","The goods on the cars were moved aside by everyone, and He Zhiran took the opportunity to settle the wages for making one hundred and thirty-one dolls.","The money everyone got was more than last time. Especially the Fang and Xie families, the silver earned from making dolls should be enough to support them until the northwest.","The women of the two families, led by the matriarch, were about to kneel down to thank He Zhiran.","As a modern person, He Zhiran was not used to receiving such a big gift.","She stopped the actions of the two families together with the sisters-in-law, and at the same time, she also saw clearly that these two families were not white-eyed wolves. They had grateful hearts anyway.","After some polite words, He Zhiran got to the point.","She casually took some colored plush fabrics in her hand.","\"You see, the fabrics I brought back this time are colorful. I plan to study several more doll styles.\"","Seeing the fabrics of various colors in He Zhiran’s hands, the women liked it very much.","Mo Hanyue got close to He Zhiran to take a closer look at those fabrics, and became more and more pleasantly surprised the more she looked.","She pointed to the brown fabric in He Zhiran's hand and said,","\"Sister-in-law, I saw in Beijing that someone used this color fabric to make teddy bear dolls, which were very popular.\"","He Zhiran did intend to make plush teddy bears with this brown fabric.","She believed that the styles she provided would be countless times better than the ones Mo Hanyue saw in Beijing.","\"Well, I’ll draw a pattern of a teddy bear doll for everyone later.\"","The women recognized that their vision was not as good as He Zhiran's, and they were used to listening to her arrangements all the way, so no one made any suggestions.","After making the future work clear, He Zhiran also gave Mo Hanyue the book explaining Chinese medicine, asking her to read it carefully and come to ask her if she didn’t understand.","Mo Hanyue happily hugged the book and went to flip through it.","There was still some time before lunch, and He Zhiran returned to the tent and flashed into the space."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: Giant Panda Doll","paragraphs":["There were still several dolls made by her best friends on the bedside table in the space.","Little Flying Elephant, Blue Elf, Mickey and others were basically based on the cartoon images in animations as templates.","He Zhiran thought that although these dolls looked good, they might not necessarily be popular when everyone didn't know them.","Therefore, He Zhiran felt that the style of the dolls could not exceed people's cognition in this era.","He Zhiran saw a round, quirky giant panda doll in Taobao that she liked at first sight.","It was just that she didn't know whether people in this era had heard of such an animal as a giant panda.","In order to confirm this, He Zhiran flashed out of the space, intending to ask Mo Jiuye about it.","When Mo Jiuye returned to the tent and did not see He Zhiran, he knew that she must have drilled into the space.","He simply sat in the tent and waited for her to come out.","He Zhiran's position when entering the space happened to coincide with Mo Jiuye's, and as soon as she came out, she was hugged by the latter.","\"When did you come back?\" Taking the initiative to throw herself into his arms, He Zhiran felt a little embarrassed.","With the soft and fragrant beauty in his arms, Mo Jiuye naturally didn't want to let go.","He naturally put his arm around He Zhiran's waist.","\"I've been back for an hour, and when I saw you weren't there, I waited for a while.\"","With a big hand suddenly appearing around her waist, He Zhiran instinctively wanted to dodge.","However, when she thought about it, on the surface they were husband and wife, and privately they had also confirmed their love relationship, so some physical contact was nothing.","So she didn't dodge, her face flushed as she asked, \"Have you ever heard of the Iron-Eating Beast?\"","She didn't forget that pandas were called Iron-Eating Beasts in ancient times.","Although Mo Jiuye had never seen an iron-eating beast, he was not unfamiliar with this name.","\"In the northwest where we’re going, it is said that there are iron-eating beasts haunting there.\"","After a pause, he asked back, \"What are you asking about the iron-eating beast for?\"","He Zhiran didn't expect that there would still be traces of the national treasure giant panda in the northwest.","In her previous life, she had been irresistibly attracted to creatures like giant pandas since she was a child.","When choosing a major at that time, she had even thought about animal protection.","That way, she would have hoped to become a panda breeder.","By a fluke, she finally chose medicine.","Now it was good, after going to the northwest, she hoped to get close contact with pandas.","With this in mind, He Zhiran looked forward to getting to the northwest sooner.","As she withdrew from her thoughts, a giant panda doll suddenly appeared in her hand.","\"Look at this one, isn't it very cute?\"","Mo Jiuye took over the panda doll and looked at it, sincerely saying: \"I believe this iron-eating beast doll will be more popular than the long-eared rabbit.\"","Iron-eating beast, iron-eating beast, this was the ancient name for pandas, but He Zhiran felt it wasn't cute enough.","\"Look, this iron-eating beast looks a bit like a bear and a bit like a cat. Why don't we change it to a cuter name and call it a panda?\"","Mo Jiuye stroked her head indulgently.","\"Panda sounds very nice.\"","Now, He Zhiran understood that people here did know about pandas.","Therefore, she decided that panda dolls could be one of the items in her business cooperation with Tang Mingrui.","He Zhiran pulled Mo Jiuye into the space with a flash.","This time, she didn't intend to continue disassembling the panda doll, but bought a book on doll making.","She chose a panda doll style that she particularly liked, and copied a set of drawings according to the style in the book.","In addition to making giant panda dolls, He Zhiran also selected a small bear in clothes and a cute little yellow duck.","Of course, the clothes of the little bear doll can be made with ordinary fabrics of this era.","Anyway, she still had some of the fabrics she had sneaked out of the treasury space left unused.","Having just started doing business with Tang Mingrui, she felt that these three styles were enough for now.","After He Zhiran finished copying the drawings of the other two dolls, the two of them left the space.","At this time, the women outside were already eager to start work, just waiting for He Zhiran’s order.","He Zhiran smiled and gathered everyone together.","\"This time I came up with three doll designs, the drawings are done, you can make the dolls according to the styles in my drawings.\"","As she spoke, she spread out the drawings to explain to the women.","\"I have marked the sizes on the drawings, as well as colors. You must strictly follow the drawings when cutting, there cannot be any deviations.\"","Hearing this, the women crowded around to carefully check the contents of the drawings.","When they saw the two words “panda” written on one of the drawings, they were all a little stunned.","Still, Sister-in-Law Two asked on behalf of them: “Sister-in-Law Nine, what is this panda?”","He Zhiran simply piqued their curiosity.","\"Sister-in-Law Two, when you make the doll according to my drawing, you will naturally know what it is.\"","Sister-in-Law Two was impatient, the more Sister-in-Law Nine didn’t say, the more impatient she was to know the answer.","So she directly took the panda doll drawing.","\"I'll take this one to study it, I must produce a finished product by nightfall to satisfy my curiosity.\"","Her words made the women laugh.","Eldest Sister-in-Law and Zhao’s wife also went up to take the other two drawings to study with everyone.","With things arranged, He Zhiran was free again.","At this time, the women had already put their minds into making the dolls, so He Zhiran could only personally prepare lunch for everyone.","Still, Mo Jiuye helped with the fire.","Just as she had just served the first dish, Mo Jiuye stood up.","\"The people who escorted Fe Mama are back, I'll go take a look.\"","Following Mo Jiuye’s direction of departure, sure enough, Song Chao and Wang Dali were waiting for him in a slightly hidden place in the distance.","Mo Jiuye did not talk to the two men for very long. Soon, he hurried back.","Without waiting for He Zhiran to ask, he took the initiative to tell about the process of escorting Fe Mama.","\"They said that thanks to the hair dye you gave, they discovered many people from Nan Qi on the way looking for Fe Mama's whereabouts.","Fe Mama dyed her hair black and avoided the search, safely arriving in the capital. \"","While He Zhiran was stir-frying the dishes in the pot, she asked,","\"Was the person delivered to Fei Nanyu's hands?\"","Fe Mama would definitely tell Fei Nanyu that she and Mo Jiuye already knew about his background when she saw Fei Nanyu.","Although both of them had expected that Fei Nanyu would not make things difficult for them because of this matter, there could always be variables in everything, and no one dared to guarantee that Fei Nanyu would definitely go in the direction they predicted."]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: The Number of Generals Can Only Be Counted","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye clutched a letter in his hand.","\"This letter was written by Fei Nanyu. I'll find a safe place to read it later,\" he said.","Exiled prisoners were forbidden from exchanging letters with anyone. Although Peng Wang treated them well, Mo Jiuye didn't want to be too brazen in his affairs.","He Zhiran was eager to know the contents of the letter. By chance, Wu Jie happened to come over to help at that moment, so He Zhiran temporarily left her here and pulled Mo Jiuye back to their tent.","The contents of Fei Nanyu's letter were not very long.","First, he thanked them for helping protect Granny Fei, a favorable witness for him.","He also assured them that he would properly arrange a hiding place for Granny Fei. If his identity were to come to light one day, the first thing he would do is clear the injustice against the Mo Family.","In reading the letter, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran looked beyond just the surface meaning.","When Fei Nanyu said \"thank you for helping me protect Granny Fei,\" it showed that he was grateful to them.","And when he mentioned clearing the injustice against the Mo Family, it indicated that he clearly knew the Mo Family's full banishment was unjust, while also hinting at his intention to win over the Mo Family.","Mo Jiuye had completely lost confidence in the imperial court by now. As long as his family's name could be cleared, he would be very satisfied.","He had never considered anything more.","They both understood this history and chose to help Fei Nanyu out of self-interest.","From how things were developing, it seemed likely that the way the Mo Family's innocence would come to light could differ from historical records.","In any case, things were moving in a good direction, which was what both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were happy to see happen.","He Zhiran directly stored the letter in her space. The two of them acted as if nothing had happened and continued preparing lunch for everyone...","For three consecutive days, the city gates and docks remained sealed as more and more officials searched the city for Nan Heng's whereabouts.","News of Nan Heng's disappearance was also quickly sent by fast horse to the capital.","When Nan Heng had left the capital earlier, it was under the pretext of investigating the Salt Gang's strengths and weaknesses.","Undoubtedly, in Emperor Shunwu's mind, Nan Heng's disappearance was absolutely related to the Salt Gang.","The audacity of the Salt Gang had gone too far, to the point of daring to make a move against an imperial prince. This was something Emperor Shunwu could absolutely not tolerate.","Therefore, he decided to send people to lead an army of 10,000 to the salt lakes area, both to search for clues about Nan Heng's whereabouts and, more importantly, to completely destroy the Salt Gang's nest.","As a result, when this matter was discussed at the morning court session, surprisingly no one volunteered to lead the troops there.","The number of military generals in the Golden Hall could be counted on one hand.","Originally, with Mo Family members guarding the borders, some generals had the chance to take up posts in the capital.","Now that the entire Mo Family had been exiled, even those generals on the borders had resigned one after another.","Seeing this situation, the enemy had already begun to grow restless, occasionally dispatching troops to harass them.","For this reason, Emperor Shunwu could only choose some generals in the capital to dispatch to the borders.","As a result, the number of generals in the capital grew fewer and fewer. Those who appeared at the morning court were all either elderly generals or inexperienced newcomers.","Emperor Shunwu was furious over this and involuntarily recalled the scenes from when Mo Family father and son were still around.","To wipe out the Salt Gang as well, back then with one call from him Mo Yunfeng had immediately volunteered to lead troops there. Now without the Mo Family people, he had actually reached a point where he had no one left he could use.","However, Emperor Shunwu did not feel that there was anything wrong with how he had punished the Mo Family.","Compared to the Mo Family's aggressive ambition that left him anxious and unable to eat or sleep well everyday, he was still more at ease with the current circumstances...","In the end, it was still an elderly general named Jin who took the initiative to volunteer and rush to the salt lakes before Emperor Shunwu's rage was somewhat placated.","In contrast to Emperor Shunwu's fury, the suburban areas upstream from the salt lakes were filled with sounds of jubilation that never ceased.","The women had successfully produced the first batch of panda, teddy bear, and duck plush toys.","Tell me, what woman could resist the allure of such adorable plush toys? Seeing the toys they had made with their own hands, everyone laughed unreservedly for the first time.","He Zhiran was very satisfied with both the style and workmanship of these plush toys.","Together with Mo Jiuye, she hurried to the teahouse as promised to meet with Tang Mingrui.","Upon seeing the three types of plush toys, Tang Mingrui immediately lit up. Particularly that utterly adorable panda plushie, even a grown man like him couldn't help fawning over it.","\"Eldest Sister Mo, is this an iron-eating beast?\"","He Zhiran also liked the panda plush. Its silly and lovable appearance instantly softened one's heart a little.","\"I had once seen illustrations of an iron-eating beast in books before. I felt they looked very cute, so I tried making them.","Also, I felt the name 'iron-eating beast' wouldn't appeal much to little girls. So I gave it a new name, panda.\"","\"Panda. This name really suits it and sounds nice,\" Tang Mingrui generously praised.","Next, he looked at the teddy bear and rubber duck plushies, extremely satisfied with those as well.","Especially those teddy bear plushies—He Zhiran had brought twenty, each one dressed in different clothes to give the identically shaped bear toys a sense of distinction.","And the bright yellow duckling was equally adorable.","Only after carefully looking over each type of plush toy did Tang Mingrui solemnly ask:","\"Eldest Sister Mo, all these plush toys are fine. Shall we talk about cooperation details now?\"","He Zhiran knew clearly that Tang Mingrui was a businessman. Thus, she decided to temporarily hand over the initiative and first listen to his suggestions.","\"For doing business, Master Tang understands it better. Why don't you share your thoughts first?\"","Tang Mingrui did not decline.","\"Eldest Sister Mo, the embroidery workshop sells these plush toys at three or two silvers each. I feel that's still an appropriate price. However, I don't plan to sell them at that price.","After all, the materials Eldest Sister Mo uses to make the plush toys come from Foreigners' goods. Surely the quantity is limited. That means the number of plush toys you can provide me is also limited.","Once the materials on hand have been used up, it will signal that there will no longer be additional plush toys. Therefore, I was thinking to sell them at a slightly higher price.\"","He Zhiran felt Tang Mingrui's explanation made a lot of sense.","Although she could purchase fabric for making plush toys without limit from the Taobao e-commerce platform, there was no way to explain that to outsiders here.","She also clearly understood one principle—this plush toy business couldn't be continued long-term.","\"Based on Master Tang's opinion, what price would be appropriate for selling the plush toys?\"","Tang Mingrui held up two hands. \"This little brother was thinking of selling the plush toys for ten taels of silver each.\"","Ten taels?","He Zhiran truly admired Tang Mingrui. Converted to modern currency, ten taels of silver was 10,000 RMB. To think such a tiny plush toy could be worth so much...","Seeing that He Zhiran remained silent, Tang Mingrui assumed his quoted price had startled her. He quickly explained, \"Eldest Sister Mo, the quantity of plush toys is limited. We can only selectively target rich people to sell them to.","Selling them this way, the turnover might not be very fast. But the profits will definitely be considerable.","Moreover, on our way traveling northwest from here, we will still pass through several cities. I believe that such nice and unique plush toys will surely be in high demand with scarce supply.\"","Although He Zhiran didn't understand business dealings, she could still fully comprehend the reason in Tang Mingrui's analysis.","At the same time, she also completely agreed with the latter's idea."]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: An Autumn Rain and a Cold","paragraphs":["\"That's no problem as long as Young Master Tang thinks it's suitable.\"","He Zhiran thought that anyway she was providing the dolls to him at cost price. Let alone ten taels, even if he sold them for twenty taels, an exorbitant price, she would not be envious.","Who knew, after Tang Mingrui stated his opinion, he was actually somewhat embarrassed.","He rubbed his hands somewhat awkwardly, an expression of wanting to speak out yet holding back.","With one look, He Zhiran could tell Tang Mingrui's discomfort and asked: \"Does Young Master Tang have some difficulty?\"","Seeing the other take the initiative to ask, Tang Mingrui lightly coughed twice to conceal his embarrassment.","\"I won't hide it from Lady Mo, recently I've been a bit tight on money, I can't pay the goods money to you first.\"","On this point, He Zhiran was not worried at all. She wasn't blindly contacting Tang Mingrui.","With his future development and accomplishments, he would absolutely not deceive her over a little bit of present benefit.","\"Young Master Tang doesn't need to worry, after the goods are sold, giving me the money is also fine.\"","Tang Mingrui had not expected her to trust him so much.","The more generous He Zhiran behaved, the more embarrassed he felt.","\"I'm grateful for Lady Mo's trust.\"","As he spoke, Tang Mingrui had already stood up and deeply bowed to He Zhiran.","\"Lady Mo, little brother has decided to cooperate with you in another way.\"","He Zhiran raised her brow. \"What does Young Master Tang plan?\"","\"I, little brother, will price these dolls with the lowest being ten taels of silver each. No matter what I absolutely won't sell for lower than ten taels. In the future the profits made, I'm willing split fifty-fifty with Lady.\"","Since she could obtain more profit, He Zhiran naturally did not decline.","Although she could not always keep an eye out for how much silver Tang Mingrui sold the dolls for, selling each doll for at least ten taels was an undisputed fact.","As long as she personally could split five taels of silver for each doll, it would be several times more profitable than selling to the embroidery house.","\"Good, we'll do as Young Master Tang says.\"","For Tang Mingrui making the most profit in business was best.","The reason he was willing to split fifty-fifty with He Zhiran was to repay her for saving his life.","After all, they were both exiled people. Compared to himself, life was even harder for them. He wanted that while he earned silver, he also wanted to change the life of Lord En's family.","As for Tang Mingrui's thoughts, He Zhiran had no intention of overthinking it.","Initially her reason for having Mo Jiuye rescue Tang Mingrui was mainly for convenience in doing business after arriving in the northwest.","Therefore, in her heart she only considered Tang Mingrui as wanting to have some business dealings.","Just like that, one wanted to repay kindness, one wanted to find a business partner for her family's future.","After the two reached an agreement, He Zhiran handed over all sixty dolls to Tang Mingrui.","In front of He Zhiran, Tang Mingrui checked over the number of dolls, and also wrote her a receipt.","The two once again agreed to meet here after five days.","Coming out of the tea house, the originally still sunny sky actually had large swaths of dark clouds.","Mo Jiuye looked at the weather, \"Let's hurry back, it looks like it's going to rain.\"","Speaking of rain, this was their second rain since being exiled.","\"It's often said, one autumn rain one chill. After this rain passes I'm afraid the weather will become colder.\" He Zhiran was somewhat worried. Everyone still sleeping in tents that couldn't preserve warmth, come night they would definitely not be able to endure it.","Mo Jiuye also had this worry.","\"Looking at the current circumstances, we won't be able to leave here to keep traveling for a while. As the weather gets colder and colder, it's not really a solution to keep going on like this.\" He Zhiran thought for a moment then said, \"Why don't we go back and discuss with Big Brother Peng, first rent a courtyard in the vicinity, sleep in the house at night, at least we can fend off the cold a bit.\" Mo Jiuye nodded. \"Alright, when I get back I'll talk to Big Brother Peng about it.","The rain came suddenly. By the time the two returned to the camp, it had started to come down. Everyone hastily ducked into their tents to avoid the rain.","Only the He family, they didn't have tents. The surroundings were empty without anywhere to avoid the rain. Very quickly their whole bodies were soaked wet.","It was even more so like this that they resented the other families. While being drenched they also cursed with a lot of foul language.","It was as if the He family felt that only this way would their hearts feel more comfortable.","And so, their cursing voices gradually shifted from initial whispers to scolding loudly and harshly.","They seemingly felt that cursing the Mo, Fang and Xie families was not enough. In the end they inadvertently even threw in words to curse Zhang Qing.","Originally, everyone was already used to the He family's behavior and just turned a blind eye to them.","Who would expect them to be so bold as to insult the officials....","The tent Zhang Qing was in was closer to the He family's location. Hearing the curses he went over, put on his rain hat, grabbed his horse whip and harshly taught the He family a lesson.","This time, the He family honestly shut up. Each becoming withdrawn again like a turtle.","This rain came quickly and left quickly. After pouring for a bit over an hour it stopped.","Mo Jiuye came out from the tent and directly went to find Peng Wang.","\"Big Brother Peng, I'm afraid we can't keep traveling for a while.\"","Peng Wang couldn't help but complain.","\"Don't know what these people are thinking about. If they can't find Prince Heng, are we going to be trapped here forever?\"","For this, Mo Jiuye also didn't know how to answer.","He was the one who killed Prince Heng, the corpse was sunk into the deep lake, it was impossible for anyone to find him.","And it was already so many days later, Emperor Shunwu should have already gotten the news by now.","He still hasn't given an order permitting them to move onward. This was enough to say that leaving here was far in the indefinite future.","Seeing that Peng Wang had already realized this logic, Mo Jiuye felt there was no need to explain too much.","\"Big Brother Peng, as the weather gets colder and colder it's not a long term solution to keep living in the tents.\"","In fact, Peng Wang also intended to rent a courtyard to temporarily reside in.","\"In a bit I'll send someone to go ask around. Find a suitable courtyard. It's just the rent for the place...\"","For the criminal group they were escorted, other than the Mo family the remaining families were penniless.","Peng Wang was drunk, this was the first escort job he had encountered such.","Not only was he unable to skim some benefits, the journey had been exceedingly unlucky the whole way.","To have him pay out of his own pocket to rent a courtyard for these criminals, he could spit out a mouthful of old blood.","If it were not like this he would have wanted to rent a courtyard to properly rest for a few days already.","Mo Jiuye naturally understood Peng Wang's meaning.","The salaries of these escort officials were the same as other officials with appointments in the capital city. The reason why they were willing to endure this hardship of long distance travel was still not because they could skim some benefits from the criminals.","The result was not only did they not receive any benefits from this escort trip, they also lost the lives of two of their men.","\"Big Brother Peng, there is no issue with the rental. For the officials portion of silver, we are also willing to help contribute a share. As for the Fang and Xie families, these past few days the children have earned some silver making dolls. Paying part of the rent should not be an issue.\"","Peng Wang had already gotten used to not getting any benefits from this trip. His earlier words were not meant to take advantage of Mo Jiuye's family either.","He was simply not willing to pay for renting housing for the criminals."]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: Some Want to rot.","paragraphs":["Unexpectedly, Mo Jiuye took the initiative to bear the rent for the government officials' residence.","This made Peng Wang feel extremely comfortable in his heart.","Peng Wang glanced in the direction of the He family.","They simply don't know how to be human. Look at how smart the Fang and Xie families are, being able to see the situation clearly early on and get along well with the Mo family.","With the help of the Mo family along the way, even though they left the capital without a penny, they did not suffer on the road.","What Peng Wang saw was only the surface.","No matter how He Zhiyuan tried to fawn over them from the start, even if he started to ingratiate himself with the Mo family, Mo Jiuye would not pay any attention to him.","Mo Jiuye followed Peng Wang's line of sight and knew that he was considering how to arrange these people from the He family.","On this matter, Mo Jiuye did not intend to express his opinion.","Anyway, whether the He family lived or died had nothing to do with him.","Peng Wang deliberately looked at the He family in front of Mo Jiuye because he felt that Mo Jiuye was generous. It would be even better if the latter took the initiative to offer to bear the expenses of the He family.","Who knew that Mo Jiuye didn't take the bait at all...","It seems that whether the He family can arrive alive in the northwest depends solely on whether they are fortunate enough.","After reaching a consensus, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran went to ask the Fang and Xie families for their opinions.","The two families happened to have similar plans. After all, the nights were cold, and they didn't know when they would be allowed to leave. As long as the rent was not too high, they could all accept it.","Peng Wang and Mo Jiuye went into town together to find a suitable yard.","They were really lucky. Originally, because of the blockade of the city, some traveling merchants were unable to leave. Some far-sighted people had rented houses early to settle down temporarily.","Therefore, it was not easy to rent houses here, and prices had also risen.","Mo Jiuye had no shortage of silver. What’s more, the larger the yard, the better.","Just happened to have a yard that was too big to be successfully rented out.","After some bargaining with the landlord, the two rented a large yard for fifteen taels of silver per month.","Fifteen taels to rent a yard for a month was indeed not a low price.","However, both Mo Jiuye and Peng Wang were clear in their hearts that during such special times, being able to rent a large yard was already very good.","Before nightfall, everyone had moved into the newly rented yard.","The yard was divided into front and back courtyards. There were twelve rooms in the front yard.","The kitchen and woodshed were in the back yard, and there were another eight bedrooms.","The distribution of residences was entirely arranged by Peng Wang.","He knew that Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran wanted to take care of the Fang and Xie families and would not let those two families share the rent equally.","Therefore, he directly assigned the eight bedrooms in the back yard to the Fang and Xie families for them to distribute among themselves.","The twelve rooms in the front yard were evenly distributed between the government officials and the Mo family members.","As for the penniless He family, they could squeeze together in the woodshed.","For Peng Wang’s allocation method, the Mo family, Fang family and Xie family were all quite satisfied.","The Fang and Xie family had already heard from Peng Wang about the rental price.","They understood clearly in their hearts that this silver had been paid by Mo Jiuye, and it had nothing to do with the officials.","Considering that they had been taken care of by the Mo family all the way, and now they had silver in their hands, they could not let the Mo family bear this alone.","After discussing it, they decided that each family would give five taels of silver to Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye understood their kindness. He had voluntarily taken on that portion of expenses for the officials initially and did not intend to make the other two families share the burden with him. However, the Fang and Xie families insisted, and in the end, Mo Jiuye could only accept their silver.","The Mo family was allocated six rooms. The sisters-in-law unanimously decided that the eighth and ninth brother and his wife must live alone in one room. The remaining four rooms would be distributed among themselves.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye chose a room on the very edge closest to them. They both liked peace and quiet, which was perfect for them.","That night, He Zhiran still brought Mo Jiuye into the space to rest.","Today just happened to be the tenth day since she opened the farm space.","The cows and sheep on the grassland had become adults in groups.","These cattle and sheep could not yet see the light at the moment. He Zhiran chose to continue breeding at the control panel.","Those mother chickens, mother ducks and mother geese could now lay eggs. He Zhiran chose to continue laying eggs. As for the male species, she chose to have the control panel system slaughter and store all of them in the warehouse.","As for the various fish in the pond, she also chose to continue breeding.","The fruit trees in the orchards on the hillside had also all reached maturity and successively bloomed. In ten days, she would harvest a lot of fresh fruits.","Looking at everything in front of her, He Zhiran felt somewhat like giving up.","If she could live a carefree life here for a lifetime, without intrigue, breathing fresh air every day.","When free, she could go for a walk in the mountains, and she could also work on the crops. Most importantly, there was also her beloved man to accompany her. Such a life was truly desirable.","However, He Zhiran's thoughts soon returned to reality.","A life like this could be realized without the space too.","The good life that was hard earned would feel even more fulfilling living it.","He Zhiran instantly had a life goal in mind, which was to build a paradise exactly like the space with her own hands.","With a new goal in life, she felt extremely sweet even when sleeping.","The next morning, He Zhiran got up vigorously and left the space with Mo Jiuye.","Sure enough, after an autumn rain, the weather outside became colder.","Considering everyone's warmth issues, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye went out specially to help everyone buy some cloth and cotton to make warm clothing.","The women knew the importance of keeping warm. Some of them temporarily stopped making dolls and hurriedly made winter clothes for everyone.","In the next few days, there was still no sign of letting people leave the city.","With a better living environment, the women worked even harder making dolls.","Until the fifth day, on the scheduled meeting time with Tang Mingrui, the women made more than one hundred dolls again.","This time, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not bring the dolls to meet Tang Mingrui. Instead, they decided to first look at Tang Mingrui’s sales situation.","Arriving at the teahouse as agreed, Tang Mingrui had already booked seats.","Seeing the two arriving, Tang Mingrui immediately stood up to lead them to a private room on the second floor.","As soon as they sat down, Tang Mingrui put a wooden box on the table.","\"Big Brother Mo, Sister-in-law Mo, there are three hundred taels of silver in it. I was going to hang some customers’ appetite by selling fewer dolls every day. Unexpectedly, those customers were too enthusiastic. I lost control for a while and sold out all sixty dolls in two days.","I went to find you near the jungle, but you had moved away from there. Helpless, I could only bitterly wait for our appointment today.”","He Zhiran smiled and said, “Isn’t that very good? It happened just as Young Master Tang wished, hanging those customers’ appetite.”","Having his original intention seen through by He Zhiran, Tang Mingrui scratched his head awkwardly.","“Hehe... I really can’t hide this little idea from Sister-in-law Mo.”"]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: Old General Kim","paragraphs":["After some small talk, Tang Mingrui got to the point.","\"Big Brother Mo, Big Sister Mo, how come you didn't bring any dolls this time?\"","He Zhiran spread his hands and told the truth.","\"I don't know about Young Master Tang's recent doll sales, so I didn't bring any dolls with me. We rented a house near the pier to stay temporarily. It's convenient to store dolls there. Young Master Tang can go get goods anytime.\"","\"Good. I'll go with Big Brother Mo and Big Sister Mo to your residence to get some dolls in a bit.\"","Tang Mingrui was eager to get the goods. He felt like even drinking tea had lost its flavor.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye didn't want to waste time on this kind of idle chat either, so they took the initiative to arrange to take Tang Mingrui to pick up goods.","Tang Mingrui knew their place of residence. He felt it was very convenient to pick up and deliver goods like this. Therefore, he only took fifty dolls today.","The income was relatively high this time. He Zhiran also raised the wages for the women's craftsmanship to one or two silvers per doll.","With the women's income increasing, the materials for making dolls ran out soon.","He Zhiran also planned to quit while ahead. Earning enough side money was good enough already. He couldn't cause trouble for this.","Tang Mingrui was too good at doing business. In seven days, he sold out all the dolls made by the women.","The Xie family and the Fang family divided fifty taels of silver again.","Now there were several dozen taels of silver in the hands of the two families because of making dolls.","As long as they used the silver wisely after arriving in the northwest, they could buy houses and land without worries about food and clothing for the whole family.","For this reason, the two families were increasingly grateful...","They thought they would have to stay here for some time, and had even prepared to spend the new year here.","Who knew plans couldn't keep up with changes?","The large army sent by the court to search for Nan Heng entered the city.","The leading General Jin received the Mo Family's kindness when he was at the border pass.","Originally, when the Mo Family property was confiscated and they were exiled, he wanted to secretly see them off.","However, Emperor Shunwu had long been wary of this. He ordered that everyone who had been close with the Mo Family must stay in the palace until the news came back that the Mo Family had left the city before releasing them.","General Jin's family members were also timid, afraid he would get in trouble with the Emperor because of the Mo Family, and strongly persuaded him not to make any moves.","For this reason, General Jin felt guilty for several days.","One of the reasons why he volunteered to come here was that he hoped to catch up with the Mo Family's exile and help them secretly.","But all the way until he reached the destination, he did not see the exiled convoy.","Just as General Jin felt he had missed crossing paths with the Mo Family on this trip, he could only routinely search the streets with his men. To his surprise, he saw a familiar figure up ahead.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran went out to buy supplies. Hearing the sound of officers behind them, they deliberately hid by the roadside to minimize their presence.","But Mo Jiuye's back was still recognized by General Jin at a glance.","\"Is that Young Master Mo of the Mo Family?\"","Mo Jiuye stopped and turned his head.","\"General Jin.\"","General Jin quickly dismounted, strode to Mo Jiuye, and carefully looked him up and down. Then he slapped Mo Jiuye hard on the shoulder.","\"Good, you kid are still alive and well, great!\"","Then he burst out laughing loudly, attracting the attention of all passersby towards them.","Seeing General Jin being watched by the public, his officers were very sensible to drive people away.","Seeing General Jin, Mo Jiuye also felt a sense of intimacy.","\"Has the general come to investigate the disappearance of Prince Heng?\"","General Jin looked Mo Jiuye up and down and asked quietly in his ear, \"Tell this old man, is Prince Heng’s disappearance related to you?\"","From the moment he saw Mo Jiuye, he had a feeling that Prince Heng’s disappearance must have had something to do with him.","\"The general really makes things difficult for Jiuye. I have no enmity with Prince Heng. How could I make a move against him? Moreover, I am now a banished person. The court’s disputes have nothing to do with me anymore. I just hope my whole family can safely arrive in the northwest and live peacefully.\"","General Jin just casually asked. Seeing Mo Jiuye's solemn expression, he didn't look like he was lying.","\"That's good that it wasn't you. Otherwise, this old man would have to think about how to help you escape.\"","Mo Jiuye smiled awkwardly, \"The general worries too much. Prince Heng's disappearance has nothing to do with me.\"","\"Okay, now I feel relieved,\" said General Jin. Then he looked again at He Zhiran beside him.","\"Is this young lady from the He Chancellor's family?\"","He Zhiran could see that General Jin was a friend rather than a foe.","She respectfully greeted General Jin with folded hands, \"Hello, General.\"","General Jin laughed loudly again, \"Very Good, very good. This brat Jiuye is lucky to have married such a beautiful daughter-in-law.\"","Mo Jiuye was happier than anyone when others complimented his wife.","\"My wife is indeed good. She has suffered a lot with me along the way.\"","\"Well, you two make a nice couple. Live well in the future and have more sons to continue the family line of Mo.\"","After a pause, General Jin said solemnly, \"Niece-in-law, don't worry. Your father is a sly old fox who knows how to adapt to circumstances. He was not implicated because he is related by marriage to the Mo Family.\"","Just a brief exchange made He Zhiran see that this old general had a hearty and casual personality.","\"Thank you for telling me, General. Please tell my father when you return to the capital that I am fine and ask him not to worry.\"","\"No problem. I will pass the message for my niece-in-law.\"","After talking for a while, General Jin suddenly realized that Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were casually walking around on the street.","In his knowledge, exiled people would always be watched by officers. How could they be so unscrupulous?","\"Young Master, how come you two are on the street?\"","And holding so much food...","Mo Jiuye did not intend to hide the truth from General Jin's inquiry.","\"Not to hide from the general, we get along pretty well with the officer in charge. He allows us to go out and buy some supplies occasionally.\"","\"Very good. I was always worried that after you all left the capital, with your injury and no one to help deal with those officers, you would suffer.","Seeing you look well now, I feel relieved.\"","After a pause, General Jin sighed and continued.","\"You don't know, on the day the Mo Family was ordered to confiscate property and exile, we ministers who were close with the Mo Family were all ordered by His Majesty to stay in the palace until you left the city before letting us leave.\"","So that was why her parents took so long to catch up after the exiled convoy left the city. It turns out they were not allowed to leave because of that treacherous emperor.","At the same time, she also thought that her sisters-in-law's families might be unable to see them off for the same reason.","It seemed her sisters-in-law had indeed wrongly blamed their in-laws."]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163: How to Get to the Northwest","paragraphs":["When Mo Jiuye was banished from the capital, he felt a sense of loss.","The Mo Family had been loyal for generations and he had also made some good friends.","But when disaster struck the Mo Family, not one of them came to see him off.","It turned out that all of this was engineered by Emperor Shunwu.","Mo Jiuye now understood clearly that the world was cold and indifferent. He did not want to dwell on those past matters anymore.","What he hoped for most now was to leave this place as soon as possible. After settling down in the northwest, he wanted to find a way to locate his elder and second brothers and help his sisters-in-law find saxifrage stalks to make an antidote.","“General, the city gates and piers have been sealed off completely. We've been stranded here for over half a month. If this drags on, I'm afraid we won't even reach the northwest by New Year,” said Mo Jiuye.","“That is indeed the case. It’s getting colder by the day and it would be very difficult for you all on the road,” replied General Jin.","After pondering for a while, General Jin continued, “My nephew, go make preparations now. Tomorrow morning I will personally arrange for ships to take you away from here.”","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were overjoyed to hear this.","The two of them saluted General Jin at the same time, “Thank you very much for helping us, General Jin.”","General Jin patted Mo Jiuye on the shoulder, “It’s just a small effort on my part. My nephew and niece need not take it to heart. I'll meet you all at the pier tomorrow morning.”","After thanking him again, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran hurried back to inform everyone of the good news.","The ones most excited were the deputy officers. If the journey went smoothly, they would be able to return to the capital to reunite with their families before New Year’s.","In order to allow Liang Hao, Tang Mingrui and the others to leave with them, Mo Jiuye could only discuss it with Peng Wang.","In fact, Peng Wang had already noticed the whereabouts of Liang Hao and the others. He just didn’t like getting involved in things and so hadn’t brought it up.","As for Tang Mingrui who often came to the residence to take dolls these days, he had also seen him several times.","Since they were able to leave smoothly because of Mo Jiuye’s efforts, he would naturally not refuse.","However, Peng Wang required that those people split off from the main group immediately after arriving at Dudao City, so as not to cause any trouble.","After Mo Jiuye finished negotiating with Peng Wang, he immediately notified Liang Hao and the others to go to the pier with them early tomorrow morning.","With everything prepared, they set off with their belongings for the pier early next morning.","As promised, General Jin was there early with a team of soldiers.","Although there were still guards at the pier, they did not hinder Mo Jiuye’s group.","What’s more, General Jin had specially arranged a passenger ship for them. The sailors were already ready and waiting for the passengers to board.","Mo Jiuye and Peng Wang walked at the front of the group. General Jin spotted them at a glance.","The General strode over, “My nephew, I've prepared the ship. I’ve paid the silver. You all just need to leave here with peace of mind.”","As he spoke, the General took out several banknotes from his bosom and stuffed them into Mo Jiuye’s hands.","“When you settle down in the northwest, you’ll need silver to buy property and other things for your family.”","Mo Jiuye was already very grateful that General Jin helped arrange for them to leave. How could he possibly accept the man’s money?","Moreover, he and He Zhiran were not lacking silver at all at the moment.","Without any hesitation, Mo Jiuye returned the banknotes.","“General, I understand your kindness. But I cannot accept this money.”","But General Jin insisted.","“I know the circumstances you all faced when you left the capital. Though this isn’t a lot, it’s just a token of my regard. You must take it.”","The pile of banknotes was tugged back and forth at the pier for a good while by the two of them.","In the end, General Jin relented and could only reluctantly take back the banknotes.","Then he signaled to the soldiers behind him.","Two soldiers came over carrying large parcels each.","“My nephew, if you don’t want the silver then forget it. But here are some rations I prepared for you to eat on the road.”","Mo Jiuye did not decline this time. After thanking General Jin again, he boarded the ship with the others.","General Jin remained standing at the pier seeing them off until the ship became a small speck in the distance before leaving with his men.","Today, the lake was calm and the sailing very smooth.","By nightfall, the group successfully arrived at Dudao City.","Without Mo Jiuye’s instructions, Liang Hao and his brothers concealed themselves at the back of the group.","Worried for his family, Tang Mingrui also bid Mo Jiuye farewell before leaving the group.","The exiled group rested overnight in Dudao City.","Before setting off the next day, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye asked Deputy Magistrate Peng for leave again, intending to go into the city and buy a mule cart.","Of course, what they really wanted was to let the mules out from the space and fit them up with a new carriage.","The group set off toward the northwest again with the mule cart.","They encountered no further trouble along the way and successfully arrived in the northwest after half a month.","The city gates of Yun City looked rather shabby. The two city guards on duty looked lazy and listless without a hint of energy.","As long as there were no special circumstances, people entering and leaving Yun City would not be inspected by the guards.","Especially when they saw deputy officers bringing people over, it was nothing unusual to those guards.","They merely cast a lazy glance before continuing their idle chatter at the side.","There were procedures to follow for bringing exiled prisoners to their designated location.","First, the deputy officers would bring the prisoners to the county government office to register, recording all their names before the local government issued new household registrations.","The household registrations for exiled prisoners were special. The paper bearing their identities would be marked with the words “exiled”, and stamped with the official seal of the local area.","Such a household registration would only allow them to move around within Yun City. If they secretly slipped out of the city and got caught, the two words marked on their registration would lead to their immediate arrest. After 50 heavy strokes of the rod, they would be sent back to Yun City.","This was one of the means by which the court restricted exiled persons.","Additionally, to prevent exiled persons from secretly leaving the city, special personnel would be sent by the government every half month to inspect the households of those people. If anyone was discovered to have secretly absconded, every single member of that family regardless of gender or age would suffer 20 heavy strokes as punishment.","That was still not all. The government would also immediately issue wanted notices to apprehend the escapee.","In short, having arrived here, unless specially permitted by the Emperor’s edict, they would spend the rest of their days here.","Peng Wang entering Yun City was like going down a familiar road. He brought the group straight to the county government office.","But they were informed by the gate guards that the previous county magistrate had just been reassigned. The new magistrate had not arrived yet. Handling the reception of these prisoners would be temporarily overseen by Deputy Magistrate Cui.","Upon hearing this, Peng Wang felt extremely troubled.","He was quite familiar with things here. That Deputy Magistrate Cui had his eyes open for money and was lustful.","Having Cui handle the reception would likely mean considerable trouble for the Mo Family."]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164: Play it by Ear","paragraphs":["Peng Wang understood Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's temperament. Although the two of them got along harmoniously with everyone on ordinary days, that was because no one had provoked them.","Especially He Zhiran. The scene of her roaring at the Eighth Old Zhou was still vivid...","In all his years as an escort officer, this was the first time Peng Wang had gotten along so well with prisoners on the road.","By now, he already regarded Mo Jiuye as a good brother and sincerely did not want them to be bothered and calculated against.","Therefore, Peng Wang felt that before going to Deputy Magistrate Cui to process the paperwork, he had to remind them first.","With this thought in mind, Peng Wang ordered the team to temporarily wait in front of the county government building while he went alone to the front of the Mo family.","Seeing Peng Wang come over, Mo Jiuye figured he must have something to say, so he took the initiative to ask:","\"Big Brother Peng, is there something you want to say?\"","Peng Wang edged closer into the crowd of Mo family members and said in a low voice:","\"Brother, the officials in front of the county government building just said that the former county magistrate of Yun City has gone to take up a post elsewhere, and the new county magistrate has not yet arrived. So now, processing your paperwork will be under the full authority of Deputy Magistrate Cui here.\"","When the official had just told Peng Wang this, Mo Jiuye had also heard some of it.","\"What's wrong with the deputy magistrate handling the paperwork?\"","Peng Wang looked at the two officials at the entrance of the county government building, then whispered:","\"Brother Mo doesn't know this. Deputy Magistrate Cui is greedy and lustful. In the past when I brought prisoners here to process paperwork, whichever cases were handled by Deputy Magistrate Cui, they would have to give him some benefits.","As for those families who don't care about their daughters, in order to be assigned a good place, they would offer up innocent young ladies...\"","Upon hearing this, the Mo family's faces darkened.","Mo Chuhan moved past Mo Jiuye and came close to Peng Wang.","\"What if my Mo family adamantly refuses to provide benefits?\"","Peng Wang sighed.","\"All the villages in Yun City accept exiled prisoners, and these villages are ranked from one to nine.","Without a doubt, Deputy Magistrate Cui would assign those who gave satisfactory benefits to villages with good environments and relatively superior conditions.","As for those families who really couldn't provide benefits but were willing to lower their stance and speak nicely, Deputy Magistrate Cui would be happy to assign them to mid-tier villages.","On the contrary, those unwilling to provide any benefits and also unwilling to lower their stance to curry favor would naturally be assigned to remote villages that no one wanted to go to.\"","After a short pause, it seemed Peng Wang recalled something. He continued:","\"Also, I heard that there are a few particularly special villages here. The environments and such are quite good, but no one is willing to go there.","The reason is that the villagers there are difficult to get along with. Whoever goes there won't last long before getting ostracized and left homeless.\"","The Mo family grew increasingly angry as they listened.","Mo Chuhan clenched his fists and angrily shouted: \"There really is no king's law! A petty deputy magistrate is actually so arrogant.\"","Seeing her husband showing signs of anger, the Eighth Sister-in-law promptly came forward to persuade: \"Husband, we should carefully discuss this matter with Ninth Younger Brother and the others first, don't be impulsive.\"","Mo Chuhan forcefully suppressed the anger in his heart and looked towards his family members.","\"Mother, Ninth Younger Brother, Ninth Sister-in-Law, all my sisters-in-law, what are your thoughts regarding this matter?\"","The Second Sister-in-Law was first to voice her stance: \"Such dog officials must not be indulged.\"","The Fifth Sister-in-Law also agreed: \"Second Sister-in-Law is right, he can't be spoiled.\"","Old Lady Mo looked towards Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","\"Jiuye, what do you and your wife think?\"","After exchanging a glance, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran replied: \"Mother, we'll act according to the situation.\"","Old Lady Mo nodded: \"Alright, act according to the situation.\"","Peng Wang didn't understand what the Mo family's \"act according to the situation\" entailed, but in any case, he had already clearly stated what he should warn them about. As for what the Mo family chose to do, that was up to them.","Without a doubt, the Fang Family and Xie Family would follow the Mo family every step of the way. Even if the Mo family really did end up in the worst place, they would certainly choose to follow.","Peng Wang went back in front of the county government building again and said a few words to the guards at the door. One official went inside to report.","Soon, the official returned and led the group inside.","Familiarly, Peng Wang entered a room. He quickly returned and beckoned for all the exiled prisoners to follow him inside the room.","Everyone stuck close behind Peng Wang as they entered the room.","The room was very big, probably arranged specifically for assigning these exiled people.","In the open space in the center, everyone stood without feeling crowded at all.","Sitting behind the desk at the head was a man who looked to be in his mid-thirties with a slender build - undoubtedly Deputy Magistrate Cui.","Deputy Magistrate Cui lazily raised his eyelids, glanced over everyone present, then arrogantly nodded towards Peng Wang.","Peng Wang was rank eight while Deputy Magistrate Cui was rank nine, so Peng Wang naturally would not debase himself before him.","However, this was Deputy Magistrate Cui's territory where he usually acted with no regard for anyone, completely looking down on Peng Wang.","Peng Wang was already used to this abnormal behavior. After all, everyone understood the logic of how local tyrants bully outsiders. Returning to the capital to report back as early as possible was most important to him. He was too lazy to contend with petty people like Deputy Magistrate Cui.","Although Deputy Magistrate Cui didn't think anything of Peng Wang, Peng Wang similarly would not lower his stance.","He beckoned to the Eighth Old Zhou, who delivered a stack of documents to the desk.","Then Peng Wang sat in a nearby chair without saying a word.","Deputy Magistrate Cui picked up the documents and glanced through them briefly, then squinted as he sized up the group of exiled prisoners standing below.","\"The Mo Family of the Duke Who Protects The Nation, the Fang Family of the Minister of War... Tsk tsk, all big shots!\"","As he spoke, Deputy Magistrate Cui's expression suddenly changed.","He slammed the table heavily: \"I don't care what kind of prominent families you were from before. Now that you're in my territory, you have to follow the rules here!\"","Next, an official stepped forward and shamelessly stated the distribution conditions here.","First he read out the names of a few villages, then said: \"Among all of Yun City, these villages are first-class places. Of course, whether you can live in this kind of place depends on your own conduct.\"","As soon as the official finished speaking, Liu, the elder daughter-in-law of the He Family, fawned over him and asked: \"Sir, may I ask what conduct is required to be assigned to the villages you mentioned?\"","The official looked Liu up and down several times. Seeing her tattered clothes, not an ounce of flesh on her skinny body, and the intolerable look of her face, his mood instantly soured.","\"You were all once part of prominent official families. Do I really need to teach you how to conduct yourselves?\"","Of course Liu understood the twists and turns in this, which was why she had politely inquired first to grasp the situation. She never expected that despite her courtesy, she would suffer ridicule!","Even so, Liu had no intention of giving up on currying favor.","The He Family had already suffered enough on the journey here. Having finally arrived in the northwest, they could not continue living such destitute lives. At the very least, their living conditions had to improve somewhat.","\"Sir, don't get angry. Let's talk nicely... talk nicely...\""]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165: What are you guys gonna do","paragraphs":["Liu turned her head and glanced at the direction of her family. The three adult men had already died on the way to exile.","What was left were the women and underage children.","When she came in, she had carefully observed Deputy Magistrate Cui.","With just a lazy glance from Deputy Magistrate Cui, she knew that he was looking at the beauties.","Speaking of beauties, the He family really had two.","Her two young aunts were a pair of twin sisters. They had been spoiled by their mother-in-law since they were young. The plan was that when they grew up, they could be married off to a good family and add flowers to the He house.","Now the two young aunts were fifteen years old, just at the budding age.","The He family did not have money, but the young ladies, one was not enough so both could be sent.","These two girls were delicate and had slowed everyone down on the way. Using them to exchange for the He family’s future living environment could be considered their contribution to the family.","In order not to continue to anger the yamen runners, Liu quickly went back to her family's position, ignoring her mother-in-law's opposition, and pushed the two young aunts out.","\"Sister-in-law, what are you doing?\"","Eldest Miss He did not know what her sister-in-law was up to and asked unhappily.","Liu smiled slyly, \"Of course it's to find a place where you can eat your fill and dress warmly.\"","At this time, Old Madam He also reacted and hurriedly tried to stop it, but was tightly blocked by the second daughter-in-law and two young grandsons.","The second daughter-in-law of the He family had the same idea as Liu. She had long been annoyed by the two young aunts who were a burden.","Now that they finally had a use, she naturally could not let her mother-in-law spoil things.","Old Madam He was blocked and did not dare to react too strongly in front of so many yamen runners.","The two young ladies of the He family were dragged by Liu and sent to Deputy Magistrate Cui.","\"Mr. Cui, take a look at this pair of twin sister flowers from our family?\"","In order not to give Deputy Magistrate Cui a chance to hesitate, Liu continued to lobby.","\"Mr. Cui, don't be fooled by their thin appearance now. That was from starving on the road. As long as they eat well for a few meals to recuperate, in less than a month, they can become glowing. Also, they have been learning music, chess, books and painting since childhood. With such a pair of beauties to accompany you, you will definitely not feel lonely.\"","When Deputy Magistrate Cui first glanced at the crowd, his main purpose was indeed to look at the women.","He had seen these two frail girls. It was just that in their tattered clothes and sallow complexions, he did not appreciate them.","After listening to Liu's words, Deputy Magistrate Cui looked at them carefully again. Indeed it was not bad. Although the skin was somewhat darker, the appearance was still good.","Especially their identical looks, which did have some attraction for Deputy Magistrate Cui.","The two young ladies of the He family resisted at first because they did not understand why they were pushed out. After listening to what Liu said, they understood clearly that the sister-in-law was going to send them to the deputy magistrate.","Thinking of the hardships they had suffered along the way, and possibly having to continue suffering in the countryside in the future, eventually still having to marry a farmer.","Rather than living in the countryside for a lifetime, it would be better to follow this deputy magistrate. At least there would be no worries about food and clothing in the future.","Therefore, after the two of them sorted out their thoughts, they no longer resisted. They even cooperated very much to let Deputy Magistrate Cui inspect them.","At this moment Deputy Magistrate Cui was in a very good mood.","\"Well, these two girls are pretty good. Keep them to serve me!\"","As he spoke, he looked at several yamen runners below: \"Come on, take the He family to settle in Yongfeng Village, and tell the headman there that these people were personally arranged by me to go there.\"","Upon hearing this, except for Old Madam He, the faces of the He family immediately showed joy.","They even raised their chins in the direction of the Mo, Fang and Xie families to show off.","The He family members followed the yamen runners out in a hurry, and the two young ladies were also temporarily settled by the deputy magistrate’s order.","Deputy Magistrate Cui was now waiting for the next family to come and curry favor.","Especially the Mo family, the women were all as beautiful as flowers, especially the one standing next to Mo Jiuye. Although wearing coarse cloth, it could not conceal her country destroying beauty.","For this reason, Deputy Magistrate Cui even began to fantasize about the scene of having such gentleness and beauty in his arms.","Who would have thought that after staring for a long time, he did not see these few families speak up.","Deputy Magistrate Cui immediately lost patience.","\"What do you guys want in the end?\"","The Xie and Fang families had already made up their minds to follow the Mo family all the way.","Giving their daughters to the deputy magistrate was out of the question. If the Mo family was willing to bribe with silver, they would give up everything they had to follow.","Therefore, they kept watching, just waiting for the Mo family’s decision.","Ever since Mo Chuhan heard Deputy Magistrate Cui’s first sentence, he had been enduring.","As a dignified adult man who had encountered countless freaks and monsters on the battlefield, he was still disgusted by Deputy Magistrate Cui's behavior.","He stepped forward, \"You are just a petty deputy magistrate. How dare you openly demand bribes? Aren't you afraid that someone will impeach you and you'll lose your job?\"","If he did not want to get Peng Wang and the others into trouble, he would have written a letter on the spot to take back to the capital.","He wouldn’t even need to give the letter to any important official, just handing it randomly to any of the brothers-in-law would be enough to ruin this Deputy Magistrate Cui.","Seeing someone voicing her thoughts, Eighth Sister-in-law hurried forward to echo: \"That's right, you, an honorable parent official, actually openly demanding bribes here. Once my Mo family has settled down, I will write to relatives in the capital city to expose your evil deeds.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were also very angry. If Mo Chuhan had not spoken first, they would also have taught this dog of a deputy magistrate a lesson.","Seeing that the Mo family had taken a stand, the Fang and Xie families stepped forward a few steps to show where they stood.","\"That’s right, although my Fang family is destitute, we still have some connections in the capital city. It is easy to convict a petty deputy magistrate like you.\"","\"The Xie family in the capital city also has some connections...\"","Deputy Magistrate Cui was so angry by them that his face turned green.","He had been a deputy magistrate for so long and was confident that he could grasp these exiled prisoners firmly.","But unexpectedly today he encountered trouble...","He was so angry that he immediately lost all reason. He slammed the table and stood up.","\"You people are so bold. A group of imperial exiles who actually dare to bluster in front of this official. This official sees that you do not want to live well.\"","As he spoke, he was about to order people to catch all of them to fix them up properly and let them know who was the authority here.","Just as Deputy Magistrate Cui was about to take action, the yamen runner beside him hurriedly came up and whispered to him.","I don't know what the yamen runner said, but although Deputy Magistrate Cui's face was still ugly, he was not as agitated as before.","Peng Wang, who was sitting on the side watching all this, was extremely anxious in his heart.","Seeing that Deputy Magistrate Cui had sat down, he hurriedly came forward to smooth things over.","\"Deputy Magistrate Cui, restrain your anger. Everything can be discussed well.\"","While speaking, he kept winking at Mo Jiuye, hoping that he could come forward to say some soft words to settle the matter."]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166: Xiling Village","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye understood Peng Wang’s meaning very well. However, facing such a deputy magistrate, he really did not want to compromise.","\"Deputy Magistrate Cui, please handle official business officially.\"","This was the first time that Deputy Magistrate Cui had encountered exiled convicts who did not take him seriously at all. If it were not for his subordinates reminding him just now that he was worried that what he had done would really be exposed by these people, he would have taught these people a good lesson.","Since these people did not let him be comfortable, then no one should think of living a good life.","He took advantage of Peng Wang's words to find a way out.","\"Mr. Peng has pleaded for you all already. As an official, I can't not give him face. Come on...\"","Two clerks immediately came up with their fists clenched: \"Here!\"","Deputy Magistrate Cui continued to order: \"The Mo family is assigned to Xi Ling Village. I’m sure the villagers there will welcome them very much.\"","Everyone present could hear the gloating in Deputy Magistrate Cui's tone.","Without even thinking, they knew that Xi Ling Village was not a good place to go. Deputy Magistrate Cui was deliberately making things difficult for the Mo family.","For Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, it didn’t matter where they went.","Especially He Zhiran, she had the space to help cheat, and wherever she went, she could lead the family to have a good life.","Mo Jiuye was not worried either. With him and Eighth Brother around, the safety of the family was fully guaranteed.","Life was lived by people, and as long as they were willing to work hard, Mo Jiuye believed that any harsh environment could be turned around through hard work.","The two clerks in charge of escorting the Mo family to Xi Ling Village looked at each other, both showing a look of watching a good show, smiling ambiguously, and greeting the Mo family: \"Come with us!\"","Seeing this, Peng Wang stepped forward and said, \"Please wait a moment, I still have something to say to them.\"","The clerks still respected Peng Wang very much. After taking the Mo family out of the room, they did not leave immediately.","Peng Wang came to Mo Jiuye somewhat angrily.","\"Brother Mo, I don't mean to criticize you, but at such a critical moment, how could you not endure it? Do you know what kind of place Xi Ling Village is?\"","Mo Jiuye did not regret his approach, but he still wanted to know about the situation in Xi Ling Village in advance.","\"Big Brother Peng, what is Xi Ling Village like?\"","Peng Wang sent convicts here almost every year, so he was naturally very familiar with Xi Ling Village.","However, whether it was the county magistrate here or Deputy Magistrate Cui, if it weren’t for extremely stubborn convicts, they wouldn’t choose to send people to Xi Ling Village.","He hadn't seen anyone assigned to Xi Ling Village in three or four years.","He sighed and said, \"It is said that Xi Ling Village is adjacent to the border. As long as those barbarians cross over a mountain, the first village they arrive at is that one.","“Recently, it has been okay. I haven't heard much about the barbarians coming to harass. In previous years, when they were short of food on their side every winter, some people would sneak in and rob.","\"And the first to suffer was Xi Ling Village. Not only that, I heard that Xi Ling Village is a clan-based village. Relying on their large number of relatives, the village chief there never valued outsiders.","\"Anyone who was assigned to live in Xi Ling Village would not be able to survive there for a year. They would either be scared away by the barbarians or squeezed out by the village chief and villagers to the point where they couldn't survive.\"","Mo Jiuye knew that Peng Wang was worried about them, but things were already like this. He could not appease such a disgusting deputy magistrate just for the sake of where he would be sent.","\"Thank you, Big Brother Peng, for informing me in advance. When I get there, I will act according to the circumstances.\"","Mo Chuhan also said, \"It’s just some barbarians. I don't think they can make much waves. That clan excluding outsiders, what can they do? Their fists won’t be harder than mine!\"","Peng Wang looked at Mo Chuhan.","Although the one he was most familiar with among the Mo family was Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, he was not completely unaware of this eighth master.","Who in the capital didn’t know that he was the one with the greatest martial power in the Mo family?","Since the other party had hard fists, he had nothing more to say. Anyway, he had done what he should do.","\"In that case, I have nothing more to worry about.\"","In the past, after Peng Wang handed over the convicts to the officials here to complete the handover procedures, he would leave. He would not care at all about who was assigned where.","If it wasn’t for worrying that Deputy Magistrate Cui would make things difficult for the Mo family today, he would have left long ago.","Now that the Mo family's placement had been completed, there was no need for him to stay here any longer either.","After saying goodbye to Mo Jiuye and the others again, he greeted his subordinates to leave together.","As Zhou Laoba left, he took another deep look at He Zhiran...","In the room.","Deputy Magistrate Cui did not know that the Fang and Xie families were united with the Mo family wholeheartedly.","From experience, stubborn people like the Mo family were rare, encountering less than once in a few years.","In particular, he had already ordered that the Mo family be sent to Xi Ling Village to settle down. He must have thought that the Xie and Fang families would take it as a warning.","Unexpectedly, when he asked the two families for benefits, they reacted the same way as the Mo family.","In a fit of anger, Deputy Magistrate Cui directly assigned the Fang and Xie families to Xi Ling Village as well.","Normally, after Deputy Magistrate Cui had assigned the destinations for the convicts, he would have them wait in the yard and issue them new household registrations before letting them leave.","However, this time the few families had indeed angered Deputy Magistrate Cui. He did not immediately handle the household registrations for them. On the excuse that the county magistrate was not there, he temporarily suspended the processing.","As a result, the Mo, Fang and Xie families were currently all unregistered residents.","As for when the household registrations would be issued, that would depend on his mood.","The few families used to be officials in the imperial court. They could not accept not having household registrations.","It was said that they could not leave Yun City without household registrations, so whether they had them was not important.","But after arriving at Xi Ling Village, they would not be allocated any good housing, let alone be given land for free.","Under such circumstances, they would have to purchase housing and land themselves, but without household registrations, how could ownership be transferred?","Mo Chuhan first turned back into the room, followed closely by Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran. Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai also came forward on behalf of their families.","Deputy Magistrate Cui was just about to leave, wanting to meet the two little beauties he had just received.","He had just stood up when he saw the door of the room being pushed open forcefully from the outside.","Seeing this, the clerks quickly came to the door to stop them.","\"How bold, disturbing County Magistrate Cui. What crime should this incur?\"","On the surface, Mo Chuhan still looked a little weak, but that was just superficial. His physique felt no different from before.","He raised one hand, lightly brushed away the clerk blocking the way, and strode across the threshold.","The clerks were not stupid. Based on the fact that they had just been brushed away without any resistance, they could determine that this person was a martial arts practitioner.","Especially since this person had come in anger, if they went forward again, it would probably not be as simple as being pushed aside.","Therefore, the clerks did not go forward again, but stood to one side and shouted loudly, \"You guys stop right there. Do not disturb the county magistrate!\""]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167: Apply for Household Registration","paragraphs":["The other officials also saw how formidable Mo Chuhan was. They didn't dare to stop Mo Chuhan, but walked towards Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran behind him instead.","Unexpectedly, Mo Jiuye was not to be provoked either. Seeing people come over, he first protected He Zhiran behind him, then, like Mo Chuhan, pushed those people aside.","Now the officials realized the might of the two brothers. No one dared to step forward to stop them, they could only shout loudly at the side, trying to frighten away the crowd.","The Mo brothers ignored those officials who were like jumping clowns. They brought the people directly to Deputy Magistrate Cui.","Seeing this battle formation, Deputy Magistrate Cui instinctively wanted to slip away from the back door.","Mo Chuhan took a big stride forward to block his way.","\"Deputy Magistrate Cui, stay and process our household registration first before leaving.\"","Deputy Magistrate Cui...","He cared about face too, okay?","However, when facing Mo Chuhan's dignified face, he felt a chill down his spine.","Looking at his subordinates who were cowering at the door, his anger flared up.","\"What are you guys still stunned for, hurry up and drive these people out for me.\"","Seeing this, the officials could only tentatively step forward.","This time they were smart enough not to stop Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan, but went straight to Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai.","The two were scholars, and quite old. When pulled by the officials, they could only retreat according to the opponent's strength.","Fang Chuanzhou was also angry.","\"Let me go, I have something to say to the deputy magistrate.\"","Hearing the voice behind, Mo Chuhan and Mo Jiuye turned around at the same time, looking like they would take action if the officials didn't let the two men go.","Seeing the sharp looks in the brothers' eyes, the officials were so frightened that they shrank their necks, and their grips on the two men instantly became loose.","Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai broke free from the officials' restraints and angrily walked past the Mo brothers and He Zhiran to Deputy Magistrate Cui.","\"Deputy magistrate, isn't it difficult for you to not process new household registrations for us?\"","Deputy Magistrate Cui did not expect that these people would dare to question him so boldly.","He had never encountered such a situation before.","Now with the officials being useless, and the aggressive Mo brothers glaring at him, Deputy Magistrate Cui was also somewhat frightened at the moment.","A real man does not suffer losses right before his eyes. Revenge can wait ten years...","Anyway, no matter what now, he could not let himself suffer losses.","Thinking of this, Deputy Magistrate Cui cleared his throat, and his attitude was much better than before.","\"This official has explained it very clearly. Your household registration can only be processed after the new county magistrate arrives.\"","Hearing his words, Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai sneered at the same time.","Xie Tianhai stepped forward, \"Although I was demoted, I was also an official for decades. I am very clear about the official procedures. Don't settle personal scores here by making things difficult for us with the household registration.\"","Fang Chuanzhou chimed in: \"Has Deputy Magistrate Cui not read the Da Shun official system and responsibilities?","According to the law, household registration should be handled by the deputy magistrate. If you think this matter needs the county magistrate to handle it personally, may I ask, why does the court still keep you deputy magistrates?\"","These were originally what Mo Jiuye wanted to say, but now both uncles had said them all, so he slapped the table heavily.","\"I'm asking you, are you going to process the household registration or not?\"","Deputy Magistrate Cui already felt a little guilty because of Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai's words.","Being shocked again by Mo Jiuye, his forehead was instantly covered in sweat.","Those subordinates were also frightened like turtling.","He believed that if he dared to say no now, he would definitely suffer losses.","\"Pr...process. This official will process it for you now...\"","After all, these people would be living in Yun City in the future, and there were plenty of ways to deal with them. He could not let himself suffer losses.","After Deputy Magistrate Cui spoke, he nimbly took out a stack of blank specialized household registration papers from under the table. In front of everyone, he wrote all of their household registrations and stamped them with the official seal.","To guard against the dog deputy magistrate making trouble in secret, Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai carefully checked them after the household registrations were processed. Seeing no problems, they nodded at the Mo brothers.","The few people strode out of the room with their household registrations. Mo Chuhan even glared fiercely at Deputy Magistrate Cui again.","Deputy Magistrate Cui was frightened into another cold sweat...","Having just been deterred by the Mo brothers, the officials who escorted them to Xi Ling Village did not dare to bluster as before. Instead, they all acted like quails, only responsible for leading the way.","Not long after leaving the yamen, He Zhiran saw Tang Mingrui waving at her from the roadside.","He Zhiran deliberately spoke loudly to Mo Jiuye, \"Husband, how far is Xi Ling Village from here?\"","With the corner of his eye, Mo Jiuye also saw Tang Mingrui. He knew He Zhiran was asking this to inform the latter of their address.","So he deliberately amplified his voice and said, \"I heard Xi Ling Village is at the westernmost edge of Yun City, I don't know the exact distance either.\"","Tang Mingrui nodded at them, indicating that he knew where they were going, then left with his head lowered as if nothing had happened.","Xi Ling Village was located at the northwest corner of Yun City, at the border of Da Shun. As the name implied, there were continuous mountains and steep ridges. The endless mountains formed a dividing line between Da Shun and the barbarians.","Just because the terrain there was steep and dangerous, it was not easy for the barbarians to come. Thus, Da Shun did not build city walls there.","However, although the terrain was dangerous, it still failed to block the barbarians. After all, crossing a mountain with difficulty was always easier than attacking a city.","Of course, the barbarians did not harass them all the time either, only choosing to take risks when they encountered crop failures or ran out of food in winter.","Even so, it made the surrounding common people suffer unspeakably.","Because they never knew when the barbarians would come, they often lived in fear and trepidation.","The officials escorted everyone for a little over an hour before finally arriving at Xi Ling Village. From afar, Xi Ling Village was nestled against the mountains.","Although it was winter now and there was no snow in Yun City yet, the tops of the mountains were already covered in snowy whiteness.","Before entering the village, they could already see the continuous farmland. It was evident that Xi Ling Village had a lot of arable land.","The houses in Xi Ling Village were built concentrated in three places. If one didn't know beforehand that these houses all belonged to Xi Ling Village, it would be easy to mistake them for three separate villages.","Mo Jiuye stopped an official and asked, \"Why are the houses here divided into three places?\"","The official habitually wanted to ask for benefits, but instantly cowered when facing Mo Jiuye's deep eyes.","\"Let me tell you the truth. You offended Deputy Magistrate Cui, so he deliberately sent you here to suffer exclusion.","There are three big families in Xi Ling Village, the Cui Family, Zhao Family, and Zhou Family respectively.","The Cuis are all our Deputy Magistrate's clansmen. They are also the largest family here.","Although the other two families are weaker, they know better than to offend the Cui Family. That's how they can live here safely.\"","Peng Wang had already briefed Mo Jiuye about the general situation in Xi Ling Village, but he didn't know that this was the village where Deputy Magistrate Cui's clansmen lived.","If not for the official's information, Mo Jiuye really wouldn't have known about this relationship.","It seemed that Deputy Magistrate Cui had sent them to Xi Ling Village not only to let them suffer exclusion from several families, but more importantly, to get the Cui family members to take action."]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168: The Cui Family Difficulties (Part 1)","paragraphs":["He Zhiran saw that the officer was quite honest, so she secretly took out a little broken silver from her spatial ring and stuffed it to him.","\"Thank you for informing us of the situation, Sir. May I ask where we are going to live after we arrive here?\"","This was also the most concerning question for the others. The officer had already said earlier that the three families in Xi Ling Village worked independently, so where would there be a place for them to live?","The officer did not expect to get silver out of this errand. He immediately became all smiles.","He pointed to the area near the mountain foot behind the territories of the three families.","\"After passing the lands of the three families, there are some dilapidated houses at the back. You all will be settled there. However...\"","The officer paused, seeming somewhat hesitant.","\"What's the catch?\" Mo Chuhan anxiously asked.","The officer was most afraid of the Mo brothers. Seeing Mo Chuhan ask in such a stern tone, he was scared that Mo Chuhan would lay a hand on him. He quickly continued, \"It's just that those houses are not well-maintained due to their age. It would be hard for you all to survive the winter there, unless you can come to an agreement with one of the chiefs to rent their houses for temporary lodging.\"","As he spoke, it was as if the officer recalled something. He walked over between the Mo brothers and whispered,","\"The Village Chief of Xi Ling is Cui Family's clan elder and Cui County Magistrate's uncle. Those who are exiled here do not need the County Magistrate's notices. His clansmen already know what to do.","They will definitely make things difficult for you all. You have to be careful!\"","He Zhiran happened to be standing next to Mo Jiuye and naturally heard everything clearly.","She was not worried about whether they would make things difficult or not. Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan surely would not care about such clowns jumping around.","It was quite clever of the officer to establish some connections with them since they were new here. If anything were to happen in the future, it would be more convenient this way.","Thus, she softly asked, \"I wonder how we should address this Sir?\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran sent out another piece of broken silver.","The officer took the silver and weighed it in his palm. His smile grew even more obsequious.","\"Ehehe... My surname is Ma, called Ma Junshan. You can find me at the yamen if there is anything in the future.\"","What Ma Junshan thought to himself was that these people were not too lacking in silver to refuse to appease Cui County Magistrate.","It was all because Cui County Magistrate acted too arrogantly without knowing how to handle them properly.","Clearly, these people only responded to soft tactics instead of hard ones.","In order to gain benefits from them, he had to cajole them.","The other officers watched Ma Junshan's actions from afar and knew that he managed to curry favor from the Mo family. Seeing this, they rushed over towards the Mo family.","One of the slightly younger officers said to the Mo brothers,","\"Ahem... Let me advise you all. Later, when the Village Chief assigns you your housing, you definitely should not choose the one furthest east.\"","Mo Jiuye's face was already icy as he asked, \"And why is that?\"","The officer did not answer immediately. Clearly, he was fishing for silver as payment before he would speak.","He Zhiran extremely disliked such people and had no intentions of giving out silver.","After waiting fruitlessly for a while, the unhappy officer turned to leave.","But before he could take a step, Mo Chuhan grabbed him by his collar.","\"Speak. What's the reason?\"","The officer reflexively tried to resist, but when he met Mo Chuhan's bone-chilling eyes, he instantly lost all courage.","\"Let go of me first, let go! I'll tell you all even if you don't!\"","Mo Chuhan's large hand suddenly went slack. The officer nearly lost his balance and fell.","He rubbed his somewhat sore neck that got grabbed and said resentfully, \"Many people have died in that residence. Everyone says it's haunted.\"","Having said that, afraid that Mo Chuhan would continue questioning him, the officer turned and fled.","Seeing this, Ma Junshan also distanced himself somewhat from the Mo family.","It wasn't that he was unwilling to describe the situation of that residence in more detail. He still had to consider his colleague's face.","The Mo brothers did not try to stop him either as everyone had already entered the village. The allotted housing would soon be revealed.","As they spoke, the group had arrived at a clustered area full of residences.","These residences looked very distinct. The enclosing walls were over ten feet high and all the gates were tightly shut.","The officer led everyone to the largest residence and knocked on the door.","Ma Junshan once again came to the Mo brothers' side.","\"This is the Cui Village Chief's home.\"","Mo Jiuye lightly nodded his head, indicating that he accepted Ma Junshan's consideration.","Very quickly, the door opened from the inside.","The one who opened the door was a brawny man who looked to be in his thirties.","Seeing the officers, the man was startled for a moment before asking, \"Has the County Magistrate sent people?\"","The officer pointed to the people behind him and said, \"Three households in total. Please make arrangements, Village Chief!\"","The man looked at the skies. It was almost dusk.","\"My father is feeling unwell. We'll talk tomorrow.\"","As he spoke, a loud thud could be heard as the man slammed the doors shut. He was completely unafraid of the officers.","The officers were already used to such treatment.","Nearly every time they came here to bring people, the Cui Family acted this way on purpose to oppress the exiles.","Arranging lodgings was the Village Chief's duty. The officers only needed to bring people here to complete their task.","Therefore, after exchanging glances, the few officers turned and left.","As Ma Junshan had taken silver from He Zhiran twice, he still cared a little for the Mo brothers. Before leaving, he softly said to Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan,","\"Cui County Magistrate has long vented all his anger onto his clansmen, but whoever he sends here that has not appeased him will definitely suffer under the Cui Family helping the County Magistrate get back at them. Not giving you housing today was only their first move.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye interestingly asked, \"I wonder what their second move is?\"","Ma Junshan shook his head. \"We only bring people here before leaving, so we aren't clear on the specifics of their second move either.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded. \"Thank you for the warning, Sir.\"","This form of address from him was already giving exceptional face to Ma Junshan.","Afraid that his colleagues would report back to Cui County Magistrate, Ma Junshan did not dare to tarry here any longer as he hurried to catch up to them.","Seeing that the officers have gone far away, Mo Chuhan said angrily,","\"Looks like this Cui Family really is cruel. Since we have already offended Cui County Magistrate, offending his clan a bit more does not matter.\"","Having said that, Mo Chuhan immediately displayed his lightness skill and leapt onto the roof of the Cui Residence.","Mo Jiuye knew his wife liked spectacles. Right in front of everyone, he pulled her by the waist and closely followed Mo Chuhan, lightly leaping over the wall.","As expected of the Village Chief's home. The courtyard was neatly lined with three rows of brick-tiled houses.","At this moment, faint wisps of smoke could be seen already rising from the kitchen house in the west chamber.","A middle-aged woman had just exited the kitchen when she saw three strangers standing in the yard."]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169: The Cui Family Difficulties (Part 2)","paragraphs":["The woman was startled by the three strangers, and the wooden bucket she was carrying fell to the ground with a crash.","What followed was her angry questioning.","\"Who are you? How dare you break into my yard?\"","He Zhiran answered calmly, \"We are looking for Village Chief Cui.\"","Hearing that they were looking for Village Chief Cui, the woman looked them up and down disdainfully.","\"My father-in-law is not someone anyone can see whenever they want.\"","As she spoke, her eyes inadvertently glanced toward the gate.","\"My gate was closed. How did you get in?","Don't tell me you thieves jumped in over the wall.\"","Then the woman started shouting, \"Come quickly, thieves have broken into the yard!\"","Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan stood with their arms crossed, watching the woman screaming there without trying to stop her.","That was exactly what they wanted her to do, to shout and call Cui out.","Not long after, several doors in the front yard opened one after another, and several men and women came out,","including the man who had just gone to open the door.","Seeing the three people, the man was clearly very angry.","\"You are very bold, daring to break into a private house. Do you believe I will take you to see the magistrate right now?\"","Mo Jiuye sneered coldly, \"See the magistrate? Go see Deputy Magistrate Cui?\"","Hearing this, the man paused for a moment, then said, \"How dare you insult Deputy Magistrate Cui.\"","He Zhiran knew that the Mo brothers were not very good with words, so she took the initiative to step forward.","\"Deputy Magistrate Cui dares to openly take bribes and wrongly enforce the law. Such an official can hardly last long. I advise you to be kind, lest you become unnecessarily implicated.\"","Seeing that the speaker was a young and beautiful woman, the man did not take her seriously at all.","\"Shut up. Deputy Magistrate Cui is incorrupt. How dare you spout nonsense here?\"","A young man who looked seven or eight parts similar to the man was now walking over to them, holding a hoe.","\"This is Cui Family territory. Get the hell out of here immediately, or don't blame me for not being polite.\"","As he spoke, the young man had already raised the hoe, about to smash it down on He Zhiran, who was standing at the front.","He Zhiran was already prepared to fight back. But just as she pulled back her stance, she was hugged at the waist by Mo Jiuye behind her and pulled aside.","Mo Chuhan then lifted his foot and kicked the man's hoe out dozens of meters away, plunging deeply into the ground.","Next, he strode forward a few steps and stomped down with one foot on the water bucket the woman had dropped on the ground.","The bucket instantly shattered into pieces...","The swaggering Cui family members were frightened by Mo Chuhan’s skill.","Especially the one who wanted to hit people with the hoe, still maintaining the posture when the hoe was snatched away, at a loss as to what to do, standing in place.","In fact, Mo Chuhan had deliberately restrained himself when he made his move, after all, they had just arrived and their identities were special, and he didn’t want to make things too extreme.","If not for that, the two men present would have gone to see King Yama.","His actions did serve to deter them. The man immediately instructed a thirteen or fourteen-year-old boy behind him:","\"Wenqiang, go quickly and call over your grandfather and uncle.\"","Cui Wenqiang didn’t bother to answer, turned around and ran into the backyard.","Mo Chuhan stood in the middle of the yard, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran behind him, with no visible joy or anger on their faces.","After about the time it takes to burn an incense stick, an old man who looked to be in his sixties or seventies was escorted over by a group of men, women and children.","Village Chief Cui first looked at the shattered wooden bucket in the yard, then at the hoe plunged nearly a foot deep into the ground.","\"Minglin, Mingshen, what exactly happened?\"","Seeing Village Chief Cui come over, Cui Minglin and Cui Mingshen were like seeing a backbone.","The two came to stand in front of Village Chief Cui, one on each side.","“Father, these are the exiled people who were just sent by the government to register as residents of Xi Ling Village. My son told them that you were unwell today and would help arrange housing for them tomorrow.","But these reckless people actually dared to climb over the wall and break into our home and damage our property.\"","As Cui Minglin spoke, his eyes glared sinisterly at the Mo trio.","It was as if he was saying: The village chief of Xi Ling Village is here now. Offending the village chief, don’t expect to have good days hereafter.","But the Mo brothers and He Zhiran completely ignored Cui Minglin's gaze.","Mo Chuhan said coldly: “I just want to ask Village Chief Cui if housing can be arranged for us today?”","Unlike his two foolish sons, Village Chief Cui at least knew how to read faces and measure people.","Just looking at Mo Chuhan once, he could determine that this person was not easy to provoke.","His not very big bean eyes turned around as he secretly cursed that his nephew had sent him a hot potato.","Village Chief Cui's small face turned green, not knowing what to say.","He coughed violently a few times and said, pointing at Mo Chuhan:","\"It’s true that housing should have been arranged for you today, but those houses at the foot of the mountain have fallen into disrepair over the years and are currently uninhabitable. Why not repair them tomorrow and move in after that?”","“Then we'll have to trouble the Village Chief here tonight.\"","Mo Chuhan said as he was about to walk towards the house directly opposite the gate.","It was Mo Jiuye's first time seeing Brother Eight being so shameless too, but it was exactly to his liking.","He pulled He Zhiran with him to follow Mo Chuhan, intending to enter the house right in front of the Cui family.","Seeing this, Cui Mingshen hurriedly blocked their path.","\"What are you doing?\"","Mo Chuhan didn’t seem to use much force at all. With just a slight wave of his arm, he pushed Cui Mingshen aside.","\"Of course we’re staying overnight.\"","After a pause, he turned his head toward the gate and said,","\"Right, there are so many more family members outside. I'll go let them in now.\"","As Mo Chuhan headed for the gate, Village Chief Cui could stand it no longer.","\"Stop right there!\"","Mo Chuhan halted in his tracks and looked at Village Chief Cui with a half-smile.","\"What, is the Village Chief going to clear up a few rooms for us?\"","\"You...\"","Village Chief Cui was so angry that his old face turned blue, not knowing what to say.","He coughed violently a few times and said, pointing at Mo Chuhan, \"This is my Cui family’s territory. How dare you strangers come here and stir up trouble?\"","Seeing Mo Chuhan messing with the Cui family there, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were already laughing inside.","Now seeing that Village Chief Cui could no longer restrain himself, they knew the real show was about to start.","Since Mo Chuhan had put on such a good performance, they couldn’t lose face for the Mo family either.","So the two of them came to stand beside Mo Chuhan. Mo Jiuye said coldly: \"Since the Village Chief is unwilling to accommodate us, arrange our housing immediately. Otherwise...\"","Don't blame us for moving the whole family in to stay overnight.","Seeing that everyone of the newcomers was so arrogant, Village Chief Cui suddenly felt a little unsure of himself.","[Story to be continued tomorrow...]"]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170: These are the houses assigned to you.","paragraphs":["At this time, Village Chief Cui was somewhat complaining about his nephew who was the county magistrate that had sent so many tricky people his way.","In order not to suffer immediate losses, Village Chief Cui could only arrange their residence as Mo Jiuye had suggested.","Of course, he also wanted to first send these people away and then go into town tomorrow to recruit reinforcements.","When the time came, he would go to the government office and accuse these people of privately trespassing into a civilian residence, and make them eat a few days of prison food to taste bitterness.","Thinking of this, Village Chief Cui's attitude suddenly took a 180 degree turn.","\"Since you are in such a hurry, I will personally take you to your place of residence.\"","As he spoke, Village Chief Cui had already started striding towards the gate.","The Mo brothers and He Zhiran were all aware that the sudden change in the Village Chief's attitude meant that he had some big trick up his sleeve.","However, they did not pay any mind to whatever so-called big trick the Village Chief had.","When the time came, they would just see his trick and counter it.","Of course, if the Village Chief was sensible enough to not provoke them, in order to avoid future trouble, they would also temporarily overlook today's matters.","It was unknown whether the Village Chief was deliberately stalling for time or if his legs and feet were really not good, but his walking speed was extremely slow.","Mo Chuhan was getting a little impatient and urged: \"Walk faster, have you not eaten your fill?\"","The Village Chief was deliberately dragging things out. He hoped that the later they arrived at their destination, the better. By that time, the sky would be completely dark.","With the houses dilapidated, plus the dark of night, it would not be convenient for them to do even simple tidying up.","Although they would not end up sleeping outdoors for the night, the dilapidated and drafty houses could still freeze someone to death while living in them.","The Village Chief did not expect that his deliberately slowed pace would actually draw urging.","In order not to arouse suspicion, he deliberately staggered.","\"Ah...when one gets older, the legs and feet are just not good anymore. Even if I want to walk faster, I can't...\"","Seeing this, Mo Chuhan wordlessly picked him up and strode forward with large strides.","Village Chief Cui's feet suddenly left the ground and he was immediately frightened.","\"What are you doing, put me down!\"","Mo Chuhan coldly said, \"You just focus on giving directions now.\"","Cui Minglin, who had come along with the Village Chief, was also scared by this scene.","He knew that his father had deliberately slowed his pace with intention, and hurried to catch up to Mo Chuhan, dissatisfied: \"Put my father down. His health is not good. You will injure him like this.\"","Mo Chuhan glanced sideways at him.","\"If you're afraid of injuring him, then hurry up and give directions. That way, I can put him down sooner.\"","Village Chief Cui lay on Mo Chuhan's shoulder, not daring to move at all, for fear that one careless move would get him flung off by the other party.","Cui Minglin did not dare continue defending his father after encountering Mo Chuhan's sharp gaze.","In order for him to \"swiftly escape this bitter sea,\" the Village Chief gave directions very carefully, afraid of taking even one wrong turn that would keep him laying over the other's shoulder a moment longer.","On the way to their residence, there was some uphill, and they still had to pass through the tribal areas of the Zhao Family and Zhou Family.","Although the weather was a bit cold and the sky was nearly dark, they still encountered a few villagers along the road.","The villagers were curious about who was so bold when they saw Village Chief Cui carried on the shoulder of a burly man, with an expression of furious but not daring to speak.","At the same time, a hint of tiny delight arose in their hearts.","Relying on a nephew who was the county magistrate, as well as the Village Chief being the head of Xi Ling Village, the Cui family had always looked down on them, the Zhao and Zhou families.","The two families lived in the same village as the Cuis without suffering a little oppression from them over the years.","And seeing how those strangers looked, they seemed to be exiled people who were assigned here.","If that was truly the case, they hoped that these people could persist in living here, creating more obstacles for the Cui family would be good as well.","When Village Chief Cui saw members of the other clans seeing his sorry state, he suddenly felt a little embarrassed.","He yelled at those people: \"What are you looking at, go back home!\"","The villagers feared Village Chief Cui. After his shout, they could only reluctantly leave, unwillingly, with no one daring to linger and continue watching.","Mo Chuhan walked fast. After going uphill for not too long, they arrived at the residences allotted to the exiled criminals in Xi Ling Village.","Glancing around, there were quite a few houses there, but many had already collapsed.","Even the ones that had not collapsed looked on the verge of tilting over.","Living in houses like these, they probably wouldn't even be able to sleep soundly at night and would have to be on guard at all times against collapse.","And not only that, because these houses had been uninhabited for so long, weeds grew wildly around them. At this time of year, the weeds had all withered, looking extremely desolate.","Mo Chuhan crudely put Village Chief Cui down on the ground.","Village Chief Cui stroked his chest, working hard to steady his breathing.","He pointed at the courtyard in front and said, \"These are the residences allotted to you!\"","Seeing these dilapidated houses, the Village Chief felt an inexplicable sense of satisfaction.","I'll be generous today. Choose whichever house you want from these houses.","He continued saying, \"I already said that these houses are uninhabitable. Tidy them up tomorrow then come back. But you insisted on not listening.\"","The people present were not fools.","Everyone could see that on the surface, the Village Chief was speaking as if caring for their well-being, but in reality he was just mocking them.","Houses like these, even tidying up might not make them inhabitable, unless they were completely torn down and rebuilt.","Especially in winter, it was simply impossible to build houses. Having them live here was practically marching to their deaths.","Seeing houses like these, everyone appeared very angry.","Fang Chuanzhou strode over.","\"Village Chief Cui, houses like these are at a complete loss even if we wanted to renovate them. Is this how you arrange residence for Xi Ling Village's new villagers?\"","Village Chief Cui did not feel he had done anything wrong at all regarding this.","\"The government also hasn't provided any places specially for you exiled people to live. These are houses left over by our ancestors. If not for this, when you came over, there wouldn't have been even houses like these for you to live in.\"","\"But how are so many of us supposed to spend winter in houses like these?\" Fang Chuanzhou wanted to reason with the Village Chief.","Little did he know, reasoning with someone harboring the deliberate intent to make things difficult would be like playing music to cows.","No matter what Fang Chuanzhou said, the Village Chief only had one response.","That Xi Ling Village had no extra houses besides these to provide for their residence. If they were not satisfied here, they were very welcome to go reason with the officials in the government.","He Zhiran had no interest in watching the two argue.","On the way over, she had already observed that other than where the three clans of Xi Ling Village lived, there really were no extra courtyards.","If they wanted to get through the present difficulty, unless they negotiated with those villagers to see if they could rent suitable housing to stay in temporarily.","Of course, those people also feared Village Chief Cui. Without his approval, even if the Zhaos and Zhous were willing to rent houses to them, they probably wouldn't dare to.","Just as He Zhiran was pondering countermeasures, Xie Tianhai walked over and pointed to the house furthest east, saying:","\"I see that house doesn't look too bad. It can be temporarily lived in after simple renovations.\""]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171: Mo Chongyuan","paragraphs":["He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked in the direction Village Chief Cui was pointing.","The house was on the far east side, presumably the one the government official had warned them was haunted.","From the outside, the house did indeed look nice, unlike the other crooked buildings.","But it was very small, probably only two rooms at most.","Aside from whether it was haunted, with just two such small rooms, how could they accommodate so many people?","Seeing a house they could live in, Xie Tianhai eagerly led his two sons towards it.","When Village Chief Cui saw him heading that way, a sinister smile flashed across his face.","Noticing this, Mo Chuhan quickly called out to the Xie father and sons to stop them.","\"Uncle Xie, please wait. I'll go take a look with you afterward.\"","He didn't know what was suspicious about the house that led to rumors of it being haunted. The Xie family had no martial arts skills. If something dangerous happened, there would be no one to help them.","Xie Tianhai always listened to the Mo family. Hearing Mo Chuhan call out, he obediently stopped and came back with his two sons.","Seeing the Xie family coming back, Village Chief Cui was clearly somewhat disappointed, though he didn't show it on his face. He solemnly said, \"Pick whichever house you want here. Wherever you want to live, go ahead. I've fulfilled your requests already and won't keep you company anymore.\" After speaking, he left, taking Cui Minglin with him.","Only after the Cui father and son had gone far away did Xie Tianhai angrily complain. \"Do they want us to freeze to death in houses like these?\"","Mo Jiuye stepped forward to placate him: \"Uncle Fang, don't worry. Let's take a look first before deciding what to do.\"","By now the sky was already dark. Xie Chao had found two thick wooden sticks somewhere and lit them to use as makeshift torches.","Considering the women were timid, Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan decided the two brothers would go take a look around first while the others waited where they were.","He Zhiran knew the two brothers were going to check out the house in the far east. Naturally, she didn't want to fall behind in this.","Under her firm insistence, the brothers finally agreed to let her tag along.","The three of them held a torch and walked towards the east, observing as they went in hopes of discovering a few more courtyards they could temporarily lodge in.","When they were halfway there, the three faintly heard sorrowful wailing coming from the east.","They immediately halted in their tracks.","\"Little brother, something is definitely suspicious over there.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded slightly. \"Right. Let's try to walk more softly so we don't alert them like startling birds.\"","The two brothers didn't believe the talk of ghosts and spirits.","Even if there were some, they weren't afraid.","The three tiptoed towards the east. The clearer the sounds became, the more suspicious Mo Jiuye felt.","With knitted brows, he said: \"Big brother, don't you feel like the voice sounds a bit familiar?\"","\"Little brother, you feel that way too?\" Mo Chuhan asked in response.","\"Let's go, walk faster and go take a look.\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye had already grabbed He Zhiran's small hand, quickening his pace by a lot.","As they drew near, they could confirm the sounds were coming from the house to the east.","From the agonized voice, they could tell it was a man, and his vitality was greatly diminished. If he wasn't in immense pain, he wouldn't be able to let out such loud wailing.","Mo Chuhan took the torch from Mo Jiuye. \"Little brother, you and sister-in-law stay here and wait. I'll go in and take a look.\"","When encountering this kind of unclear situation, it was most reasonable to leave someone outside as backup. Mo Jiuye didn't object.","\"Alright, big brother be careful.\"","Holding the torch, Mo Chuhan carefully entered the house.","After about ten seconds, he loudly shouted: \"Little brother, come quick! It's fifth brother. Fifth brother is still alive!\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran along as he rushed into the house.","In the torchlight, they could see that directly facing the door was a disheveled, tattered man.","The man was emaciated like skin and bones. His arms were spread apart and chained so he couldn't move.","His eyes were unfocused as he ceaselessly cried out in anguish.","Mo Jiuye stepped forward to take the torch from Mo Chuhan and examined the man closely. \"It really is fifth brother. How could he be here?\"","By now, Mo Chuhan had already strode forward. He touched the chains, trying to figure out a way to rescue Mo Chongyuan.","He Zhiran immediately went to stop him. \"Eighth brother, wait a moment.\"","Mo Chuhan looked at her uncomprehendingly. \"Sister-in-law, with fifth brother like this, it's very painful for him. I should rescue him first before anything else.\"","\"Eighth brother, fifth brother has likely been poisoned. If you rescue him now, I'm afraid he'll become even more out of control.\"","Ever since entering, He Zhiran had observed Mo Chongyuan's condition. Based on his somewhat purplish eye sockets, she could confirm fifth brother had undoubtedly been poisoned.","As for what exact poison it was, she would need to examine him further to find out.","Right now should be when the poison was taking effect.","Mo Jiuye understood He Zhiran's abilities. He knew she would never speak groundlessly.","Wanting to help persuade, he said: \"Eighth brother, listen to Zhiran. She knows medicine and certainly won't be wrong.\"","Mo Chuhan reluctantly pulled his hands back, unable to bear it. \"Sister-in-law, what should we do now?\"","He Zhiran didn't immediately reply. Instead, she signaled for Mo Jiuye to hold the man down a bit more firmly. Then she stepped forward to take Mo Chongyuan's pulse.","The results of her examination were indeed the same as what she had guessed.","Luckily, the poison Mo Chongyuan had wasn't unfamiliar to He Zhiran.","Its effects were similar to the Loss of Spirit poison she made from the venom of Silver Ring Snakes.","It's just that whoever concocted this poison had added several ingredients to drive one mad.","\"Eighth brother, husband, fifth brother has indeed been poisoned. The poison he ingested can make people lose their senses and even become insane.","However, this kind of poison only makes one turn into this during attacks. I estimate it won't be long before fifth brother regains his senses.\"","\"How long will it take for fifth brother to regain his senses?\" Mo Jiuye anxiously asked.","\"Based on fifth brother's current condition, his attack has probably been going on for some time already. I estimate no more than two hours for him to recover.\"","Upon hearing that fifth brother would have to endure such torment for two whole hours, Mo Chuhan felt extremely distressed.","\"Sister-in-law, is there any good way to temporarily alleviate fifth brother's suffering?\"","A good method?","The best method was to first detoxify the poison in Mo Chongyuan.","Although He Zhiran was confident she could formulate an antidote, it wasn't something she could immediately accomplish right now.","Currently, she still didn't know what other medicinal ingredients had been added on top of the Loss of Spirit poison Mo Chongyuan had ingested. She needed to determine that before she could start preparing the antidote.","This required a process. Even if everything went smoothly, she would still need some time.","Shielding with her sleeve, He Zhiran took silver needles from her space and swiftly inserted them at several of Mo Chongyuan's acupoints.","Very quickly, Mo Chongyuan quieted down as if he had fallen asleep, no longer struggling."]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172: He had a little bruise on his head.","paragraphs":["When Mo Chongyuan calmed down, everyone took the chance to look around the room.","The room was not big. Aside from a bed, there was only an iron pot in the corner next to the door and a set of bowls and chopsticks.","Next to them was a dead wild rabbit, likely hunted back by Fifth Brother.","Everyone guessed that these were probably what Mo Chongyuan used daily.","After looking around, Mo Jiuye spoke.","\"Eighth brother, mother and sisters-in-law are still waiting for news from us. Why don't you go back first to update them while I stay here with Zhiran to look after Fifth Brother.\"","Since there were no inhabitable houses here, it was unlikely they could find lodging in the other two families' places at this time. Fortunately, everyone had set up tents nearby. Setting up a few more campfires around should allow them to get through the night.","Mo Chuhan first looked at the passed out Mo Chongyuan before replying, \"Alright, I'll go back to arrange things now. Ninth Sister, I'll have to trouble you and younger sister to stay here with Fifth Brother.\"","After watching Mo Chuhan's figure disappear into the distance, He Zhiran took out a flashlight from her interspatial ring, using it temporarily for lighting.","Mo Jiuye asked, \"Zhiran, do you have an antidote for Fifth Brother's poison?\"","\"I can make the antidote, but it will take some time.\"","As she spoke, she took out a set of blood drawing instruments from her interspatial ring, drawing some of Mo Chongyuan's blood to bring into her space.","\"It's not convenient to research the toxins now. We'll talk about it later.\"","Although they couldn't help detoxify Mo Chongyuan yet, they couldn't leave him chained up like that either.","Just then, He Zhiran's flashlight shone on a key lying on the ground.","She bent over to pick up the key, trying it against the lock on the chains and finding it was the right size.","Mo Jiuye took the key and directly unlocked the chains.","From this key, they could infer that Mo Chongyuan had likely locked himself up.","The most probable reason was that he was afraid of losing control of himself during his poison flare ups.","Mo Jiuye moved Mo Chongyuan onto the bed to lie down properly.","Many questions were running through his mind.","If Fifth Brother was still alive, why hadn't he contacted his family?","Also, why was Fifth Brother here?","Who poisoned Fifth Brother?","Six years ago, the first son of the Mo family to perish was Mo Chongyuan.","At that time, Mo Jiuye was still studying under Nan Qi.","What the Mo family heard was that Mo Chongyuan had led troops to chase the enemy but unfortunately fell into the enemy's trap.","The surviving soldiers brought back his corpse that very night.","The more Mo Jiuye thought about it, the more muddled he felt. No matter how he wracked his brains, he couldn't imagine why Fifth Brother was clinging to life here after being poisoned.","It seemed like they could only get answers after Fifth Brother woke up.","He Zhiran calculated that after Mo Chuhan went back to inform Old Lady Mo and the women that Mo Chongyuan was still alive, it would take at least ten minutes for them to rush over.","Mo Chuhan had left for about five minutes now, so there were still ten minutes left. She planned to do a quick examination on Mo Chongyuan in this time.","With this thought, she pulled Mo Jiuye along to bring Mo Chongyuan into her space.","She used her instruments to check his head and heart, two important organs, at top speed.","To avoid leaving behind traces that might be discovered by the Mo family members arriving later, she brought the two of them out of her space after the checkup.","After settling Mo Chongyuan back onto the bed, Mo Jiuye finally couldn't resist asking anxiously, \"Zhiran, how is Fifth Brother's condition?\"","\"Apart from some issues in his head, Fifth Brother's condition is fine otherwise.\"","Mo Jiuye was puzzled.","\"What's wrong with Fifth Brother's head?\"","\"There's a hematoma in a small area of his head, likely caused by external factors.\"","Mo Jiuye probed further, \"Will this hematoma cause Fifth Brother any impairment?\"","He Zhiran shook her head. \"Fifth Brother hasn't woken up yet so I'm not sure exactly what impairments there are. The most common possibilities could lead to temporary blindness or impacted hearing.","There could also potentially be half-body paralysis, memory loss, etc...\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye immediately furrowed his brows.","\"If Fifth Brother really develops those issues, can they be cured?\"","\"That's hard to say for sure. It depends on the specifics.\"","The room lapsed into a brief silence.","He Zhiran was wondering just what effects the hematoma in Mo Chongyuan's head would have.","The only thing she could rule out for now was half-body paralysis. When they had first discovered Mo Chongyuan, his entire body was in an upright standing position and the strength in both feet looked quite balanced. Thus, this possibility could be excluded.","As for anything else, they'd have to wait until Mo Chongyuan woke up to uncover the truth.","Mo Jiuye felt rather worried. Fifth Brother had a stubborn personality. When he became clear-headed and found out about his own impairments, he would surely be in immense anguish.","Just as both of them were lost in their respective thoughts, hurried footsteps and female sobbing sounds could be heard from outside.","He Zhiran immediately put away the flashlight into her space ring.","Old Lady Mo's voice traveled ahead of her actual arrival.","\"Chuhan, is your Fifth Brother really here?\"","\"Mother, Fifth Brother is here. You'll be able to see him soon.\"","Soon, the door was pushed open from outside. The first to rush in was Fifth Sister-In-Law.","She strode swiftly to He Zhiran, grabbing her arm in one hand.","\"Ninth Sister, where is your Fifth Brother?\"","Using the torchlight Mo Chuhan held, He Zhiran led Fifth Sister-In-Law to the bedside.","\"Sister-In-Law, don't get agitated. Fifth Brother is currently still unconscious. Look after him here first.\"","At this time, where could Fifth Sister-In-Law still heed He Zhiran's reminders?","She threw herself onto Mo Chongyuan's body, wailing loudly.","\"Husband, you're really still alive! That's wonderful, you're not dead... wah wah...\"","Fifth Sister-In-Law shook Mo Chongyuan's body with crazed abandon, as if wanting to immediately shake him awake on the spot.","Helped in by Mo Chuhan and Mo Hanyue on either side, Old Lady Mo also arrived at Mo Chongyuan's bedside.","He Zhiran pulled Fifth Sister-In-Law back up forcibly.","\"Sister-In-Law, Fifth Brother's health isn't good. Don't hurt him.\"","Actually, Fifth Sister-In-Law shaking Mo Chongyuan a few times didn't really do any harm. He Zhiran thought that with the high emotional state Fifth Sister-In-Law was in right now, this was probably the only way to advise her properly.","Sure enough, upon hearing that her actions could affect her husband's health, Fifth Sister-In-Law immediately stopped moving.","Reluctantly, she moved away, forcefully holding back her tears.","\"Younger Sister, I beg you, you must save your Fifth Brother!\"","He Zhiran knew Old Lady Mo wanted to see her son. She pulled Fifth Sister-In-Law aside to make space.","\"Sister-In-Law, don't worry. I will definitely think of a way to cure Fifth Brother.\"","Fifth Sister-In-Law nodded vigorously. \"Mm. Ninth Sister is the most capable divine doctor I've ever met. You'll surely be able to heal your Fifth Brother.\"","By now, Old Lady Mo had arrived at Mo Chongyuan's bedside. Using the torchlight, she carefully inspected his features.","\"Chongyuan, Mother is here. Open your eyes and look at Mother...\"","As she spoke, Old Lady Mo could no longer hold back her emotions and broke out into loud weeping.","Just what wrong had the Mo family committed that even when a son returned alive from death it would still be so tragic?","Mo Hanyue wept nonstop at the side as well. The sisters-in-law also felt their hearts ache upon seeing Mo Chongyuan's current beggar-like state on the bed.","Everyone stood guard over Mo Chongyuan, with no intention to leave."]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173: Become a Loser","paragraphs":["He Zhiran was still the most sensible one. She thought that since the family had all come here, the tents for them to rest tonight still had not been set up.","\"Mother, eighth elder brother, sisters-in-law, it's getting late. Why don't you first go back and set up the tents? Jiuye and I will stay here to keep watch. We'll notify you immediately when fifth elder brother wakes up.\"","Old Lady Mo knew that what the ninth daughter-in-law said made sense. Besides, Mo Chongyuan was still unconscious now, and it was useless for them to stay. It would be better to go and settle the sleeping arrangements first.","\"Everyone listen to the He family girl. Go back and tidy up first.\"","After she finished speaking, Old Lady Mo walked out first, and the others followed closely behind.","Only the fifth sister-in-law was reluctant to leave. Her husband had just come back alive from the dead. She wanted to stay and take care of him.","He Zhiran understood the fifth sister-in-law's feelings at the moment, but she was planning to enter her space to research the antidote. It was indeed inconvenient for the fifth sister-in-law to stay.","\"Fifth sister-in-law, I will notify you first thing when fifth elder brother wakes up.\"","Since even the ninth younger sister-in-law said so, the fifth sister-in-law could only reluctantly leave with Old Lady Mo.","Now, only Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were left.","Mo Chongyuan should be regaining consciousness soon. He Zhiran didn't dare rashly bring anyone into her space.","Although she couldn't enter her space, she could still operate it with her consciousness. She planned to first analyze Mo Chongyuan's blood to determine the components of the poison.","While He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were here trying to help Mo Chongyuan detoxify, Liang Hao and the others who were still in Yun City were also not idle.","They had witnessed the whole scene of Cui County Magistrate bullying the Mo family today. They planned to stay and teach the dog official a lesson.","That was why they didn't follow the exiled people to Xi Ling Village.","Now it was late into the night and dark winds were howling. It was the perfect time for the 'Jiang Yang Bandits' to take action.","During the day, they had already found out the location of Magistrate Cui's residence.","They sneaked into the courtyard using their lightness skill , planning to first teach the dog official a lesson in the main courtyard.","Coincidentally, they just happened upon Magistrate Cui enjoying pleasure with the twin sisters from the He family.","The few of them swiftly knocked unconscious the nearby guards and servants. Liang Hao lifted his leg and kicked the door open.","The three naked people inside immediately screamed in fright. Since the people outside had been knocked out unconscious, no matter how loudly they screamed, nobody came running.","Magistrate Cui didn't even care about the two beauties now. He hastily grabbed the blankets to wrap around himself as he stared at the few masked people in fear.","\"Who...who are you?\"","Liang Hao and the others were very experienced in acting as the Jiang Yang Bandits. When they didn't plan to hurt anyone, they would not communicate with the other party at all.","Song Chao and Wang Dali moved in tacit understanding, and went forward to knock the twin sisters from the He family unconscious with hand chops.","At the same time, Xu Qingfeng dragged Magistrate Cui down from the bed.","\"Don't hurt me. I'm an official. I have money. Just name your price.\"","Xu Qingfeng completely ignored him. He thought to himself, I can get money with my own hands. I don't need you to give me any.","Magistrate Cui was dragged rudely in front of Liang Hao. Liang Hao grabbed his hair with one hand, and controlled both his arms with the other.","Xu Qingfeng cooperated perfectly by pressing down both his legs.","Then Li Mingrui timely pulled out a shiny dagger and stabbed down towards Magistrate Cui's lower body.","Following an extremely miserable scream, the man who was still enjoying pleasure with two beauties just moments ago instantly became an impotent.","Magistrate Cui had already fainted from the excruciating pain that accompanied his scream.","Liang Hao released his grip and went forward to viciously kick him one more time.","Seeing that Magistrate Cui was completely unresponsive, only then did he wave towards the others.","The few of them moved in great tacit understanding and immediately began ransacking the room.","It seemed this was not the room Magistrate Cui usually lived in. Other than a few worthless pieces of jewelry, there was nothing else.","Wang Dali stuffed the jewelry into his clothes, waved towards the others, then they cleanly left the room.","The few of them quickly turned Magistrate Cui's residence upside down.","Unexpectedly, the treasures they uncovered left them flabbergasted.","A small county magistrate actually had 50,000 silver taels worth of bank notes in his residence.","Apart from these bank notes, there was also close to 10,000 silver taels in hard currency.","On top of that, there was gold and silver jewelry, precious gems, silks and satins, antiques, calligraphy and paintings. Half a storeroom was filled full.","Unfortunately, the five of them could only take items that were easy to carry. As for those overly bulky silks, satins, antiques, calligraphy and paintings, etc, they could only temporarily let the corrupt official enjoy them for now...","The few figures flashed out of Magistrate Cui's residence, and sprinted towards Xi Ling Village.","With so much stuff on them, they couldn't blatantly walk in the streets.","Liang Hao led his brothers scaling walls and traveling on roof edges using their lightness skill. Very soon, they were out of the city.","At last, they all heaved a sigh of relief.","Song Chao weighed the large heavy bag full of silver sycee in his arms, and laughed, \"With this much silver, the ninth master's family doesn't have to worry about the future.\"","Wang Dali chimed in in agreement. \"Hehe... The dog official bullied ninth master. He must pay the price.\"","Now that the Mo family were no longer exile criminals, Liang Hao and the rest no longer needed to conceal their identities.","The few figures entered Xi Ling Village, searched around for a bit, and finally spotted the Mo family at the foot of the mountains.","Because of Mo Chongyuan's matter, the Mo family had not rested yet. Everyone was gathered around a bonfire, hoping to await news of Mo Chongyuan regaining consciousness early.","And so, it was very easy for Liang Hao and the rest to locate where the Mo family had settled down.","Mo Chuhan had heard the footsteps early on and went to check cautiously.","Discovering that it was Liang Hao and the others, he brought them to the bonfire.","Not seeing Mo Jiuye, Liang Hao instructed them to hand all these treasures to Mo Chuhan directly.","Then piles of gold, silver, pearls, and gems, along with silver ingots and silver bank notes came crashing messily onto the ground with a clanging sound.","The Mo family members all widened their eyes in shock.","Mo Chuhan asked dubiously, \"Liang Hao, what are these?\"","Liang Hao spoke somewhat proudly, \"Eighth master, brothers went on a stroll around at Magistrate Cui's residence just now.\"","Hearing this, Mo Chuhan laughed.","\"I really have to hand it to you brothers. If I knew earlier, I would have waited in Yun City instead of coming back too. Then I could have joined you all to vent some anger.\"","Song Chao moved closer and whispered in a volume only the two of them could hear, \"Eighth master, you still don't know. Just now, we severed the dog official's offspring...\"","As he spoke, Song Chao made a snip gesture with his hand. His eyes even shone with a gloating look.","Mo Chuhan shook his head with a smile. \"Hehe... You guys really are...\"","The Mo family's womenfolk saw the two whispering to each other and felt curious about their topic of conversation.","The eighth sister-in-law thought to herself that no matter what it was that could make her husband laugh so blithely in this kind of situation, she must find an opportunity to ask clearly...","Liang Hao swept his gaze around. If the ninth master was around, just hearing their voices he would definitely have come over already. Yet after they had returned for so long, there was still no sign of the ninth master.","\"Eighth master, isn't ninth master here?\""]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174: Who am I then","paragraphs":["Upon finding Fifth Elder Brother in Xi Ling Village, Mo Chuhan felt there was no need to conceal anything from his loyal subordinates.","So he briefly recounted how they had discovered Mo Chongyuan here, and explained that at this moment, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were on the other side taking care of Fifth Elder Brother.","Hearing this, everyone present widened their eyes in surprise.","This was simply inconceivable...","First Elder Brother had returned from the dead, then immediately afterwards Third Elder Brother did too, and now Fifth Elder Brother was also alive.","Could it be that all the Mo family men were still living?","Thinking of this, Liang Hao shook his head vigorously.","That was impossible. Back then, when Sixth Elder Brother and Seventh Elder Brother had died and their bodies were carried back, he had personally gone to verify it. He had even helped wipe the blood stains off their faces.","Those two were undoubtedly real, both in appearance and build.","This showed that even if the Mo family had other elders who were alive, it could not possibly be Sixth or Seventh Elder Brother.","In any case, being able to discover another survivor was tremendously good news for the Mo family and for them.","At the same time, in the room to the east...","He Zhiran was carefully looking over Mo Chongyuan’s blood test report.","Seeing that she had been reading for a long time, Mo Jiuye could not help but anxiously ask,","\"Ranran, is there a cure for Fifth Brother’s poison?\"","He Zhiran put the report away into her storage space, then revealed a smile.","\"It shouldn't be too difficult. I will study it later and I believe I can quickly formulate an antidote.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye was overjoyed, \"That's wonderful. Fifth Brother can finally be saved.\"","Just as he finished speaking, movement could be seen from Mo Chongyuan lying on the bed. Soon after, he opened his eyes.","Mo Chongyuan looked at the two strangers in front of him. His body nimbly sat up as he assumed a defensive stance.","\"Who are you two?\"","Mo Jiuye thought his appearance hadn't changed much from six years ago.","Why would Fifth Elder Brother ask this?","He hurriedly moved closer, trying to get his face as near to Mo Chongyuan as possible.","\"It's me, Jiuye!\"","\"Jiuye?\" Mo Chongyuan was clearly unfamiliar with this name.","Seeing Mo Chongyuan's current state, He Zhiran could now confirm that the blood clot damaging his brain was undoubtedly affecting his memory.","Noticing that Mo Jiuye was still stubbornly trying to get Mo Chongyuan to recognize him, He Zhiran could only helplessly remind:","\"Dear husband, Fifth Elder Brother seems to have lost his memory.\"","In fact, after seeing Mo Chongyuan's condition, Mo Jiuye had also considered this possibility. He just didn't want to believe it.","With He Zhiran's reminder, Mo Jiuye had no choice but to face reality.","\"Ranran, can memory loss be cured?\"","He Zhiran had just carefully checked the inspection results of Mo Chongyuan's head while in her storage space.","Although the hematoma was not large, surgery was not suitable for that location.","Also, looking at the area of ​​Mo Chongyuan's cerebral hematoma, he should have self-absorbed some of it relying on his own functionality.","\"It's hard to say for now. We'll have to look at the future situation of hematoma absorption. I can also give him some medicine to promote blood absorption, so it's still too early to determine the outcome.\"","Mo Jiuye knew He Zhiran would do her utmost to treat Fifth Elder Brother.","No matter the result, as long as Fifth Elder Brother could live, it would be an immense blessing.","While the two were discussing Mo Chongyuan's condition, he had already gotten out of bed.","He kept staring at the two strangers in front of him.","He didn't know why, but when he looked at the man, he felt a strange sense of familiarity.","Unfortunately, no matter how much he racked his brains, he couldn't remember where he had seen this person before.","Sensing Fifth Elder Brother's gaze, Mo Jiuye smiled back at him.","\"Fifth Brother, your head was injured, leaving residual blood clots in your brain, which led to your inability to remember things from before.\"","Hearing this, Mo Chongyuan subconsciously touched the back of his head.","There really was a scar there, though he didn't remember how it had occurred.","Although the guess was probably correct about his condition, Mo Chongyuan still did not relax his vigilance.","\"How do you know all this?\"","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran to his side and patiently explained:","\"Fifth Brother, this is my newlywed wife. She is also your ninth sister-in-law. Since childhood she has studied medicine and just now while you were unconscious, Ranran has already helped examine you.\"","He had thought that saying this would somewhat allay some of Mo Chongyuan's concerns, but instead, he became even more vigilant.","He swiftly reached out to grab Mo Jiuye by the throat.","Mo Jiuye didn't even try to dodge and was caught just like that.","Seeing this, He Zhiran wanted to step forward to stop him, but was prevented by a look from Mo Jiuye.","At this time, Mo Chongyuan spoke up.","\"How can you prove that you are truly my ninth younger brother?\"","Unhurriedly, Mo Jiuye took off his shirt, revealing a crescent-shaped birthmark on his shoulder.","\"Fifth Brother, this imprint is unique to the Mo family men. No matter what, it cannot be faked.\"","Upon seeing this mark, Mo Chongyuan also pulled down part of the clothes on his shoulder.","Not only were the two imprints exactly the same in shape and size, but their positions were also identical without the slightest difference.","Mo Chongyuan now believed Mo Jiuye's words and immediately loosened the grip on his neck.","\"Since you are my brother, then who exactly am I?\"","\"Fifth Brother, your surname is Mo. You are called Mo Chongyuan. There are nine brothers total in our family, plus a sister named Mo Han'yue.","The Mo family are military generals who have rendered outstanding service to Da Shun.","Six years ago, you were stationed to guard the frontier. Shortly after, news came saying you had died in battle...\"","Mo Jiuye briefly recounted to Mo Chongyuan what had happened to the Mo family over the past few years.","Hearing all this, Mo Chongyuan clenched his fists tightly.","\"So you mean I've been considered dead by my family for the last six years?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded, \"Yes, among eight elder brothers you were the first of whom death news came back.\"","Seeing that Mo Chongyuan did not continue asking new questions, Mo Jiuye then started interrogating him instead.","\"Fifth Brother, can you still remember how you ended up coming here?\"","What had happened after he lost his memory were things Mo Chongyuan naturally could recall.","\"All I know is that after getting injured, I was rescued by a peasant family. They were kind enough to invite a doctor to treat my wounds.","By evening, I realized my physical condition was getting stranger and stranger. Especially after sunset, I would feel an urge to go mad. Moreover, this feeling grew stronger day after day.","That agony caused me to become entirely irrational. My strength would also greatly exceed that of normal times.","I didn't know who I was or where to go. In order not to harm my benefactor when my toxicity erupted, I could only choose to leave there.","So I fled about aimlessly like this. Of course, I would only do so during the daytime.","I knew I would lose consciousness after sunset, and worried I might hurt innocent people, so before sunset I would run into the wilderness or up a mountain to hide and wait until returning to normal before continuing on my way.","Unknowingly, I ended up here. Discovering that there was basically no human activity here, I settled down temporarily.","I was worried I might injure villagers during my deranged states, so I used the silver earned from hunting to custom order shackles at a blacksmith's shop. Before sunset I would lock myself up, then unlock the chains once I regained clarity.\""]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175: Can't take away the fact that we're the same mother.","paragraphs":["At this point, Mo Chongyuan looked out the window.","\"It's not even midnight yet. Usually at this time, I'm not even awake. Could it be that you helped me?\"","Mo Jiuye looked at He Zhiran: \"Fifth brother, it was Zhiran who administered acupuncture to suppress the toxins in your body.\"","Following Mo Jiuye's lead, He Zhiran asked, \"Fifth brother, has the duration of your attacks been getting longer and longer?\"","Mo Chongyuan nodded: \"Yes, at first, I would recover in less than an hour, but now it takes at least three hours, sometimes even longer.\"","\"That makes sense. This kind of toxin is very special - it will spread throughout your body over time, getting closer and closer to your heart. The closer it gets, the longer the attacks will last.","Eventually, when the toxins erode your heart, whether day or night, you will be in a constant state of madness.\"","Although Mo Chongyuan didn't know what state he was in during his attacks, judging from the protruding veins and bloodthirsty eyes when he regained consciousness, it must have been terrifying.","\"If that's the case, I'll have to take my own life, lest I hurt innocent people.\"","He Zhiran knew that Mo Chongyuan didn't want to bring harm to others when he lost control.","\"Fifth brother, don't worry. Things aren't that serious. Tomorrow, my husband and I will go into town to buy medicinal ingredients to detoxify you.\"","Mo Chongyuan had never thought there could be an antidote to his poison.","\"Lil'...lil' sister...you're saying you can detoxify me?\"","When he was lucid, he had consulted with several imperial doctors about his condition.","Most couldn't detect any poison in his system. Only one somewhat competent doctor was able to confirm he had been poisoned, but didn't know what kind of poison it was, let alone how to treat it.","Because of this, Mo Chongyuan had felt hopeless for a long time, resigned to living out the rest of his miserable life this way.","He Zhiran flashed a confident smile. \"Fifth brother, don't worry. I will definitely be able to cure your poison.\"","Not only that, He Zhiran hoped to formulate the antidote quickly - she wanted to eliminate Mo Chongyuan's poison before the next sunset, so fifth brother wouldn't have to suffer another attack.","Just as Mo Chongyuan was about to say something more, Mo Chuhan came running over, worried about the situation.","Mo Chongyuan was vigilant by nature. As soon as he heard footsteps approaching from afar, he assumed a defensive stance.","He strode to the door, coincidentally bumping into Mo Chuhan head-on.","Mo Jiuye quickly stepped forward to introduce them. \"Fifth brother, this is eighth brother, Mo Chuhan.\"","Hearing it was his own brother, Mo Chongyuan immediately relaxed his clenched fists.","Mo Chuhan didn't know fifth brother had lost his memory. He was very curious why little brother still needed introductions when they were family.","Mo Jiuye quickly explained the situation to Mo Chuhan.","\"Eighth brother, fifth brother suffered a head injury that resulted in amnesia. He doesn't remember anything from six years ago.\"","\"What did you say? Fifth brother has amnesia?\" Mo Chuhan was clearly very shocked by the news.","Facing his inability to recognize relatives, Mo Chongyuan felt somewhat ashamed.","\"Eighth brother, was it? I'm afraid I don't remember anything from the past.\" This was his way of greeting them.","Mo Chuhan stepped forward and pulled Mo Chongyuan into an embrace.","\"Fifth brother, no matter if you remember the past or not, it doesn't change the fact that we came from the same mother's womb.\"","After briefly explaining Mo Chongyuan's condition to Mo Chuhan, Mo Jiuye asked:","\"Eighth brother, did you get the family settled in alright?\"","Mo Chuhan nodded. \"I settled everyone in, but no one wants to rest. They're all waiting for news about fifth brother.\"","Mo Jiuye looked at Mo Chongyuan and cautiously asked,","\"Fifth brother, do you want to come with us to see Mother now? And fifth sister-in-law - when she heard news of your death, she nearly cried herself blind.\"","When little brother mentioned this \"fifth sister-in-law,\" Mo Chongyuan felt a strange twinge in his heart.","Although he didn't remember having a wife, this peculiar feeling couldn't have been fake.","\"Alright, I'll go back with you.\"","Pushing open the door, a gust of icy wind blew in from outside. Amidst the whirling wind, they could vaguely make out the faint howl of some creature that sounded vaguely canine.","The sound wasn't very loud - at first listen it resembled a dog's bark, but not clearly so.","Mo Jiuye scanned their surroundings but didn't notice anything amiss.","Glancing at Mo Chongyuan, he saw his expression had softened considerably.","\"This little guy is back.\"","As he spoke, Mo Chongyuan had already broken away from Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan, striding towards the back of the house.","Exchanging glances, the others hurried after him.","After walking about fifty meters out, Mo Chongyuan halted his steps.","They could see him bent over, cradling a furry bundle in his arms.","In the moonlight, they could make out the bundle's white rear.","He Zhiran's eyes lit up instantly. \"Fifth brother, is that an Iron-Eating Beast?\"","Mo Chongyuan turned to face them, tenderly cradling the bundle.","\"Does lil' sister recognize this creature?\"","He Zhiran nodded emphatically. \"I recognize it! I saw it in a picture book before.\"","She simply couldn't resist such an adorable creature.","Zhiran hurriedly walked over to Mo Chongyuan.","\"Fifth brother, may I hold it?\"","The little bundle was clearly still a cub, no bigger than four or five months old.","At this age, it wasn't very large at all. Curled up into a round furball in Mo Chongyuan's arms, it made He Zhiran's heart melt.","Glancing between the tiny He Zhiran and the cub, Mo Chongyuan asked uncertainly:","\"Isn't lil' sister afraid?\"","He Zhiran shook her head vigorously. \"Not afraid, not afraid at all!\"","Seeing this, Mo Chongyuan carefully transferred the bundle into He Zhiran's arms, reminding her:","\"This little guy is timid. Be gentle with him, lil' sister.\"","Whether due to He Zhiran's special cat-whisperer talent or what, the moment the bundle was placed in her arms, after nuzzling around for a bit, it fell fast asleep...","Even Mo Chongyuan, who often interacted with the critter, couldn't help but sigh in wonder.","\"Looks like this little guy quite likes lil' sister.\"","Standing to the side, Mo Jiuye gave a sniff. In his heart he thought: Who wouldn't like gentle, capable, beautiful Zhiran?","Once ensuring the cub wasn't causing He Zhiran any trouble, the group headed towards where the rest of the Mo family was resting.","Along the way, curious Mo Jiuye asked: \"Fifth brother, is this Iron-Eating Beast your pet?\"","Mo Chongyuan didn't deny it.","\"I suppose you could say so! A few years ago, I rescued a mated pair of Iron-Eating Beasts on the mountain. At the time, they had been mauled by tigers. I brought them back here to recover.","Once their injuries had healed, I released them back into the mountains. I didn't expect the beasts to still have a sense of gratitude - every time I have an attack after sunset, they would come keep watch outside my house.","If anyone neared, they would let out a ghostly wail to frighten the intruders away. Over time, the villagers were convinced this place was haunted by spirits and wouldn't dare come close anymore.","Precisely because no one dared approach this place, I chose to settle here long-term.\"","Off-topic: Got inspired by Hua Hua and Ya Ya's videos lately and decided to go with \"Tuantuan\" [ie furball, fuzzy lump] for this novel's pet."]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176: Rice Ball","paragraphs":["He Zhiran became more and more interested as she listened, and asked eagerly, \"What happened after that?\"","When it came to later events, Mo Chongyuan felt somewhat sentimental.","\"At the beginning of this year, for some unknown reason, the pair of iron-eating beasts stopped coming here.","I was worried that something dangerous had happened to them, and went up the mountain to search for them many times but was never able to find them.","It wasn't until last month when an severely injured iron-eating beast came before me, carrying its child in its mouth.","Its injuries were too serious. After giving me this little one, it breathed its last.","I felt bad for the little one losing its parents at such a young age, so I kept it by my side to take care of it.\"","Upon hearing that this little creature was an orphan without parents, He Zhiran felt extremely pained, and held it even tighter.","As Mo Chongyuan told the story of Little Dumpling's experiences, he also indirectly explained the reason behind the hauntings here.","No wonder Ma Junshan had said the house furthest east was haunted - it turned out to be the noises made by the two giant pandas trying to repay an act of kindness.","Mo Chongyuan could see that the Ninth Sister-In-Law was very fond of the little one.","\"If the Ninth Sister-In-Law likes it, just keep it. I'm just a big, clumsy man who can't properly take care of it.\"","Hearing this, He Zhiran immediately broke into a radiant smile, the first time she had acted so ungracefully since coming to ancient times.","\"Then you have my gratitude, Fifth Brother.\"","This was the first time Mo Jiuye saw He Zhiran look so delighted.","Seeing her happy was more important than anything.","He went up and gently stroked the little one's back: \"Since you'll be keeping it, why don't you give the little fellow a name?\"","He Zhiran thought for a moment, then laughed. \"It looks round and plump like a rice ball, so why don't we call it Rice Ball?\"","Mo Jiuye indulgently stroked her head. \"Good, we'll call it Rice Ball.\"","As this couple flirted with sweet words in front, Mo Chuhan and Mo Chongyuan following behind really could not stand to keep watching.","In order not to disturb the Ninth Brother and Sister-In-Law's intimacy, Mo Chuhan pulled Mo Chongyuan to walk faster by several steps.","\"Fifth Brother, let's hurry on. Mother and Fifth Sister-In-Law are still waiting for you.\"","At this time, He Zhiran was still excited about gaining a precious treasure.","In order to provide better food for Rice Ball, her consciousness directly entered her spatial ring, where she spent 3,000 yuan to open up a bamboo forest, which she filled with delicious bamboo.","At the same time, He Zhiran also prepared formula milk for it, to feed Rice Ball conveniently later.","The treasure she He Zhiran raised had to enjoy national-treasure level treatment.","Although Mo Chuhan and Mo Chongyuan quickened their pace, over such a short distance they didn't get much further ahead than Mo Jiuye and his wife.","The four returned to where the Mo family members were resting.","Mo Chongyuan first acknowledged his mother under Mo Chuhan's introduction, then his daughter-in-law.","Upon finding out Mo Chongyuan had lost his memory, the two women broke down in loud sobs at the same time.","Especially the Fifth Sister-In-Law - having lived as a lonely widow for many years, her husband had finally returned from the dead, yet he didn't recognize her.","For a time, this was something she could not accept.","The Fifth Sister-In-Law unbelievingly grabbed Mo Chongyuan's arm.","\"Husband, you really don't recognize me? You once said that after winning battles and returning home, you would take me to Yueman Building in the capital to eat Dongpo pork.","You also said you would find time to accompany me to the temple to pray to Bodhisattva for a child. Could it be you've forgotten all this?\"","Seeing the woman before him crying her eyes out, Mo Chongyuan tried his hardest to think back to what she described.","But the harder he tried, the more his head would hurt, to the point he could only clutch his head in pain as he squatted on the ground, his expression very agonized.","He Zhiran knew this was a symptom that would appear in many amnesia patients.","Such symptoms usually occurred because the patient was trying hard to recall their past, only for their heads to hurt more the harder they tried.","In fact, for Mo Chongyuan, this was a good sign, indicating high probability of regaining his memories.","Even so, the patient could not be provoked too severely.","Seeing the Fifth Sister-In-Law become agitated as if she wanted to say more to get Mo Chongyuan to remember things, He Zhiran hurriedly went up to stop her.","\"Fifth Sister-In-Law, Fifth Brother suffered head trauma. Stimulating him like this can easily harm him.\"","The Fifth Sister-In-Law didn't know how doing so could harm her husband. But she had no doubts about the Ninth Sister-In-Law's words.","Thinking that her actions might injure her husband, no matter how much more she wanted to say, the Fifth Sister-In-Law didn't dare speak anymore.","Especially seeing Mo Chongyuan's agonized appearance, all the Fifth Sister-In-Law felt now was heartache.","She went up to gently help Mo Chongyuan stand up.","\"Husband, I won't say any more. If you can't remember, just think slowly. I'll have plenty of time in the future to tell you about our past.\"","Old Lady Mo also wanted more contact with her son, but seeing the young couple reunited after long separation, as an elder she knew better than to be so insensitive.","So Old Lady Mo called for the others to go to the bonfire area.","Mo Chuhan and Mo Jiuye took the initiative to tell their mother about Fifth Brother's circumstances.","Only then did the attention of the sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue shift to the rice ball in He Zhiran's arms.","There were still teardrops brimming Mo Hanyue's eyes. She casually wiped them with her sleeve, then moved next to He Zhiran.","\"Ninth Sister-In-Law, the little thing you're holding looks a lot like the giant panda plush toys we make.\"","He Zhiran gently flipped the rice ball over, making it face everyone.","\"This is a giant panda.\"","Mo Hanyue's eyes instantly lit up.","\"Ninth Sister-In-Law, this is really a giant panda? It's so cute. Can I hold it for a bit?\"","Since it was just for a short hold, He Zhiran was not stingy about it.","But as soon as Rice Ball's body touched Mo Hanyue, it violently shrank back with a faint cry.","The sudden movement frightened Mo Hanyue, who instantly retracted her hand.","\"Ninth Sister-In-Law, seems the little one doesn't like me.\"","\"Fifth Brother said just now that Rice Ball is somewhat afraid of strangers.\"","Mo Hanyue blinked her large eyes, seemingly in disbelief.","\"Is Ninth Sister-In-Law not a stranger to it?\"","He Zhiran also found this very odd. Ever since arriving in her arms, the little one had been very well-behaved without any visible discomfort.","Could she really have the so-called cat-attracting physique?","To verify this, He Zhiran tried letting the other sisters-in-law hold Rice Ball too.","The result was the same - Rice Ball flatly refused.","Now He Zhiran could completely confirm that she and Rice Ball were destined to be together.","She never expected that a dream unfulfilled in her past life would be realized after transmigrating.","After the women played with Rice Ball for a bit longer, they happened to look up and see Liang Hao still sitting alone over there.","Recalling that He Zhiran still did not know about what Liang Hao and the others did tonight, the Second Sister-In-Law opened up the conversation box and gave He Zhiran another rundown.","He Zhiran had originally thought that after settling down here, she would go take a tour of Magistrate Cui's residence with Mo Jiuye. She didn't expect Liang Hao and the others to steal a march on them.","As long as the benefits didn't flow into outsiders' pockets, it didn't matter who took action.","Moreover, she heard that many large antiques and artworks were still left in Magistrate Cui's home that hadn't been taken away. He Zhiran's heart stirred with desire once more."]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177: I just want to ask you something.","paragraphs":["When the opportunity arises, she can go there again. The money she gets in exchange can be used to buy all kinds of delicious things for Rice Ball on Taobao.","Of course, there is no rush for this matter. Cui County Cheng's mansion is still there and won't run away with legs.","The most important thing now is to solve the poison in Mo Chongyuan first, as well as the housing problem for the family.","The Mo family made quite a stir here, although the Fang and Xie families didn't know exactly what had happened, they could tell from the situation that something must have happened here.","Out of concern, Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou came over to take a look.","Old Lady Mo thought that her fifth son’s return from death was a good thing. He would also need to appear in front of people frequently in the future, so there was no need to conceal it.","So, the old lady briefly told the two men about finding Mo Chongyuan.","When Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou heard the news, they were truly happy for the Mo family.","After learning that Mo Chongyuan had lost his memory, the two comforted Old Lady Mo before returning to their own camps.","Old Lady Mo looked at the sky. It was already past midnight. If they didn’t rest now, they would have no energy to face more things tomorrow. So she urged her family members to go to rest.","Now Liang Hao and the others belonged to the newly added people, as did Mo Chongyuan. The number of tents was limited and could not accommodate them.","He Zhiran suggested letting Old Lady Mo and Mo Hanyue stay in the mule cart together, the fifth brother and sister-in-law could stay in their tent, while Liang Hao and the others could be settled temporarily in the room on the east side.","Everyone agreed with this arrangement and returned to rest separately.","He Zhiran had just turned around when Rice Ball hugged her calf.","Mo Jiuye also saw it. The little guy was sticking to his wife. Helplessly, he could only bend down to pick it up.","Unexpectedly, Rice Ball did not reject his embrace.","Mo Jiuye held He Zhiran's hand with one hand and carried Rice Ball with the other, and returned to the tent.","As soon as they entered the tent, He Zhiran pulled Mo Jiuye and Rice Ball into the space eagerly.","Seeing the lush greenery in the farm space, Rice Ball immediately forgot to cling to the new owner. It ran towards the mountain with its little short legs.","He Zhiran had prepared tender bamboo shoots, carrots and milk for it to enjoy when it got tired of running on the open space of the farm.","At this moment, what she needed to do was to formulate an antidote as soon as possible to solve the poison in Mo Chongyuan’s body.","After a night of research and experimentation, He Zhiran finally made the antidote before dawn.","At this time, Rice Ball seemed to have run out of energy and walked slowly back to the two.","He Zhiran checked the food she had fed it, which had been completely eaten up by Rice Ball.","She bought some more bamboo and bamboo shoots for it on Taobao.","Rice Ball was a complete foodie. When it saw delicious food, it would forget to cling to its owner.","Taking this opportunity, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye washed up before taking the well-fed Rice Ball out of the space.","Outside, the sky was still gray and gloomy.","The sisters-in-law had gotten up and set up bonfires in the center of several tents to keep everyone warm.","Perhaps because he had his family's company, Mo Chongyuan looked much more spirited this morning.","After a simple breakfast, Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou came over.","They had the same idea as He Zhiran, planning to go to Zhao and Zhou families in the village to see if they could rent suitable houses to live in temporarily.","The antidote made by He Zhiran was ready. Their trip into the city to buy medicine was just an excuse to give a reason for the antidote to see the light of day.","For now, the antidote was kept in the space, so they were in no hurry to go to the city.","Therefore, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye decided to go to the village to look for a house first before going to the city later.","After making the decision, the two intended to follow Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai into the village. However, as He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were about to leave, their feet were tripped by a meaty object.","He Zhiran bent down affectionately to pick up Rice Ball and said gently, \"Rice Ball, I have something to do. You be good and stay here waiting for me.\"","Rice Ball blinked its black eyes staring at her, refusing to leave.","Seeing this, Mo Hanyue tentatively reached out her hand to Rice Ball, \"Rice Ball, be good, let me hug you, okay?\"","Rice Ball looked at He Zhiran, then at Mo Hanyue, seemingly aware that its owner had something to do. It reluctantly went into Mo Hanyue's arms, though its heart was unwilling.","After settling Rice Ball, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran called Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai to go to the village together.","The living areas of the three families in Xi Ling Village were very concentrated. The Zhao Family and Zhou Family were located on opposite sides of the village road.","The Cui Family occupied a large area of land and was located in the center of the village. As a result, the housing clusters of the three families formed a triangular shape.","Through yesterday's events, they did not intend to have any more dealings with the Cui Family unless necessary. Therefore, the goal was to rent houses from the Zhao Family and Zhou Family.","When the group arrived at the boundary between the Zhao and Zhou families, they looked left and right.","Xie Tianhai asked, \"Niece, which side should we go first?\"","Instead of answering immediately, He Zhiran wanted to understand the situations of the Zhao and Zhou families first.","At this moment, a woman holding a child walked out from the Zhao Family side.","He Zhiran strode forward to politely greet the woman.","\"Hello sister-in-law, I am one who was assigned here by the government yesterday.\"","The woman looked nervously at He Zhiran and hurried away without turning her head.","It was hard to meet someone who could ask for information so early in the morning. He Zhiran did not want to give up this opportunity.","So she quickly caught up.","\"Sister-in-law, I'm not a bad person, I just want to ask you about some things.\"","The woman continued walking towards the Zhou Family side, showing no signs of stopping at all.","\"Go ask Village Chief Li for anything you want to ask about. I don't know anything.\"","From the woman’s words, it could be heard that she was very wary of Cui Li Zheng.","However, He Zhiran was not willing to give up so easily.","Using her sleeve to hide the view, she took out a small string of copper coins from her space, caught up with the woman's pace and stuffed them into her hand.","\"Sister-in-law, don't worry, I just want to ask some questions.\"","Feeling the heavy copper coins in her hand, the woman immediately stopped.","Her expression was tangled, unable to resist the temptation of money while worrying about being discovered having dealings with these people.","At this moment, the little baby in her arms began to cry.","Only then did He Zhiran notice that the child's face was flushed red with snot dripping from his nose.","The child must have caught a cold.","\"Sister-in-law, the child has a cold. I happen to know some medical skills and I have medicinal materials with me. Let me take a look and try to help.\"","Actually, He Zhiran didn't know that the reason this woman came out from Zhao’s place was that her child was sick but she didn’t have money to seek treatment, so she was on her way to her natal family on the Jiang side to think of solutions.","The bunch of copper coins He Zhiran had just given out was indeed very tempting to her.","There was no less than 100 wen, enough money to get medical treatment for the child."]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178: Everyone usually calls me osmanthus","paragraphs":["Having just heard that the other party could help treat the child's illness, the woman's fear in her heart was instantly defeated.","The woman knelt down before He Zhiran and pleaded, \"I beg Young Mistress to save my daughter.\"","He Zhiran quickly helped the woman stand up.","\"Treating your child is no problem, as long as Sister-in-law is willing to answer some of my questions,\" said He Zhiran.","The woman nodded vigorously. \"Okay, ask away!\"","\"May I ask, Sister-in-law, what are the relationships between the Zhou Family, the Zhao Family, and the Cui Family like?\" asked He Zhiran.","Upon hearing this question, the woman seemed somewhat nervous.","She looked left and right for a while before whispering:","\"Young Mistress, you have just arrived at Xi Ling Village yesterday and have already offended Village Chief Cui. Last night, he sent people to notify the Zhao Family and Zhou Family not to have any dealings with you.\"","He Zhiran frowned. \"What would he do if someone did have dealings with us?\"","The woman sighed. \"A few years ago, one of my clan uncles took pity on the people the government had sent here and secretly gave them some rations. When the Cui family found out, they told Village Chief Cui about it.","Village Chief Cui brought a group of people and nearly broke my uncle's legs.\"","After hearing this, He Zhiran gasped.","\"How can a small village chief be so overbearing and unreasonably bully people like this? And you all don't fight back?\" He Zhiran asked in disbelief.","The woman shook her head helplessly. \"The Cui family has a relative who's a county magistrate. Us commoners don't dare offend them!\"","He Zhiran asked again, \"Then what are the relationships between the Zhao Family, the Jiang Family and the Cui Family like?\"","\"On the surface, it seems like the Zhao Family and Zhou Family get along harmoniously with the Cui Family. But behind their backs, we all hate the Cui Family to death,\" said the woman resentfully.","After listening to the woman's account, He Zhiran understood clearly that if they wanted to rent houses from the Zhao Family and Zhou Family, the first thing they needed to do was restrain Village Chief Cui. Otherwise, those two families definitely wouldn't have the guts to rent houses to them.","Having asked all she wanted to know, He Zhiran kept her promise to treat the child.","She first felt the child's forehead and judged from experience that her fever was at least over 39 degrees Celsius.","After taking the child's pulse, He Zhiran completely confirmed that she had caught a cold.","Due to the prolonged high fever, the child now lacked energy and showed little reaction even when He Zhiran's rather cold hand touched her forehead.","Intravenous infusion was the best treatment in this situation.","But unfortunately, He Zhiran was unable to openly use injections for treatment here.","As a second resort, she could only choose medication therapy.","Her consciousness entered her space ring. In the infirmary's dispensary, she chose several pediatric medicines for the symptoms and changed their packaging into oil paper wraps. Then, hiding them up her sleeve, she took them out from her space ring.","She handed the medicine packs to the woman and carefully explained the usage methods.","\"Sister-in-law, this is medicine to reduce fever. Give it to your child as soon as you get home. And this is medicine for the child's inflamed throat, while this cures her cold and flu. Give her the cold and flu medicine half an hour after the antipyretic.","Also, we're currently living at the foot of the mountain. If the child's condition worsens, you can come find me there.\"","The woman clutched the medicine packs tightly and knelt before He Zhiran once more.","\"Thank you so much, Doctor. My maiden name is Zhou. I married into the Zhao family. People usually call me Guīhuā.\"","He Zhiran quickly helped her to her feet. \"Sister-in-law Guīhuā, there's no need to stand on ceremony. From now on, we're all villagers here, so helping each other is only right.\"","After thanking her profusely once more, Guīhuā finally hurried home with her child in her arms.","Mo Jiuye and the others had witnessed the entire exchange between the two women. They agreed with He Zhiran's judgment.","Given the current circumstances, if they didn't suppress the Cui Family's arrogance, they wouldn't stand a chance at renting houses from the Zhou Family or Zhao Family.","Both Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou were rather indignant at this moment.","\"Dear niece, I'm going to the Cui Family right now to argue this out with them.\"","However, He Zhiran did not try to stop them. But she didn't plan on going with them either.","The reason was simple. The Cui Family had suffered at their hands yesterday. Village Chief Cui must have rushed to the county magistrate to tattle first thing in the morning. Even if they went to the Cui residence now, Village Chief Cui wouldn't be home.","Although they wouldn't see Village Chief Cui himself, going to cause some trouble and vexation was still worthwhile.","Mo Jiuye also understood this rationale. Seeing that both uncles were weak scholars incapable of putting up a fight, he was worried they would suffer losses. So he reminded them,","\"Uncles, the Cui Family has many members and great power. If just the two of you go, I'm afraid you'll suffer losses. Why not go back and call up more people to go with you?\"","Hearing his words, Xie Tianhai seemed puzzled. \"Dear nephew, do you not plan on coming with us?\"","Mo Jiuye glanced at the sky and said,","\"My wife and I were originally planning on going into town today to buy some medicinal ingredients. Thinking it wouldn't take long to find housing, I just came along.","But if we go argue with the Cui Family, I'm afraid it'll take a very long time. In that case, we won't have enough time to go into town.\"","Xie Tianhai nodded. \"If nephew and niece have matters to attend to, then go on ahead. We'll call up our family members right now and go reason things out with the Cui Family.\"","What Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were thinking was that even if Village Chief Cui wasn't home, it would still be good for their group to go kick up a big fuss. At the very least, it would let the Cui Family know they weren't easy to bully.","To prevent Riceball from pestering her again, He Zhiran chose to stay put and wait for Mo Jiuye there. Mo Jiuye went back alone to fetch the mule cart.","Soon, he returned driving the mule cart. Once He Zhiran was seated securely, the mule cart sped off.","The road into town wasn't very near. The villagers of Xi Ling Village usually rode on the Cui Family's oxcarts.","But today, there were no oxcarts waiting at the village entrance offering rides.","The reason was simple. At the crack of dawn, Village Chief Cui had people take ox carts to carry him to Deputy Magistrate Cui to tattle.","Just as the villagers were sighing and complaining about this, they suddenly caught sight of a mule cart racing over from the distance.","The villagers didn't know who the mule cart belonged to. They assumed it must be someone else from the Cui Family who had bought another mule cart.","One villager strode forward to block Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's way.","The mule cart was forced to stop. Only then did the villagers see clearly that the driver was a stranger.","Although the people from the Zhao Family and Zhou Family didn't recognize the pair, they had heard about the new group of exiled people the government had sent yesterday.","Thinking of this, they could roughly guess the identities of the two.","The Zhao and Zhou family members quickly retreated, looking as if they were avoiding some ferocious beast.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran didn't find this reaction strange at all. They had just learned of the general circumstances from Guīhuā.","Seeing the villagers make way, Mo Jiuye ignored them and urged the mule cart forward, intending to continue on.","Just then, a villager rushed out from the crowd.","The newcomer was dressed like a scholar and even carried a coarse cloth satchel.","Somewhat embarrassed, he cupped his fists towards Mo Jiuye.","\"Brother, I'm rushing to get to school. May I trouble you for a ride there?\"","Right after the scholar's request, someone else chased up to them from behind.","\"Zechuan, get back here!\"","Zhao Zechuan looked back at the newcomer. \"Brother, you're afraid of the Cui Family, but I'm not. We're all villagers alike. Why should we let the Cui Family oppress us so?\""]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179: Look at the way things are here.","paragraphs":["Zhao Zeqiang grabbed Zhao Zechuan's arm: \"Don't talk nonsense in front of so many people.\"","Zhao Zechuan shook off his elder brother's grip, displeased: \"Elder brother, the more you act afraid of the Cui family, the more arrogant they will become. You're just fueling their ego.\"","After speaking, Zhao Zechuan forcefully broke free of Zhao Zeqiang's grip and went to Mo Jiuye again.","\"Sir, please give me a ride. I can pay the fare.\"","As he spoke, Zhao Zechuan had already taken out three copper coins and showed them to Mo Jiuye in his palm.","Whether there was a fare or not was secondary. This was the first time Mo Jiuye had seen someone in Xi Ling Village who was not afraid of the Cui family.","Therefore, he was willing to give Zhao Zechuan a ride. He could also take the opportunity to chat and learn more about Xi Ling Village along the way.","\"My cart isn't for carrying passengers, but since we live in the same village, giving you a ride shouldn't be a problem.\"","Zhao Zechuan was not pretentious. Hearing Mo Jiuye's words, he directly put away the copper coins.","\"Then thank you, sir.\"","He Zhiran was in the carriage, so Mo Jiuye let Zhao Zechuan sit with him on the cart's plank.","The mule cart slowly drove away under the complicated gazes of the crowd.","Everyone looked at Zhao Zeqiang sympathetically, worried what kind of trouble this would bring if the Cui family found out...","On the way to Yun City,","Mo Jiuye asked with interest while driving the mule cart: \"Aren't you really afraid of the Cui family?\"","Zhao Zechuan first carefully sized up Mo Jiuye, then smiled bitterly: \"Actually, by doing this today, I'm bound to upset the Cui family. They will also bring people to cause trouble for my family.","I was thinking, we are all just ordinary farmers. Who is above whom? Why does my Zhao family have to be suppressed by the Cui family?","Just because the Cui family has a relative who's a county magistrate?\"","Hearing Zhao Zechuan's words, he was determined to oppose the Cui family.","\"Aren't you worried that your family will suffer losses?\"","Zhao Zechuan sighed, \"I won't hide it from you, sir. Of the three families in Xi Ling Village, my Zhao family has the most people. If we really fought with the Cui family, they might not necessarily win.","It's just a pity that the Zhao family members are too timid. When something happens, they always want to resolve matters peacefully. Giving in again and again, we have been completely taken advantage of by the Cui family.","I deliberately did what I did today. I wanted to take this opportunity to change people's thinking. Ever since I was little, I started reading and have now passed the county exam to become a scholar. The clan has high hopes for me that I will be able to pass the exam in the future and gain an official position to stand up to the Cui family.","But in recent years, the Cui family has become more and more outrageous, not only suppressing the Zhao and Zhou families, but even trying to seize our land.","I cannot tolerate things like this. So I've also called on everyone to resist before, but I couldn't change their minds because the Zhao family is too afraid of the Cui family.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye looked at Zhao Zechuan with some admiration.","\"So your purpose today in deliberately taking my mule cart was to see if your clan would protect you when the Cui family comes to cause you trouble?\"","Zhao Zechuan nodded, \"Yes, as you said, sir, I do intend to use this opportunity to change people's thinking.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't know if Zhao Zechuan's plan would succeed, but he could be sure that the Cui family was going further and further down the path of self-destruction.","Deputy Magistrate Cui was severely injured by Liang Hao and the others last night. According to the laws of the Da Shun Dynasty, officials who are maimed are not allowed to remain in office.","His official career must have come to an end.","With the loss of support from their relative the deputy magistrate, let's see what the Cui family can still rely on to show off their power!","I believe this matter has already spread in Yun City. Zhao Zechuan would find out as soon as he enters the city.","Upon entering Yun City, Mo Jiuye discovered a strange phenomenon.","At this time, the doors of several clinics were all closed, although crowded with peasants who wanted treatment outside. The clinics showed no signs of opening for business.","Zhao Zechuan also noticed this.","\"Why have none of the clinics opened their doors today?\"","Mo Jiuye had already guessed the reason.","It was nothing more than Deputy Magistrate Cui arrogantly summoning all the doctors to treat his injuries.","Of course, he could not personally explain this to Zhao Zechuan.","Looking at the streets, groups of officers were going from door to door with large knives in their hands, searching houses.","Mo Jiuye drove on as if nothing had happened.","After going not far, he happened to run into Ma Junshan who was patrolling the streets with two officers.","Mo Jiuye drove the mule cart towards them.","Ma Junshan saw him at a glance and greeted him first.","\"What are you doing in the city?\"","Mo Jiuye could see that this officer was quite familiar.","So he didn't stand on ceremony too much.","\"I brought my wife into the city to buy some medicine, but I wonder why all the clinics in the city are closed today?\"","Upon hearing this, Ma Junshan looked around before moving closer to Mo Jiuye and said:","\"Last night, the deputy magistrate was injured in his genitals by several masked men. Before dawn, he had sent people to summon all the doctors from the clinics to treat him at his residence.\"","Mo Jiuye had already guessed the reason, but he asked on purpose to find out from someone else.","Although Ma Junshan spoke softly, Zhao Zechuan, who was sitting next to Mo Jiuye, heard it clearly.","At this point, Zhao Zechuan no longer cared about going to school. All he could think of was to bring this gratifying news back to the village to tell his clan.","Believing that after they learned Deputy Magistrate Cui had suffered such an injury, they would no longer fear the Cui family coming to cause trouble.","With this thought, Zhao Zechuan jumped off the cart.","\"Sir, thank you for the ride into town today. Something urgent came up so I must be going first.\"","From Zhao Zechuan's expression, Mo Jiuye could see how excited he was at the moment.","\"Alright.\"","Zhao Zechuan couldn't be bothered with more pleasantries as he swiftly ran back the way they came.","Ma Junshan exchanged a few more words with Mo Jiuye before leaving with his men.","Hearing the people outside leave, He Zhiran lifted the curtain and came out from inside.","\"Husband, where should we go first?\"","The purpose of the two coming to Yun City was to find an excuse for the antidote to see the light. They didn't really have a plan for how to pass the time.","Mo Jiuye looked at the sky. It was still early.","\"Let's just casually walk the streets and take a look at the customs here.\"","Indeed, since they had just arrived, it was necessary for them to learn more about the place where they would reside long-term.","Mo Jiuye drove the mule cart, wandering aimlessly through the streets.","Perhaps because Deputy Magistrate Cui was injured, there were officers everywhere on the streets.","Nevertheless, it did not affect the commoners' normal lives.","Aside from the clinics, the other shops were operating as usual, and street peddlers could be seen plying their trades from time to time along the roadside.","In order to find out about Deputy Magistrate Cui's condition, Mo Jiuye deliberately drove the mule cart towards his residence.","It really was a narrow escape from calamity—when they were some distance away from the Cui residence, they bumped right into Village Chief Cui's party."]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180: Difficulties for Officials","paragraphs":["Village Chief Cui sat dejectedly on the ox cart.","Cui Minglin also had his head drooped, seemingly lost in thought.","Mo Jiuye held the mentality of minding his own business and wanted to quickly pass by them, so as to avoid any verbal conflict.","However, just as the ox cart was passing by them, Cui Minglin lifted his head and happened to see Mo Jiuye.","Cui Minglin shouted loudly, \"What are you doing here? Don't tell me you've come to laugh at my cousin?\"","Village Chief Cui and several other Cui clan members on the ox cart also saw Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","Everyone's eyes fell upon them in unison.","A Cui clan member who looked somewhat unfamiliar asked, \"Brother Lin, could they be the exiled criminals assigned to our Xi Ling Village yesterday?\"","This person's tone was clearly very disdainful towards Mo Jiuye couple. They had now arrived in the northwest and were no longer exiled criminals.","Other than not being allowed to leave Yun City without permission, they were no different from these commoners.","Mo Jiuye glanced coldly at the man without saying a word.","The speaker shivered instantly under that icy look.","He had also heard that the exiled criminals who came this time had quite the temper, and not even the Cui family was able to get any favors from them.","However, in his mind, the Cui clan's prestige could not be lost as Cui clan members, otherwise how could the Cui family gain a foothold in Xi Ling Village in the future?","Upon thinking of this, the man jumped directly down from the ox cart and pointed at Mo Jiuye yelling,","\"What are you looking at? Be careful or I'll dig your eyes out!\"","For such a person, Mo Jiuye was too lazy to bother with excessive words.","With a 'snap', the whip used for driving struck the man's body severely.","Village Chief Cui had intended to stop his clansman from confronting Mo Jiuye forcefully, but his actions were not as fast as the youngster's.","Seeing Mo Jiuye raise the whip in his hand, he shouted loudly, \"Cui Liang, get out of the way quickly!\"","However, his reminder was still too slow, as the whip had already greeted Cui Liang's body.","For someone who practiced martial arts all year round, even without internal energy infused, the force of this whip on a human body was beyond compare to ordinary people.","Cui Liang yelled out in pain, \"Ah...you dare to attack in broad daylight, is there still royal law?\"","Mo Jiuye sneered coldly, \"You still know about royal law?","When your Cui family relied on the county magistrate clansman to bully and domineer in Xi Ling Village, where was this talk of royal law?\"","By now, quite a few onlookers had gathered.","They didn't know the relationship between the quarreling sides, but even so, they could still see that it was the people on the ox cart who provoked first.","For such people, one could deduce without thinking that they must have bullied others relying on power frequently.","Therefore, when Cui Liang mentioned royal law yet was refuted by Mo Jiuye, the onlookers all laughed.","Cui Liang was unwilling to admit defeat. He pointed at Mo Jiuye and shouted, \"You dare to attack people in the streets, I'm going to report you to the authorities!\"","Mo Jiuye sneered coldly, \"Do you think your Cui family county magistrate has time for you now that he is severely injured?\"","Upon hearing this, Cui Liang instantly lost some confidence.","Coincidentally at this moment, several officers had just come out from the Cui residence. Cui Liang's eyes turned swiftly as he hurriedly ran over.","He pointed in Mo Jiuye's direction and told the officers, \"Do you see that man over there? I suspect he is the one who injured the county magistrate, hurry and arrest him!\"","Hearing that the assailant who stabbed the county magistrate had appeared, several officers surrounded Mo Jiuye brandishing their weapons.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was about to be humiliated soon, Cui Liang revealed a wicked smile.","The officers surrounded the mule cart. One recognized Mo Jiuye instantly.","Yesterday at the government office, the Mo family did not give County Magistrate Cui any face at all. Hence, their impression of Mo Jiuye was extremely deep.","Carefully thinking back, given how the county magistrate made things difficult for them yesterday, it would not be unjustified for them to resent this. They truly had the motive to harm someone.","Upon realizing this, the officer shouted loudly, \"Come with me to the county office now to assist in the investigation!\"","Mo Jiuye did not move an inch.","\"What have I done that requires assisting in an investigation?\"","\"Stop wasting words. I suspect you are the one who harmed the county magistrate!\" The officer left no room for disagreement. He came forward wanting to make an arrest.","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran along skillfully dodging to the side, easily avoiding the officer's salty pig hands that reached out.","The officer was furious seeing this. \"How bold, actually daring to evade capture. Your crimes have increased one level!\"","He clearly understood Mo Jiuye's former position and that as someone who had led troops into battle before, his skills must be formidable. Although his tone was still forceful, he no longer dared to recklessly use force.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye's face had completely blackened.","He first glared angrily at the Cui clan members, then looked towards the officers. In a low voice he asked sternly,","\"For capturing thieves, what evidence do you have to determine that I am the one who harmed Cui County Magistrate?\"","In actual fact, the officers did not suspect Mo Jiuye at all.","County Magistrate Cui had said there were a total of 5 assailants last night who were all masked.","They also saw the people from the Mo family who came yesterday, just 2 men with the rest being women. It was impossible for them to make up 5 people to commit the crime.","However, there was urgency from the county magistrate's side to apprehend the murderer within 3 days.","Without thinking, one could deduce that the 5 people who dared to sneak into a government official's home to commit assault at night could not be ordinary folk.","To capture such people, let alone 3 days, even if given 3 years it would likely be impossible.","Thus, the officers had the idea to catch a few scapegoats to close the case early.","Now that Mo Jiuye was in sight, they had this thought.","Not to mention how many Mo family men there were, using their unpleasant altercation with County Magistrate Cui yesterday was already an excuse to apprehend them.","Once at the government office, whether they would admit guilt would no longer be up to them. This would allow the case to be closed early.","Mo Jiuye had long seen through these officers' sinister intentions. How could he possibly go along with their wishes?","The officers harbored impure motives for the arrest to begin with. How could they possibly have any evidence?","Furthermore, together with the few officers behind was only a total of 4 men. Dealing with someone who had been on the battlefield, they likely lacked confidence.","Just as the officers were still considering countermeasures, another group of officers came running from the other end of the street.","That group appeared to at least have 6, 7 men. Gathered together they achieved upward of 10 men.","The officers instantly regained confidence. Towards the rushing colleagues he yelled loudly, \"Hurry up! The assailant who injured the county magistrate last night is here!\"","Unexpectedly, the approaching officers did not come to help arrest Mo Jiuye. Instead, they breathlessly notified the others,","\"Quick, return to the county office now. The new county magistrate has arrived!\"","This news was rather sudden. The officers who wanted to catch Mo Jiuye as a scapegoat were stunned briefly before calling to the men behind them to rush to the county office. They completely disregarded Mo Jiuye.","Hearing that a new Yun City county magistrate had arrived, the crowds that were watching also ran over to see the commotion.","The place instantly became empty here.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran also wanted to go take a look at what background the newly arrived county magistrate had. However, before leaving this place, they had to settle things properly with these clueless Cui clan members first.","Mo Jiuye picked up the ox cart driving whip again and unhurriedly walked towards the Cui clan members' ox cart."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181: In My Turn","paragraphs":["Village Chief Cui and Cui Minglin had just learned yesterday how formidable the Mo Family people were. Now, seeing Mo Jiuye walking over with a cold expression on his face, they cowered at once.","\"What are you trying to do? Don't come over here!\" Cui Minglin said fearfully.","Seeing this, Village Chief Cui's body also instinctively shrank back.","Mo Jiuye didn't bother explaining and immediately raised his whip, lashing out at Cui Liang first.","Cui Liang wasn't able to dodge in time and was hit hard several times, crying out painfully and losing all dignity.","Next, Mo Jiuye's whip ruthlessly struck Cui Minglin.","Cui Minglin had always been the village bully. Where had he ever suffered such humiliation?","After several lashes, he suddenly felt his blood boil.","He shouted at the other Cui family members in the ox cart, \"Come on, everyone get him together!\"","Seeing this, Village Chief Cui also forgot his earlier fear and pushed several Cui family members to surround and attack Mo Jiuye together.","Facing the group of Cui family members, Mo Jiuye showed no mercy. His whip lashed viciously at them with crushing force. The Cui family could only passively take the beating.","After pushing his clansmen forward, Village Chief Cui didn't join the attack. Instead, he circled around to He Zhiran's side from the other end of the mule cart.","He knew clearly that they were no match for Mo Jiuye. The best tactic was to control the woman and threaten the opponent that way.","Mo Jiuye had already noticed Village Chief Cui's actions long ago. He didn't go help because he knew He Zhiran was capable of handling an unskilled man without trouble.","As Village Chief Cui climbed down from the ox cart, he grabbed a not very long hemp rope along the way. He carefully crept up behind He Zhiran, just about to loop the rope around her neck, when He Zhiran suddenly leapt down from the mule cart.","He Zhiran spun and kicked out fiercely, her leg slamming into Village Chief Cui's lower abdomen.","Although He Zhiran didn't have inner energy, her technique was executed perfectly.","The kick sent Village Chief Cui flying back several meters. His whole body crashed heavily onto the ground.","He Zhiran revealed a mocking smile.","\"Tsk, the village chief actually stooped so low as to sneak attack a powerless woman. It really makes one laugh.\"","Village Chief Cui rubbed his aching back that had hit the ground. He stared at He Zhiran in terror.","He absolutely hadn't expected that the Mo Family woman would be so formidable as well. Today, they had really kicked an iron panel.","He pointed a trembling finger at He Zhiran. \"You... don't come over, or I'll report to the authorities!\"","He Zhiran sneered coldly. \"Report me? Go ahead. The new county prefect just arrived. I want to see if every official is as corrupt as Deputy Magistrate Cui.\"","When Village Chief Cui heard He Zhiran's words, his heart thudded.","He had been too angry and overlooked the news mentioned earlier by the deputies - that a new county prefect had arrived in Yun City.","He didn't know yet what kind of person this new prefect was.","If this prefect wasn't of the same circle as his nephew, then his family's good days would be over.","Furthermore, he had just witnessed with his own eyes Deputy Magistrate Cui's root being injured. This news didn't know which big mouth had spread it far and wide. By now, all the commoners in Yun City must know.","Things had gotten to this point. Even if Deputy Magistrate Cui wanted to conceal it, he couldn't possibly manage.","Originally, Village Chief Cui had thought it fortunate that Yun City currently had no prefect. His nephew could use this time to suppress discussion and continue concealing the matter in order to keep his position as magistrate.","But now, it seemed unlikely.","That meant his nephew would inevitably lose his magistrate's seat.","Thinking of this, Village Chief Cui instantly felt he had lost his footing.","He looked at his clansmen who had been whipped by Mo Jiuye until covered in injuries. \"Nevermind not reporting. First make your husband stop.\"","He Zhiran glanced at Mo Jiuye and saw him wielding the whip in a lazy manner. Clearly he didn't take the Cui family people seriously at all.","Originally, He Zhiran had considered that this was on a main street after all. If Mo Jiuye wasn't careful with his strength and beat someone to death, it would be hard to smooth things over. So she had thought to stop him.","But upon hearing Village Chief Cui's threatening tone, she immediately didn't want to interfere anymore.","Not interfering didn't mean she had no other methods.","He Zhiran shot Village Chief Cui a look, then walked over to Mo Jiuye's side.","\"Dear husband, are you tired from beating them? Why not take a break and let me have a turn.\"","This was good. Her strength would be gentler and it was a chance for her to practice.","Mo Jiuye looked at her affectionately. Knowing it was safe to beat these people without real danger, he handed over the whip without hesitation.","The Cui family had personally witnessed Village Chief Cui get kicked flying by this pretty woman earlier. So when facing He Zhiran, they didn't feel relieved at all.","Other than lacking Mo Jiuye's stamina, He Zhiran's strikes were no lighter.","Furthermore, her agility was quite good. If these people tried to flee, they wouldn't have a chance.","After wielding the whip for a while, when He Zhiran felt the timing was right, she stopped.","The so-called right timing was when the Cui family was hurt enough to be in agony but not fatally wounded.","With He Zhiran's medical expertise, she gauged these injuries would need at least half a month to heal.","Gripping the whip in hand, she panted, \"I'm tired. You all can go report now.\"","As she spoke, she deliberately glanced at Village Chief Cui who had been scared witless.","This look conveyed her meaning thoroughly to Village Chief Cui.","As long as you don't mind the pain, feel free to go report us.","Recalling the kick to his lower abdomen earlier by this woman, at this moment Village Chief Cui still felt lingering fear.","\"I won't report. None of us will report.\"","After he finished speaking, Village Chief Cui signalled to his clansmen with his eyes for everyone to leave quickly.","The Cui family were beyond relieved. They tumbled and crawled back onto the ox cart.","The cart driver fled as if avoiding the plague god, whipping the ox cart away at the fastest speed before Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran also tidied their clothes and got back in the mule cart.","If they hadn't run into the Cui family's provocation here, upon hearing the news of the new prefect's arrival they would have joined the crowd to watch the hubbub.","But now, they had changed their minds.","A new prefect had arrived. If he was a good official, then investigating Deputy Magistrate Cui's misconduct over the years - along with his current disability - would certainly lead to Deputy Magistrate Cui's dismissal and prosecution.","On the flip side, if the new prefect was similarly corrupt as Deputy Magistrate Cui, then Deputy Magistrate would certainly take this chance to give gifts and favors, smoothing the matter over.","In the former case of Deputy Magistrate Cui being investigated, his family property would surely be confiscated. In the latter case, Deputy Magistrate Cui would use his remaining assets to bribe the prefect. Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran didn't want to give him that chance.","Therefore, the two unanimously decided to first rob the Cui residence clean to avoid future troubles."]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182: Your husband, I am in good health.","paragraphs":["It just so happened that at this time, all the government officials had gone to the government office to welcome the new magistrate, so there probably wouldn't be too many people left in the Cui Residence.","As long as they acted carefully, they would definitely succeed without any problems.","Having made up their minds, the two brought the donkey cart to a remote corner. He Zhiran waved her little hand and brought Mo Jiuye and the donkey cart into her space.","They had no other purpose for entering the space in broad daylight than to disguise themselves before going to do bad things.","He Zhiran took out some makeup tools and disguised Mo Jiuye as an ugly man with upturned eyes, a flat nose, and everted lips.","That wasn't all. She even put on a goat beard for Mo Jiuye.","Then she bought a set of gray casual clothes on Taobao and changed out of his black clothes.","When she looked at Mo Jiuye again, none of his original appearance remained.","He Zhiran couldn't help but laugh out loud, \"Mo Jiuye, do you know? There are two types of people in the world who attract the most attention.\"","Not realizing she was making fun of him, Mo Jiuye asked earnestly, \"What two types?\"","\"Hahaha, one is the especially good-looking kind, the other is your current look.\"","As He Zhiran spoke, she had already pushed him in front of the bathroom mirror.","When Mo Jiuye caught the first glimpse of himself in the mirror, he instinctively took a step back.","Pointing at his own nose, he asked in some disbelief, \"This ugly monster is me?\"","He Zhiran laughed heartily, \"That's right, this is you. What do you think, aren't my makeup skills amazing? Looking like this now, I bet even your mother wouldn't recognize you.\"","Indeed, not to mention his mother failing to recognize him, even he himself didn't know who he was...","In any case, it was worth looking ugly to make his beloved wife laugh merrily.","After He Zhiran had her fill of laughter, she also disguised herself.","Her costume was much simpler. She just put on the men's clothing she wore in Pingyang County and casually smeared some stuff on her face to finish up.","After getting into costume, the two immediately left the space.","When they arrived outside the Cui Residence, after observing for a bit, Mo Jiuye directly swept up He Zhiran in his arms and used his lightness skill to leap over the wall.","What met their eyes were seven or eight women dressed in silk, being driven towards the main gate by some steward-looking men.","The women were crying loudly, and some even tried to run back but were crudely grabbed by the hair and pulled back by the stewards.","Among these women, He Zhiran immediately spotted the pair of twin sisters from the He family.","The two of them did not cry out or make a fuss. They just kept pleading with the stewards.","\"Dear Sir, please have mercy on us sisters and don't sell us into places like that.\"","Seeing that these sisters didn't cry and shout like the others, the steward's heart softened a little out of pity.","\"This is ordered by Master Deputy Magistrate Cui. Pleading with us is useless. You'd best obediently come with us. That way you can avoid some physical suffering.\"","The He sisters continued pleading, \"Dear Sir, could you please take us to see Master Deputy Magistrate Cui so that we may plead our case with him directly?\"","\"You'd best abandon that idea. If Master Deputy Magistrate Cui had any sympathy for you, he wouldn't sell you off to the brothel.\"","\"Dear Sir, please...\"","Their pleas grew fainter and soon disappeared at the entrance to the Cui Residence.","He Zhiran scoffed, \"This Deputy Magistrate Cui is quite realistic. Knowing that he can no longer perform, he decides to exchange these women for silver.\"","He Zhiran had merely meant to vent some frustration with those words, but they took on a different meaning in Mo Jiuye's ears.","Out of habit, he stroked her hair and said, \"Don't worry, your husband's body is perfectly healthy and I will also protect myself well.\"","He Zhiran...","Your train of thought has gone way too off track here.","Without lingering on those thoughts, this was the perfect time to infiltrate the back residence where there were currently few people.","Mo Jiuye took her by the hand and jogged towards the front court.","He had specifically asked Liang Hao last night and knew the storehouse was right next to the main courtyard.","Therefore, with little effort, the two were able to locate the position of the storehouse.","The storehouse was only separated from the courtyard where Deputy Magistrate Cui lived by a single wall. They could see several medicine chest-carrying physicians standing there.","Those physicians' expressions were as ugly as if they had just lost their fathers.","No wonder, as the steward kept pressuring them.","\"You are all famous physicians in Yun City, yet you cannot cure the magistrate's injuries?","The magistrate has ordered that if his injuries show no sign of improvement for a day, you will not be allowed to leave for a day.\"","The physicians looked at each other, and a white-bearded elderly man stepped forward with a bitter expression.","\"Steward, Deputy Magistrate Cui is asking too much of us here. Those eunuchs in the palace try every possible way to regain their manhood after gaining status and wealth, yet no one from ancient times till now has succeeded.","How could we small-town physicians possibly have such great abilities?\"","The other physicians echoed his words.","\"That's right, we are truly powerless against Deputy Magistrate Cui's illness.\"","\"Steward, please help plead our case before the magistrate and let us go.\"","\"I still have a family relying on my medical practice to make ends meet. Please help us say some good words!\"","\"...\"","Faced with the physicians' desperate pleas, the steward ignored them and yelled towards the outside of the yard, \"Come over here, keep an eye on these physicians. If anyone runs away, you will pay.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran watched from the shadows as three of the stewards guarding the storehouse immediately left, leaving only one.","With only one guard left, it was much more convenient for them to act.","Mo Jiuye swiftly flashed behind that steward and chopped him unconscious before dragging him to a corner.","He Zhiran seized the chance to rush over, and the two nimbly climbed in through the window.","The storeroom had clearly been tidied up with no signs of theft.","Indeed, as Liang Hao and the others had said, all that remained were some bulky items that were difficult to transport.","After scanning the surroundings, He Zhiran also broadened her horizons.","In addition to the lack of silver and banknotes, the storeroom contained gold, silver, pearls and jewels, jade articles, antique calligraphy and paintings, silks and satins filling the shelves around.","He Zhiran waved her little hand and all the items in the storeroom vanished without a trace.","The space had expanded and she no longer needed to consider storage issues. She took everything including the shelves into it.","After carefully checking that no items were left behind, the two exited.","But as soon as they had just jumped out of the window, they ran into an elegantly dressed woman in her thirties, accompanied by two maids.","Seeing the two strange men, the maids immediately screamed, \"Madam, thieves!\"","Madam Cui also saw them and shouted loudly for someone to catch the thieves.","Seeing this, He Zhiran quickly took out a bottle of anesthetics from her space and sprinkled it towards them.","Madam Cui and her maids soon collapsed.","Hearing approaching hurried footsteps, Mo Jiuye swept up He Zhiran and leaped onto the roof.","Without waiting for the stewards to get close, the two had already leapt out of the residence."]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183: It's Him","paragraphs":["Returning to that remote place, the two people slipped into the space, changed into their outfits, and reappeared outside together with the donkey cart.","Just like nothing had happened, Mo Jiuye drove the donkey cart towards the county government building.","There was a sea of people at the entrance of the county government building, all waiting to see the new county magistrate.","From this, it was evident that the county magistrate had not yet arrived.","Mo Jiuye parked the donkey cart at one side and held He Zhiran's hand as they stood among the crowds.","The two had just stood there when a line of people walked over from the east.","The person walking at the very front wore an official county magistrate uniform, walking with a upright and heroic posture.","What's more, he was actually someone they recognized.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran looked at each other, both softly uttering the person's name at the same time.","\"Meng Huaining!\"","It turned out to be him!","\"How did he end up becoming the county magistrate of Yun City?\"","Full of questions.","Looking at Meng Huaining's side, there was a blonde westerner following him, waving his hands and jumping around, seeming to be expressing something.","Meng Huaining's brows were locked in a frown as he kept shaking his head.","As the line of people drew near, the officers swiftly lined up a long queue to block the commoners, preventing them from charging forward to harm the county magistrate.","Only that blonde westerner still stubbornly tried to convey something to Meng Huaining.","He Zhiran could see that Meng Huaining completely did not understand what the westerner was saying.","Coincidentally at this moment, Meng Huaining glanced towards the crowd and happened to spot Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","Upon seeing the two of them, Meng Huaining paid no more attention to the westerner beside him and strode towards them instead.","Just as the commoners were still guessing why the county magistrate had come over to this side, Meng Huaining spoke.","\"Brother Mo, Sister-in-Law, I didn't expect you two to arrive earlier than me.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had originally wanted to privately meet Meng Huaining, they didn't expect that he would so openly greet them first.","Mo Jiuye cupped his fists, \"Long time no see, Brother Meng.\"","The common people did not know Mo Jiuye's identity, they only assumed he was an old acquaintance of the county magistrate from his hometown.","However, it was different for those officers.","Yesterday, the Mo family was bullied by Steward Cui, many of them witnessed it personally. And there were also several officers including Ma Junshan who had escorted them to Xi Ling Village, they were even more dumbfounded.","Just what was going on here?","Not only was Mo Jiuye acquainted with the new county magistrate, but the county magistrate even addressed him intimately as brother. It was evident that the two of them had a deep relationship.","Thinking of this, a few officers secretly heaved a sigh of relief.","Fortunately yesterday they did not join Steward Cui to bully the Mo family, otherwise with the relationship those people had with the county magistrate, they would definitely be made to suffer for it.","Those few officers who had affirmed on the streets today that Mo Jiuye was the culprit who had harmed Steward Cui were stunned speechless now.","They had randomly wanted to find a scapegoat to quickly close the case, but it seems they had kicked against an iron panel.","A few officers with guilty consciences lowered their heads as much as possible to fade their presence.","Meng Huaining warmly made a welcoming gesture, wanting to invite Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran into the government building to catch up.","Just then, the westerner approached again.","He fluently said in English, \"Dear Sir, please help me.\"","Meng Huaining turned his head with a difficult expression towards the westerner.","\"I'm sorry, I don't understand what you're saying.\"","He Zhiran faintly smiled and took a step forward, similarly asking the westerner in English, \"Excuse me Sir, what difficulties have you encountered?\"","The westerner's mood lifted when he heard the familiar language.","He spread out both arms towards He Zhiran with a laugh and said, \"Oh wonderful, I've finally met someone here who knows English, and it's even a very beautiful lady.\"","As he spoke, the westerner was just about to step forward to give He Zhiran a big hug.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye unhappily blocked He Zhiran in front, glaring at the westerner.","Regardless of whether the other party could understand his words, he angrily said, \"Watch your words and actions, otherwise don't blame me for being impolite.\"","He Zhiran knew that westerners liked to hug others to express their excitement or gratitude.","This action had definitely been misunderstood by Mo Jiuye.","Of course, as a woman deeply rooted in Eastern culture, she also could not accept the western style of expression.","Even without Mo Jiuye blocking, she would have avoided the westerner's hug herself.","She knew that this westerner did not have malicious intent. She explained to Mo Jiuye, \"This is a form of etiquette in their Western culture, and I won't be cooperating with him either.\"","Mo Jiuye did not have time to carefully ponder why He Zhiran understood foreign languages. He still glared furiously at the westerner.","The westerner saw the suddenly appearing unfriendly man and felt utterly confused.","\"Dear Sir, we're meeting for the first time, why are you treating me this way?\"","Mo Jiuye knew the westerner was talking to him but he couldn't understand it, so he turned to ask He Zhiran.","\"What is he saying?\"","He Zhiran smiled and translated the westerner's words for him to hear.","Mo Jiuye's face was cold as he said, \"Tell him that the women of our Da Shun Dynasty can only be embraced by her own husband.\"","He Zhiran secretly chuckled to herself in her heart. She didn't expect this man would have such a strong sense of possessiveness...","She very professionally translated Mo Jiuye's words for the westerner to hear.","And simply explained to him in English that the people of Da Shun had relatively conservative mindsets. Whether as an expression of gratitude or otherwise, it could only be conveyed verbally.","The clever westerner immediately gained new understanding about the etiquette in Da Shun after He Zhiran's explanation.","He apologetically placed a hand over his chest and bowed to He Zhiran.","\"I'm sorry for causing you trouble, please excuse me.\"","Finally having encountered someone he could communicate with, the westerner eagerly spoke without delay after apologizing.","\"Dear Miss, could I trouble you to be my translator for a few days? I will definitely pay you very handsomely.\"","Payment or not, He Zhiran did not care at all.","She decided to help this westerner.","Not for anything else, truly getting to know a westerner would be the biggest aid to verifying the items from her space.","\"It's no problem, may I ask for Sir's name?\"","Seeing her agreement, the westerner immediately beamed joyfully.","\"My name is Henry, from across the seas. May I know what this beautiful lady is named?\"","He Zhiran politely greeted him and told him her name.","After their mutual introductions, Henry impatiently brought up the difficulties he had encountered.","\"Miss He Zhiran, when my ship anchored near the Yun City port just now, the anchor broke off. Also, the translator I brought from home died on the journey here. So I wanted to look for a ship repair master here but due to the language barrier, I have not managed to find one. Could you help ask the officials here to help me find a master proficient in repairing ships?\"","He Zhiran could only serve as an interpreter. Finding someone to repair the ship would have to depend on Meng Huaining's help."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184: How Can the Future Be Worthy of Great Responsibility","paragraphs":["He Zhiran translated Henry's words for Meng Huaining.","Meng Huaining did not reject foreigners. After all, at that time, foreigners had not yet done any harm to this land.","However, he had just arrived and was not familiar with everything in Yun City.","So Meng Huaining directly called an attendant to ask: \"Are there any shipbuilders in Yun City?\"","The attendant appeared very respectful: \"Sir, our southern Yun City borders the sea. Most of the fishermen there know how to repair boats.\"","Meng Huaining understood and told He Zhiran: \"Sister-in-law can pass this information on to him.\"","He Zhiran translated the attendant's original words to Henry.","Upon hearing this, Henry was overjoyed: \"Ms. He Zhiran, can you accompany me on a trip?\"","He Zhiran knew that even if Henry was clear on where to find the shipbuilders, he would be unable to communicate with them. It was absolutely necessary for her to go along.","However, it was probably not possible today.","It was almost noon already. Their purpose in coming out today was to buy medicinal ingredients.","Not only did they have to hurry back before the fifth brother fell ill, but they would probably also have to ask Meng Huaining to help resolve where to stay for the night.","Only if Meng Huaining stepped up could this matter be resolved from the root.","Therefore, they now had to explain their situation clearly to Meng Huaining.","He Zhiran apologetically waved her hand at Henry: \"I'm sorry, my family has some things to deal with today. I can accompany you to the fishing village tomorrow when I'm free.\"","Henry had been stranded in Yun City for several days. Now that he finally found someone he could communicate with, he had to be patient even if he was anxious.","\"Okay, tomorrow then.\"","After communicating with Henry, He Zhiran took Mo Jiuye to catch up with Meng Huaining.","It just so happened that Meng Huaining also had this intention and invited the couple to chat at the county office.","Meng Huaining was still not familiar with the environment here. When he went to Dongfeng County to take office, the local county magistrate briefed him and handed over the work very clearly.","But the news of his arrival had already been notified here, so why didn't he see the county magistrate here?","Meng Huaining found this very strange.","He called over an attendant who led the way and asked, \"Where is your county magistrate?\"","When the county magistrate Chui was mentioned, the attendant hemmed and hawed, not knowing what to say.","If the county magistrate learned from him about what happened to County Magistrate Chui’s grandson, and Chui was not removed from office, would he not become an offender?","On the other hand, if he did not tell the truth, he would offend the county magistrate.","The attendant did not dare offend either of them and seemed very embarrassed.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye took the initiative to clarify for him:","\"Brother Meng, when we entered the city today, we heard the common people talking about County Magistrate Chui's grandson being injured last night and still lying at home recovering now.\"","Such news did indeed surprise Meng Huaining very much.","The person who made the move must have hated the county magistrate greatly to injure the man there.","Seeing Meng Huaining was still thinking, Mo Jiuye did not want to beat around the bush either. Their main purpose in coming here was to resolve things.","\"Brother Meng doesn't know that when we arrived in Yun City yesterday, we were bullied by County Magistrate Chui. He deliberately assigned us to the village where his clansmen live. In such weather, all thirty-some of us had to spend the whole night sleeping outdoors.\"","\"Brother Mo, let's go inside to talk in detail.\" As he spoke, Meng Huaining had already led the couple into the study.","The attendant was very tactful. As soon as a few people had just sat down, he brought tea and then went out and closed the door.","Meng Huaining took a sip of tea before slowly speaking.","\"I won't hide it from Brother Mo and Sister-in-law, but I was sent to Yun City as county magistrate by Mr. Fei Nanyu's arrangement.\"","Yun City was located in a remote area with a harsh environment. Mo Jiuye could not think of why Fei Nanyu would arrange for Meng Huaining to be sent here.","\"Why is that?\"","Meng Huaining smiled bitterly. \"It's nothing but the corpse burning incident in Dongfeng County.\"","Pausing for a moment, Meng Huaining continued:","\"My younger sister's suggestion to burn the bodies of the victims was indeed a good way to eradicate future troubles.","When Prince Qi led people for disaster relief, I also explained this rationale very clearly to him.","Prince Qi agreed at first and ordered his men to actively cooperate with my work.","We worked together to burn the bodies of the victims. Later we also tried every means to find medicinal ingredients to make medicine to treat the plague, and we could say that we minimized casualties among the common people.","Just when the disaster relief work was about to achieve great success, I don't know who was inciting the commoners behind my back, saying that our burning of corpses was unacceptable morally, and the court must give those families an explanation.","Regarding this, Prince Qi sent people to arrest some of those troublemakers, but the common people had already completely believed what those people were saying. They held on to the idea that as long as they kept pressing the issue, they would definitely get compensation from the court.","Seeing this, Prince Qi also changed his original intention. He believed that giving the common people an explanation was the desire of the masses. He could not provide any compensation to the commoners himself, so the only thing he could do was to remove and investigate the scapegoat responsible for burning the corpses.","Speaking of this “scapegoat”, it would undoubtedly be me.","Seeing Prince Qi showing his true colors, I did not wait for him to propose my dismissal. I planned to resign directly.","Mr. Fei saw all of this. Prince Qi trusted him very much. Under Mr. Fei's advice, Prince Qi decided to transfer me away from Dongfeng County.","At that time, there were three remote county towns for me to choose from. Before I made a choice, Mr. Fei found me and suggested that I come to Yun City.","The main purpose of coming here was because you were exiled here, and it would be more convenient for a familiar official to take care of you.","Even if Mr. Fei had not said so, I was also going to come here. Mr. Fei and I were of the same mind.","Three days later, under Mr. Fei's arrangement, I left Dongfeng County and hurried here.\"","After listening to Meng Huaining's words, He Zhiran scolded Prince Nan Qi in her heart. How could a prince have so little backbone? He had missed the opportunity to win over a capable minister...","Mo Jiuye thought a little more. \"If Nan Qi did not punish you, returning to the capital afterwards would surely leave the disaster relief efforts fruitless.\"","Meng Huaining smiled bitterly. \"Indeed, running into something like this, I might as well pour out my bitterness to Brother Mo.\"","Mo Jiuye also lamented. A person who could not even resolve the grievances of his own officials, how could he be up to important tasks in the future? No wonder the history books recorded that Prince Nan Qi's throne would be seized from him...","Of course, all the troubles at Nan Qi’s feet were brought upon by himself. He was thinking about those fathers and brothers who had served Da Shun Dynasty loyally on behalf Na Qi’s behalf.","After telling his story, Meng Huaining quickly adjusted his mindset and continued to inquire about Mo Jiuye's family being bullied by the county magistrate Chui.","Mo Jiuye gave an original account of what happened yesterday without any embellishment for Meng Huaining to listen to.","Upon hearing this, Meng Huaining pounded the table angrily.","\"A petty county magistrate has grown guts as big as the heavens!\"","As he finished speaking, Meng Huaining stood up and shouted at the door: \"Come in!\"","Soon, a pair of attendants walked in: \"Sir, your order?\""]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185: How Dare you publicly bribe an Official","paragraphs":["Meng Huaining waved his hand grandly: \"I'll give you half an hour. No matter what method you use, make Deputy Magistrate Cui come see me immediately.\"","The officers looked at each other blankly for a moment before taking their orders and leaving.","Meng Huaining didn't idle either. He called over his personal attendant, Meng An.","\"Meng An, go to the entrance of the county government building now and spread the word that I will hold court today to personally try Deputy Magistrate Cui. Tell those who have suffered injustice but have nowhere to appeal to all come and watch. I will serve justice for them today.\"","As an experienced county magistrate, Meng Huaining didn't even need to think to be certain that for Deputy Magistrate Cui to do this to the Mo Family, it showed what kind of person he was. He must not have rarely exploited and oppressed the common people in his day-to-day duties.","He had just arrived in Yun City to take over today before immediately taking aim at the corrupt official Deputy Magistrate Cui.","Meng An responded and ran off to take care of it.","Meng Huaining looked at Mo Jiuye and his wife. \"Big brother Mo and sister-in-law, why don't you come with me to the court hall?\"","\"Alright,\" Mo Jiuye said as he pulled He Zhiran up with him to follow behind Meng Huaining.","After sitting in the court hall for a long time without seeing any commoners coming to accuse Deputy Magistrate Cui of his misdeeds, Meng An came running back.","\"Sir, I've already passed on your intentions to those commoners, but...\"","Meng Huaining raised his brows. \"But what?\"","\"I could tell that when those commoners heard Deputy Magistrate Cui's name, they gnashed their teeth in hatred. But they don't seem to believe that you can serve justice for them, sir.\"","Meng Huaining stood up and walked toward the exterior of the court hall. \"I'll talk to those commoners personally.\"","The court hall directly faced the entrance to the county government building. Meng Huaining strode straight to the entrance.","At this time, there were even more commoners gathered at the entrance than when they had welcomed his appointment.","Moreover, many of the commoners had very complicated expressions.","Meng Huaining didn't want to waste time. He loudly addressed the commoners, \"I just arrived in Yun City today and have already heard many rumors about Deputy Magistrate Cui's corruption. Today, I will publicly try Deputy Magistrate Cui in front of you all. If any of you have suffered oppression from Deputy Magistrate Cui, go ahead and tell me. I will surely serve you all justice.\"","He had just finished speaking when an elderly couple supporting each other came up to him.","The old couple knelt before Meng Huaining.","\"Sir, can you really stand up for us common folk?\"","Seeing his master questioned, Meng An hurriedly stepped forward and said, \"Magistrate Meng is famously upright. Naturally he will stand up for the common people.\"","Hearing this, the elderly couple kowtowed to Meng Huaining three times again.","Meng Huaining stepped forward to help them up.","\"Elders, no need for such etiquette. Just go ahead and tell me your grievance.\"","Upon hearing his words, the old woman immediately burst into loud sobs.","\"Merciful heavens! Please stand up for my pitiful daughter...\"","Seeing his wife crying so hard she couldn't speak clearly, the old man worried that the magistrate would grow impatient. He quickly spoke first,","\"Sir, three years ago when my sixteen-year-old daughter went to the market to sell eggs, she happened to catch the eye of Deputy Magistrate Cui with her looks. He forcibly took her back to his residence to be a concubine.","Our family is poor, but we didn't want our girl to be a concubine to someone else. When we heard, my two sons and I went to the Cui residence to ask for her back.","The Cui family servants didn't bother to hear us out before viciously beating my two sons. Now, one of them is still paralyzed in bed, while the other walks with a limp.","My pitiful daughter didn't want to stay with Deputy Magistrate Cui. She hanged herself inside the Cui residence that very day.","Sir, with my family torn apart like this, all thanks to Deputy Magistrate Cui, yet we had nowhere to appeal. We could only swallow this injustice for three years. Please stand up for my family, sir...\"","As the elderly couple spoke, their words dissolved into uncontrollable sobs.","The surrounding commoners also continuously wiped tears from their eyes, deeply sympathetic toward what had happened to this family.","After hearing the couple's story, blue veins bulged on Meng Huaining's face and he smashed his fist furiously against the pillar by the entrance.","\"Deputy Magistrate Cui, what a fine officer you are. Let's see how I deal with you today!\"","Seeing Meng Huaining's reaction, the commoners could now be certain that this newly arrived magistrate genuinely intended to serve justice for the people.","Thus, more people stepped forward to tell their own experiences one after another.","There were a few more cases where Deputy Magistrate Cui had forcibly taken their daughters home to be concubines. Some had their family property exploited by his corruption.","Most commonly, Deputy Magistrate Cui had taken bribes from others, leaving the commoners unable to appeal their grievances.","Before long, the entrance to the county government building was filled with kneeling commoners accusing Deputy Magistrate Cui.","Meng Huaining had never imagined that just a casual call would bring out so many crying injustice.","And this was merely making a spur-of-the-moment appeal at the entrance to the county building. If he publicized it more widely, who knows how many more would come to accuse Deputy Magistrate Cui?","Meng Huaining waved to Meng An, \"Meng An, take these people inside first and clearly record their grievances and addresses.\"","With so many cases, collecting evidence and holding trials would definitely take more than just a short time to resolve.","Meng Huaining planned to focus on handling the Deputy Magistrate Cui matter over the next few days. He would summon these commoners to appear in court in batches based on case categories.","Of course, his trials would also be held openly for the Yun City commoners to vent their anger.","At this time, the people he had sent to 'invite' Deputy Magistrate Cui still hadn't returned. Meng Huaining wanted to go see the detailed testimonies of the commoners' accusations first.","He had just turned around when a woman's wail came from outside the crowd,","\"Magistrate, someone openly stole from my Cui residence in broad daylight today, even injuring my female family members. Please serve justice for me...\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were standing just inside the entrance. Hearing this voice, they smiled at each other.","The newcomer was none other than Deputy Magistrate Cui's wife, Liu.","Liu came through the crowd of onlookers with two servant girls. She flung herself at Meng Huaining's feet, kneeling before him.","Before she could even open her mouth, Liu signaled to the servant girls behind her with her eyes.","The girls immediately crawled up to Meng Huaining on their knees and delivered a handkerchief-wrapped package to him, softly saying, \"Sir, this is a token of appreciation from my mistress. Please accept it with a smile.\"","Meng Huaining smiled, but there was no smile in his eyes.","\"Who are you to dare so openly try to bribe me?\"","His voice wasn't small. The surrounding commoners could hear very clearly.","The commoners all knew the newly arrived magistrate wanted to punish Deputy Magistrate Cui. Thus, they no longer feared Liu as they used to.","Someone in the crowd shouted loudly,","\"Sir! That's Deputy Magistrate Cui's wife!\"","In fact, when Meng Huaining heard Liu crying injustice earlier, he had already guessed her identity. He had just pretended ignorance.","\"Oh? You are Deputy Magistrate Cui's wife?\"","Liu thought Meng Huaining's smile showed the Cui family friendliness. Instantly emboldened, she said,","\"Yes sir, I am Deputy Magistrate Cui's wife.\"","Meng Huaining let out a cold laugh before his expression instantly hardened.","\"Guards, tie this woman up!\"","Very soon, several officers ran out from inside the building. After a brief hesitation, they tied Liu up."]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186: How This One Won't Work","paragraphs":["Meng Huaining's sudden move left Liu somewhat puzzled.","\"Sir, I'm here to plead injustice. Why do you treat me like this?\"","Meng Huaining's face was cold as he said in a low voice, \"How dare a deceitful woman openly bribe an official like me? What crime should she be charged with?\"","Liu was instantly dumbfounded.","Usually when people came to Deputy Magistrate Cui's house to ask for help with something, this was how it was done.","Moreover, as long as the gifts were valuable enough, there was nothing that couldn't be accomplished.","How could it not work when she tried it on the new county magistrate?","Not only did it not work, she was actually charged with the crime of bribing an official in public?","The family treasury had already been stolen bare, and the jade bracelet she just pulled off her wrist was meant as a gift.","She had spent a lot of money to buy this jade bracelet many years ago. If she hadn't wanted to leave a good impression on the county magistrate, she would have been reluctant to give it away.","Now, with the bracelet in the other's hand, she was to be convicted.","Liu felt extremely wronged.","\"Sir, you can't treat me like this. I'm really wronged.\"","Hearing Liu's cries of injustice, the yamen runners immediately eased their actions and looked towards Meng Huaining, waiting for his cue.","Meng Huaining didn't even glance at Liu. He waved his hand at the yamen runners.","\"Take her inside.\"","Although the yamen runners had been with Deputy Magistrate Cui for a long time and had done some shady business for him, they could also see the situation clearly now.","The county magistrate was now the biggest official in Yuncheng, and it was undoubtedly clear that Deputy Magistrate Cui would be dismissed from his position. They must clarify their stance at the first moment.","Therefore, at Meng Huaining's command, the yamen runners pushed Liu inside the yamen.","Seeing this, several maids turned to run away, but were blocked by the onlooking commoners.","He Zhiran saw there were no idle yamen runners behind Meng Huaining. He took the initiative to grab two maids by their collars and threw them into the yamen.","Meng Huaining was not idle either. He held up the jade bracelet the maid had stuffed into his hand earlier for all to see.","\"Everyone, take a good look. This is the jade bracelet that Liu just had her servant sneak to me. This is evidence of her attempt to bribe me.\"","This move was met with a round of applause from the commoners.","\"Heaven has eyes. Finally, a grand magistrate from heaven has been sent to our Yuncheng.\"","\"The commoners of Yuncheng will have good fortune.\"","\"In the future when we suffer injustice, we shall seek justice from the grand magistrate!\"","\"......\"","Meng Huaining was delighted to gain the recognition of the commoners on his first day in office.","He waved his hand at the commoners while the yamen runners also came out to signal them not to clamor loudly in front of the yamen.","Meng Huaining looked up at the sky. The yamen runner he had sent to ‘invite’ Deputy Magistrate Cui had left for almost an hour but still hadn’t returned. Instead, his wife had come pleading injustice. This inevitably made Meng Huaining suspect that Deputy Magistrate Cui intended some dirty tricks.","Just as he was pondering this, Deputy Magistrate Cui was carried to the front of the yamen on a stretcher by several servants.","At this point, Deputy Magistrate Cui still didn't know exactly what had happened.","Seeing Meng Huaining, he did not forget to greet him obsequiously.","\"County Magistrate, you have just arrived in Yuncheng today while I have an injury on my body and couldn't personally welcome you. Please forgive me, sir.\"","Meng Huaining looked scornfully at Deputy Magistrate Cui.","He saw that Cui's body was wrapped tightly in a brocade quilt, with only his head poking out to speak to him.","Although his tone was ingratiating, the fleeting contempt in his eyes was caught by Meng Huaining.","Meng Huaining sneered inwardly: Still so arrogant even when nearing death...","He kept a straight face and ordered the yamen runners: \"Take him to the public hall.\"","Deputy Magistrate Cui realized his bootlicking attempts were futile. He instantly felt something was wrong.","\"Sir, my uncle is the Prefect of Qingzhou.\" As a last resort, Deputy Magistrate Cui had to play his trump card, hoping that mentioning this would make Meng Huaining change his attitude.","Prefect of Qingzhou?","Meng Huaining was not unfamiliar with this role.","On his way to take up his post in Yuncheng, he happened to pass by Qingzhou where something had occurred that he did not forget.","Prefect Liu offended someone, his acceptance of bribes was reported to the capital, and his official post had already been revoked.","Judging by Deputy Magistrate Cui’s manner, he probably hadn't received the news yet.","Moreover, in Meng Huaining’s mind, even disregarding the fact that Prefect Liu had already been dismissed, even if he was still in office, he would surely severely punish an official like Deputy Magistrate Cui.","As a local father and mother official, an inability to eliminate harm for the people meant he was unworthy of this position.","At this moment, seeing Deputy Magistrate Cui, Meng Huaining felt like he was watching a clown jumping wildly on stage.","He couldn't help but step forward and said unhurriedly, \"I have good news to tell you on my first day in office today.\"","Deputy Magistrate Cui thought Meng Huaining was intimidated after he mentioned his uncle and intended to appease him.","\"Sir, what good news? Tell me quickly!\"","Meng Huaining suddenly changed his expression. He raised his hand and forcefully overturned Cui's stretcher.","\"How dare a dog like you not bow before me, an official, and even lie arrogantly in front of me? Do you believe I will convict you this instant of the crime of disrespecting your superior?\"","Just when Deputy Magistrate Cui was gleefully waiting to hear the “good news,” in the blink of an eye, he was dumped off the stretcher.","Unfortunately for him, he fell face down. The wounded area of his body also collided with the ground intimately.","Deputy Magistrate Cui was in so much pain he almost fainted.","After what seemed to be an eternity, he finally cried out in pain.","\"Ah...I’m dying...\"","Meng Huaining angrily strode over and gave him a kick: \"Who gave you the gall to address yourself as 'this official' before me?\"","He then moved closer and whispered to Deputy Magistrate Cui: \"The good news this official has for you is that yesterday on my way through Qingzhou, I witnessed Prefect Liu dismissed from office by the court for bribe taking.\"","Upon hearing this, Deputy Magistrate Cui froze in shock. He was in too much pain to care. His expression became increasingly panicked.","\"What did you say? That's impossible. My uncle cannot possibly be dismissed. You must be lying to me!\"","Meng Huaining was too lazy to explain. He clasped his hands behind his back and strode into the yamen hall in big steps.","\"No one is allowed to help him. In one incense stick's time, even crawling, he must get into the hall to see me, or he'll get the rod as punishment.”","The yamen runners were all hip to which way the wind was blowing. Who would still help Deputy Magistrate Cui?","No sooner had Meng Huaining left when some of the yamen runners swaggered over to Deputy Magistrate Cui to hurry him along, even threatening him with the rod if he moved too slowly.","Deputy Magistrate Cui had seen such scenes no shortage of times, he knew better than to continue irritating the county magistrate now.","In unbearable pain, he had no choice but to crawl into the grand hall.","As soon as Deputy Magistrate Cui crawled into the hall, he saw Mo Jiuye and his wife sitting to one side."]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187: Ask Your Grace to see clearly","paragraphs":["It was clear without even thinking that these two must have a close relationship with the new county magistrate, otherwise, not just anyone could sit in this court hall.","Deputy Magistrate Cui felt a tingling sensation go through his scalp, knowing that he had kicked an iron plate yesterday.","Now it looked like the main reason why the county magistrate treated him like this was to vent his anger for these two people.","Deputy Magistrate Cui believed he had found the root of why the county magistrate treated him this way.","It seemed that if he wanted to resolve the current crisis, he could only appease these two people.","Deputy Magistrate Cui struggled to crawl in front of Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, squeezing out a smile uglier than crying.","\"You two, yesterday it was negligence on this official's part that caused me to wrongly assign you to the wrong place. This official will immediately order someone to help you switch to a better village.\"","Mo Jiuye sneered coldly: \"Hehe... then it depends on whether Deputy Magistrate Cui still has the authority to reorder us a village or not.\"","\"You--\" Before Deputy Magistrate Cui could finish what he was saying, Meng Huaining slammed the court block on the table.","\"How bold, Cui Wen. Without this official giving you permission, who allowed you to talk freely in the court hall?\"","Cui Wen was already wary of what Mo Jiuye had just said, and seeing the county magistrate's attitude, he was now fully aware that the current situation was very unfavorable to him.","His lower body was injured, and even the slightest movement would cause unbearable pain. When he crawled in from outside the county government earlier, Cui Wen was already drenched in sweat from the pain. Still, he endured the pain and knelt towards Meng Huaining's direction.","\"County magistrate, this subordinate has been serving the people of Yun City diligently for many years. Even if I don't have merit, at least I have hard work. I beg you to show mercy...\"","As he spoke, Cui Wen shed tears in front of everyone.","If they didn't know better, they would have thought he suffered terrible injustice.","Meng Huaining had seen this kind of scene many times before and felt no sympathy for him at all.","He slammed the court block forcefully again.","\"Cui Wen, you have wantonly committed evil in Yun City by taking advantage of your position to oppress men and covet women. Are you aware of your crimes?\"","Cui Wen looked up with tears in his eyes, \"My lord, this subordinate has been framed. I have never done such things before, please discern this clearly.\"","Meng Huaining knew that it would be useless to give someone like Cui Wen a hard time if he kept insisting on his innocence.","He looked towards the yamen runners on both sides of the court hall and ordered, \"Come, drag Cui Wen out and give him twenty heavy beatings.\"","\"My lord, this subordinate is framed... My lord...\" Upon hearing that he would receive twenty heavy beatings, Cui Wen was already so frightened that he could not speak properly.","The yamen runners did not hesitate to come up and drag Cui Wen out of the court hall.","Cui Wen still desperately begged for mercy, \"My lord, this subordinate is injured and cannot be beaten...\"","If it were in the past, the yamen runners would hesitate for a moment when a prisoner pleaded for mercy to see the county magistrate's intention.","But today they could be certain that the new county magistrate was determined to punish the Yun City County Magistrate no matter what, so there was absolutely no chance for reprieve.","Therefore, the yamen runners had no intention of stopping as they directly dragged the man outside to the public square, and in front of all the onlooking commoners, gave Cui Wen a brutal twenty heavy beatings.","The planks landed heavily on his skin and flesh, and screams were endless.","Inside the court hall, Meng Huaining did not idle either. He ordered several commoners who had previously accused Cui Wen to come in and kneel on one side of the hall.","The commoners knelt down one by one.","The battered Cui Wen, who now looked like mud, was dragged back in by the yamen runners and thrown hard in the middle.","Meng Huaining slammed the court block again.","\"Cui Wen, will you confess yourself or shall I have each of these commoners state their grievances one by one?\"","It was only now that Cui Wen noticed several commoners had appeared in the court hall.","When he looked closely, it seemed he did have some impression of these people.","There was the one whose daughter he had seized. There was also the one whose shop he had occupied. And there was...","Cui Wen was dumbfounded.","These people used to not even dare show anger towards him. Now that the new county magistrate had arrived, they rushed over eagerly to accuse him.","Thinking of this, Cui Wen's gaze towards those commoners instantly turned extremely sinister.","It was as if threatening them that if they dared speak nonsense, he would settle accounts with them someday.","The commoners were originally quite afraid of Cui Wen. Although the county magistrate was backing them today, when they saw his expression, they couldn't help but tremble.","Cui Wen had glared at the commoners with his back facing Meng Huaining, so he naturally did not notice.","However, Cui Wen's little gesture did not escape Mo Jiuye's eyes.","\"Cui Wen, what do you mean by glaring at those commoners?\"","Upon hearing this, Meng Huaining slammed the court block heavily again.","\"Cui Wen, with this official present, you still dare threaten the commoners?\"","This loud noise frightened Cui Wen so much that his body shuddered.","He struggled to move his body to kowtow to Meng Huaining, but with his lower body injured and his back battered from the twenty heavy beatings, he was now no different from a high paraplegic patient.","Still, Cui Wen exerted great effort to bow down on the ground towards Meng Huaining.","\"My lord, this subordinate is framed. I haven't said a word, how could I threaten those commoners?\"","\"Humph! Glib tongue, this official will ask you again. Will you confess yourself or shall I let these grievously harmed commoners state their case?\"","After all, Cui Wen was still a county magistrate. He was very clear about trial proceedings like this.","If he confessed, it would substantiate the charges and make it difficult to recant his confession later.","Therefore, he gritted his teeth and decided he could not confess.","\"My lord, this subordinate serves the people wholeheartedly and has nothing to confess.\"","Meng Huaining sneered inwardly. It's already come to this, yet you still insist on dying. This official will show you whose words carry more weight, yours or my authority.","He looked towards the kneeling commoners, \"The one who once harmed you, Cui Wen, is here. State your grievances and this official will serve justice for you.\"","The few commoners looked at each other and gradually stepped forward to tell of Cui Wen's evil deeds.","Initially, Cui Wen kept denying the accusations stubbornly, but Meng Huaining ordered someone to shut his mouth.","After the first group of commoners had finished telling their grievances, the second group came up to testify.","The surrounding commoners who were observing could not help but curse Cui Wen for being deranged as they listened to everyone's accounts.","Some had even run home to fetch rotten vegetable leaves and stinky eggs to pelt the crazy, treacherous dog after he left the court.","It was not until Meng An could no longer grip the writing brush steadily that Meng Huaining ordered the halt of hearing commoners' grievances.","Even though there were still many unspoken grievances, just these were enough for Cui Wen to die a hundred times over.","Meng Huaining publicly announced the removal of Cui Wen from the position of Yun City County Magistrate. As for how he would be dealt with, it would be decided after all the cases had been fully tried.","Of course, everyone present understood clearly that there was no possibility of Cui Wen staying alive. The things he had done warranted lingchi, at the very least."]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188: When the magistrate arrives, all the other people stay away at the same speed.","paragraphs":["This news was very pleasing to the commoners.","Outside the county government office, the commoners led the cheer \"Long live the fair county prefect\" ...","At the same time, Meng Huaining also sent people to seal up the Cui Residence. Cui Wen and his wife Liu were temporarily imprisoned in the County Prison to await interrogation and sentencing.","Today's trial of County Magistrate Cui has come to a temporary end. Meng Huaining once again returned to the study with Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","\"Brother Mo, Sister-in-law, shall I rearrange a new residence for you now?\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran knew Meng Huaining wanted to make their living environment more comfortable.","However, neither of them responded immediately.","If it weren't for the Cui family's deliberate harassment, He Zhiran felt Xi Ling Village was not bad.","When they first entered the village, she noticed that the northernmost part of the village had a very wide river, which meant there was no problem with the water supply here.","There was also such a vast farmland, possibly because Xi Ling Village did not have a large population, and much of the land was obviously left unused.","With so much unused land available, they could also make good use of it in the future without having to worry about not being able to buy farmland.","Xi Ling Village was backed by mountains, and there were several men with high martial arts skills in the family. It would be very convenient to eat some game in the future.","What's more, she also wanted to take advantage of the seeds in her space to create an extraordinary fruit garden.","Considering all these factors, Xi Ling Village was a very suitable place for them to live.","Now that Meng Huaining has come to Yun City as the county prefect, he has dealt with County Magistrate Cui on the very first day. The Cui family must know that their backer has fallen, so they would also have to keep a low profile.","Mo Jiuye liked Xi Ling Village because it was located in a remote place with mountains and waters. As long as they build a good house there next spring, it would be great for the family to live a carefree life there away from worldly affairs.","After the couple discussed their ideas with each other, Mo Jiuye spoke up to reply to Meng Huaining.","\"Brother Meng, my wife and I both feel that Xi Ling Village is good, so there is no need to rearrange the residence.\"","Seeing his sincere attitude without trying to be polite with him, Meng Huaining stood up and said,","\"Since this is the case, I will accompany Brother Mo and Sister-in-law to take a look and see what the environment there is like.\"","In fact, both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran knew that Meng Huaining accompanying them was not just to take a look at Xi Ling Village.","He wanted to help establish prestige for his relatives and let those villagers know clearly that they were closely related to the county prefect. So if anyone wanted to make things difficult or squeeze them in the future, they would have to think twice.","The two of them did not object to this.","Although they were not afraid of the villagers making trouble, who would dislike a comfortable life?","Mo Jiuye stood up with his fist and said, \"Then we'll have to trouble Brother Meng.\"","Meng Huaining gestured for them to go ahead. He followed Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran out of the study.","In order to make a bigger scene, he also ostentatiously rode a tall horse and brought more than a dozen officers with him.","As soon as the group left the front door of the county government office, Henry ran over.","\"Ms. He Zhiran, we haven't set the time and place to meet tomorrow yet.\"","When He Zhiran heard this, she slapped her forehead.","She really blamed herself for this. She was in a hurry to catch up with Meng Huaining just now and neglected this matter.","She smiled and replied to Henry in English, \"Mr. Henry, shall we meet at the front door of the county government office at around 10 am tomorrow?\"","Facing the foreigner, He Zhiran did not mention the time in shichens. She just saw a pocket watch chain on Henry's chest, so she could deduce that Henry told time with clocks and watches.","Henry nodded repeatedly, \"Good, it's settled then. We have an appointment at 10 am tomorrow morning. It's a promise.\"","After seeing Henry leave, Meng Huaining ordered the group to set off for Xi Ling Village.","On the way there, Meng Huaining rode alongside the mule cart and chatted with Mo Jiuye to carefully inquire about the situation in Xi Ling Village.","He thus learned that Cui's clansmen were also rampant tyrants in Xi Ling Village.","Meng Huaining already had plans to deal with this. If there was time today, he would dismiss the Cui family members from their official positions and elect a suitable village chief later on.","At that time, it was already shen hour in the afternoon. Winter days were shorter, so Mo Jiuye was worried Five would have an outbreak and urged the mule cart to its fastest speed.","Naturally, Meng Huaining had no trouble keeping up while riding his horse at such a speed.","However, those officers had a miserable time. In order not to fall behind, they ran almost all the way until Mo Jiuye slowed down the mule cart as they approached Xi Ling Village.","The officers were gasping for breath but still did not dare to utter a word of complaint in front of Meng Huaining.","Not only that, they had to line up in neat rows with the two in front banging gongs and shouting to clear the way.","\"The county prefect is here. All irrelevant people must make way quickly...\"","It had to be said that when Meng Huaining entered Xi Ling Village, he put on quite an impressive show.","The villagers had never seen such a spectacle before. Hearing the sounds, they hurried back into their own yards one after another.","In the past, the highest ranked official to visit Xi Ling Village was County Magistrate Cui. It would always be Cui family members coming out to greet them.","So in the minds of these villagers, when the county prefect came here, it should still be Cui family members coming out to greet him.","And that was indeed the case. The Cui family members who did not yet know that County Magistrate Cui had been dismissed all ran out when they heard the commotion outside.","Village Chief Cui walked in the middle of the crowd. Seeing Meng Huaining, he immediately knelt down.","\"Your humble servants pay their respects, My Lord.\"","However, Meng Huaining made no indication for them to stand up.","The Cui family kowtowed on the ground for a long time but did not hear County Prefect ask them to rise. Some cautiously glanced around with the corners of their eyes.","When they took a look, they saw that the two Mo family members were actually standing beside the county prefect!","When faced with this situation, the Cui family immediately had a bad premonition.","Especially Village Chief Cui. He had originally planned to plead with the county prefect on behalf of himself and his clansmen who were beaten today after the formal greeting.","But what did he see?","He saw that the two culprits who beat people up were actually standing side by side with the county prefect.","Being able to stand side by side with the county prefect was enough to explain one problem.","That was that the county prefect knew these two people and had a close relationship with them.","With this thought, Village Chief Cui clearly felt cold air rushing from the crown of his head. At the same time, his body shuddered involuntarily.","Meng Huaining still showed no intention of asking them to get up. He was in a hurry to see the situation of Mo's family and had Mo Jiuye lead the way, completely ignoring the Cui family as he walked towards the back of the village.","Seeing the county prefect leaving, the Cui family members were in an awkward situation of not knowing whether to get up or remain kneeling.","In the end, Village Chief Cui boldly made a decision for them to get up and follow the county prefect to take a look.","Just in case those exiled people were speaking ill of them behind their backs to the county prefect, they could still find a chance to refute.","On the way to the foot of the mountain, they would pass the Zhao and Zhou families.","Although those people did not dare to come out, with such a high ranked official in the village, they would naturally crouch on top of the walls to watch.","(Side note: Will detoxify Five tomorrow.)"]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189: Thank you for saving me.","paragraphs":["Seeing the friendly interaction between the county magistrate and the Mo family couple, the Zhao and Zhou family members seemed to understand something as well.","Today, several people from the Mo family came over to rent a courtyard to spend the winter here, but because of the threat from the Cui family, even though they had vacant courtyards, they did not dare to agree.","Not only did they lose a lot of income, but they also seemed to have offended these people.","They only hoped that the Mo family would not take it out on them common folk and tell on them to the county magistrate, isolating them was not their original intention...","He Zhiran also noticed these villagers peeking over the walls, but did not know what they were thinking.","At this moment, she only hoped to see her family sooner and give the antidote to the Fifth Elder.","With a group of officials, everyone headed towards the foot of the mountain mightily.","Just as they approached, a black and white furball came staggering towards them.","Rice Ball ran straight towards He Zhiran's direction, while Mo Hanyue chased after him.","\"Rice Ball, don't run, auntie will be back soon.\"","Rice Ball tumbled a few times on the road and dove straight into He Zhiran's arms.","At this time, Mo Hanyue had caught up.","This was a bend in the road. Because Mo Hanyue was in a hurry chasing Rice Ball, she did not pay attention to her footing and was suddenly tripped by a large rock.","Her whole body lunged forward instantly.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye's attention was completely on the Rice Ball in He Zhiran's arms. When he realized his sister was falling, it was already too late to come to her rescue.","At the critical moment, Meng Huaining leapt from his horseback and steadily caught the falling Mo Hanyue.","\"Be careful, miss.\"","Having been taught the etiquette and rules of noble households since childhood, upon feeling physical contact with a strange man, Mo Hanyue quickly took a few steps back.","After steadying herself, she looked towards her savior.","She saw that Meng Huaining was in his early twenties, handsome and dignified in his official county magistrate uniform, making him look mature yet dashing.","At this time, Mo Jiuye had also rushed over, asking with concern,","\"Hanyue, are you hurt?\"","Mo Hanyue shook her head. \"I'm fine brother, thanks to this gentleman for saving me.\"","Mo Jiuye had also witnessed Meng Huaining saving his sister. He had been too concerned about his sister just now to thank him immediately.","Seeing that Mo Hanyue was unharmed, he clasped his fist towards Meng Huaining, \"Many thanks to Brother Meng for lending a hand.\"","Seeing that this gentleman was acquainted with her brother, and even addressed each other as brothers, Mo Hanyue immediately felt much more at ease than before.","She politely bowed to Meng Huaining, \"Thank you for saving me, sir.\"","Meng Huaining had only thought the girl falling was a Xi Ling Villager when he went to save her instinctively. He did not expect that coincidentally, it turned out to be Big Brother Mo's sister. Only now did he look closely at the girl before him.","The girl had a pair of clean, bright eyes, curved willow leaf eyebrows, and a very endearing smile. Her way of speaking was natural, completely different from other young ladies he had met from prominent families.","In front of the Mo family, Meng Huaining never saw himself as an official, only wishing to interact with them as friends.","After a brief silence, he clasped his fist in return to Mo Hanyue.","\"It was effortless on my part, Miss Mo need not stand on ceremony.\"","This was Mo Hanyue's first time interacting at such close distance with a man other than her father and brothers. Seeing the dignified county magistrate return her gesture with no pretense at all, she felt a little embarrassed and ran off to find He Zhiran with her head lowered.","She had accompanied Rice Ball the whole day today and had been terribly frightened when Rice Ball suddenly ran off just now. Now seeing Rice Ball snug in auntie‘s arms, Mo Hanyue instantly felt relieved.","Mo Jiuye was also anxious to return, beckoning Meng Huaining to keep walking towards the foot of the mountain.","By now, it was nearing dusk. As they had failed to rent a house in the village, simple stoves had already been set up outside, with the women busy preparing dinner.","When Meng Huaining first arrived at the foot of the mountain, he was stunned by the dilapidated houses there.","At the same time, he felt even greater resentment towards Deputy Magistrate Cui for his abuse of power.","\"Big Brother Mo, how can people live in houses like these? Why don't you all temporarily stay with me at the county government for one night? Tomorrow I will reassign you all proper lodging.\"","He had already promised Mo Jiuye to let them continue residing at Xi Ling Village. Despite the harassment from the Cui family, he believed that he could deal with this perfectly once he stepped in personally.","How would Meng Huaining imagine that the houses given to them at Xi Ling Village turned out to be like this.","The more intact ones were lopsided, while a large portion had totally collapsed...","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had already made up their minds and did not want to change locations.","\"I think this place is not bad. Next spring, we will buy this place and renovate it properly. By then, Brother Meng can come back and see that the scene will not be like this.\"","Meng Huaining shook his head helplessly, he also saw that Big Brother Mo was determined to stay here and it was not suitable for him to persuade them otherwise.","Mo Jiuye formally introduced Meng Huaining to his family and briefly told them how they got to know each other. The Mo family's impression of Meng Huaining improved even more upon hearing that he had been specially arranged to come to Yun City to be the county magistrate.","Meng Huaining had also just learned that Mo Chuhan and Mo Chongyuan were still alive, and felt genuinely happy for the Mo family.","The entire Mo family being exiled was already too unfair. For them to find two living male members of the family now was simply like heaven blessing them.","Meng Huaining had always greatly admired the heroism of the Mo men. Hence, he behaved very respectfully towards Mo Chuhan and Mo Chongyuan, referring to them as Fifth Elder and Eighth Elder like Mo Jiuye.","His form of address to Mo Jiuye had also changed to Ninth Elder.","He carefully surveyed the surroundings. If not for the surrounding dilapidated houses being too shabby in contrast, based on just the location, it was indeed not a bad settlement place.","To further understand the situation here, Meng Huaining called over one of his officials.","\"Who do these courtyards belong to?\"","Ma Junshan who came forward was relatively well-informed about this place.","\"My lord, these courtyards all belonged to the ancestors of Xi Ling Village villagers. I heard that these used to be where their elders lived.","Because of occasional raids from barbarians, the elders of the few families here decided back then to move their residences to the village center for safety. Over time, these houses had all become vacant.","And due to being neglected over many years, this is how they became today.\"","After listening to Ma Junshan's account, Meng Huaining had another headache.","\"Brothers, the location here is indeed good, but if there are raids from barbarians, it would be very troublesome. Why not...\"","Mo Jiuye knew that Meng Huaining still intended to persuade them to change locations. He interjected,","\"Brother Meng need not worry. Even if barbarians come to raid, their numbers will not be too significant. With us brothers around, there is absolutely no need to worry.\""]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190: You take the cure Now.","paragraphs":["What's more, there were also Liang Hao and others whose combat power could not be underestimated.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was determined, Meng Huaining shook his head helplessly and did not intend to spend more words on this matter.","Seeing that the sun had already set in the west, He Zhiran winked at Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye was also anxious about detoxifying the Fifth Brother, so he pulled Mo Chunhan to his side, \"Eighth brother, you keep Fifth Brother company first. I have something to talk to Fifth Brother about.\"","Although it was a bit impolite to Meng Huaining, the detoxification was imminent.","The Eighth Brother was also anxious about this and knew that the Ninth Brother and Sister were going to help the Fifth Brother detoxify.","\"Alright, Brother Meng can just stay here with me.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded at Meng Huaining and pulled the Fifth Brother away.","He Zhiran drilled into the tent and sent Rice Ball into the space to eat. Then she followed Mo Jiuye and Fifth Brother to the house in the east.","The Fifth Brother was already showing signs of the onset of poison and was using his internal energy to suppress it.","When they entered the room, the Fifth Brother instinctively reached for the iron chain to restrain himself before the outbreak of the poison.","Mo Jiuye stopped him, \"Fifth brother, He Zhiran has prepared the antidote in the city. There is no need for you to torture yourself anymore.\"","Although the Fifth Brother had heard from his younger siblings yesterday that they would help him make the antidote, with so many medical practitioners unable to identify the poison, how could his sister-in-law have made the antidote so quickly?","He Zhiran used some advanced medical equipment from the modern world to configure the antidote, so it was no wonder that the Fifth Brother found it unbelievable.","They both saw the disbelief in the Fifth Brother's eyes, but now was not the time for lengthy explanations.","He Zhiran took out a black pill from her sleeve through the space.","Mo Jiuye took the pill and brought it to Mo Chongyuan.","\"Fifth brother, take this antidote now.\"","Mo Chongyuan took the pill without hesitation and put it directly into his mouth.","The pill dissolved as soon as it entered his mouth, so there was no need to wash it down with water.","He Zhiran stared closely at the Fifth Brother's reaction, ready to provide emergency treatment in case anything went wrong.","Soon, the Fifth Brother's body reacted. The restless feeling that had made him go mad gradually disappeared without needing to forcibly suppress it with internal energy anymore.","Next, he felt his body heating up from the lower abdomen, gradually spreading to all parts of his body, and the hot flow finally reached his limbs and even the tips...","At the same time, his hands and feet felt swollen.","At first, Mo Chongyuan endured it with all his might, but at last, his feet were so swollen that he could no longer stand, and his hands were also swollen like big steamed buns.","Not only that, his exposed hands turned blackish red, which was shocking to behold.","Unable to stand, the Fifth Brother fell back onto the bed behind him.","Even so, he didn't let out a sound, trying hard to endure.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye became a little worried.","\"He Zhiran, is this a normal reaction for Fifth Brother?\"","He Zhiran nodded, \"Yes, the toxins are slowly spreading to his limbs. When the time comes, his blood vessels will bulge. We just need to let the poisoned blood out.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran had already seen the blood vessels in the Fifth Brother's left hand bulge.","She quickly took out silver needles from her space, picked up the thickest one, and steadily pierced the bulging blood vessel on the Fifth Brother's left hand.","Black blood spurted out like a thin fountain.","He Zhiran was caught off guard and was splashed all over.","She didn't have time to wipe herself off as the silver needle had already pierced the bulging blood vessel on the Fifth Brother's right hand.","Similarly, black blood sprayed out from the eye of the needle.","By now, Mo Jiuye understood He Zhiran’s method. As she successfully let blood from the Fifth Brother’s right hand, he had already taken off his shoes and socks.","After all, the idea of differentiation between men and women was deeply ingrained in ancient people.","Although Mo Chongyuan was extremely uncomfortable, he was still conscious and instinctively resistant to his sister-in-law seeing his feet.","Mo Jiuye was also aware of this, but did not dare to be careless about the Fifth Brother's detoxification.","If he rushed in to operate and pierced the wrong spot, it would be counterproductive.","Therefore, he took the initiative to persuade Mo Chongyuan.","\"Fifth brother, He Zhiran won't touch your body.\"","With both hands already feeling much more relaxed, Mo Chongyuan knew that bleeding his feet was necessary. He could only turn his head away, tacitly approving Mo Jiuye’s words.","He Zhiran worked very quickly. In the blink of an eye, she had pierced the bulging blood vessels on Mo Chongyuan’s feet.","Black blood continued to flow out steadily, so much that He Zhiran became a little worried that Mo Chongyuan might lose too much blood.","Fortunately, shortly after He Zhiran’s worries, the blood flowing out of the Fifth Brother's limbs gradually turned bright red.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye was overjoyed.","\"He Zhiran, Fifth Brother's blood has turned red. Doesn't this mean his poison has been cured?\"","He Zhiran let out a sigh of relief, as if a heavy load had been lifted.","\"We have succeeded.\"","Her words barely left her mouth as she had already stealthily taken sterile cotton balls from her space. She first gave two to Mo Jiuye to press on the needle holes in the Fifth Brother's feet.","Then she pressed on the needle holes in the Fifth Brother's hands herself.","After about a minute, they both removed the cotton balls at the same time.","Mo Jiuye helped Mo Chongyuan slowly sit up.","\"Fifth brother, how do you feel now?\"","Mo Chongyuan shook his head. \"Other than some dizziness, everything else is fine.\"","Dizzy? No wonder...","He Zhiran had already roughly estimated the Fifth Brother's blood loss, at least over 600ml.","With so much blood lost, an unhealthy person would probably have gone to meet the King of Hell.","Even though the Fifth Brother looked strong and sturdy, He Zhiran still did not dare to be careless.","After taking his pulse and confirming that he only had blood loss without other effects, she finally said,","\"The Fifth Brother's poison has been completely removed. He has lost too much blood for now. He will be fine after resting well for a few days.\"","Knowing that the Fifth Brother was fine, Mo Jiuye heaved a deep sigh of relief as well.","\"As long as you’re alright. Fifth brother, just listen to He Zhiran these days. Don't do anything, just lie down and rest.\"","He Zhiran added: “Tomorrow we’ll go into town to buy some recuperative food for the Fifth Brother. I believe he’ll recover soon.”","Hearing the two’s words, the Fifth Brother laughed heartily.","\"Thanks to the Ninth brother and sister. Once the Fifth Brother recovers, I’ll go hunting in the mountains to feed our big family.\"","Considering that Meng Huaining was still outside, Mo Jiuye could not let him wait for too long.","Knowing that Liang Hao and the others were not far from the house, he called them over to temporarily take care of the Fifth Brother here until his wife came, then they could leave.","After arranging everything, Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran away.","By then, it was already somewhat dark outside. He Zhiran sensed the space and saw that Rice Ball was already full and frolicking on the grass.","To avoid arousing suspicion from others, she could only reluctantly tell Rice Ball to temporarily exit the space.","The change of scene before Rice Ball’s eyes confused him a little. He let out a few murmurs."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191: You'll be justified as soon as you do this.","paragraphs":["However, it soon smelled the familiar scent, and the little guy instantly hugged one of He Zhiran's legs.","He Zhiran indulgently patted the little guy's head: \"Rice Ball is good, let's go back first, hug later.\"","Rice Ball seemed to understand, although reluctantly, but still obediently let go of the owner's leg.","The little guy followed Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran back to the camp with small steps.","At the same time, He Zhiran took out some wet wipes from the space and simply wiped off the black blood splashed on him.","Seeing Meng Huaining's appearance, he didn't seem to leave immediately.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran looked at each other and walked over to him.","At this time, Meng Huaining and Mo Chuhan were chatting happily, and Mo Chuhan's laughter could be heard from afar.","Mo Jiuye walked a few quick steps and came to the two.","\"What's the matter that makes the eighth brother laugh so happily?\"","When Mo Chuhan heard Mo Jiuye's voice, the first thing he thought of was the matter of the fifth brother detoxifying.","In front of Meng Huaining, he couldn't ask too much.","However, it was not difficult to guess from Mo Jiuye's tone that the fifth brother had successfully detoxified.","With this in mind, Mo Chuhan's smile widened a bit more.","\"Ninth younger brother, Brother Meng said that he wants me to go to the yamen to be a catcher. I have already agreed that after the family affairs are settled, I will go directly there.\"","In Mo Chuhan's opinion, it would be best for him to be this catcher.","First of all, he could use the fixed salary to make up for the family expenses. In addition, with a catcher at home, at least no one would dare to come to the house to make trouble again.","Most importantly, Mo Chuhan felt that no matter where he went, he needed some connections. By being this catcher, he could get to know more connections.","Mo Jiuye did not object to this. He knew that the eighth brother had a restless temperament and had been used to playing with knives and guns since he was a child. If he was kept at home to farm and hunt all day long, he believed this was not the life he wanted.","Moreover, there was no existence of the eighth brother on the list of exiles. If it weren't for the unkindness of Deputy Magistrate Cui, there would be no need to have the mark of exile on the eighth brother's household registration.","Therefore, there was no problem with the eighth brother being a catcher in terms of legitimacy.","Just as he was thinking about it, Meng Huaining spoke up.","\"Tomorrow I will change the eighth brother's household registration status to normal. This way, being this catcher will be completely legitimate.\"","Mo Chuhan laughed heartily again: \"Good, I'll leave everything to Brother Meng then.\"","After chatting for so long, Meng Huaining finally had time to ask about the black and white ball beside He Zhiran.","\"Is this sister-in-law's pet?\"","Seeing her little black and white ball being asked, He Zhiran hurriedly picked it up.","\"This was given to me by the fifth brother, I like it very much.\"","Seeing He Zhiran say this, Meng Huaining did not look very optimistic.","\"Sister-in-law, do you know what this is?\"","He Zhiran raised her eyebrows: \"It's an iron-eating beast!\"","\"Sister-in-law, according to the book, the teeth of the iron-eating beast are very sharp. You think it's cute now, but it will hurt people when it grows up.\"","He Zhiran was not ignorant at all about the habits of pandas.","Animals, like humans, have feelings. As long as you treat it well and guide it in a good direction from an early age, nothing is immutable.","He Zhiran was clear in her heart that although Meng Huaining said this for her own good, she was also thinking about how to respond to his words.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye spoke up.","\"Brother Meng, don't worry. With us brothers here, this little thing can't make any waves.\"","Meng Huaining was also a martial artist. Although his martial arts were not as strong as those of the Mo brothers, when he thought about it carefully, dealing with an adult iron-eating beast would not be a big problem if it was left to him.","Moreover, there were three people with strong martial arts in the Mo family, and there was indeed no need to worry about this.","\"It was me being overcautious.\"","Speaking, he also reached out to rub the little cutie's head.","Unexpectedly, Rice Ball seemed to have understood Meng Huaining's words. Seeing him reach out, he opened his mouth and bit towards him.","Seeing this, He Zhiran reacted swiftly and took a few steps back, preventing Rice Ball from succeeding.","She pretended to be angry and scolded: \"Rice Ball, if you bite someone again, I won't want you anymore.\"","Rice Ball stared at the owner with big eyes, looking extremely aggrieved.","Seeing Rice Ball's pitiful appearance, He Zhiran's heart was about to melt.","With outsiders present, she couldn't show too much doting, she could only continue to frown.","Seeing the owner not coaxing him, Rice Ball aggrievedly lay on her shoulder, no longer looking at Meng Huaining.","This move made the few big men laugh out loud.","As the laughter fell, Eldest Sister-in-law came over quickly to call everyone for dinner.","At this time, Meng Huaining still did not propose to leave, clearly he had no intention of leaving. Naturally he had to have dinner with them and those officials.","The sister-in-laws had long noticed this point, so today's dinner was prepared much more sumptuous than usual.","In addition to some of the ingredients He Zhiran had purchased earlier, there was also a porcupine that the fifth brother had hunted in the mountains today.","When the Mo family was in the capital city, they had also tasted all kinds of delicacies.","Since their cooking skills were not as good as He Zhiran’s, they simply wrapped dumplings with porcupine meat.","With the addition of several appetizers, this dinner could be described as sumptuous.","While the food was well prepared, the dining environment posed a problem that made them scratch their heads.","They still had to sleep in tents at night because they failed to rent a yard today. Not only that, even eating was outdoors.","Without tables, chairs, benches or stools, oilcloth was spread on the ground with a variety of delicacies on it, just like when they were exiled.","The Fang and Xie families also saw Mo Jiuye bring the county magistrate back together, and they could also confirm that this county magistrate had an extraordinary relationship with the Mo family.","For this reason, they also prepared some side dishes in their own homes and brought them over to invite the county magistrate to taste.","After all, there were quite a few people to entertain today, and the food prepared by the Mo women was not enough to go around. Therefore, they only invited Fang Chuanzhou and Xie Tianhai, the two family patriarchs, to have dinner together.","Meng Huaining knew that there were two other families who came here with the Mo family. They were all one heart with the Mo family. Therefore, his attitude towards Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou was also very kind.","By now, the sister-in-laws had learned some of the cooking skills of He Zhiran, and the dishes they made were also very tasty.","While enjoying the delicious food, Meng Huaining had already made up his mind.","Since he had come, he must solve their housing problem before leaving tonight no matter what.","After eating his fill, Meng Huaining stood up and called several officials to the village.","He ordered the officials to beat gongs and assemble all the villagers of Xi Ling Village together.","The villagers had been watching the situation outside eagerly to find out if the county magistrate had left. When they heard officials beating gongs and calling them to gather in the center of the village, the Zhao family and Zhou family rushed to the designated location like bees, wanting to know what had happened.","At the same time, the nearest Cui family also came over one after another."]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192: A New Official has Three fires.","paragraphs":["Village Chief Cui thought that the county magistrate would leave soon, so he ordered his clansmen to continue kneeling. However, the county magistrate did not show up until it was dark.","If they kept kneeling like this, his old bones might not be able to take it. Therefore, he had to reluctantly allow the clansmen to return to their homes.","At this moment, the county magistrate ordered people to beat gongs and gather the crowds. Village Chief Cui started to worry.","Could it be that the county magistrate intended to publicly punish them for showing disrespect?","Supported by his two sons, Village Chief Cui stood at the front of his clansmen. He silently prayed that the county magistrate had not summoned them over that matter.","He even scolded that useless nephew of his in his heart for not sending someone to notify them ahead of time of the county magistrate's visit to Xi Ling Village, so that he could have been better prepared...","Meng Huaining did not even glance at Village Chief Cui and directly swept his eyes over the crowd. Seeing that most people had arrived, he finally spoke up.","\"This official has just arrived in Yun City to take office today and has already received an outrageous case.","Our County Steward Cui, not satisfied with just exploiting the common people to fulfill his selfish desires, actually condones his own clansmen to do things even lower than beasts.","Today, this official has already dismissed County Steward Cui from his position to be investigated...\"","As he spoke, his gaze finally fell upon Village Chief Cui.","When Village Chief Cui heard that his nephew has been dismissed from his position and would be investigated, he was so frightened that he almost fainted on the spot.","Not to mention other tribesmen, even he himself had done far too many harmful things to aid Cui Wen.","It was not difficult to hear from the county magistrate's words that he took this matter very seriously.","As the saying goes, a new official fires his first shot upon taking office. It is clear that this first shot is aimed at his Cui family.","It's over, they were finished.","Just as Village Chief Cui was panicking internally, Meng Huaining spoke again.","\"Guards, arrest Village Chief Cui and temporarily detain him in the jail to await trial.\"","The guards acknowledged and ruthlessly tied up Village Chief Cui in public.","Seeing this, the Cui clansmen knelt down one after another, crying out injustice...","Meng Huaining signaled to the guards behind him. The guards immediately went up and kicked a few of the Cuis who were crying out the loudest.","\"How dare you make loud noises in front of the county magistrate. Are you looking to die...\"","After getting kicked a few times, the Cui family instantly fell silent. Everyone knelt in their original places, not even daring to breathe heavily, afraid that the incident would implicate themselves.","Seeing this scene, the Zhao Family and Zhou Family felt extremely delighted.","They could tell that the county magistrate was determined to punish the Cuis, so they would no longer have to live under Cui's oppression in the future.","The first to come to this realization was Zhao Zechuan. He loudly shouted:","\"Brilliant county magistrate, please serve justice for the people of Xi Ling Village.\"","Right afterwards, several Zhao clansmen followed and agreed. All were criticisms of the Cuis.","Seeing this, the bolder people from Zhou Family also pleaded for the county magistrate to serve justice for them.","The sun had already set for the day and Meng Huaining originally planned to just make an example out of Village Chief Cui for now mainly to show the Cui family that the Mohists were not to be bullied by them.","He did not expect that as soon as he ordered Village Chief Cui to be arrested, so many people would immediately plead for him to serve justice for them.","As the parent official of this place, he had to serve justice for these villagers.","At the same time, Meng Huaining also wanted to understand what other law defying deeds the Cui clansmen besides Cui Wen had done.","\"Meng An, this official is going to immediately put the Cui clan on trial. Tell the villagers to speak up if they have any grievances.\"","Carrying out the order, Meng An loudly conveyed Meng Huaining's intention to the Zhao and Zhou families.","Upon hearing this news, the Zhao and Zhou families were confused at first.","The reason why they dared to loudly criticize just now had largely stemmed from their immense hatred for the Cuis.","They did not expect that the county magistrate would decide to serve justice for them so swiftly.","The good news came so abruptly that the villagers of the two families could not fully comprehend it right away.","Zhao Zechuan reacted the fastest and pulled his father out to kneel before Meng Huaining.","\"County magistrate, please serve justice for my Zhao family.\"","Zhao Zechuan's father was currently the Zhao family patriarch. When he initially heard that the county magistrate would serve justice for them, he originally planned to wait and see if the county magistrate truly would act like an honorable gentleman.","Who would have expected that he would be pulled out by his own devious son without realizing it.","Since he had already knelt before the county magistrate, he no longer had anything to worry about.","The Zhao patriarch kowtowed to Meng Huaining.","\"County magistrate, your humble servant is named Zhao Hua and is the Zhao family patriarch. My ancestors have lived in Xi Ling Village for generations.","Initially, the three families got along. But ever since Cui Wen became county steward, that was when the nightmare began for my Zhao family and the Zhous.","Abusing Cui Wen's power, the Cuis forced the beautiful young ladies of our two families to marry into theirs. We would have conceded if the matches were age appropriate, but the men were always those who had not gotten wives because they were too poor and had lived long fruitless lives.","The daughters of the Cuis who were ugly or disabled were forcibly married off to fine young men from our families.","That would still be tolerable if those women could peacefully live their lives after marrying into our families. But each and every one of them was problematic and brazenly sent stuff back to their maternal homes without allowing our families to criticize.","If our families protested against such marriage arrangements, Cui Wen would send government officials to oppress us.","The Cuis also forcibly traded their barren lands for our fertile fields. Likewise, if we refused, the officials would come forward and crack down on us.","Come autumn harvest time, Cui Wen only needed to say a word and our two families would have to shoulder the entirety of the grain tax for the Cuis.","Over the past decade or two, life for my Zhao family and the Zhous could only be described as seriously miserable. Many people starved to death during bad crop harvest years.","Everything your humble servant has stated is true. I plead with you, esteemed sir, to serve justice for us...\"","When he finished speaking, Zhao Hua kowtowed three times to Meng Huaining again.","Before Zhao Hua even got up, the Zhou family patriarch knelt before Meng Huaining as well.","\"This lowly one is the Zhou family patriarch. My whole clan can bear witness that every sentence Patriarch Zhao has spoken is true. Esteemed sir, I beseech you on our behalf as well.\"","Likewise, three thuds from his kowtows landed heavily on the ground.","At the same time, the Zhao and Zhou clansmen all knelt down together and shouted in unison: \"County magistrate, we plead with you to serve justice for us...\"","After listening to the accounts of the two patriarchs and seeing so many kneeling villagers, Meng Huaining's rage boiled over.","For the first time, he did something ungraceful.","Meng Huaining then took big strides toward the Cui clansmen and fiercely kicked a few of the kneeling men in front.","Meng Huaining trained martial arts since he was young so each kick was very powerful.","The several men cried out in pain...","The Cui clansmen had lorded all over Xi Ling Village relying on Cui Wen's influence these past few years. When had they ever suffered such mistreatment?","Not daring to retaliate against the county magistrate, they still were unwilling to let the Zhao and Zhou families off."]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193: Call me Mo Lao Jiu","paragraphs":["After several men knocked down by Meng Huaining got up, they all glared at the people from Zhao and Zhou families.","Their looks seemed to say - just you wait.","Seeing the looks on Cui family's faces, the villagers from the two families shivered out of habit, and the horrible images of Cui family bullying their own families even emerged in their minds.","In the dim light of several torches around, Meng Huaining immediately noticed Cui family's actions.","He ordered the officers behind him.","\"Give each of these Cui men ten heavy strikes. If they refuse to obey, double the punishment.\"","Among these officers, there was no lack of people who had pressured Zhao and Zhou families under Cui Wen's order.","At this moment, they were extremely nervous, always thinking of finding a chance to show their stance to the new county magistrate, so as to avoid getting involved with Cui family.","Just when several officers were thinking about countermeasures in their minds, the county magistrate ordered to beat Cui family men with sticks.","Now, the opportunity for them to show themselves has finally come.","Several officers who used to act as accomplices for Cui Wen took the lead to rush out and hit Cui family men with clubs in their hands.","Cui family men were not unfamiliar with these officers. Seeing them coming, they thought the strikes on them would be lighter.","However, the result was just the opposite. These officers were implicated by Cui family, and now they hated Cui family so much. How could they go easy on them?","If ten strikes could beat one to death, they would spare no effort.","As soon as Cui family men felt the weight of the strikes at the first moment, they burst into scolding.","\"Feng Laowu, you bastard, we used to drink together. How can you turn your face ruthlessly now?\"","Feng Laowu: \"Damn you, if you dare to babble more, I will beat you to death...\"","Not only one pair had the same scene, there were also two other Cui men burst into scolding.","The result was just more brutal strikes falling on them, almost breaking their bones.","Soon ten heavy strikes were finished. Those beaten Cui men finally learned the lesson, daring not to say more. All of them begged Meng Huaining for mercy with their teeth gritting.","Meng Huaining completely ignored them and ordered the officers to keep a close eye on all Cui family members starting today. Before Cui Wen's case got closed, no Cui family member was allowed to leave Xi Ling Village.","Then Meng Huaining called the chieftains of Zhao and Zhou families over.","\"Cui family has committed so many evil acts that even if I don't sleep all night, I'm afraid I still can't finish the trial. Do you have anyone in your families who can read and write?\"","When it came to people who were literate, all eyes turned to Zhao Zechuan.","Due to Cui family's exploitation, they led such an impoverished life that having enough to eat was already beyond hope, let alone having spare money to send kids to school.","Zhao Zechuan was the only exception.","Having suffered oppression from Cui family for many years, in order to stand out, there must be someone from the family holding higher official post than Cui Wen.","For this reason, Zhao family secretly decided to send a smart boy to school, with tuition fees donated by all family members.","Zhao Zechuan's intelligence and wit had obtained unanimous approval from everyone.","Therefore, Zhao Zechuan was the only educated one among Zhao and Zhou families.","Before Meng Huaining had finished, Zhao Zechuan had already come to the front across the crowd.","\"My lord, your student Zhao Zechuan is not talented. I'm willing to write this plaint.\"","Seeing Zhao Zechuan addressing himself as a student, Meng Huaining raised his brows. \"Do you have an official title?\"","Zhao Zechuan answered neither humble nor pushy: \"I passed the county examination last year and became Xiucai (a successful candidate in the imperial examination at the county level).\"","Meng Huaining didn't expect that such an impoverished family was able to nurture a Xiucai.","Moreover, seeing his age, he must be only sixteen or seventeen.","He had become Xiucai last year at such young age. This could prove this man's excellence.","Thinking of this, Meng Huaining was in no hurry to talk about writing the plaint.","\"Since this is the case, it's truly not easy for your families to nurture a Xiucai, considering the extreme poverty described by your chieftains.\"","If what Zhao Hua said was true, under Cui family's oppression, just getting enough food had already become a big issue for Zhao and Zhou families, let alone supporting someone to pursue education.","Meng Huaining was also a well-educated person. He understood clearly that cultivating a Xiucai cost a lot.","If Zhao Zechuan failed to give a reasonable explanation to this question, then what Zhao chieftain said might not be all true.","Zhao Zechuan sensed the magistrate's suspicion. He bowed and told the story of all Zhao family members donating money together to support his study.","Hearing this, Meng Huaining had to give Zhao family a big thumb up for their solidarity and wisdom.","\"Well, since this is the case, I'll give you one day to write a good plaint against Cui family and submit it to the county government.\"","Zhao Zechuan bowed with his hands cupped again. \"Please rest assured, my lord. I'll present the plaint early tomorrow morning.\"","Meng Huaining looked up to the darkening sky, and then asked the two chieftains of Zhao and Zhou.","\"I'm dismissing Cui family's position as village head today. Do you have any good candidates for the new village head in mind?\"","When it came to the position of village head of Xi Ling Village, the two chieftains had never thought about it. As long as Cui family was there, this position would never fall into their hands.","But now things were different. The county magistrate settled Cui Wen on his first day taking office. It was imaginable that Cui family would become helpless without Cui Wen's support in the future, even though they wanted to make troubles.","Thinking of these, there was a faint wish to give it a try in both chieftains' minds.","Let alone the monthly allowance of one or two silvers from the government, their families would also benefit a lot from it indirectly .","The reason why the two chieftains didn't promote themselves was that they didn't want to spoil the relationship because of competing for the position of village head.","Seeing neither of them speaking, Meng Huaining guessed what was on their minds.","However, fortunately, neither of them took the initiative to speak for the sake of that position. This showed that they were taking each other's feelings into consideration to some extent.","Undoubtedly, the future village head of Xi Ling Village must be one of these two chieftains.","He sized them up and saw clear minds in both of their eyes.","\"Since this is the case, Zhao chieftain will be the village head of Xi Ling Village in the future!\"","The reason was simple. Zhao chieftain was younger, and there was also an educated son in his family, which was convenient to record something.","Zhou chieftain just froze for an instant and then bowed with his hands cupped to Zhao chieftain. \"Congratulations to village head Zhao.\"","The surprise came so suddenly. Zhao Hua was still reacting. Before he could respond, he had already received the congratulations from Zhou chieftain.","He hurried to return the courtesy and said some polite words. After all, with the county magistrate present, this was not his home ground. The two finished the small talk and stepped aside.","Meng Huaining's eyes fell on the two men again.","\"I wonder if there are any vacant houses in your families?\"","Hearing this, the eyes of the two chieftains fell on Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran, who hadn't spoken a word at the same time.","They were very clear in their minds that the reason why the county magistrate asked this must be for the newcomers.","Someone had made inquiries about this today. Back then, hindered by Cui family, they didn't dare to agree.","Now the county magistrate asked them in person, and it was after he had started to punish Cui family. Of course they wouldn't refuse to rent houses to those newcomers anymore.","Zhao chieftain was the first to speak. \"Our Zhao family has two vacant houses. They are quite spacious, absolutely no problem for a big family to live in.\"","Zhou chieftain also said, \"Our Zhou family also has an empty house compound, with ten rooms in total if counting the main room and side rooms. We can rent them all to these newcomers.\"","He Zhiran felt their luck was really good.","Mo, Xie and Fang families, three families of people, happened to need three houses. And here were exactly three available houses.","While she was thinking about this, Meng Huaining had already turned around.","\"Brother Mo Jiuye, sister-in-law, since the two chieftains can provide three house compounds, why not go take a look now. If suitable, move in tonight. Don't catch cold by sleeping outside.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were also thinking the same way.","\"That's perfect.\" As soon as Mo Jiuye spoke, he walked toward the two chieftains.","\"Chieftains, may we go see those houses now?\"","Both chieftains replied at the same time: \"No problem. Just go take a look whenever Young Master Mo wants.\"","The most important thing Meng Huaining came here for was already settled. And it was getting late too. So he ordered to take away Cui Wen with those officers and leave Xi Ling Village.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran sent him and those officers to the village entrance before heading back to find the two chieftains.","Back to the original spot, except that Cui family men had been driven back home by officers, people from the other two families were still waiting there.","The attitudes of the two chieftains toward Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were extremely polite.","Chief Zhao stepped forward first to ask: \"May I ask how this gentleman is called?\"","Mo Jiuye politely answered: \"Chief Zhao, my surname is Mo, I'm the ninth child in my family, you can call me Old Nine Mo.\"","Then, he introduced He Zhiran to them to get acquainted, after all they would become neighbors in the future, so it was necessary to be familiar with each other.","The two chiefs were indeed simple and straightforward, calling Mo Jiuye \"Old Nine Mo\" directly, and calling He Zhiran \"Old Nine's wife\"!"]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194: I'll tell my family to move.","paragraphs":["After introducing themselves and exchanging greetings, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran followed Zhao Clan Chief to look at two vacant houses belonging to the Zhao Family.","As the group entered the Zhao family's territory, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's first impression was that compared to Village Chief Cui's brand new brick houses, these were like heaven and earth.","All the houses here were made of rammed earth, although there were some signs of repairs, they still looked quite sturdy overall.","Zhao Clan Chief pointed to the courtyard with the shortest wall in front and said, \"This is our family's old house. Later, as our sons grew up and wanted to get married, it became a little crowded living here, so we moved to a slightly bigger place and built a new courtyard.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran exchanged glances and walked towards that courtyard together.","The courtyard was not small. In the middle were three main rooms, with two side rooms on either side to the east and west. There was also a vegetable garden about half a mu in size in the back yard.","Seeing them look around, Zhao Clan Chief came over with a smile and asked, \"Although this house looks a bit old, it is sturdy enough to withstand the winter cold.\"","Mo Jiuye did not give his opinion. With only three courtyards available for rent, he could not afford to be picky.","\"Zhao Clan Chief, let's go take a look at the other one!\"","Zhao Clan Chief knew that not a small number of exiled people were sent here by the officials this time, but he did not know exactly how many households there were.","Seeing Mo Jiuye say this, he guessed that they were not interested in this courtyard.","But Zhao Clan Chief was not discouraged. The other courtyard also belonged to their clan. As long as he could rent out one, there would be some income.","Zhao Clan Chief called over a clansman.","\"Zhao Fu, take Old Nine and his wife to see the courtyard at your house.\"","Zhao Fu nimbly ran ahead to lead the way. In his heart, he also prayed that the house could be rented out successfully, so that the family would have some extra income.","The courtyard at Zhao Fu's house was about the same size as Zhao Clan Chief's, but the houses looked a little better.","After looking around, Mo Jiuye finally turned to Zhao Clan Chief and Zhao Fu, who had been staring intently at him.","\"May I ask how much rent you charge for these two courtyards?\"","Zhao Fu always listened to the clan chief, so he simply handed over the right to speak to him directly.","Zhao Clan Chief was an easygoing man. Even though he knew Mo Old Nine was eager to rent a house, he did not ask for an excessive price.","\"These two courtyards have been vacant for several years. Leaving them empty is leaving them empty, so two hundred wen a month from you will do.\"","This price was very cheap for Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","One had to know that renting a ten-person guesthouse room for one night cost at least one hundred wen.","A big courtyard with several rooms only cost two hundred wen a month. It was evident that this clan chief was quite genuine.","Mo Jiuye also understood clearly in his heart that they had to rent these courtyards no matter what, as his three families needed to rent houses, and moreover, there were only three vacant courtyards here.","\"Zhao Clan Chief, we'll rent both these courtyards. After we have seen the Zhou Family's courtyard, we will discuss the details with you.\"","This news was quite shocking to Zhao Clan Chief. He had thought that since they did not like the first courtyard, they would not be interested in the second one either.","He did not expect that both would be rented out!","\"Very good, I'll take you to the Zhou's now.\"","Saying so, Zhao Clan Chief made a \"please\" gesture, intending to personally take Mo Jiuye and his wife to the Zhou Family.","\"No need, I'll take them to see the courtyard myself.\"","Zhou Clan Chief had been following behind them. He thought after they were done looking at the Zhao family's courtyards, there would be no business left for his Zhou family. He was just there to watch the show.","He did not expect that they actually wanted to go to his Zhou family's place to see the courtyard!","Faced with such good news, how could Zhou Clan Chief not act enthusiastically?","Zhou Clan Chief looked quite a bit older than Zhao Clan Chief and walked slower.","Luckily the two families' residences were not far apart, and after walking for about ten minutes or so, they arrived.","Indeed as Zhou Clan Chief had said, the Zhou family's courtyard was bigger than the two Zhao family ones.","Although still built from rammed earth, there were six main rooms, with two side rooms on each side. The whole courtyard was rectangular in shape.","There was also a vegetable garden in the backyard, covering an area of almost one mu.","Although still rammed earth houses, they were much bigger than the Zhao family's courtyards. Moreover, there was also a well in the center of this courtyard.","Of the three houses, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran preferred this one.","However, there were still the Xie and Fang families. They could not make a decision hastily before informing the other two families.","At least they had to let the other two families know before making a decision.","Mo Jiuye still asked about the price first: \"Clan Chief Zhou, how much is the rent for this courtyard?\"","Clan Chief Zhou smiled and said, \"The Zhao family's courtyards are smaller than mine, with a monthly rent of two hundred wen. Mine is a bit bigger, so how about three hundred wen?\"","He was afraid that if the price was too high they would not rent it, thus missing out on income for no reason.","Compared to the Zhao family’s house, this price was quite fair.","Without any hesitation, Mo Jiuye nodded, \"Alright, we'll rent this courtyard too.\"","Winters are cold in the northwest, with possible snowfall. After looking around, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran realized that almost every room had a kang heated bed which could serve to keep warm. This saved them from the trouble of not having beds for the time being.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye decided to move in tonight. Although the house was rather cold and cheerless from having been unoccupied for years, it was still warmer than living in tents.","Having made up his mind, Mo Jiuye spoke: “Clan chiefs, we plan to move in immediately tonight. Do you have any objections?\"","\"No objections, no objections. If you need any help, we can all lend a hand.\" Zhao Clan Chief said with a beaming smile.","\"Good, I'll go notify my family to move now.\"","With that said, Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran along to stride quickly towards the foot of the mountain.","At this time, everyone had not yet gone to sleep.","Just then, Fifth Brother also returned from the eastern house. Although he still looked a little weak, as long as he did not make big actions, there would be no issues.","Besides, Fifth Sister-in-Law was always attentively taking care of him, so the others did not have to worry too much.","When the two returned, they shared this piece of good news.","Hearing that they had rented a courtyard, everyone seemed very excited.","The bitterly cold feeling from last night in the tents was still fresh in their memories. Just thinking of that cold made them unwilling to sleep.","Now things were finally looking up. They had rented a courtyard at last and would no longer have to freeze tonight.","After everyone got over their initial excitement, Mo Jiuye talked about the three courtyards’ situations and asked the Xie and Fang families which one they wanted to rent.","Without a doubt, the Fang and Xie families were already looking up to the Mo family, so of course the best courtyard had to be given to them.","The two families took the initiative to propose renting Zhao Clan Chief's two courtyards respectively, leaving the biggest Zhou family courtyard for the Mo family.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had liked the Zhou family courtyard to begin with, so there was no dispute over this.","Having settled on this, everyone started packing up their belongings.","As they were all exiled here, they did not have much besides some luggage and simple daily necessities. Packing up was very easy, they only needed to carry some items each."]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195: No Need to Pay","paragraphs":["Soon after getting everything packed, a large group of people set off mightily towards the village.","Rice Ball followed closely behind He Zhiran, afraid that its owner would leave it behind.","There were many eyes in the village, and He Zhiran was worried that Rice Ball would be too conspicuous. So she slowed down her pace and fell behind the crowd. With a wave of her hand, she put Rice Ball into her space.","Everyone was busy moving now, surely no one would notice Rice Ball's disappearance.","Even if someone did notice, she could just say the little one had run out to play.","Zhao Clan Chief and Zhou Clan Chief led a few clansmen and waited in their respective directions. Seeing the mighty crowd coming, they quickly went up to greet them.","Mo Jiuye walked at the very front. He first introduced the two chiefs to the Fang and Xie families.","The Fang and Xie families knew they were renting the Zhao Family's yard.","So they went directly to Zhao Clan Chief to pay the rent.","Mo Jiuye did the same, going with He Zhiran to Zhou Clan Chief to pay the rent.","\"Chief Zhou, how much rent in advance do you think is appropriate?\"","Mo Jiuye was thinking that they could rent for half a year at most. When spring arrived next year and flowers bloomed everywhere, they could build their own houses and naturally would have to move out after the houses were built.","If the other party asked for a whole year's rent upfront, he would definitely have to say something.","Zhou Clan Chief was also simple and honest. He smiled and said, \"I guess you all rushed here from the capital city and don't have much silver on you. Just pay monthly.\"","This was beyond what the two had expected.","When they rented houses around Salt Lake, the landlord insisted that they pay at least three months' rent in advance.","If it hadn't been for the high rent and Fifth Elder Brother's eloquence, they probably wouldn't even have gotten a house rented to them if they only offered one month's rent.","However, this old man had considered their possibly straitened circumstances and only asked for one month's rent.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's good impression of this old clan chief kept rising.","They accepted this kindness from the old man.","Just as He Zhiran was about to take money out of her space, Fifth Elder Brother, supported by Fifth Sister-In-Law, walked over.","\"Ninth younger sister, Fifth Elder Brother said he earned some silver from hunting. We'll pay the rent.\"","After she finished speaking, Fifth Elder Brother had already taken out a cloth bag of indistinguishable color from his bosom. In front of everyone, he poured out some broken silver and took out a piece to give to Zhou Clan Chief.","Zhou Clan Chief grasped the broken silver in his hand and weighed it roughly, only to find it was more than enough.","The old man was quite meticulous in his affairs.","\"I can't weigh this silver now. I’ll have my family members take it to town tomorrow to weigh it properly. Any extra I’ll pay you back in copper coins.\"","Such a sincere old man, He Zhiran quite liked.","\"No need, Old Father. You can keep any extra to buy meat to eat. If it falls short, you can ask us again.\"","A person who spent his whole life digging in the dirt would begrudge every copper coin he could squeeze out for use.","After being taken advantage of by the Cui Family all these years, she didn't want to take advantage of others like the Cui Family did everywhere.","\"No no no, renting is renting. If there's any extra I must pay it back.\"","Seeing the old man's sincere attitude, He Zhiran simply didn't want to waste words on this topic.","\"Old Father, it’s getting late. Let’s go to the yard early to tidy up a bit. You should also go back early to rest.\"","Zhou Clan Chief smiled and nodded. He thoughtfully called over a few young tribesmen to help the womenfolk move things.","The Xie and Fang families received the same gracious treatment. Zhao Clan Chief only collected one month's rent from them before sending people to take them to their lodgings.","After the Mo Family group arrived at their lodging, Old Lady Mo looked it over before personally assigning rooms for everyone.","The main central house naturally went to her, this elder. The five adjoining central houses on either side were given to Mo Chongyuan and his wife, Mo Chuhan and his wife, and the couple Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran got one.","Of the remaining two, considering that Mo Yunfeng was still alive, one was given exclusively to Third Sister-In-Law.","As for the last one, the sisters-in-law unanimously felt that living together would allow them to keep warm and have someone to chat with, so they asked to stay in one room together.","Seeing this, Old Lady Mo gave them the room with the largest earthen bed.","As for Mo Hanyue, she was assigned to the east wing close to the main house.","Old Lady Mo did not forget about Liang Hao and the others either. The five of them would temporarily live in the west wing.","Having already gained some experience of village life, when Fifth Elder Brother saw that the rooms were icy cold, he went to gather some firewood to warm everyone up.","Gathering firewood was a given, but with so many grown men around, no matter what they could not let such a physically frail person do the work.","Just as Mo Jiuye and Mo Chuhan had stopped Fifth Elder Brother and were about to go themselves, they heard footsteps coming from outside the yard.","The two brothers strode to the door to check.","They saw two men from the Zhou Family carrying over bundles of firewood over their shoulders.","They directly put the firewood down at the Mo Family's door.","\"The Chief sent these over. Old Father said you all might not be able to go up the mountain for firewood tonight, so use these first.\"","Looking at the four big bundles of firewood before them, He Zhiran hurriedly took out a string of copper coins from her space to give them.","But the two men quickly refused.","\"We gathered this firewood from the mountain. No need for money.\"","Having said that, the two turned and ran off.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran looked at each other, both smiling helplessly.","There was such a huge gap between people of the same village.","The Cui Family was petty everywhere and always tried to take advantage. Meanwhile, the Zhou and Zhao families were so simple and honest.","Having such people as neighbors in the future could be considered a blessing.","The Mo brothers each carried two bundles of firewood back.","The sisters-in-law rushed forward, vying to start the fire.","They had basically learned living skills along the way. Building fires and cooking were no longer difficult tasks.","Liang Hao and the others were not idle either. Seeing a large water vat in the kitchen, the few men carried the vat to the well, scrubbed it clean, and drew it full of water.","The others returned to their rooms and simply tidied up the dust a bit before going to bed.","It was late after they finished busying about.","After the sisters-in-law extinguished the kitchen fire, they each returned to rest.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's room was the cover, so the two flashed directly into the space.","He Zhiran had been busy outside for a whole day and was covered in dust. At this time, it was absolutely necessary to take a nice hot shower.","After playing with Rice Ball for a while, she went into the bathroom to wash up.","Mo Jiuye also washed himself until fresh and fragrant before climbing into the king bed.","He Zhiran was truly exhausted. Soon after her head hit the pillow she went to meet Master Zhou (god of dreams).","Mo Jiuye lightly kissed her on the forehead before lying down contentedly beside her to enter dreamland.","No matter how tired they were, the two could still wake up at first light. After tidying up, they brought Rice Ball out of the space together.","Liang Hao and the others had long since woken up and gone up the mountain to chop firewood, while the sisters-in-law had also come out of their rooms to prepare breakfast."]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196: Naturally, to buy some land.","paragraphs":["Having finally settled down, everyone became much more enthusiastic about their work than before. A peaceful atmosphere prevailed in the spacious courtyard.","Seeing this, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye also joined in.","After breakfast, Ba Ge called up Liang Hao and others, intending to go up the mountain to take a look.","Mo Jiuye also wanted to follow everyone up the mountain, but He Zhiran had an appointment with Henry today to help find a shipwright to repair the ship. He could not let such a beautiful daughter-in-law go there alone, so he had to give up on that idea.","The time agreed with Henry was not very early. The two set off in a mule cart after the hour of Chen (7-9am).","Just after they got to the middle of the road in the center of the village, they saw Zhao Zechuan walking towards the village entrance.","Mo Jiuye had a good impression of Zhao Zechuan, so he took the initiative to greet him.","\"Is Scholar Zhao going into the city?\"","Seeing that the speaker was Mo Jiuye, Zhao Zechuan immediately smiled.","\"So it turns out to be Brother Mo Jiu of the Mo family. Please don't call me Scholar Zhao, it sounds a bit awkward. Just call me by my name like the villagers do.\"","Yesterday when he went to the school, he specifically asked the well-informed teacher if he had heard of any officials with the Mo surname in the court.","The Mo surname was not very common in the Da Shun Dynasty. As soon as the teacher heard this surname, he immediately thought of the Mo family in the capital's Duke Who Protects the Nation's mansion.","After communicating with the teacher for a while, Zhao Zechuan learned that the Mo family in the capital had already been exiled to the northwest.","That matched up perfectly. Brother Mo Jiu in front of him was undoubtedly the former Duke Who Protects the Nation.","He just didn't know why such a prominent figure had fallen to the point of exile?","Zhao Zechuan was not to blame for not being able to figure out the reason. Even the Mo family themselves did not understand why they had received such a result in return for shedding their blood on the battlefield to defend the Da Shun Dynasty.","Although Zhao Zechuan did not understand the reason why the Mo family was exiled, he still deeply respected a family that had defended the Da Shun nation with their lives.","Therefore, when facing Mo Jiuye, who was exiled by the imperial edict, he did not have any sense of superiority.","On the contrary, he felt that Mo Jiuye was the one he should respect.","\"Brother Mo Jiu, last night I finished writing the petition and was going to deliver it to the county prefect early. If you're going into the city, could you give me a ride?\"","Mo Jiuye shifted his body to the side to make room next to him.","\"I'm going to meet someone near the county government, so it happens to be on the way.\"","After Zhao Zechuan thanked him, he sat on the other side of Mo Jiuye.","Driving a mule cart into the city would take at least an hour and a half. Mo Jiuye simply asked about the houses at the foot of the mountain.","\"Brother Zechuan, who owns those houses at the foot of the mountain?\"","\"Those old residences all belong to our three families. More than ten years ago, before Cui Wen became the county magistrate, the Cui family had just moved here, and there were also fewer people than our two families.","So most of those courtyards at the foot of the mountain belonged to our Zhao and Zhou families, while the Cui family only had five or six. \"","Mo Jiuye continued to ask, \"I see there is still a lot of barren land around those courtyards. Do those wastelands have owners?\"","As the eldest son of the head of a clan, he was still very clear about the situation in the village.","\"That land was reclaimed by my father's generation just to get more harvest.","Later, our Zhao and Zhou families were bullied by the Cui family. They forcibly exchanged the wasteland they had reclaimed themselves for our good fields. So our two families simply stopped taking care of the land at the foot of the mountain.","After working hard for several years to improve the soil quality, we had to let the Cui family take advantage in the end. Therefore, our two families gave up the land there. It has been abandoned for more than ten years.\"","After a pause, Zhao Zechuan asked back, \"Is Brother Mo Jiu planning to buy farmland?\"","Mo Jiuye did not deny it. \"Since we will be living here long term, we naturally need to acquire some land.\"","Zhao Zechuan continued to ask, \"Does Brother Mo Jiu also plan to build a house in the village?\"","\"I do have this idea, I just don't know if those old houses at the foot of the mountain are for sale?\"","Mo Jiuye knew clearly that those dilapidated houses were uninhabitable. Even if he bought them, it would only be to use the place as a homestead.","After all, both he and his daughter-in-law were very fond of that location.","He had expected Zhao Zechuan to patiently continue to clarify his doubts, but the latter instead advised him not to build a house there.","\"Brother Mo Jiu, it's not suitable for long-term living there, especially in winter.\"","Mo Jiuye raised his eyebrows. \"Why?\"","\"Brother Mo Jiu may not know, in the bad years before, the barbarians often climbed over mountains and crossed ridges to come and rob food.","If you live at the foot of the mountain, you will definitely become a target for the barbarians to rob. The reason why our several families moved away from there and built high courtyard walls was to prevent them from coming to rob.","Also, there were many people in our families who were united. As soon as the barbarians were discovered coming, everyone would gather together to drive them away.","Perhaps because those barbarians could not take advantage of us here in recent years, they have not come in the past few years.\"","Mo Jiuye had caught wind of this in the past few days.","Facing tens of thousands of enemy troops, he was not afraid, so how could he be afraid of these barbarians who existed like bandits?","Moreover, he and He Zhiran had already discussed that if they built a house there, they could also raise the height of the courtyard wall. When the time came, they would also raise a few dogs in the house. They would discover any movement at the first moment.","Therefore, he was not worried about the problem of barbarians coming to harass and rob them.","\"I'm not afraid of barbarians. If they are discovered, beat them back. I just want to know now if those abandoned courtyards can be sold to us.\"","Zhao Zechuan also thought, this person led thousands of troops onto the battlefield to kill enemies. How could he be scared by a few barbarians?","As for whether those abandoned residences could be sold, Zhao Zechuan did not need to ask his father to give an answer.","\"The old residences have been abandoned for many years, and we won't live there anymore either. If Brother Mo Jiu proposes to buy them, I think everyone will agree.\"","\"It's just that the price must not be as suitable as buying wasteland and building new houses.\"","Mo Jiuye also understood this logic. Although the houses there were dilapidated and uninhabitable, after all it was still a courtyard. It was unrealistic to want to purchase them at wasteland prices.","His chat with Zhao Zechuan was also just to learn more about it. He still had to negotiate with the two clan heads if he wanted to purchase those houses and land.","There was no hurry about this matter. He had to carefully discuss it with his family before deciding.","There was also the Xie and Fang families. They had come to Xi Ling Village for his family’s sake, so he also had to ask their opinions when choosing land and building houses.","As the two chatted, they were nearing the county government.","From afar, they could see the county government gate surrounded by commoners, with officials pointing around and saying something unknown.","After thanking Mo Jiuye, Zhao Zechuan took the lead and walked over there with the petition."]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197: Real Seafood Freedom","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye looked at the sky, there was still some time before the agreed meeting time with Henry. He tethered the mule cart at the roadside and took He Zhiran to the front of the county government building to watch the liveliness.","It turned out that the commoners gathered in front of the county government building had heard that the county magistrate was going to punish Cui Wen. They came here to expose his evil deeds.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran looked at each other, both surprised that Cui Wen, who had been the county chief for more than ten years, had actually harmed so many commoners. He really deserved to die.","At the same time, according to the current situation, Meng Huaining must be busy at this time. Their original intention to visit was also dispelled.","While the two were enjoying watching the liveliness, a familiar \"bird language\" sounded behind them.","\"Hello, Ms. He Zhiran. You are very punctual.\"","The couple turned around at the same time.","\"Hello Mr. Henry. We can go to the fishing village now.\"","When Henry heard that he could go to the fishing village, he immediately became jumpy, showing his joy to the fullest.","\"Great. I will pay you for this.\"","The two took Henry to the mule cart. He Zhiran sat inside as before, while Henry sat next to Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye was also new to Yun City and was not familiar with the environment.","Asking all the way for the location of the fishing village, they finally arrived after half a hour.","The style of the fishing village was very different from that of Xi Ling Village. There was no farmland here. The houses of the villagers were all built on the outskirts of the beach.","The fences of every household were full of fishing nets, and there were no vegetable gardens in the yard, only some boat oars and wooden barrels and other tools left casually.","It could be seen that the villagers here did not farm but relied on the sea to make a living.","The mule cart slowly drove into the village and met a man carrying a shoulder pole. Mo Jiuye politely asked, \"Excuse me, is this the fishing village?\"","The man first looked at Mo Jiuye, then stared at the blonde foreigner Henry for a while before replying:","\"This is the fishing village. Who are you looking for?\"","Mo Jiuye continued to ask: \"Are there any masters here who can repair boats?\"","\"Repair boats? Most of us in the fishing village can repair boats.\"","The man felt this question was a bit funny. They had been making a living by fishing for generations since they were young to play with the boats at home. How could they not be able to repair them?","Mo Jiuye didn't care about the man's attitude.","He pointed to Henry next to him and said, \"The foreigner's boat is broken. He wants to find someone to help repair it. Of course, he will pay the corresponding remuneration.\"","When the man heard that there was remuneration for repairing the boat, his attitude changed immediately.","He put down the shoulder pole he was carrying.","\"I can repair it. Where's the boat?\"","He Zhiran knew it was time for her to appear.","She asked Henry in English.","\"Where is your boat?\"","\"It's at the dock, not far from here.\"","He Zhiran told the man the location of Henry's boat.","When the man heard that the foreigner's boat was at the dock, he became a little hesitant.","He had seen the boats at the dock. They were mostly large ships, completely different from the fishing boats he used at home.","He could still fix fishing boats, but he really didn't know how to fix those big ships.","The man tentatively asked, \"Is the boat you want to repair a large cargo ship?\"","He Zhiran became a translator again.","Henry said that his ship was a very large cargo ship, tens of thousands times larger than the fishing boat they just saw.","He Zhiran translated Henry's statement to the man.","Now the man was completely discouraged.","\"I don't know how to repair that kind of ship.\"","\"Do you know anyone who can repair it?\" He Zhiran asked.","The man pointed his lips to the westernmost end of the village.","\"Keep going to the end of the village over there. There is a man named Hu Cong. I'm afraid only he can repair such a ship.\"","The name Hu Cong was not unfamiliar to Mo Jiuye. In order to further confirm his guess, he asked, \"Is this Hu Cong you mentioned the exiled person distributed by the government a few years ago?\"","The man nodded, then asked back, \"Do you know him?\"","Mo Jiuye did not admit it. \"I don't know him, I just heard about this person.\"","Although the man did not answer his question positively, Mo Jiuye was already certain that this Hu Cong was the person he knew.","Hu Cong had served as an attendant at the Ministry of Public Works. Although Mo Jiuye did not have much contact with him, the two could be said to be acquainted.","A few years ago, when the Empress Dowager celebrated her birthday, she asked the Ministry of Public Works to prepare a batch of small trolleys with wheels for serving food.","At that time, this task was handled by Hu Cong.","It was estimated that he had offended someone. The prepared trolleys were secretly sabotaged, causing them to suddenly collapse when the palace maids and eunuchs were serving food, spilling the prepared wine and dishes all over the floor.","The Empress Dowager was very angry about this and blamed everything on Hu Cong, which led to Hu Cong's exile.","Mo Jiuye didn't want to reveal too much about himself to a stranger. If he said he knew Hu Cong, the other party would probably ask how he knew him, and it would be too tiring to explain back and forth.","Seeing Mo Jiuye say so, the man kindly reminded: \"Hu Cong has a weird personality. He never communicates with villagers. Even if someone finds him to repair boats, it depends on his mood whether he will do it or not. You will have to rely on luck now if you go to find him. \"","While the two were talking, the man had picked up his shoulder pole again.","At this time, He Zhiran also came out of the carriage. She just glanced casually at the bamboo basket carried by the man, and couldn't help swallowing a few mouthfuls of saliva involuntarily.","It turned out to be lobsters.","Not only were there lobsters, but also mantis shrimps. These were her favorite things to eat in her previous life.","Unfortunately, in her previous life, she was just a military doctor living on subsidies and couldn't afford seafood as she wished.","Although she achieved financial freedom after transmigrating here, she didn't dare to buy these untraceable things recklessly.","Well, tonight she was going to achieve true seafood freedom.","\"Brother, are you going to sell all these seafood?\"","The man didn't see He Zhiran's greedy expression at all.","\"These things are not worth any money. I felt it's a pity to throw them away, so I wanted to carry them to the city to sell them cheaper.\"","Sell them cheaper?","How cheap?","\"Brother, how much do you plan to sell these seafood for?\"","The man casually picked up a live lobster: \"No matter the size, each of these longnose lobsters is 20 wen.\"","Then he pointed to the basket of mantis shrimps and said, \"These mantis shrimps are 3 wen per jin.\"","In order not to let the man realize she was an outsider, He Zhiran didn't show any abnormality when she heard two terms that were completely different from her previous life, especially when she heard lobster. The character \"dragon\" was a taboo in this era. Who would dare to use it to name a marine organism?","As for mantis shrimp, it did look a bit like a mantis, so it made sense to call it that.","What she cared most about now was the price of these two seafood items."]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198: Hu Cong","paragraphs":["Here a copper coin's purchasing power is about the same as one yuan in my previous life. That is to say, a big lobster that looks at least two catties only costs 20 yuan. Fresh shrimps cost only 3 yuan per catty.","This is much cheaper than what she could buy on Taobao.","\"Brother, I want all of these in your bamboo basket.\"","The man was stunned for a moment, somewhat incredulously asking back:","\"Little lady, are you sure you want all of these?\"","Not only did she want them all, she didn't even bargain on the price.","It should be known that shrimp heads and mantis shrimps are not as valuable as some copper coins compared to sea fish.","These things not only have hard shells, but they are also prickly to eat. They may not even be sold if carried into the city.","If it wasn't for him having nothing to do today and wanting to earn a little something, he would not have gone through so much effort to carry these into the city to try his luck.","Seeing the man's expression, He Zhiran knew that she was being seen as a fool for not bargaining.","Although she had plenty of silver in her space, she didn't want to be seen as a sucker after buying something.","\"Cough cough... Brother, if I buy all of these, can we negotiate the price?\"","Upon hearing that she would buy them all, the man even suspected that he was having hallucinations.","It should be known that no one really wants to buy these hard-shelled seafood.","Isn't this pretty girl silly?","In any case, there was business at his door, so there was absolutely no reason to turn it away.","The man tentatively asked:","\"Little lady, do you really plan to buy all of these?\"","He Zhiran did not deny it.","\"Well, as long as the price is reasonable, I want them all.\"","Hearing this, the man put down his carrying pole again.","\"I have twelve shrimp heads here. If you want them all, I'll charge you 200 wen.","As for those mantis shrimps, there must be at least 30 catties. I'll charge you 50 wen. This price is already very fair.\"","At the end, he explained again, afraid that she would find it too expensive.","250 wen? What a auspicious number.","Seeing that He Zhiran was about to pay, Mo Jiuye quickly stopped her.","Although he had never eaten this kind of seafood, he also knew that this was unwanted stuff.","He believed that even if the man carried these seafood into the city, he would not be able to sell them for such a high price.","It was obvious that he was trying to take advantage of their ignorance.","\"250 wen is too expensive. You might as well carry them into the city to sell. I want to see how much they can sell for in the city.\"","He Zhiran's thoughts were the same as Mo Jiuye's. As newcomers, they did not want to be seen as suckers.","The man did not expect that his intention to pluck a bit of wool would be seen through so quickly.","Moreover, judging from their attitude, it seemed that they were not going to buy anymore.","This would not do. Having encountered a buyer, there was absolutely no reason to let them get away.","\"Hehe... Brother, how much do you think is fair for these seafood?\"","In fact, Mo Jiuye did not understand the market price for seafood either. He only knew that this stuff was definitely not worth 250 wen.","\"You name a fair price yourself. If it's suitable we'll buy them. If not, then forget it.\"","Seeing that they had a rather firm attitude, the man did not dare to continue harboring the intention to take advantage.","He said with an awkward smile, \"Alright, including the two bamboo baskets, I'll give them all to you for 150 wen. What do you think?\"","Mo Jiuye was also not going to waste more time here. He simply made a counter offer right away.","\"100 wen. If that's fine with you we'll take them all.\"","After he spoke, seeing that the man had no reaction, he was about to lead the mule cart away.","Seeing that they were leaving, the man quickly agreed, \"Okay, okay, 100 wen.\"","He was afraid that they would change their mind, so he hurriedly carried the two bamboo baskets onto the mule cart.","He Zhiran had not expected that Mo Jiuye also had the talent for bargaining. With just a few words, he had brought down the price of these seafood by more than half.","It was obvious that this man was trying to take advantage because they were ignorant.","He Zhiran was not going to say any more. She directly paid the money and happily got on the mule cart.","The mule cart moved on. According to the man, they soon found Hu Cong's residence.","This courtyard was quite different from the others. The enclosure was not made of wooden fences, but was built with stones.","There were no fishing nets hung out to dry on the walls like in other fishermen's houses, it was bare.","The courtyard gate was not closed. Mo Jiuye politely stood at the entrance and asked aloud, \"Excuse me, is this the Hu Cong residence?\"","After a long while, the door in the middle of the house opened. A slovenly looking middle-aged man walked out from inside.","Hu Cong asked impatiently, \"Who's looking for me?\"","As his voice fell, his gaze also fell on Mo Jiuye.","\"Ninth Young Master?\"","When Hu Cong was exiled, Mo Jiuye was not yet the Protector of the Nation, at that time, people in the Capital city all called him this.","Mo Jiuye smiled and said, \"I didn't expect it to really be Mister Hu.\"","Hu Cong had immediately shed his earlier lazy appearance upon seeing Mo Jiuye at first glance. A feeling of empathy arose in him because of the great incident of the Mo Family's exile.","Therefore, his attitude towards Mo Jiuye was very warm.","\"How did the Ninth Young Master find his way here? Please come in if you have anything to say.\"","Seeing that Hu Cong's courtyard was quite spacious, Mo Jiuye simply led the mule cart in.","After Mo Jiuye parked the mule cart and helped introduce He Zhiran and Hu Cong to each other, he recounted how he had found his way here.","Hu Cong's gaze fell upon Henry when he heard that they had come to find him to repair a boat.","After looking Henry up and down, Hu Cong, thinking that Henry could understand his words, bluntly said:","\"I didn't originally want to deal with you Westerners, you should thank the person who brought you here, otherwise I would not have helped you fix your boat.\"","Henry knew Hu Cong was talking to him but he didn't understand a word of what was said.","He reflexively asked He Zhiran, \"Miss He Zhiran, please help translate what he just said for me.\"","At this moment, He Zhiran was pondering Hu Cong's words.","It was obvious that Hu Cong had a very bad impression of Westerners, and even somewhat hated them.","Why was that?","Before getting to the bottom of it, He Zhiran did not intend to translate immediately.","She looked at Hu Cong and asked, \"Was Brother Hu bullied by Westerners before?\"","Hu Cong also realized that the Westerner could not understand his words. His question was directed at the wife of the Ninth Young Master, whom he guessed could understand the Westerner's language.","Therefore, he did not immediately answer He Zhiran, but asked back, \"Can the Ninth Lady understand his words?\""]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199: Where's the boat Show me the Boat.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran humbly answered, \"I just learned a little bit by chance and can barely communicate.\"","Hu Cong was silent for a long time before speaking again.","\"When I first arrived in the northwest, in order to make ends meet, I went to the dock to work as a laborer. My wife went to bring me food, and happened to be seen by a passing foreigner.","That foreigner used some kind of means and actually made my wife willing to leave with him...\"","Over the years, Hu Cong had always regarded this matter as his own shame and had never mentioned it to anyone.","Perhaps it was because he saw the foreigners today that provoked the anger buried in his heart for many years, or maybe it was because he saw an acquaintance and wanted to pour out his sorrows.","In any case, he finally couldn't help but speak out.","Mo Jiuye knew a little bit about Hu Cong's situation. He had stepped by step to the position of Minister of the Ministry of Works through the imperial examination.","What's more, Hu Cong was an honest man. He had only married one wife and had no children even in his middle age.","Someone advised him to take a few more concubines to have children, but Hu Cong did not do so.","Hu Cong was exiled but did not implicate nine clans. So only he and his wife were sent here together.","For a wife who relied on each other for life to be taken away by foreigners, not to mention Hu Cong, any man would not be able to stand it.","Mo Jiuye reached out and patted Hu Cong's shoulder a few times, \"Older brother Hu, it's all in the past.\"","Hu Cong nodded with difficulty, and his eyes fell on Henry again.","\"Where is the ship? Take me to see it.\"","Because He Zhiran did not help translate Hu Cong's words to him in time, Henry still had a bewildered look on his face at this moment.","He Zhiran hurried to translate again.","First, she translated what Hu Cong had said earlier, and then told the story of Hu Cong's wife being taken away by foreigners.","Henry could only desperately defend himself.","\"Miss He Zhiran, please help me convey that this is my first time here, and the person who did this kind of thing must not be me.","Also, there are good and bad people everywhere in the world. I must be one of the good guys from my country.\"","After hearing Henry's defense, He Zhiran laughed to herself as she translated his words to Hu Cong verbatim.","Hu Cong sighed, \"I know, hatred should go to the debtor and grievances to the perpetrator. This matter wasn't done by him either, so I naturally shouldn't vent my anger on him.\"","With that said, Hu Cong was already standing up and beckoning Mo Jiuye and the others to go see Henry's ship together.","Only two people could sit inside the mule cart. This time Henry and Hu Cong sat in the carriage while He Zhiran sat outside with Mo Jiuye to drive the cart.","Following the coastline all the way, after walking out for about twenty minutes or so, they arrived at the dock.","It was called a dock, but it was completely different from the prosperous Salt Lake Port.","Here was on the border of the Da Shun Dynasty. Apart from a few cargo ships docking here from the coastal cities, there was nothing else.","Today there were only three cargo ships docked at the pier.","One of the cargo ships was quite far from the shore compared to the other two, and its appearance was very different from the other two Da Shun cargo ships.","This cargo ship was not only tall in hull, but also had a sail on it.","It was very obvious that the other two native Da Shun cargo ships did not have sails but relied entirely on manpower to move forward.","Without a doubt, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran had already determined that the ship with the sail was Henry's.","The mule cart stopped and Henry impatiently lifted the curtain to look outside.","He pointed to his cargo ship and said, \"That's my ship. That cargo ship is mine.\"","Following Henry, everyone came to the seaside. In an inconspicuous place, a small boat was docked.","It was obvious that with the cargo ship so far from shore, Henry had come ashore on this small boat.","He jumped onto the small boat first, then turned around and beckoned He Zhiran and the others to get on together.","Arriving safely under the cargo ship, Henry shouted a few words to the people on the ship, and someone lowered the ropes.","After all, the ship was too high. Henry was worried that they might be afraid and explained, \"This rope is very strong, don't worry.\"","After saying that, Henry took the lead to prove that he was not lying by climbing up the rope first.","Mo Jiuye asked Hu Cong, \"Older brother Hu, can you get on?\"","Hu Cong nodded, \"No problem.\" With that said, he also imitated Henry's style and started climbing.","Seeing that Hu Cong was safely standing on the deck, Mo Jiuye hugged He Zhiran by the waist and leapt lightly, landing right next to Henry.","This move left Henry and his companions dumbfounded.","In his cognition, he did not know that there were still people who could fly.","He looked at Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran with envy in his eyes.","\"You guys are so awesome, you can actually fly.\"","He Zhiran just shook her head with a smile, but did not explain anything.","As for Hu Cong, he was quite used to this. When he was in the capital, he had also seen those guards running across roofs and walls.","How could Mo Jiuye, as a military commander, not be able to do such feats?","After the foreigners got over their amazement, He Zhiran urged,","\"Henry, aren't you going to fix the ship?\"","Henry collected his wandering thoughts and led everyone to the top of the cargo ship with his companions.","He Zhiran didn't know anything about ship repair, so all she could do now was to help Henry translate.","After an explanation, Hu Cong had roughly figured out where the malfunction was on the cargo ship and started checking it out by himself.","Henry left his assistant there to assist Hu Cong, and wanted to take Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran for a tour inside the cargo ship.","He Zhiran was not very interested in this kind of primitive cargo ship.","She knew that foreigners from this era sailed across the sea and came here for the sole purpose of making money.","When the foreigners came, they would fill the warehouses of their cargo ships with goods from their own country and sell them in Da Shun. Then they would take back some Da Shun specialties.","So what really interested her was the goods Henry had brought over.","\"Henry, can you show me your goods?\"","Although this was Henry's first time in Da Shun, during these past few days of looking for someone to repair ships in Yun City, he also discovered that whether people here lived wealthy lives could be seen from their attire.","He could confirm that He Zhiran and her husband were not rich people.","Therefore, he had never thought of doing business with them.","Even so, Henry readily agreed to He Zhiran's request.","He Zhiran had helped them so much that letting them broaden their horizons was good too.","Henry led the two into the cargo hold and uncovered the tarpaulin covering the goods.","The goods he had brought were now in full view of both.","Henry pointed proudly at the goods and said, \"These are all good stuff from our country. Feel free to look around.\"","He Zhiran was not at all unfamiliar with these items.","Apart from some grains that the Da Shun Dynasty did not have, there were also porcelain tiles that did not look very finely crafted, fabrics spun by foreigners, sheet glass and glassware.","When He Zhiran saw the glass, she thought of her future need to build a house. This glass could definitely come in handy.","Moreover, openly obtaining them from the foreigners, there would absolutely not be any issue of forbidden dealings."]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200: Killing three birds with one Stone","paragraphs":["In addition to the glass, there was another item that caught He Zhiran's attention.","That thing looked a bit like plastic cloth from her previous life, but it seemed thicker than plastic cloth and its transparency was also much worse.","He Zhiran could determine that this was the most primitive form of plastic cloth.","Thinking of the seasons in the northwest, although the winters were not as cold as the north, there was still snowy weather. At that time, the land would still be frozen for a period of time, so that two crops a year could not be planted here.","In other words, the climate here was somewhat similar to North China in her previous life, very suitable for building greenhouses in winter.","With greenhouses, not only would they be able to eat green vegetables that they couldn't see in winter, but it could also serve as a cover for her to take food out of her space. If the scale of the greenhouses expanded, it could also create profits for her family.","It would serve several purposes at once.","There were also fabrics. They looked more delicate than the cotton cloth of the Da Shun Dynasty, especially the colors and patterns which were very special.","As for those grains, He Zhiran couldn't really muster any enthusiasm.","After all, her space had seeds for whatever crops she wanted.","It seemed that she really needed to purchase some items from Henry to help conceal her taking things out of her space.","Because Mo Jiuye had been in He Zhiran’s space, he was also not very interested in these things.","Their calm performance was completely beyond Henry's imagination.","Supposedly these things could not possibly exist in the Da Shun Dynasty. Why were they not attracted at all?","If they were interested, he could completely give some to them as a reward.","Just as Henry was distracted, He Zhiran spoke up.","\"Henry, did you only bring these things to the Da Shun Dynasty?\"","At this point, Henry was even more certain that his goods had not attracted the two.","In order to demonstrate the superiority of his country, Henry went to the corner of the warehouse and brought over a large box.","\"The good stuff is all here. Let me show it to you now.\"","As he spoke, Henry had already carefully placed the large box on the ground. His delicate lifting showed that he clearly cherished the items in this box.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye stuck their heads together to look at the items in the box.","Inside the box, each item had an exquisite packaging box on the outside.","Henry first picked up the top one, opened the box, inside was a very ancient copper telescope.","This thing was not unfamiliar to either of them.","When Mo Jiuye was bored in the space, he would often pick it up and play with it.","Henry took the telescope out of the box and said proudly,","\"This thing is a treasure of our country. I went through a lot of trouble to get one.\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye simply nodded. Clearly, they were not very interested in the telescope.","Seeing this, Henry only thought they didn’t know the value.","Anyway, in his cognition, these two people simply could not afford such advanced things. If they didn’t want to look, then forget it.","He put the telescope back in the box and continued to showcase the treasures in the box.","What appeared in front of the two again were several palm-sized mirrors.","The mirrors were not the copper mirrors used by the people of the Da Shun Dynasty, but the glass mirrors that could be seen everywhere in later generations.","Looking at the workmanship on the back of the mirrors, they were all hand-crafted, and the carved patterns on them were also very characteristic of Western style.","Seeing that He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye still did not show any surprising reaction, Henry only thought they were dumbfounded. He continued to arrogantly display the other items.","This time, what he took out finally aroused He Zhiran's interest.","They were diamonds.","Diamonds more than a dozen times larger than a pigeon egg.","He Zhiran’s eyes instantly lit up.","Diamonds this big, if auctioned in later generations, would definitely be sky-high prices.","What was even more exciting was that there were dozens of such diamonds in that box.","In fact, He Zhiran did not know that diamonds were worthless in ancient times.","Because of the extreme hardness of diamonds, the forging technology at that time could hardly separate them, let alone crafting them into regular shapes to inlay into jewelry.","Henry brought so many diamonds over to exchange for some benefits by capitalizing on their aesthetic value.","Seeing that He Zhiran liked them, he very generously picked one up and placed it in her hand.","\"I see you really like these diamonds, so I’ll give you one.\"","He Zhiran knew a little bit about the price of diamonds in ancient times.","Originated from the West, they were not worth much money because they were too hard.","It could be seen from Henry's performance that if this thing was invaluable, he would not have given it to her so readily.","Since this was the case, He Zhiran readily accepted it.","After thanking him, He Zhiran pointed at the box of diamonds and asked, \"Henry, what price are you selling these diamonds for?\"","Before coming to Da Shun, Henry had already consulted with his predecessors about the silver and copper coins here, so he was not unfamiliar with them.","Therefore, when He Zhiran asked about the price, he directly reported the selling price he had already planned.","He stretched out a hand towards He Zhiran: \"Fifty taels, these diamonds for fifty taels.\"","\"Good, I want all these diamonds.\" Upon hearing this price, He Zhiran didn't even bother bargaining.","This was too cheap...","Seeing her say this, Henry was clearly somewhat surprised.","After all, in his impression, fifty taels was an absolute fortune for ordinary people in Da Shun.","Moreover, no matter how he looked at it, He Zhiran did not look like a rich person.","Considering that she helped him this huge favor, Henry sincerely did not want her to go bankrupt because of these diamonds.","\"He Zhiran, if you really like these things, I'll give you another one.\"","He Zhiran did not know Henry's thoughts.","“What? Are you selective about who you sell your goods to?\"","Henry was clearly very embarrassed and kept waving his hands. \"No no no, it's not like that. I was thinking this stuff is a bit expensive...\"","He Zhiran finally understood Henry's meaning at this point.","She chuckled and said, \"Henry, don't worry about me, I don't lack silver.\"","Henry could see that He Zhiran did not mean to bluff when she spoke.","\"Since that's the case, these diamonds are all yours.\"","As he spoke, he had already placed the box in He Zhiran's hands.","He Zhiran did not pay the silver immediately. She guessed that Henry probably would not want silver notes. Fifty taels was a large pile of silver. If she took it out to give to him with no packages on her body, she would definitely be questioned.","\"The silver is on our boat. I'll bring it to you when we go ashore later.\"","Henry readily agreed, then continued to showcase the other treasures.","The things he took out later were still very attractive to He Zhiran.","Rubies, emeralds, sapphires, and crystal clear amethysts. In short, the quantity of each gemstone was considerable.","In the eyes of Westerners at this time, these colorful gemstones were much more valuable than diamonds."]}]);
